{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread","id":32483,"title":"The Mental Health Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-18T09:39:49-08:00","id":32483,"title":"The Mental Health Thread","content":"A lot of people have a lot of stuff going on in their heads right now, so I thought we need a place where we can have open, supportive discussions about our issues. I would very much appreciate it if we could keep this a safe place free of judgment and bickering, but at the same time, I know most of us tend to see problems as puzzles that need solving and are likely to try to present solutions to the people talking about their problems here. That's fine; all I ask is that no one be a dick about it.<br /> <br /> I'll get the ball rolling.<br /> <br /> My depression history is well-documented on the old forums and in the White Wolf archive. I don't want to go into it again because I'm sure we're all bored with it by now. I will mention a more recent occurrence probably caused by it being winter and my depression is therefore being stronger than usual, to the point where I think no part of my life is safe from it, nothing too good to be corrupted.<br /> <br /> For instance, back in 2012 I met Loxofish for the first time. They invited me up to his place, I accepted, I went. I wrote a big story about it. When I got to their place, Devilfish was waiting for me out on the porch,* and the first thing she did--well, actually, the first thing she did was ask, &quot;Jim?&quot; because I guess the next thing she did would have been embarrassing to do if it had turned out I wasn't Jim but was a Jehovah's Witness or something who showed up with comical timing. The <i>second</i> thing she did was hug me hard. I don't handle being treated with things like love or kindness well at all, but a friend who trusted me and whom I trusted in return had called me and asked me to spend time with her and was hugging me like there was nothing weird or repulsive about it, and it was one of the best things that's ever happened to me.<br /> <br /> One detail I left out of that big ol' story I referenced earlier is that when I hugged Devilfish, I marveled at how small she was. I chose to exclude that detail from the story because it seemed a little creepy and was too open to too many bad interpretations, but I was just amazed at how far around her my arms went when I got to hug her. It's something that's stuck with me this last year and a half, every time I think about how once a brave friend hugged me and made me think maybe things were going to be okay.<br /> <br /> A few days ago, when I was thinking about that moment and how surprised I was at how small she seemed, the voice of depression spoke up in the back of my head and said, <i>You marvel at it because you have been alone for so long you don't know how another human being feels in your arms. Your astonishment is because you have no frame of reference for being embraced.</i><br /> <br /> So there's the best moment of my life, tied seemingly inextricably to a reminder of how alone I feel most of the time, which opens the door wide open for analysis of why I'm alone; the usual self-pitying bullshit about how I am too low and despicable to have friends. I'm not letting that one get to me--it doesn't get to win, it doesn't get to get to me, fuck that--but I'm hurt to discover how easily I can pervert the things I rely on for a defense against this stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *For some reason, I think Loxosceles was inside the house at the time. I don't trust that memory--it doesn't seem like that's how he would have chosen to let our first meeting go down--but according to my insistent memory, he was upstairs in the living room, standing next to the couch furthest from the stairs, where I met him and his dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T10:03:02-08:00","id":32506,"title":"","content":"Or, and this is just something to consider.... Devilfish is built thinner than the average. There's a reason people comment that she could be a model, because she has the currently popular build for it. There's nothing good or bad in this, it just is. <br /> <br /> For comparison, I used to hang out a bit with a model out when I was living in the Bay Area. She was a moderately huggy person. Again, not good not bad just nature. Every time I was amazed at how teeny-tiny and light she was.<br /> <br /> Because in my experience it was not typical. And hey, it's not.<br /> <br /> If you hug Lox, you'd probably feel like you were getting tackled by a dwarven linebacker who was excessively polite, and it would seem odd.<br /> <br /> If you hug me, you'll probably feel like you're being crushed by a really fat bear ( I have some issues properly judging how much pressure ribs can take before they start to dislocate). This would likely seem odd as well.<br /> <br /> In other words, your astonishment is not due to a lack of contact with other humans, it's from a lack of contact with Devilfish specifically, or at least someone with a very similar build since everyone is somewhat unique.<br /> <br /> So... there?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T16:01:23-08:00","id":32784,"title":"","content":"I don't know the people or situation involved but its good to be hugged, and size is relative. I'm a relatively short guy, 5'4 and I know especially going to college how their are people waaay taller then me and waaay shorter then me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T17:18:28-08:00","id":32847,"title":"","content":"I visited a friend of my mom's today and she is close to falling to pieces. After the first of the year, she wants us to take her to where I am being treated at. She gets into these bad bouts of depression and either my mom or her sister have to talk to her. She is trying to keep her boyfriend away from her because he does drugs and being a former nurse, she does not want it around her. Luckily she has Medicare so she should be accepted easily.<br /> <br /> As for me, at times I don't want people touching me. I will hug the kids, but I stay in my chair. I have not had any adult relationships in years, but I don't mind. Blame my drugs...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T17:22:52-08:00","id":32853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=32506#post32506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, and this is just something to consider...Devilfish is built thinner than the average.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh shush, you; quit acting like logic is supposed to have some kind of place in my thought processes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T21:49:48-08:00","id":32964,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T03:20:39-08:00","id":33046,"title":"","content":"Killer, you got a &quot;promotion&quot; at work, doing the garden section. Use your job as therapy....plants can pick up on your emotions. Don't be afraid to talk to the plants (Boston ferns are a bit snotty anyway). I love dealing with our roses and I am going to get some chives and rosemary to put in a patch in the front yard. Last year, I had to teach Mom how to BBQ, mainly because I wanted hamburgers and hotdogs and I remember how to cook that way from Bo (that man can do a mean ribeye and beef ribs). Mom mention something about the front patch yesterday, so I hope she is not going to pull the irises out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T07:28:47-08:00","id":33167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=32964#post32964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm doing better. probably because I quit drinking like a fucking idiot. Not sure what else I should write here. I'm still feeling melancholic but starting to just feel numb now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep telling you, find your bliss (or fudge). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, not discussing my own problems on here right now because A) I just did it elsewhere and 2) it's one of the few things I am a total fucking coward about.<br /> <br /> So, just letting you guys know you've got some serious guts for spilling your guts on here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T13:52:47-08:00","id":33377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=32964#post32964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so I curbed my drinking. this is after I realized that drinking every night out of self pity for 3 weeks was causing terrible side effects to my body (the most obvious being the runs I had for 2 days). Truth is, I wasn't drinking to make myself feel better about a what truly bothered me. I was doing it because I was trying to kill myself in the most passive aggressive way possible. The fact that was the goal is obviously troublesome. I need to probably talk to my therapist again but I can't afford that right now. My insurance company told me to eat shit and I have to pay $75 for each visit now (and this is after the doctor's office decided to help me out by giving me 25% off). I'm not taking excess medication or anything bad and I'm pretty well recovered from my little stunt. I'm worried to tell her though. I know that a few months ago I nearly broke all the way down and I was almost carted off. I don't want to be carted off.<br /> <br /> I'm doing better. probably because I quit drinking like a fucking idiot. Not sure what else I should write here. I'm still feeling melancholic but starting to just feel numb now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really sorry about this. I don't drink myself because I've been depressed my whole life and I know it would mean oblivion for me to latch onto a habit. I didn't even want to take any meds because I was stubborn and wanted to handle things on my own. But I had a friend who had a drinking problem and she wouldn't listen to me or anyone else when we were concerned. She only started handling it because she almost got fired. But at least you know why you drink and you could stop. I hate feeling numb myself, I had to feel that way just to get through highschool and I absolutely hate it. So you need to let your emotions out to yourself at least.<br /> <br /> So many of us have such suffering and problems but I've found at least here you can get basic human empathy, especially if you feel alone, or worse surrounded by hostility.<br /> <br /> Its embarrassing to talk about your problems, but my advice is I hit rock bottom and vented here and it helped. You still feel depressed and vast amounts of doom, but you also feel some sparks of hope and gratitude from the basic empathy. At least know others are concerned, even if it is just others who are down on their luck and suffering too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T16:12:01-08:00","id":33498,"title":"","content":"I'm currently seeing a therapist about feelings of gender dysphoria.<br /> <br /> I've been a pretty unhappy person for some time. In addition to periods of overriding sadness, generalized anger, difficulty sleeping, and relying on videogames/eating/buying stuff to feel better, part of that has been a feeling of disconnect with my own gender and comfort with the opposite gender. Over the course of the last year or two, I got curious whether gender issues might be a big part of why I feel so unpleasant most of the time. And upon actually speaking with some transgender people, I learned that the complicated mess of thoughts and feelings I've been dealing with is a <i>lot</i> more common and familiar than the whole &quot;I've known since I was little that I'm a (man/woman) trapped in a (woman/man)'s body&quot; idea that tends to be broadcast as what transgender people experience.<br /> <br /> Still, I don't feel comfortable just yet with the idea of getting a prescription for hormone pills and setting in motion major changes to my body. I worry that maybe gender issues aren't actually the root problem here, and that maybe I've just built them up to be a scapegoat for all the things I'm unhappy about. I don't know, so I'm doing what I can in therapy to come to an answer (i.e. what, if anything, should I do.)<br /> <br /> So that's fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T16:24:05-08:00","id":33514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=33498#post33498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently seeing a therapist about feelings of gender dysphoria.<br /> <br /> I've been a pretty unhappy person for some time. In addition to periods of overriding sadness, generalized anger, difficulty sleeping, and relying on videogames/eating/buying stuff to feel better, part of that has been a feeling of disconnect with my own gender and comfort with the opposite gender. Over the course of the last year or two, I got curious whether gender issues might be a big part of why I feel so unpleasant most of the time. And upon actually speaking with some transgender people, I learned that the complicated mess of thoughts and feelings I've been dealing with is a <i>lot</i> more common and familiar than the whole &quot;I've known since I was little that I'm a (man/woman) trapped in a (woman/man)'s body&quot; idea that tends to be broadcast as what transgender people experience.<br /> <br /> Still, I don't feel comfortable just yet with the idea of getting a prescription for hormone pills and setting in motion major changes to my body. I worry that maybe gender issues aren't actually the root problem here, and that maybe I've just built them up to be a scapegoat for all the things I'm unhappy about. I don't know, so I'm doing what I can in therapy to come to an answer (i.e. what, if anything, should I do.)<br /> <br /> So that's fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a big thing to deal with. I've had transgender friends and just the hormone treatments alone have caused lots of emotional stress. I'm glad you're reflecting on the possible sources of your issues rather then immediately jumping to an arduous road. I think over all it beneficial to take your time thinking on this major subject carefully before make your choice. I know someone who in my opinion seemed to rush into this and rushing into the process at such a complicated time in the persons life just made the person regularly fall apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T19:03:22-08:00","id":33627,"title":"","content":"In late July, I got a job with a very excellent company that involved inbound phone customer service. The training was seriously fantastic, and I had a lot of fun through it... Right until I started actually taking calls. Now, I'd always had some anxiety issues, but generally I could control them. After a few days on the phones, not so much. I started having breakdowns, started calling off.<br /> <br /> I made it through until the tail end of September, finally resigned in October. The anxiety had gotten so bad I was having panic attacks on my way to work and in the parking lot, just sitting down in my work chair made me feel like I was going to pass out. My body was doing its typical reaction to stress, to the point that I ended up on medication for IBS - I thought perhaps leaving the job would take care of the anxiety, or I'd have anxiety medication as well.<br /> <br /> My job life was bad enough, but my then-roommates were also getting distant at best and nasty at worst [their animals were using part of the upstairs, which was my section of the house, for a lavatory, but I got told I'd have to get rid of my cat for much more minor things in <i>their</i> rooms], and my online social life was falling apart. I'm not going to drag anybody through the mud over it, because we're all trying to make amends, but suffice it to say that I spent most of my time bawling or staring blankly. I finally moved back in with my parents earlier this month, and lemme tell you: Best decision I've made all year. Graduating college doesn't count, because I decided that last year.<br /> <br /> I'm still falling apart at the seams a lot of the time, but I always manage to drag myself back up to my feet. Onward and upward I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T19:48:37-08:00","id":33641,"title":"","content":"At least you have the option of moving back home. That is nothing to sneeze at.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Friggin dying seems like a very real possibility for me sometimes do to not having a default option to go to. So seriously don't feel bad about going back home with your parents, unless its an abusive household. Save pride for when your better.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T19:54:39-08:00","id":33643,"title":"","content":"Haha it'd been the plan since shortly after I'd gotten said job - the problems with my roommates had already started. And it's honestly not a bad thing - my mother has parkinsons, and though she's finally got the diagnosis and treatment having someone home or nearby who can take care of things for her is important. I had just wanted to have a job and be able to help with bills before moving in.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Believe me, Elda, if there were more I could do for ya I would. It seems like everybody's got shit luck right about now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T20:25:31-08:00","id":33656,"title":"","content":"Roommates can be pains, if you get good ones your lucky. I've had roommates that I've taken in and literally gave my room too and let them not even pay rent and they still ended up taking out their frustrations on me. Its good though that you get to be home when your parent is sick. You'll be able to help out even if you don't start off with a job, I'll bet your mom appreciates having one of her kids/her only kid back in the house. Parkinsons is a scary illness too. Moral support can be infinitely helpful, my mom passed away when I was really young so even getting a hug from her would be unprecedented miracle for me.<br /> <br /> Don't beat up on yourself though. Things will look up. I'm just trying to point out you are not in any sort of corner now that you moved back home. That should help your anxiety right there, especially since you don't have to talk as customer support. You have time to get off your feet, and you can be infinitely helpful without immediately getting a job. Just take your time. Anxiety can get really bad when cornered in a bad position just remember your not cornered anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And you've helped plenty so don't beat yourself up over my situation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm absolutely terrified everyday, I've been off anti anxiety and antidepressants for half a year and its not helping, but I'm trying to concentrate on making it past winter and if I can do that that buys me some more time at least. And I've got the worst of winter hopefully over and by march I hope things will be warmer, and if I'm lucky I would have cut through enough red tape to have something done.<br /> <br /> Things feel insanely dark for me but I have no choice but to try to look on the bright side, and hope I can get my cats out of this damned dungeon and back into the sun. I still don't feel well but just knowing how bad I felt a week ago and a week before that I know there are several degrees of worse for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T21:47:09-08:00","id":33682,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the good thing. That and I've discovered that if I pay attention, the dumb panicky voice at the back of my head is <i>male</i>. Most of my narrated thoughts are female, so if it feels male I know to question it within an inch of its metaphorical life. And dear gods yes. I like customer service. I'm a badass at it! And I rock the house in person. It's just on the phone I go to pieces.<br /> <br /> c:<br /> <br /> Yeah. You can do it! You've got the spirit to pull through this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T22:31:33-08:00","id":33708,"title":"","content":"I suffer from clinical depression. It runs in my family; my dad has it, my mom has it, her mom had it and her sisters all had it. Her mom and all 3 of her sisters eventually ended up committing suicide in fact. So I tend to keep a close eye on my mental health. When I start having bad days, I do what I can to lift my spirits. It sounds a bit trite, but I know if I don't, there's a good chance I could just spiral down and never come back up. Things have been going fairly well for me lately though, and I don't have much to complain about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T02:41:44-08:00","id":34368,"title":"","content":"This actually begs a question that I always wonder whenever I see people posting about these sorts of issues on a hobby forum. If people feel comfortable saying, does tabletop roleplaying aid you in dealing with whatever you suffer from? Do you use it as a tool to explore your issues, or as something to help escape from them? Is your enjoyment and experience of roleplaying disconnected from your issues?<br /> <br /> I'm certain there's some very in depth examples of using tabletop roleplay to treat issues, but I'm curious about individual experiences. I've noticed that as I've become more depressed and retreated from people around me, I've spent a greater amount of time working on preparing game material for sessions that I'm frankly not going to be running until weeks in the future.<br /> <br /> I've also noticed that while I have a tendency to play characters of both genders with an even distribution, I <i>really want </i>to play female characters more than I do now, but I feel immensely self-conscious about it, as I've roleplayed a lot in other mediums and been very not happy with the way men have portrayed female characters, and I desperately don't want to be labeled as one of <i>them,</i> those people who play those characters for the sake of titillation.<br /> <br /> I'll also admit, as terrifying as it is to admit it (I haven't really written about this to anyone anywhere) there's a tiny voice in the back of my head suggesting that my reasoning for playing these characters has to do with dissatisfaction with my own gender. The thought terrifies me, because I'm utterly unprepared about how to deal with it. I'm fortunate that I have family that's really cool about issues of identity, it's entirely my own thoughts that constrain me from dealing with the issue in a broader context. I am... okay, being male, if that makes sense. But I think if I had a choice, I would be female. I look at myself in the mirror and while I am... okay with what I see, I like to imagine what I'd be like if I were different. I feel like I would be happier. Is that wrong? I don't feel wrong in my body, so much as I feel like I'd be more right in a different one.<br /> <br /> ... Which I guess describes feeling wrong? Anyway, I sit there thinking about that, thinking about how I play my characters. I'm not going to do anything that makes anybody uncomfortable, but should it make others uncomfortable that there is an element of exploration in my playing characters of differing gender? For added complication, I play tabletop with my girlfriend, who I love very much. I haven't discussed these feelings with her at all, because I see no sense in rocking the boat, and doubt I'll ever have the opportunity to act on them to my satisfaction.<br /> <br /> I also have to admit sexuality is also a component of that. In the past I've treated myself as firmly heterosexual. I've only had sex with women, not men. The thought of <i>me</i> actually having sex with men makes me distinctly uncomfortable, but the thought of men having sex in general? It's a thing I think about in a pleasant context. So I don't know what this means for me. It almost feels useless, like I might as well identify as heterosexual because nothing will ever come of it. That's a thought that upsets me, but I don't know how to meaningfully talk about it with anyone.<br /> <br /> For added weirdness (as in the <i>&quot;what the hell is wrong with you, Leet?&quot; </i>kind) my twin brother openly identifies as bisexual, I love him to absolute death and it makes me happy that he's figured that out and is comfortable identifying as that. I don't think I'd be considered bi and I feel super uncomfortable identifying myself as anything other than hetero to family and friends. There's absolutely no reason to feel that way, given their track record with my brother and in general. In fact, I'm sure they've seen things about the likelihood of twins sharing or having similar sexual orientations. But I feel like I can't say anything, because, get this, <i>I don't want to steal what I feel is 'my brother's thunder.' </i>How screwed up is that? I really don't like myself for thinking that way.<br /> <br /> I apologize for the oversharing. It's on my mind. As is my original question!<br /> <br /> EDIT: After posting this, I'm starting to get an intangible feeling of dread. Some friends of mine frequent particular forums on these boards and I absolutely <i>dread </i>the thought of any of them reading this. But I don't want to delete it either, because it feels pretty tremendous for me to have finally said some of this stuff out loud somewhere.<br /> <br /> But god. The terror. White hot fear.<br /> <br /> If they see it, it's my fault for putting it in public. I just hope they don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 12-21-2013, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T05:01:41-08:00","id":34401,"title":"","content":"I play men half the time because I grew up as a tomboy. You would have a hard time catching me to put on a dress (same here but I do have a skirt for funerals). My female characters were smart-ass or had some disability (Lasombra partially deaf due to clubbing before turning, lots of Malkies with obsessions, suicidal thoughts, bipolar). Luckily MHMR has finally found the right drug regime to work with my bipolar but I still hear voices from time to time but I ignore them (unless its Mom trying to find me in a store).<br /> <br /> Right now it is raining so I might lose my connection....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T07:10:20-08:00","id":34433,"title":"","content":"I work as a cashier at a grocery store. There's a girl who comes through my line a lot, and she's always super friendly and sweet and chatty, complements me on all manner of things, etc. So on monday I gave her my number and told her to call me. She has not, and it's tearing me up inside. I feel so alone. I miss having affection in my life, but I'm really particular about my friends and my SOs even moreso. And I don't really see myself as having any real &quot;draws&quot;; I'm a fucking cashier, I barely make enough money to survive, and my hobbies are pretty much all based around gaming/RPGs. And it's so hard for me to even conceptualize someone being interested in me, let alone actually asking her out. I feel like I'm just going to be alone forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T07:38:37-08:00","id":34445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=34368#post34368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also admit, as terrifying as it is to admit it (I haven't really written about this to anyone anywhere) there's a tiny voice in the back of my head suggesting that my reasoning for playing these characters has to do with dissatisfaction with my own gender. The thought terrifies me, because I'm utterly unprepared about how to deal with it. I'm fortunate that I have family that's really cool about issues of identity, it's entirely my own thoughts that constrain me from dealing with the issue in a broader context. I am... okay, being male, if that makes sense. But I think if I had a choice, I would be female. I look at myself in the mirror and while I am... okay with what I see, I like to imagine what I'd be like if I were different. I feel like I would be happier. Is that wrong? I don't feel wrong in my body, so much as I feel like I'd be more right in a different one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your experiences sound very similar to mine, and the feelings I got when playing an opposite-sex character in tabletop RPGs and video games were a big part of what led me to the idea that I might be transgender. I'm not going to tell you that the same is true for you. Only you can decide what, if anything, this means for you. But I will tell you something others told me when I started exploring and asking questions - there is no wrong way to be who you are.<br /> <br /> Maybe you'll decide, as I did, to seek out a therapist and talk through whether you might be transgender (and if so whether you should seek a gender transition through hormones and/or surgeries.) Maybe you'll decide that you want to experiment with crossdressing (either behind closed doors or in public), or that you'd like to adopt some stereotypically feminine habits like wearing your hair longer, incorporating jewelry into your wardrobe, or putting on makeup in the mornings. Maybe you just like playing female characters and want to do so without fearing judgment.<br /> <br /> I also want to say that whatever you decide this means for you, and whatever you decide to do, none of this <i>has </i>to have anything to do with your sexuality. Being more comfortable as a female doesn't mean that you have to want sex with men. There have been plenty of people with feelings much like yours, and while many of them do enjoy sex with men (or taking on a receptive role as part of sex, e.g. pegging), there are also many who don't. You can be a trans girl, or dress in girls' clothes, and still be sexually attracted exclusively to women. Lesbianism isn't restricted to girls who've been designated female since birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T09:44:31-08:00","id":34483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgmoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=34433#post34433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I work as a cashier at a grocery store. There's a girl who comes through my line a lot, and she's always super friendly and sweet and chatty, complements me on all manner of things, etc. So on monday I gave her my number and told her to call me. She has not, and it's tearing me up inside. I feel so alone. I miss having affection in my life, but I'm really particular about my friends and my SOs even moreso. And I don't really see myself as having any real &quot;draws&quot;; I'm a fucking cashier, I barely make enough money to survive, and my hobbies are pretty much all based around gaming/RPGs. And it's so hard for me to even conceptualize someone being interested in me, let alone actually asking her out. I feel like I'm just going to be alone forever.</div> </div> </div> </div> And as a special double post: you did the hard part. Maybe she will call you - after all, it's almost Christmas and that tends to dominate your time - but if not, you can do it again. Dating advice sucks. The way people talk about it, you need to be a romantic comedy protagonist whose life is a nonstop highlights reel to have a prayer of getting a relationship - but that's crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T14:46:43-08:00","id":34617,"title":"","content":"I would be surprised if the person ever sees her at the grocery store again.<br /> <br /> It's easy to be friendly to a person in a &quot;professional&quot; relationship. Giving a phone number? Possibly crossed the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T16:10:14-08:00","id":34651,"title":"","content":"Kinda worrisome today. I got relatives all along this storm front...some getting sleet and snow, some in tornado warnings. The rain finally went away and the mother to one of my school friends died last night. We had Christmas for my nephew and his half sister/niece since they are going to Florida tomorrow. Their momma has brain cancer so it is kinda hard for them to deal with it. I know my nephew has anxiety about it because he is stuttering. I tried to nap today but I was a little bit upset. Mom made chocolate and peanut butter fudge today. I could not find the wrapping paper so I used a printed tissue as wrapping paper instead. I got the present under the tree.<br /> <br /> As for dating...no. Blame the meds. I have no interest in dating and frankly I am sick and tired of these websites trying to get me to sign up for dating. I have friends on a BDSM site and we chat half the time if not advising new people that 50 Shades of Grey is just failed fanfic. When I am on Facebook, I am chatting with either Elisabeth or Bo, her dad. When I go down to Austin, Bo cooks me up a steak, usually ribeye. If not, we go out to a restaurant as friends...our intimacy died years ago. He gave me the greatest gift ever...our daughter after being told that I could not get pregnant (blame Beltane and $1 longnecks).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T16:15:00-08:00","id":34653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=34368#post34368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually begs a question that I always wonder whenever I see people posting about these sorts of issues on a hobby forum. If people feel comfortable saying, does tabletop roleplaying aid you in dealing with whatever you suffer from? Do you use it as a tool to explore your issues, or as something to help escape from them? Is your enjoyment and experience of roleplaying disconnected from your issues?<br /> <br /> I'm certain there's some very in depth examples of using tabletop roleplay to treat issues, but I'm curious about individual experiences. I've noticed that as I've become more depressed and retreated from people around me, I've spent a greater amount of time working on preparing game material for sessions that I'm frankly not going to be running until weeks in the future.<br /> <br /> I've also noticed that while I have a tendency to play characters of both genders with an even distribution, I <i>really want </i>to play female characters more than I do now, but I feel immensely self-conscious about it, as I've roleplayed a lot in other mediums and been very not happy with the way men have portrayed female characters, and I desperately don't want to be labeled as one of <i>them,</i> those people who play those characters for the sake of titillation.<br /> <br /> I'll also admit, as terrifying as it is to admit it (I haven't really written about this to anyone anywhere) there's a tiny voice in the back of my head suggesting that my reasoning for playing these characters has to do with dissatisfaction with my own gender. The thought terrifies me, because I'm utterly unprepared about how to deal with it. I'm fortunate that I have family that's really cool about issues of identity, it's entirely my own thoughts that constrain me from dealing with the issue in a broader context. I am... okay, being male, if that makes sense. But I think if I had a choice, I would be female. I look at myself in the mirror and while I am... okay with what I see, I like to imagine what I'd be like if I were different. I feel like I would be happier. Is that wrong? I don't feel wrong in my body, so much as I feel like I'd be more right in a different one.<br /> <br /> ... Which I guess describes feeling wrong? Anyway, I sit there thinking about that, thinking about how I play my characters. I'm not going to do anything that makes anybody uncomfortable, but should it make others uncomfortable that there is an element of exploration in my playing characters of differing gender? For added complication, I play tabletop with my girlfriend, who I love very much. I haven't discussed these feelings with her at all, because I see no sense in rocking the boat, and doubt I'll ever have the opportunity to act on them to my satisfaction.<br /> <br /> I also have to admit sexuality is also a component of that. In the past I've treated myself as firmly heterosexual. I've only had sex with women, not men. The thought of <i>me</i> actually having sex with men makes me distinctly uncomfortable, but the thought of men having sex in general? It's a thing I think about in a pleasant context. So I don't know what this means for me. It almost feels useless, like I might as well identify as heterosexual because nothing will ever come of it. That's a thought that upsets me, but I don't know how to meaningfully talk about it with anyone.<br /> <br /> For added weirdness (as in the <i>&quot;what the hell is wrong with you, Leet?&quot; </i>kind) my twin brother openly identifies as bisexual, I love him to absolute death and it makes me happy that he's figured that out and is comfortable identifying as that. I don't think I'd be considered bi and I feel super uncomfortable identifying myself as anything other than hetero to family and friends. There's absolutely no reason to feel that way, given their track record with my brother and in general. In fact, I'm sure they've seen things about the likelihood of twins sharing or having similar sexual orientations. But I feel like I can't say anything, because, get this, <i>I don't want to steal what I feel is 'my brother's thunder.' </i>How screwed up is that? I really don't like myself for thinking that way.<br /> <br /> I apologize for the oversharing. It's on my mind. As is my original question!<br /> <br /> EDIT: After posting this, I'm starting to get an intangible feeling of dread. Some friends of mine frequent particular forums on these boards and I absolutely <i>dread </i>the thought of any of them reading this. But I don't want to delete it either, because it feels pretty tremendous for me to have finally said some of this stuff out loud somewhere.<br /> <br /> But god. The terror. White hot fear.<br /> <br /> If they see it, it's my fault for putting it in public. I just hope they don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow its really brave to reflect upon such cornerstones of your personality and identity. Its scary but you may be finding out who you are. Don't worry about stealing your brother's thunder, if anything he should be concerned and should give words of guidance, but I don't know him so I can't speak for how well that would go.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as for the first part, I've found when I'm gaming is usually when I'm doing better, because its a sign my life is stable enough where I can do a weekly event, and usually its with good friends and will help me relax, and give me something to look forward too. It can also be a cause of Anxiety too, particularly if the game starts falling apart or when the players put all the burden on the ST and don't try to make things easy by say being on time or communicating schedule changes.<br /> <br /> But from my understanding some people will roleplay any gender, because its fun to play a different character type (like an old person or young person) then normal. Though I haven't played a female outside of a computer games, and even then I'm usually male the first go through. But I think computer games are one of the things that helped to encourage players try playing different Genders in RPGs.<br /> <br /> Once again I will say you're very brave to question yourself like this, and I'm sorry its scary, I guess that can't be helped. But I don't think anyone here feels any stigma towards you. Even if you aren't bisexual, gay, or transgender its probably good for you to be introspective, and discussing it is probably good for your growth. I mean I guess that's what this threads about! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But Good Luck! I have no idea what it must be like to be a twin!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T16:18:13-08:00","id":34654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=34483#post34483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And as a special double post: you did the hard part. Maybe she will call you - after all, it's almost Christmas and that tends to dominate your time - but if not, you can do it again. Dating advice sucks. The way people talk about it, you need to be a romantic comedy protagonist whose life is a nonstop highlights reel to have a prayer of getting a relationship - but that's crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> To be frank even if a random friendly sexy redhead threw herself at me right now and said &quot;take me&quot; I'd have to just politely put her aside and ask her to come back in a few weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T16:25:47-08:00","id":34656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgmoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=34433#post34433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I work as a cashier at a grocery store. There's a girl who comes through my line a lot, and she's always super friendly and sweet and chatty, complements me on all manner of things, etc. So on monday I gave her my number and told her to call me. She has not, and it's tearing me up inside. I feel so alone. I miss having affection in my life, but I'm really particular about my friends and my SOs even moreso. And I don't really see myself as having any real &quot;draws&quot;; I'm a fucking cashier, I barely make enough money to survive, and my hobbies are pretty much all based around gaming/RPGs. And it's so hard for me to even conceptualize someone being interested in me, let alone actually asking her out. I feel like I'm just going to be alone forever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Loneliness is a very real problem, and you might have to prepare yourself if it gets awkward with this girl again. But I don't know your situation, and it might end up working and she gives you a call. These things are complicated, but it is pretty gutsy to ask people out period. I was always someone not looking to fall in love, so I don't look for dates because I've seen enough of what misery desperation can wrought. But that's kind of what I liked about College, and to a lesser extent Highschool, If you have classes with people or live near them you can find people who charm you, where as for instance I don't really fall for people if I haven't interacted with them or seen them interact very much.<br /> <br /> But then again I'm a lonely fella, half the time filled with self loathing.<br /> <br /> But the bright side is you have a job, that's at very least an indication of a minimum measure of success, and going out with somebody is much more likely when you're supporting yourself! Do you live in a small town? That could be a hurdle in itself. I was never one for bars, that's why I found College to particularly keen because it had a lot of broke bored people to just befriend! :P Maybe you can find a hobby store, or a local college nearby if you're say in your 20's? If older I don't know besides hobby shops and internet to find others who share your interests. But its a good sign you're at least trying!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T20:33:53-08:00","id":34754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=34483#post34483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And as a special double post: you did the hard part. Maybe she will call you - after all, it's almost Christmas and that tends to dominate your time - but if not, you can do it again. Dating advice sucks. The way people talk about it, you need to be a romantic comedy protagonist whose life is a nonstop highlights reel to have a prayer of getting a relationship - but that's crap.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I know christmas is a rough time for a lot of people, but I keep hoping that she'll show up and/or call me. And I keep being let down. And I shouldn't let this bother me as much as it does, but it does and I do.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=34617#post34617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's easy to be friendly to a person in a &quot;professional&quot; relationship. Giving a phone number? Possibly crossed the line.</div> </div> </div> </div> You'd think, but a lot of people just cannot be bothered to put down their phone for 10 seconds and be halfway decent. This girl however would chat with me until another customer showed up and complemented me multiple times, so I took a chance. She seemed genuinely happy to get said number, but maybe her subterfuge beat my empathy roll.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=34656#post34656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the bright side is you have a job, that's at very least an indication of a minimum measure of success, and going out with somebody is much more likely when you're supporting yourself! Do you live in a small town?</div> </div> </div> </div> I live in minneapolis. There's plenty of people, but 99% of them are completely closed off. I'm in a Magic club at one of the art schools, but there's not a whole lot of people I'd be interested in who would be interested in me. I'm kind of picky about who I associate with, especially if I intend on taking them to bed. It's also hard because my hours are nothing even in the same county as the concept of stable, and I end up with a lot of 12-8p and 2-10p shifts, which makes it hard to do anything fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T21:57:59-08:00","id":34786,"title":"","content":"Hey that's good news in my opinion! You can afford to be picky when in larger populations. I've known a lot cool attractive single people that work crap shifts. :P<br /> <br /> As said its December, from what you said she seems at least friendly with you so its understanding if you gave her a number even if she wasn't interested. It could still work out. But you're in a city! I can't stress that enough, even comparing small towns to slightly less small towns is a degree of difference for when trying to find a partner. And well a lot of the catches that I personally know of are often single for long periods of time before finding someone they genuinely click with. Its sad but in my opinion patience pays off more then the shotgun approach. I had a friend and she would freak out immediately if she wasn't currently dating someone, even if it was for only a month or two of being single, and because of this she would date the first person she finds remotely acceptable and then she spends like a year or so bitter because she feels she compromised... She never took my advice that she needed to just be single for a while rather then get into awkward relationships.<br /> <br /> I personally say be as picky as you feel you should be. I was never a fan of friends trying to hook me up with someone because they only just tried placing any two single people they knew together. But some people are good at matchmaking, and some people rely off of it, so to each their own.<br /> <br /> I'm used to having friends with awful awful shifts, and one I knew married the first female he worked with out of desperation and loneliness and that didn't work out the best...<br /> <br /> So I'm saying you live in a city, so things are never hopeless for finding an interesting match! You just might have to be patient. And a wider circle of friends/associates can perhaps lead to finding someone you enjoy. But cultivating companionship, both platonic and amorous, can be difficult in general particularly when working inconvenient shifts. But let me say this, at least you have a job where you see a large group of all kinds of people. Its so far at least provided you with the opportunity to give your phone number out to this person. That's much better prospects then a job isolating you to an environment with no viable partners, such as say working in a building after hours, or dealing with only men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T22:06:46-08:00","id":34790,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T22:34:31-08:00","id":34800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=34790#post34790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it weird that I consider it a much larger setback if I start smoking cigarettes again but not if I become an alcoholic? My father is an alcoholic kind of. I'm sure he's bipolar as well and uses it to self medicate when things start going bad. the thing is, I'm taking meds. I'm already trying to better myself but I just hate myself. I'm not going to get anywhere because I hate myself. I'm going to end up throwing a dart at a board like my dad, picking something I hate and going to school for that then drinking until my liver gives out and I die at 50. I hope and wish every day that I die before then. What the fuck is wrong with me? What really bothers me is that when I drink I don't hear or see things. Visual shit is coming back. Its just at shadows and corner of the eye movements, not gone into real things yet. I mean what the fuck am I supposed to do, drinking makes it where I don't see or hear things. I don't know this whole thing is disorganized and confusing so I'm sure it's hard as fuck to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>God I'm sorry you have to go through this. That's precisely why I don't drink and never had, I know access to some form of Oblivion would be to tempting for me. But its not healthy for you! And you probably recognize that Cigarette smoking is just a dead end, its obvious that is bad for you, at least alcholism is insidious and people don't necessarily know you are in its clutches. But with cigarette smoking its like there is no mask to hide it, it will leech money and health.<br /> <br /> Its horrible, when someone is in such a situation when they want to drink themselves into a stupor all the time they should have loved ones hugging them and stopping them, but the world is so screwed up and too many people don't have that. I know its just the internet but moral support is what you need to beat this! You need much more of it than the bloody internet can provide but know at least that some people are concerned about you. It always saddened me when my friends smoked because I never smoked, and most of my early friends never smoked, but too many people I know smoked, and they were always people with too many problems on there shoulders. I'm cheering that you don't go back to smoking, and that you can keep from just giving in to alchohol. I've only had one friend who was an alcholic but it broke my heart to see her drink her pain away, and I used have just come and sleep it off at my apartment so she would try to drive, and also so I could help her keep her emotions in check. It really hurts to watch someone like that, so please believe me when I say I really hope you don't fall back into it. God I wish we had better health care, but we don't. But seriously from someone else that feels like he is in a hole don't I'm cheering for you not going back into a hole.<br /> <br /> Please take some solace in this thread, it was a good idea from JimKupopompom. There are some rather nice people in this community that will listen. If you need to vent post here. PM me or anyone else you trust here if you have too. Just don't feel like you're in a hole or a corner and there is no way out. I absolutely HATE feeling that way.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> God if I get out of my hole one thing I feel I should do is find a way to give back to the free clinic I used to go to back in Michigan. All the troubles I went through everywhere, that was the only place that would help me even if I didn't have any money. I took it for granted I guess because I haven't found anywhere like it since I moved, and I want to move back in no small part to get back to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T22:58:42-08:00","id":34811,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T06:57:43-08:00","id":34932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=34811#post34811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty good at masking.</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps that most people never suspect suicide unless they've been suicidal themselves. I know I used to take a weird sense of comfort in the idea that no one would see it coming and thus I'd always have the out of killing myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T14:19:16-08:00","id":35119,"title":"","content":"Ok, lets give this a shot. My mother is 64 and has terrible dementia. She can't really string an intelligible sentence together, badgers my dad to help her with every minute task, focuses on her negative memories (unintentionally), forgets and then remembers weeks later people she has known for 40 years, is starting to have bathroom issues of some kind, can't be alone for any time at all without getting super paranoid and upset, forgets that I exist, forgets that I am an adult, and has missed out on the first year of life of her only granddaughter. The doctors have no idea what is wrong, with one set saying Frontotemporal dementia and the other not knowing at all. All the while my wife and I are helping as much as possible and my dad is fraying around the ecdges. He is fighting with insurance to try to get some in-home help, but that's slow going. It feels like my mom has already died and my dad just lives with some crazy lady who looks like my mom but does not shower. I'm worried so much about my dad, if something happened to him too I would lose it I think. I'm an only child, so no brothers and sisters to help out. Anyways, that my issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T18:00:43-08:00","id":35230,"title":"","content":"Message removed by me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1090-tobias","user":"Tobias","date":".  no one deserves to read my message. You don't deserve to know my pain. You refuse to comment, well I refuse to let you see my pain. 12-25-2013, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1090-tobias","name":"Tobias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1090_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T18:03:33-08:00","id":35232,"title":"","content":"That's rough, ChewyGranola. It's also kind of in my line of work, so if you want, I can get you some information on ways to cope with her state of mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T18:53:30-08:00","id":35272,"title":"","content":"Okay. So.<br /> <br /> I don't feel safe talking about my mental problems here. That is entirely my fault. No one here has said or done anything to make me feel uncomfortable. My problem is with myself. I can talk about my weaknesses to strangers because fuck them, who cares what a stranger thinks about anything. My problem is that I know you guys, I care about your opinions, and I desperately want to keep your good regard of me. I cannot bear the thought of confessing to you that I'm still struggling with the same shit I was years ago, that in all this time I haven't been smart enough or driven enough or good enough to overcome my illness, because I imagine you will all be as disappointed in me as I am in myself. That is a blow I cannot currently handle.<br /> <br /> This sounds like I'm begging for reassurance. I'm not. It's not about that. It's about me having to do this thing in stages, and this is the prelude. This is me taking a first step. I am not brave enough to take the second step right now, but that's what the first step is for. I will add more when I feel like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T23:11:53-08:00","id":35400,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T23:51:15-08:00","id":35412,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry Cereal, here is the website for it. <a href=\"http://www.aa.org/?Media=PlayFlash\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.aa.org/?Media=PlayFlash</a>. For some reason I thought you already knew of them. I don't know much of the organization, but that is the website that should lead to all the information to get you in touch with your areas AA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T00:07:24-08:00","id":35416,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T00:11:12-08:00","id":35419,"title":"","content":"Good luck my friend, sleep well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T01:24:57-08:00","id":35446,"title":"","content":"I honestly can't talk about some of my issues because some of the people I have issues with frequent the forums. Twofold reasoning there - some of them are worth working it out with; others aren't worth the time it would take to enumerate my issues with them. [And realizing I really <i>do</i> mean that is... remarkably relieving.]<br /> <br /> In more positive news, I'm figuring out some of my anxiety triggers [a few songs I really love set off attacks; I am noticeably calmer and less likely to overanalyze after a <i>day</i> of not listening to them] and the signs to <i>look</i> for in myself - for example, uncontrollable trembling. Like I'm doing right now, yay. I'm slowly figuring out how to self-manage though, hopefully soon it won't be so big and overwhelming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T05:31:24-08:00","id":35517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=35416#post35416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Eldagusto. I'll check it out in the morning.</div> </div> </div> </div> Two things about AA: first, they're not the only ones around who do this kind of thing. Second, AA groups can vary quite a bit in their tone - some groups are very religious, for example, while others are almost totally secular. (This is a particularly relevant distinction since God figures into several of the twelve steps.) So if a group doesn't seem like a good fit, feel free to find another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T08:42:47-08:00","id":35599,"title":"","content":"A friend of my Mom's died Friday and her funeral is today. I can't find my velvet shoes but I find my black heavy duty Reeboks from when I was in the restaurant business. We were going to pick up a friend but she is already drunk so we won't be dealing with her. After the first of the year, we are taking her to the MHMR where I get treated at. Alcohol and depression and cystic fibrosis is not a good combination. <br /> <br /> I have not attended a funeral in years. Usually Mom represents the family but I am friends with the woman's daughter and I want her to know that I am here for her. I actually suppose to be a grief counselor but I let it lapse. The last funeral I attend was my exe-husband's, I was still in love with the guy but I was dealing with the beginning of mental illness (mania phrase). I can't attend family funerals...I would break down. I had an aunt died about 2 years ago and I did not go. Mom stayed with her brother for 2 weeks. He has not gotten rid of her stuff. Her sister cleans the house for him. Mom cooks for him when she goes visits him (he loves chocolate pies and cakes). He has his sons living with him, one being disabled, the other a cancer survivor. My uncle gets sun cancer himself because he is a farmer. He refuses to deal with his wife's death...my niece Myia love my aunt so much, each time they go to the cemetery, she cries on her gravesite. That is how loved my aunt was.<br /> <br /> So I will go to this funeral. I got my tissue ready. I found a purple shirt that was never worn (Mom had to cut off the price tag) that actually fits. I tend to take death personally. When Anne McCaffrey died back in 2011, I almost had a breakdown. She was my favorite author. Mom got on my eBay account and ordered the Freedom series for Christmas for me that year. I still tear up when I think of her. <br /> <br /> At least I think I am brave enough to face death now. I did not cry when Ray Price died last week. I knew he was due to pass on.<br /> <br /> And life goes on...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T04:15:17-08:00","id":36856,"title":"","content":"I should have taken a note from JimB and refused to divulge my problems. You don't deserve to read them. None of you. I am going to remove my post because frankly I am under the impression that you guys don't really give a damn. Others get compassion, I get ignored. I don't need you nor do I want you. This is the last time you will see me in the off topic forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1090-tobias","name":"Tobias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1090_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T05:26:24-08:00","id":36874,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry no one commented on your problem, Tobias. I don't know why no one else did, but for my part, I didn't even know you had posted here; I guess you wrote your post while I was still writing the one immediately beneath it. I meant no offense, and I'm sure no one else did either. I wish you'd asked why no one commented before condemning us all and storming out, though. After all, it is Christmas, and people are probably very busy.<br /> <br /> Ah, well. I hope you have fun with your choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T15:04:22-08:00","id":37036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tobias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=36856#post36856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should have taken a note from JimB and refused to divulge my problems. You don't deserve to read them. None of you. I am going to remove my post because frankly I am under the impression that you guys don't really give a damn. Others get compassion, I get ignored. I don't need you nor do I want you. This is the last time you will see me in the off topic forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry. I thought I responded to everyone's. I know you have a very serious issue, and the only thing making you functional is poisoning your body. I'm really sorry about your situation, please don't take offense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T19:14:25-08:00","id":37604,"title":"","content":"I take Artane because I get the shakes from taking Geodon (for the PTSD). I was just informed today that my Medicare Part D will no longer have it in their formulary. I can't see my NP until February and I got 3 refills left so I called in a refill so I can pick it up on Saturday. I hate it when the government decides to dictate what I have to take so I can act normally. If they take me off of Depakote ER and put me on lithium, I will go crazy and try to hurt myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T19:27:40-08:00","id":37609,"title":"","content":"As I don't even like to take aspirin, I'm pretty sure I'd go crazy if I had to take any of that stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T21:57:40-08:00","id":37694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=37609#post37609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I don't even like to take aspirin, I'm pretty sure I'd go crazy if I had to take any of that stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah before for me the only thing I had was Caffeine, and I was very unwilling to start taking meds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T17:15:17-08:00","id":38076,"title":"","content":"I was using MD Code Red and Amaretto to self-medicate before I crashed into a major depression and trying to hurt myself. These days, I drink diet MD and a bottle of Amaretto about every 2 years (I blame that Italian, God bless his soul, for introducing me to that liquor). I was also smoking...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T18:09:16-08:00","id":38094,"title":"","content":"I'm slowly weaning myself off of caffeine and sugar; both seem to aggravate my anxiety like woah - probably because the caffeine irritates the heck outta my guts which causes a sneaky anxiety spiral. Thankfully I've figured out the right ratio of decaf-to-caf coffee to keep me perky but not anxious and tea rarely has enough to aggravate it. Yay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T18:34:18-08:00","id":38101,"title":"","content":"There are some stores that sell half caff. Mom drinks it. I do know that Folgers make it as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T20:22:17-08:00","id":38147,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but my ratio tends to be 4 decaf to 1 caf, otherwise I'd go for that. c:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T09:49:15-08:00","id":38317,"title":"","content":"Depending if we go shopping or not, I get a 20 oz Diet MD to drink on the way home, drink a glass of decaff green tea (diet of course) and the rest of the time water. I am on Lasix for edema (THANKS DAD!) so I am usually going to the restroom. If a store has soda on sale ($12 for 4 half cases), I might get a half case of diet MD and have a can a day. I really can't have dairy because it flares up my IBS (we have a gallon of ice cream in the freezer for the kids). I have been told by my GP not to have orange juice or tomato juice (can cause me to have a UTI).<br /> <br /> I am on SSI mainly for the bipolar but my meds caused massive weight gain (was up to 326, now at 274, depending on clothing). I also got PTSD, fibromyalgia, BPD and gout in my left knee. My back is out of whack so once in a while I go to a chiropractor to get popped. If my back is hurting when I get up, I take 2 tramadol and sit in my computer chair. Mom accuses me of being a computer addict...and a book addict and chocolate addict. At least I am not drinking like I use to or smoking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T12:19:04-08:00","id":38375,"title":"","content":"Yikes. I can generally handle soda okay as long as it's not, well, too many MDs in the same day. Usually it evens out to about 3 2liters of generic [frequently diet] soda a week. My dietary restrictions aren't really all that bad, especially since they're very similar to my mother's [we both have IBS as well]. Mainly &quot;no high fructose corn syrup&quot;.<br /> <br /> My real issues come from a nasty combination of the IBS, PCOS, PMDD [which is currently not being properly treated =_=], and some sort of anxiety disorder. Thank goodness for knitting and roleplaying, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T13:04:43-08:00","id":38393,"title":"","content":"I got crocheting and Runescape. I kick HFCS years ago and I think that helped out with the weight loss. When it gets warmer, I will try to start walking again if it does not flare me up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T13:29:15-08:00","id":38404,"title":"","content":"Soda is very bad for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T08:44:25-08:00","id":38750,"title":"","content":"The girl isn't going to call. She has a boyfriend. I found this out yesterday, as she was coming in right as I was leaving and so I asked her out. So I got stupidly drunk last night. Like seriously, a dozen beers went into me. I threw up for the first time in about 3 years. Guess it's back to the old standby of crippling loneliness and depression for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T10:35:57-08:00","id":38784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgmoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=38750#post38750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess it's back to the old standby of crippling loneliness and depression for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fight it.<br /> <br /> You might not be able to win--I don't know your diagnosis or the strength of your depression versus your strength of will--but it doesn't matter if you can win. It matters that you do not make a choice to accept it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T13:59:36-08:00","id":38866,"title":"","content":"Yeah...crippling loneliness and depression make a person an instant chick-magnet.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T15:03:00-08:00","id":38909,"title":"","content":"Right now we are watching the Broncos game...my SIL has a cousin who plays for them (Vaquez, 65). I prefer the Saints...hey, those guys converted me when I was living in NOLA. We got my nieces for the next 2 nights while my SIL drives extra early to Tyler for her carrier training. I don't mind the kids but I feel I have done my stint of motherhood since Elisabeth is 18 and we get together for movies, bingo or cons when I can spare the money. This last time, I got to watch Doctor Who since they got Directv. Elisabeth wants to cosplay an elf (I know where to get elven ears in Austin).<br /> <br /> But right now, tired, bored, trying to hear the game over the noise while the kids play with their lincoln logs. I can stand for a few fuzzy navel wine coolers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T15:32:14-08:00","id":38924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=38866#post38866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...crippling loneliness and depression make a person an instant chick-magnet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't tell where the irony in this statement is directed. Would you please explain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T15:39:05-08:00","id":38928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=38784#post38784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fight it. You might not be able to win--I don't know your diagnosis or the strength of your depression versus your strength of will--but it doesn't matter if you can win. It matters that you do not make a choice to accept it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you. I know this wasn't directed at me, but it's something I needed to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T16:28:35-08:00","id":38949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=38404#post38404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soda is very bad for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll back that, I can't even take the stuff while I'm off basic meds.<br /> <br /> But I'm sorry Yawgmoth, but at least you know now and she wasn't ignoring you. But nothing is ended, you live in a city man you'll find someone eventually, the downside is it could take a while, like a legit while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T17:32:08-08:00","id":38985,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=38924#post38924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't tell where the irony in this statement is directed. Would you please explain?</div> </div> </div> </div>The last time I went out with someone that was all about the depression it just wasn't any fun. Needless to say, she had to get her act together first.<br /> Never went out again with anyone like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T19:13:24-08:00","id":39031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=38985#post38985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last time I went out with someone that was all about the depression it just wasn't any fun. Needless to say, she had to get her act together first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you mean, but still, I don't think &quot;Yeah, you're pretty much undate-able&quot; is the most supportive sentiment one can offer to someone who describes himself as cripplingly lonely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T19:43:12-08:00","id":39049,"title":"","content":"Well, there's a time for crutches, and a time to toss 'em. A person that's a font of negativity brings everyone else down. Whenever I feel depressed, I avoid people because of that, and I don't want others to see me in that way. A person that's a constant drag, is a person that others avoid.<br /> <br /> At least this is how I see things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T19:55:16-08:00","id":39058,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T19:58:13-08:00","id":39064,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T20:50:16-08:00","id":39086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's as true today as the day he... started this thread. Here. This one. That you're responding to when you tell a person that's feeling depressed because a romantic overture didn't go they way they wanted that they are undatable. So maybe don't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Undatable? Hmm...it would depend on who the person is trying to attract. If the person comes across as <i>&quot;Oh woe is me&quot;</i> and is trying to attract a self-confident outgoing intelligent person..well, all I can say is good luck with that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding a time for crutches... yeah. Here. This thread. This is a time and place for people to voluntarily rely on one another for support when they feel it would be helpful. It is a crutch, being used by people who feel that a crutch would help. You should not bully depressed people under a thin veneer of &quot;tough love&quot; or &quot;keeping it real&quot; or whatever minimal justification you're applying here in the same sense that you do not kick the literal crutches out from under a person with a broken leg. &quot;No one be a dick,&quot; it's not that difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and the problem with the whole of this is...What happens when you have to turn off the computer and actually attempt to live life, not virtual reality?<br /> Not saying that there aren't people with genuine problems. But real problems need real psychiatric help. Anyone that believes that he/she can get that over the internet should definitely turn off the pc and face his/her real life.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T21:09:29-08:00","id":39097,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T21:48:06-08:00","id":39124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=39097#post39097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many of us are already. This isn't us &quot;trying to receive psychiatric help&quot; its about us seeking help from our community and our friends. You never do that? Must be lonely up on that pedestal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah seriously this Thread isn't, Fix my Problem: the Thread. Its just a thread trying to derive some measure of support, and venting. Its better then nothing. But it isn't touted as a miracle cure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T00:13:25-08:00","id":39210,"title":"","content":"*pokes head in* I just want to vent whats on my mind at the moment.<br /> <br /> I'm struggling pretty hard. I'm somewhat happy for the first time in a very long time but i'm not sure it'll last and I fear the crash. Though i'm happy I still cannot control myself. I get so mean and uncaring without meaning to.(I have bi-polar, borderline personality disorder and sever depression, its a great combination really...) I'm calling a few places tomorrow to find out if'll accept my insurance that kicks in jan.1 but its a state insurance i get for free for being broke, and not many places actually will take it. Since I still have not rec ivied my paper work regarding my insurance(which says it covers mental health) I have no idea just what it will cover. If its limited visits its pointless. I cannot afford treatment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To top it off my health is not so great, i know I have some concerning health issues and have for the last year and a half but due to not having insurance NO ONE will see me. The free clinics simply are not specialized enough. My last trip to the ER I was refereed to go see a specialist, but the specialist despite my referral and lack of any income wanted 250 bucks for the visit hah if I had that kind of cash i wouldnt have gone to the ER in the first place. I'm in pain daily, have to be so careful of what I eat and even then it hurts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Somedays its like my stomach is trying to tear its self out and I want to die. I stopped going to the ER because all they do is give me malox(which does NOTHING) and send me home telling me its &quot;gas&quot;... Its hard to manage my mental health issues when i'm always in pain. I'm calling a few doctors tomorrow to try to find one that takes my insurance but an internet search has turned up VERY few who will. I'm just ranting because hubby is sick of hearing this and doesnt take my mental issues/health seriously. I cannot work(my mental issues, combined with my health problems make it impossible for me) and was denied for SSI 3 times before I gave up(they were appeals, I was on the last appeal and my attorney dropped me so I didnt file for the last one) I'm just sad and angry so much because there are things I want so badly to do, but cant. I dont even get out of bed much anymore, my room is set up so that i can use my computer without getting up. I dont have any friends really or anyone I can rant to.<br /> <br /> My only solace in all this crap is my cat Roseblack whom is such a sweetheart! and role-playing...sadly rpgs let me have a life outside of this crap. Heres to hoping the new year brings some better changes!<br /> <br /> /end rant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T00:42:41-08:00","id":39220,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Don't threadcrap.<br /> <br /> If posters choose to make themselves vulnerable in this thread by talking about personal mental health issues, they should not be mocked or otherwise given grief over it.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T00:48:02-08:00","id":39225,"title":"","content":"Today was not a good day. That's all I really want to say about it. I think it's about time I took a lesson from the pups for a day; if I can't eat it or play with it, oooooh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T04:48:22-08:00","id":39314,"title":"","content":"Thanks Ian...so far I am in a pain mood and I am getting on the computer before my nieces wake up and want to play Cartoon network.<br /> <br /> Last night I got Mom to start watching Harry Potter....now she sees why I love the series and the kids love it. Elisabeth has my movies and books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T07:20:09-08:00","id":39367,"title":"","content":"IT SNOWED!!!!<br /> <br /> Not much but the girls are happy and want to play in it. Not enough to make a snowball! Watching The Smurfs (tv series) with the kids and having breakfast with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T13:39:52-08:00","id":39562,"title":"","content":"Just got fired today. Fuck this world and everyone in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T14:25:00-08:00","id":39596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yawgmoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=39562#post39562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just got fired today.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been fired from a job once (well, maybe twice, but that was a school job the faculty decided to take away from students, so I don't count it). I am immensely proud, far too proud to let people know when they've hurt or humiliated me, so that termination is something I've never talked about because I felt judged and discovered to be not good enough. It is perhaps the largest blow to my pride I've ever suffered, so I'm impressed that you can bring it up. I couldn't have done.<br /> <br /> Want to talk about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T15:14:24-08:00","id":39624,"title":"","content":"Getting fired, especially after the holidays, is a bugger. One time the district manager wanted to have me fired but my manager said &quot;she knows the entire inventory and memorizes the customer's phone numbers!&quot; That job lasted 2.5 years when Elisabeth started to crawl and we lost the lease to the store. I bowed out of the job gracefully and several managers tried to hire me because I could run their stores by myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T15:34:22-08:00","id":39644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=39596#post39596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Want to talk about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I <i>was </i>a cashier at a local Whole Foods competitor. I was as friendly with the customers as they would let me be (if you don't respond to either &quot;hi&quot; or &quot;how are you?&quot; I assume you aren't feeling chatty and stop talking), I knew roughly 98% of the PLUs in the store, and I could get your shit in bags and ready to go by the time you had paid. But some people can't be pleased and are actively hunting for a reason to be butthurt. So I had a couple complaints because... oh right I was never fucking told what I did or when or where or to whom or how to rectify the situation. Just &quot;you got a complaint sometime last week from someone. Do better at service!&quot; When asked how exactly to do that, I got stonewalled. So today, the last day they could wait to fire me before I had union protection, they fired me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T16:08:41-08:00","id":39662,"title":"","content":"It is a common thing to fire people before benefits kick in...saves money, but you have a high turn over and the manager might be told to bad mouth you if you apply for another job.<br /> <br /> Here, I got Elisabeth her food server cert and alcohol server cert so she can work in good restaurants. Its just that no one calls her back after applying and she feels that is wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T23:06:47-08:00","id":39814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=39210#post39210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*pokes head in* I just want to vent whats on my mind at the moment.<br /> <br /> I'm struggling pretty hard. I'm somewhat happy for the first time in a very long time but i'm not sure it'll last and I fear the crash. Though i'm happy I still cannot control myself. I get so mean and uncaring without meaning to.(I have bi-polar, borderline personality disorder and sever depression, its a great combination really...) I'm calling a few places tomorrow to find out if'll accept my insurance that kicks in jan.1 but its a state insurance i get for free for being broke, and not many places actually will take it. Since I still have not rec ivied my paper work regarding my insurance(which says it covers mental health) I have no idea just what it will cover. If its limited visits its pointless. I cannot afford treatment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To top it off my health is not so great, i know I have some concerning health issues and have for the last year and a half but due to not having insurance NO ONE will see me. The free clinics simply are not specialized enough. My last trip to the ER I was refereed to go see a specialist, but the specialist despite my referral and lack of any income wanted 250 bucks for the visit hah if I had that kind of cash i wouldnt have gone to the ER in the first place. I'm in pain daily, have to be so careful of what I eat and even then it hurts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Somedays its like my stomach is trying to tear its self out and I want to die. I stopped going to the ER because all they do is give me malox(which does NOTHING) and send me home telling me its &quot;gas&quot;... Its hard to manage my mental health issues when i'm always in pain. I'm calling a few doctors tomorrow to try to find one that takes my insurance but an internet search has turned up VERY few who will. I'm just ranting because hubby is sick of hearing this and doesnt take my mental issues/health seriously. I cannot work(my mental issues, combined with my health problems make it impossible for me) and was denied for SSI 3 times before I gave up(they were appeals, I was on the last appeal and my attorney dropped me so I didnt file for the last one) I'm just sad and angry so much because there are things I want so badly to do, but cant. I dont even get out of bed much anymore, my room is set up so that i can use my computer without getting up. I dont have any friends really or anyone I can rant to.<br /> <br /> My only solace in all this crap is my cat Roseblack whom is such a sweetheart! and role-playing...sadly rpgs let me have a life outside of this crap. Heres to hoping the new year brings some better changes!<br /> <br /> /end rant</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow I'm really sorry, this reflects so much what I've been going through. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I hate going to the ER when they don't even tell you what to do if you are ever in a situation/having an episode again. So I will give this advice, apparently they have to see you at the specialist, even if you have no money if you were referred by the ER. They won't tell you this, and they will try to discourage you. But in my last visit to the ER they told me to go the same doctor and I told them they wouldn't accept me even after I made an appointment because I had no money, and they revealed that that is illegal. So when I called that doctor again and pointed out that the ER told me that denying me was illegal they accepted me that day. So they know what they are doing it wrong, and if you point it out to them they should get scared enough to actually see you.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps. I'm sorry once, again I'm going through the same thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I just want to go back to my old town, where I could get a Free Clinic again because where I am at right now they have no actual Free clinics...<br /> <br /> Good Luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T23:12:56-08:00","id":39817,"title":"","content":"Yaw I wouldn't be able to stand it not knowing the exact reason for being terminated. I'm very sorry for your loss. There feels like there should be some way to get a specific reason for termination. I'm bad with how all that works though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T03:04:40-08:00","id":39873,"title":"","content":"He should be able to get unemployment benefits now until he finds a new job. I did temp jobs until I was hired by the state years ago and started getting benefits. Each job was different and I had fun. One job was reorganizing a teacher's union office in a beautiful Victorian in downtown Austin. Another was editing an infectious disease newsletter. One taught me to use Lotus 1 2 3 for a military contractor and one of the main bosses there got me tickets to a UT Austin football game because he was not able to attend (emergency in S. America).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T06:17:44-08:00","id":39929,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I wonder if my intensely literal nature isn't part of some undiagnosed mental condition. I mean, I was in my thirties before it ever occurred to me that the phrase &quot;brush your teeth&quot; might refer to cleaning parts of the mouth other than the teeth and that maybe I should do, like, the gums and the tongue and stuff.<br /> <br /> I'm probably just being a hypochondriac. I do wonder, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T06:36:22-08:00","id":39939,"title":"","content":"I can't stand brushing my tongue...makes me gag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T12:38:38-08:00","id":40110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever read any of the... rampant supposition in essay form... write-ups of the idea that most/many men exhibit behaviors that qualify for consideration on the autistic spectrum?</div> </div> </div> </div>No I have not, and from the way you talk about it, it sounds like I might not be missing anything of importance beyond an anecdotal oddity. I don't want to clutter up the thread with unrelated content, but would you mind PMing me with a little more context about you described hearing this from? I am very curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T13:30:54-08:00","id":40134,"title":"","content":"Going to do my semi-serious/semi-joking/totally-not-researched answer to such things.<br /> <br /> I think if a lot of men exhibit behavior that's not considered to be a social norm, maybe it's because it's an enforced &quot;norm&quot; and not something we're all comfortable with in the first place. Which questions the &quot;normality&quot; of it and, to me, questions the necessity of it. Are we doing it because it genuinely makes others feel more socially comfortable, or are we doing it because we've been <b>told </b>it makes others more socially comfortable?<br /> <br /> And for these little un-norm social norms, I blame women. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My wife insists on doing all sorts of things because they are the &quot;right&quot; or &quot;polite&quot; things to do and her mother and her sister all get it, but the rest of us men around them do not. When men deal with women or women deal with women, these things seem to be &quot;necessary&quot;. When men deal with men, we don't seem to care anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T15:07:38-08:00","id":40171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=39814#post39814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow I'm really sorry, this reflects so much what I've been going through. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I hate going to the ER when they don't even tell you what to do if you are ever in a situation/having an episode again. So I will give this advice, apparently they have to see you at the specialist, even if you have no money if you were referred by the ER. They won't tell you this, and they will try to discourage you. But in my last visit to the ER they told me to go the same doctor and I told them they wouldn't accept me even after I made an appointment because I had no money, and they revealed that that is illegal. So when I called that doctor again and pointed out that the ER told me that denying me was illegal they accepted me that day. So they know what they are doing it wrong, and if you point it out to them they should get scared enough to actually see you.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps. I'm sorry once, again I'm going through the same thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I just want to go back to my old town, where I could get a Free Clinic again because where I am at right now they have no actual Free clinics...<br /> <br /> Good Luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just had the chance to read that thread of yours *hugs* The ER seems to just be interested in getting you out of there quickly unless its life threatening (and pain just doesnt seem to count to them)<br /> I wish I had known that bit about the specialists last year when I gave up trying to be seen and just decided to to &quot;live with it and hope its not serious.&quot;, Luckily my state insurance card got here yesterday, i'm for the first time in 7 years able to see a real doctor, and I've already called and made an appointment, I''m concerned about the price since they were VERY unclear on that, just that it would be 300-380 minimum +tests if done, and whatever the insurance doesnt cover I would be billed. Though I made damned sure to make sure bill meant they would mail me a bill and not a&quot;we expect you to pay at time of service bill&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm just so afraid its something serious, or that they are not going to be able to figure out whats causing it or how to stop it x.x<br /> <br /> Does your state not offer free health insurance to people of low/no income? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T16:49:15-08:00","id":40222,"title":"","content":"That is an excellent question. I am on Medicare/Medicaid...the only bills I pay so far is my chiropractor (Medicaid will not pay her) and once in a while radiology or my leg brace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T00:06:04-08:00","id":40390,"title":"","content":"I'm trying, I applied for medicaid and its over three months now... closer to 4...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T04:50:53-08:00","id":40455,"title":"","content":"After today, give them a call. Do you have a case number? Every few months they update my Medicaid without me having to fill out paperwork but use what Medicare provides. With my SNAP, I have to provide actual numbers (rent, bills) every 6 months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T21:06:32-08:00","id":40911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=35272#post35272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will add more when I feel like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like it.<br /> <br /> One of the things about my depression is that facts which should carry with them absolutely no emotional weight can become horrible. For instance, on satellite radio there is a station called Pop2K, which only plays pop music from the years 2000-2009. Whenever they play a song on that station, there's a two-digit number in parentheses behind the song's title to indicate the year it came from, presumably because they think people will change the station if they are not given textual assurance that Nickelback's &quot;Photographs&quot; debuted in 2005. That Pop2K has this policy should have no impact on anyone at all except possibly as fodder for dumb jokes like the previous one, but when I get depressed, that fact casts a sinister, grasping shadow in my mind, like a vampire's profile cast in moonlight through the terrace windows. That the station would document and broadcast such information is sad for reasons I can't explain.<br /> <br /> Don't even get me started on the time I had to leave Walmart because I saw they had double-tall cans of Mountain Dew with a hunter camouflage print on the can and large red letters along the top near the rim explaining that the can is camouflaged. That one was a bad one.<br /> <br /> When a thing that shouldn't matter matters, that in and of itself hurts. It hurts worse that I can generally tell when something oughtn't to matter and I judge myself for it, hating myself for being so weak as to let pointless things prick me. I wouldn't judge any of you if you feel the same way; if it was any of you, I'd make sympathetic noises and say, &quot;You have an injury in your brain, and what's going on up there is no more your fault than a stroke victim being unable to lift her left arm after the connections have gone down,&quot; but when it's me, it's unacceptable. That should tell you everything you need to know about my ability to keep a sense of perspective.<br /> <br /> I was going somewhere with this, but I've forgotten where, so I'll be quiet now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T00:19:08-08:00","id":40954,"title":"","content":"I don't see why anyone would judge you negatively for those two instances, hating what that radio station does and the stupidity of Mountain Dew. Seriously I see people act waaaay more petty about pet peevs then this, this doesn't even register as annoying in any way, its just your preference. But it seems to bother you that you feel this way. Have others mocked you for feeling annoyed and depressed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T01:28:50-08:00","id":40979,"title":"","content":"Aw, Jim... I... know what you mean about stuff that shouldn't matter, mattering. I'd attempt some advice but I am in an egregiously upbeat mood right now so it would probably not be helpful.<br /> <br /> ... Said egregiously upbeat mood is because I <i>caught</i> myself starting to panic and was able to go calm down before I did more than babble a whole lot about a very small thing.That's something I've had a lot of trouble with lately, and I <i>did it</i>. Yeah, I started panicking, but I figured out that I was cold and hungry and should go eat dinner and sit by the fire for a while instead of getting more stressed. That sounds like a little bitty thing but it's one of the first times I've caught on that it was happening before I went full rant-mode. It feels good to have a victory under my metaphorical belt.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm sure everyone here <i>can</i> beat what's getting them down. You rock! Maybe you haven't got a handle on it now, but you'll get one! Even if it's hard to believe it, you can do it! You really can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T04:52:42-08:00","id":41036,"title":"","content":"I was reading a story about a Marine and I started crying. I am former Army so I should not give a damn about Jarheads but what this guy did was beyond the call of duty. Now I got another trigger to avoid. Maybe I should avoid anything military all together because we are Army and Navy around here (Dad was a hospital corpsman in Cambodia, my brothers and I are former Army). I can't even play military style video games, just medieval ones or WOD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T05:22:51-08:00","id":41052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=40954#post40954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why anyone would judge you negatively for those two instances, hating what that radio station does and the stupidity of Mountain Dew.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a hate thing, though. It's a hurt thing. It makes me feel empty inside, and wounded. Or, well, it doesn't make me feel that way--I do that to myself--but you get the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=40954#post40954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have others mocked you for feeling annoyed and depressed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, just me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tluthal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=40979#post40979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aw, Jim... I... know what you mean about stuff that shouldn't matter, mattering. I'd attempt some advice but I am in an egregiously upbeat mood right now so it would probably not be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's okay. It's not about advice. It's just about talking about shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tluthal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=40979#post40979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels good to have a victory under my metaphorical belt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't it, though? Good on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T06:42:41-08:00","id":41074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=40911#post40911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it.<br /> <br /> One of the things about my depression is that facts which should carry with them absolutely no emotional weight can become horrible. For instance, on satellite radio there is a station called Pop2K, which only plays pop music from the years 2000-2009. Whenever they play a song on that station, there's a two-digit number in parentheses behind the song's title to indicate the year it came from, presumably because they think people will change the station if they are not given textual assurance that Nickelback's &quot;Photographs&quot; debuted in 2005. That Pop2K has this policy should have no impact on anyone at all except possibly as fodder for dumb jokes like the previous one, but when I get depressed, that fact casts a sinister, grasping shadow in my mind, like a vampire's profile cast in moonlight through the terrace windows. That the station would document and broadcast such information is sad for reasons I can't explain.<br /> <br /> Don't even get me started on the time I had to leave Walmart because I saw they had double-tall cans of Mountain Dew with a hunter camouflage print on the can and large red letters along the top near the rim explaining that the can is camouflaged. That one was a bad one.<br /> <br /> When a thing that shouldn't matter matters, that in and of itself hurts. It hurts worse that I can generally tell when something oughtn't to matter and I judge myself for it, hating myself for being so weak as to let pointless things prick me. I wouldn't judge any of you if you feel the same way; if it was any of you, I'd make sympathetic noises and say, &quot;You have an injury in your brain, and what's going on up there is no more your fault than a stroke victim being unable to lift her left arm after the connections have gone down,&quot; but when it's me, it's unacceptable. That should tell you everything you need to know about my ability to keep a sense of perspective.<br /> <br /> I was going somewhere with this, but I've forgotten where, so I'll be quiet now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're weeping for the sad state of humanity and the lack of cognitive skills amongst the general populace. Nothing wrong with that, it's how anyone who can think their way out of a paper bag should feel. I decided a long time ago to quit being sad about those things and instead have righteous outrage over it (which my wife calls &quot;being on my soapbox&quot;) or laughing at the sheer stupidity of the situation.<br /> <br /> Crying, outrage or ridiculous laughter are the only realistic reactions, since actually changing the circumstances are beyond the capability of anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T12:50:12-08:00","id":41255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=41052#post41052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's okay. It's not about advice. It's just about talking about shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Sometimes it just feels good to get it out. c:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=41052#post41052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't it, though? Good on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also one of those things where I will flabbergast myself with how I can go from terrified and crying more often than I would ever care to admit, to believing in everyone and reminding people why they're important to me. Freakin' mood swings, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T13:15:49-08:00","id":41279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=41074#post41074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're weeping for the sad state of humanity and the lack of cognitive skills amongst the general populace. Nothing wrong with that, it's how anyone who can think their way out of a paper bag should feel. I decided a long time ago to quit being sad about those things and instead have righteous outrage over it (which my wife calls &quot;being on my soapbox&quot;) or laughing at the sheer stupidity of the situation.<br /> <br /> Crying, outrage or ridiculous laughter are the only realistic reactions, since actually changing the circumstances are beyond the capability of anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, the guy who built the asylum. For anyone who hasn't read them (<i>for shame!</i>) the guy's house was inside out, the interior was where he lived putting the rest of the world in the asylum. He was driven to do this because he saw instructions on a box of toothpicks, and if people need instructions for that they are in no way sane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T14:01:43-08:00","id":41305,"title":"","content":"One of my favorites, warning label on a hair dryer stating not to use while <i>in </i>the shower.<br /> <br /> And I am 99% certain that it's on there because someone tried to do <i>exactly that.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T14:28:33-08:00","id":41326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=41279#post41279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This reminds me of Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, the guy who built the asylum. For anyone who hasn't read them (<i>for shame!</i>) the guy's house was inside out, the interior was where he lived putting the rest of the world in the asylum. He was driven to do this because he saw instructions on a box of toothpicks, and if people need instructions for that they are in no way sane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonko the Sane.<br /> <br /> I've stolen the name for characters a few times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T08:41:32-08:00","id":41738,"title":"","content":"Venting!<br /> <br /> My anxiety is higher then its been in awhile <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have 3 appointments over the next week starting with a dentist appointment later today, my intake appointment for therapy on tuesday, and a doctors appointment on friday...ALL of my doctors/etc are men..I should have said i cannot have a male doctor especially if i'm getting a physical(which i have to at my first visit), but I couldnt say that i didnt want to seem...weak, or have these appointments put off because i couldnt get over something that happened over a year ago...But i'm realllly not looking forward to any of this...I dont like going out at all, and the thought of a strange man, doctor or not touching me in any way makes me sick...its making me think of things i havent in a while now. I thought I was over it but i guess i'm not, i've spent most of the night awake and scared and wishing I could rip memories out of my head because they wont stop. As usual I have to deal with this alone. Hubby had work and his &quot;it happened a year ago you should be fine by now.&quot; Speech would just make me feel worse. To top it off my stupid tummy pain flared up again, and i had to joy of for a split second thinking of ways to make it everything stop. Though it was just a passing thought, nothing serious.<br /> <br /> I'm tired, cranky, upset, and when hubby gets home we're going to fight because I dont feel like doing anything more then going to sleep, and he wants the group over to role-play(which i already told him is fine, but i wont be playing)... I really just want to be left alone today, to curl up in my room safe and warm with my cat and try to feel better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is why I made sure my insurance covered therapy cause I need it x.x even if it just gives me someone to vent to in person, that would help me a ton. I dont even want advice i just want to be listened to for once without feeling criticized or stupid for what i'm thinking or how i feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T08:54:06-08:00","id":41751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=41738#post41738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont even want advice i just want to be listened to for once without feeling criticized or stupid for what i'm thinking or how i feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that's what we were here for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T08:57:36-08:00","id":41754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=41751#post41751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that's what we were here for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>true, i more meant a person in the same room as me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> typing and speaking are 2 very different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T09:03:18-08:00","id":41757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=41754#post41754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> true, i more meant a person in the same room as me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> typing and speaking are 2 very different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, easier to do stream of thought and get it all out while speaking. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T11:56:49-08:00","id":41858,"title":"","content":"I've been on anti-depressants now for... a little over two months, I think. They started me off with 10mg Lexapro (because that was the drug my sister was taking that was effective for her), and told me to take it right before going to bed. I started doing so, but my sleep was all kinds of fucked up: I was going to bed at about 0400 every night and getting up at 0700 in order to go to school. I felt &quot;rested&quot;ish. A week to a week and a half later, I started taking it in the morning and they upped my dosage to 20mg, which is the normal adult dosage. I started taking it in the morning, and that was better: now I was getting enough sleep... going to bed around 1900 and waking around 0400. Much preferable to me. But, a month after upping my dosage, the doc said he didn't like how it was affecting my sleep, and also asked if I had felt more frustrated on the drug. I said that at the very beginning I had felt much more frustrated, but that that had abated after about a week. He said he wasn't really satisfied and wanted me to switch drugs: he wanted me to switch back to 10mg and do that for a week, then start taking a half dose of Zoloft for another 6 days after that, then start a full dosage of Zoloft (50mg). I started this on January 1, so today is the third day of the full dosage, 9 days total. The Lexapro started helping with the depression right away (though whether this was the effect of the drug, or a placebo effect for starting SOMETHING, I'm not sure). I don't feel like the Zoloft is helping at all. I've had suicidal feelings several times over the last three days.<br /> <br /> If you got through that, I applaud you. Thank you for reading my block of text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T12:45:02-08:00","id":41880,"title":"","content":"I work in behavioral health. Call the office, talk to a nurse, tell her what's going on. They'll get you fixed up, or have you go back in to see the doc. Deal with a nurse when possible, they know as much and have less of an ego.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T12:54:00-08:00","id":41894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=41858#post41858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel like the Zoloft is helping at all. I've had suicidal feelings several times over the last three days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaand that's where the train stops; everyone off. Speak with a medical professional immediately. What you're experiencing may be nothing, or it may abate over time, b