14-01-03T20:07:13-08:00","id":42117,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T20:16:50-08:00","id":42123,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T20:45:40-08:00","id":42134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=41986#post41986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry again that I was a dick about it. It wasn't okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=42095#post42095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Classes resume on Monday for me. Which means Monday starts off another months-long stretch of barely scraping by, surrounded by people who alternately ignore that I exist or treat me like garbage.<br /> <br /> I feel like shooting myself. I don't want to go back.</div> </div> </div> </div>If misery enjoys any kind of company, that's pretty much how I feel about going back to work every Monday.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=42117#post42117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Work is going much better now that I'm out of that fucking deli.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really glad to hear that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T23:51:14-08:00","id":42163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=41858#post41858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't feel like the Zoloft is helping at all. I've had suicidal feelings several times over the last three days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different anti-depression drugs affect the brain in different ways. Each person's chemical makeup is different, so some people might see a benefit from one anti-depression drug but no benefit from another. And sometimes you'll see side effects from taking one drug.<br /> <br /> One side effect from certain anti-depressants is an <i>increase</i> in depressive feelings and suicidal thoughts. In that case, not only is the anti-depressant not working, it's actually having a negative effect. That sounds like what you're experiencing; you need to tell your doctor ASAP and try something different. <br /> <br /> When I was taking anti-depressants I had to go through 8 different ones before they found some that worked with no side effects (Luvox actually made me impotent; that made for an incredibly embarrassing night with my then-girlfriend). But just keep trying them till you find some that work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T09:39:12-08:00","id":42326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=42134#post42134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry again that I was a dick about it. It wasn't okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all right. As P. Bear said, we knew where you were coming from.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T10:39:40-08:00","id":42354,"title":"","content":"Caseworker on the 14th, bloodwork on the 24th, NP on the 10th of February. Medicare part D has kicked Artane off of my formulary and I need that for the shakes that Geodon gives me. The new doctor did get my thyroid and simvasatin ordered, which I picked up along with my sleeping pills and Depakote.<br /> <br /> I just got my HTML5 for Dummies (it has been over 10 years since I did web design and I know things has change) book so in the next week or two, I will develop a site pertaining to having bipolar, fibromyalgia and crocheting.<br /> <br /> Having a mental illness can be draining on a person. I was first DXed about 10 years ago but I had suicidal thoughts since I was 18, just did not act on it. I treated myself with alcohol so I avoid that now except an occasional wine cooler or Amaretto (Mom makes sure I don't buy alcohol yet she has spiced rum in the pantry, I am not into rum). It took several years to find the right drug combination to settle me down. While in the hospital in Tennessee, they called my Mom and told her that I needed a place to get treatment at and a home to be in. No one has any idea how many homeless people actually suffer from mental illness, especially after Reagan cleared out the hospitals back in the 80's. A friend got the money together for me and I was on a bus from Clarksville TN to home, a 24 hour trip. I had 2 months of pills with me and a standing appointment with MHMR who accepted me back with the paperwork from the TN hospital. Now I am 'balanced', just hearing voices once in a while, seeing shadows but I am no longer suicidal. I still have racing thoughts, especially at bedtime. That is why I read 5 chapters a night of any books I have (I read Baali clanbook in 2 days because I passed out while reading it). I collect books that deal with the Tudor regime and the War of the Roses. Once in a while I buy books for Mom because she constantly reads since she retired a few years ago. The library is small here in town so she might recheck out books by accident. I need to get her into sci-fi and paranormal but she loves mysteries and romances instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:18:24-08:00","id":42964,"title":"","content":"I started hurting myself over last summer and stopped some time in September. I didn't cut--too messy. I hit myself, and drew on my martial arts training to find places where I could cause the most pain with the least exerted effort. Simple and efficient.<br /> <br /> I hit myself again a few times today, because I hate myself so much for not being able to get a job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:33:53-08:00","id":42984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=42964#post42964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started hurting myself over last summer and stopped some time in September. I didn't cut--too messy. I hit myself, and drew on my martial arts training to find places where I could cause the most pain with the least exerted effort. Simple and efficient.<br /> <br /> I hit myself again a few times today, because I hate myself so much for not being able to get a job.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're hurting yourself you need to find a professional. Someone here probably knows specifically who can aid you if you don't know a free clinic. If not look up 211, its an information hub number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T17:47:21-08:00","id":43246,"title":"","content":"Contact the social services at the ER of your nearest hospital. They should be able to either get you to the right hospital for treatment or the clinic. They got me to the right hospital when my bipolar was DXed (imagine a mania stage for years and then crashing bad to the thought of suicide). Took 2 more hospitals to finally get the right drug routine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T20:58:50-08:00","id":45357,"title":"","content":"I think its possible I may be approaching a manic phase x.x I haven't had one in at least 9 months, and yet the symptoms are glaringly obvious to me. (I very well aware of my moods and when they shift) the rising irritability, combined with the ungodly levels of happiness, my ability to focus is COMPLETLY shot, as it gets worse in the coming weeks(if it does that is) I will get violent, and go from being irritable all the time to being so pissed off all day every day that my poor husband just looking at me funny makes me fly off the handle. Yet at the same time I will be happy because to rage and yell and scream and hit things feels so good and even though the voice in the back of my head screams at me to stop I CANT, because it doesnt feel like its me..., and this will last for months, before I crash down so hard, Every crash gets worse and worse that I worry that if it happens again I will have no choice but to be hospitalized for my own safety.<br /> <br /> I saw my new therapist on tuesday, I initially said I was not interested in any form on going back on my medications. However, IF this gets any worse I will have no choice. My husband will leave me if I get violent with him again, regardless if its not entirely my fault, and honestly I wouldnt blame him. He's dealt with my mental illness for 7 years...I fully understand he's at his limit. Still I dont want to loose myself again, it scares me...So I'll probably ask my therapist to help me get back onto medication, at least my lithium, maybe the Geodon at a higher dose(i build up tolerance quick, when i stopped taking it it had stopped working...)Or if they can find something better suited to handling this fucking uncontrolable rage, that will be fine... and maybe an anxiety med...I dont like the idea at all..I really dont, but they helped and I dont want to hurt him again...I do not want to be a terrible person and hate myself for taking my own pain out on him anymore... I never meant to loose myself, and I dont know how it happened. Excuse me while i get all self loathing and pitiful. /end rant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T22:15:40-08:00","id":45393,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T03:50:51-08:00","id":45491,"title":"","content":"Ouch...I am glad I don't have to take that one.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am up early. We started babysitting little Myia...my niece who does belly flops on me. 5 years old and can count to 40, play on Cartoon Network and loves Powerpuff Girls. Dora is so boring. She gets to play on PBS kids today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T00:33:44-08:00","id":47995,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure my family thinks of me as a suicide risk. That's fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T00:57:03-08:00","id":48000,"title":"","content":"I don't know what to do anymore. My head is full of screaming and yelling and broken glass. I feel hollow inside. I can't get these ideas out of my mind, like a flood pain and filth pouring behind my fucking eyes. I'm not crazy. I wish I was. I wish I could cope and still stay sober. I wish I was normal. Maybe I need to be locked up in a padded room. Wouldn't be the first time, won't be the last...... I'M SO FUCKING TIRED OF BEING ME!!! FUCK!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T08:12:28-08:00","id":48173,"title":"","content":"Disregard the above.... I was having a rough time....<br /> <br /> \u200bSorry...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T08:19:16-08:00","id":48178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=48173#post48173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disregard the above.... I was having a rough time....<br /> <br /> \u200bSorry...</div> </div> </div> </div>S'okay, I think we all saw the other posting with the cause. Just maybe call your nearest psych provider, see if they can squeeze you in for a bit. Just to be certain, k?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:58:10-08:00","id":48269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=48178#post48178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S'okay, I think we all saw the other posting with the cause. Just maybe call your nearest psych provider, see if they can squeeze you in for a bit. Just to be certain, k?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's sound advice... but with me, there's a very fine line between seeing a psychiatric professional and being hospitalized...so I'm really hesitant to go that route. Pills don't usually help, and I've been legally committed before because they simply had nothing else that they could do for me. I... I'm terrified of residential treatment and the state mental hospital. <br /> <br /> ..I'll think about it....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T11:50:34-08:00","id":48361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=48269#post48269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat's sound advice... but with me, there's a very fine line between seeing a psychiatric professional and being hospitalized...so I'm really hesitant to go that route. Pills don't usually help, and I've been legally committed before because they simply had nothing else that they could do for me. I... I'm terrified of residential treatment and the state mental hospital.<br /> <br /> ..I'll think about it....</div> </div> </div> </div>You can always ask to speak with a nurse or crisis counselor (most places have a few on staff) and just make sure you don't trigger the safety words (seeing things, harming self or others). You probably know better what will set them off since you've dealt with them before (or the doctors they work with). Most of the time, those calls are free, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:12:56-08:00","id":48385,"title":"","content":"Remind me not to read certain books...sets off nightmares and getting up in the wee hours of the morning, looking for pills because I got hurt. Need to keep a bottle of water nearby for the pills I have hidden in my dresser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T04:14:34-08:00","id":48862,"title":"","content":"My pills aren't working tonight. Can't relax at all. Ugh, I hate the way I feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T07:25:34-08:00","id":48939,"title":"","content":"I hate my body and mind...racing thoughts and trying to get into the right position for sleeping...not going to happen. Now I am up, in need of caffeine and got a meeting with my caseworker later.<br /> <br /> I hate being bipolar and having fibromyalgia and not getting the rest necessary for moving about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T12:43:31-08:00","id":49213,"title":"","content":"Hope you're feeling a bit better, Brujah. Fibromyalgia is rough.<br /> <br /> \u200bI've been taking a benzodiazepine, klonopin, for generalized anxiety, but so far, the only thing helping is medicinal marijuana. I'm just lucky it's legal here. <br /> <br /> \u200bThe legal disparity between states really cramps any future travel plans, though. It's strange. I'm legally disabled, I have a LEGAL source for my medicine, but I travel to most other states (or Countries) with my medication and I'm a felon. Bleh. <br /> <br /> I'm less functional now than I have been in years...<br /> <br /> I'm not taking care of myself the way I should. I feel locked in my mind. If this goes on for much longer, I might have to see a doctor for symptom management...<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T14:35:18-08:00","id":49297,"title":"","content":"Elisabeth went to her GP today and he prescribe a mood stabilizer for her and to lay off the caffeine after 4 o'clock. I lay off of mine after 2 myself. He is also testing her for thyroid trouble since it runs in the family.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, she is pissed at HP. Her Envy fell apart so she hooked the computer part to her TV (Dell monitor). She wants to buy a Macbook (no experience with apples, I fear...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T16:50:35-08:00","id":49350,"title":"","content":"Elisabeth is taking Celexa (generic form) and hydroxyzine. I know Celexa is a SSRI that has a very interesting side effect involving sex. Told her that since her girlfriend is in France, we won't worry about that. Told her to knock off the wine (a weekly wine cooler won't hurt). I am just happy that her doctor sit down and listen to her...I tried a couple of times to have her committed when she was in a maniac mood but her dad stopped it (I nearly kicked him in the balls for being so anti-medicine but he now realizes if I don't have MY meds, I go crazy). She went to the doctor on her own accord since she is 18 and her dad can't do a damn thing. I just wish she would get a flu shot seeing how there is an endemic going around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T01:40:30-08:00","id":49626,"title":"","content":"... well that sure was an anxiety attack today. Took a while to completely calm down, too, despite heading it off before it could spill over into panic mode. Bluh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T17:25:23-08:00","id":50273,"title":"","content":"I made an appointment for tomorrow with the Multicultural Affairs office on campus, where I'll be talking to a school official about the possibility of gender transition and how that might affect my time at the school.<br /> <br /> It's both exciting and nerve-wracking. Higher education is (from all I've heard) pretty much the most accepting environment there is, but there's always the fear of something going wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T20:30:11-08:00","id":50383,"title":"","content":"Good luck Cielle! I hope you get a very understanding and enthusiastic staff member. c:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T21:35:15-08:00","id":50421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JadedTrueBrujah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=49350#post49350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elisabeth is taking Celexa (generic form) and hydroxyzine. I know Celexa is a SSRI that has a very interesting side effect involving sex. Told her that since her girlfriend is in France, we won't worry about that. Told her to knock off the wine (a weekly wine cooler won't hurt). I am just happy that her doctor sit down and listen to her...I tried a couple of times to have her committed when she was in a maniac mood but her dad stopped it (I nearly kicked him in the balls for being so anti-medicine but he now realizes if I don't have MY meds, I go crazy). She went to the doctor on her own accord since she is 18 and her dad can't do a damn thing. I just wish she would get a flu shot seeing how there is an endemic going around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just on a side note, the effects of SSRI on sex drive can be highly variable from person to person and drug to drug. As in it's possible there will be an increase rather than a decrease.<br /> <br /> <br /> I highly doubt you intended to use the term endemic there as well. It's also not really an epidemic. It's pretty much a typical 'flu year with a dramatic name allowing media organizations to attach a lot of hype and pointless fear mongering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T22:07:51-08:00","id":50436,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T04:15:15-08:00","id":50577,"title":"","content":"Texas is being hit by the H1N1 virus bad. One lady in Dallas lost her baby (she was like 25 weeks pregnant) because she did not get the shot. My doctor before his stroke made sure I got my shot because fibromyalgia is not only a painful disease, it is also autoimmune...if I get sick, I really get sick. I keep dayquil and cherry nyquil in the cabinet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T12:21:08-08:00","id":50936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tluthal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=50383#post50383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good luck Cielle! I hope you get a very understanding and enthusiastic staff member. c:</div> </div> </div> </div>The meeting went well. Since I'm going to be rotating through a variety of positions over the next two years, a lot of our conversation focused on when might be the most opportune time to make any transition I did public (i.e., switch my gender presentation at work). He also noted that the next few years would indeed be an opportune time to carry out transition.<br /> <br /> I talk to my therapist later tonight, who has mentioned getting a consultation about hormone treatments pretty soon. So today's meeting is likely to be a topic of conversation. And to be totally honest, I found myself kinda excited when I imagined getting a supportive response, so...maybe that's a clue in figuring this out. I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T03:54:27-08:00","id":51516,"title":"","content":"I feel really scared right now. I feel los and sad and alone. I'm terrified of myself right now. I don't have anyone to talk to who can help me, that won't call the police or an ambulance. I don't know what to do anymore. I'm hoping it might get better if I wait it out. I don't want to hurt myself. I just want to feel better. I have no place else to go. I don't want to be alone. I'm trying as hard as I can. I promise. I just need a place that's safe. because the whole world is an empty fucking hole and I can't breathe. I want to scream and cry for my mom. I don't know what to do. I just need everything to be okay again. I'm so fucking worthless and ugly and nobody will ever fucking love me. I'm such a fucking freak and if I wasn't a waste of space shitforbrains coward, I would just be gone. I'm so so sorry. I can't breathe. Please god helpme I'm SO sorry. I just want to be safe again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T03:59:21-08:00","id":51518,"title":"","content":"I'm ok I im sorry I just need Fucking FUCK GODDAMNIT I need to know the world isn't a heartless fucking void because it feels like one now and . I can't think I'm yelling at . Myself and Jesus I don't get it anymore, idont know how knife to fix it and I'm so TIRED. I'm so tired of feeling this way","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T04:00:10-08:00","id":51520,"title":"","content":"I can't stop crying. I'm pathetic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T04:37:29-08:00","id":51539,"title":"","content":"I'm really sorry if I alarmed anyone. I realize there's a difference between venting and shouting one's inner monologue onto a forum in text form. Please forgive me. I can't say that I'm better, because I'm not. I'm calm, though. I'm calm because I broke down and hurt myself. I won't say how. I don't need an ambulance. I just don't know what the hell I'm doing anymore. I'm so lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T04:54:48-08:00","id":51550,"title":"","content":"Just to let you know that we are here for you. Go get some chocolate (I do hot fudge milkshakes myself). Take a hot shower. Call a counselor and talk to them. I am sorry that you had to hurt yourself in order to get those feelings gone. I used to do it myself for years until I tried to do something else and realized I needed help. Go to NOLA and do a parade, catch some beads!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T05:35:49-08:00","id":51557,"title":"","content":"I... can do the chocolate part, I think. It's the middle of the night, and, to be honest, I have the same freedom of movement in my house at night as a child with a bedtime. I live with my mom, and have been legally disabled since before I became an adult. I can't do things that make a lot of noise, can't walk outside for &quot;no reason&quot; after dark, etc. So even a shower is out until morning (loud). Nobody bothered to teach me how to drive, either, so I can't go places without someone knowing where I am (because they drove me, of course) and that puts me in a predicament all by itself. (This is doubly embarrassing when I show people my truck, which I'm proud of due to it being the only piece of property that I legally own under my own name. &quot;Yeah, those are custom made steel headlight cages. I got really lucky with the seller. Drive you somewhere?oh..uh...Sorry...&quot;) Once my family knows I'm&quot;sick&quot;again, I go from being treated like a child to being treated like a mentally unstable infant. Friends became &quot;too much to deal with&quot; and I'm suddenly not in charge of my own medication. Shit like that. I'm not trying to complain, I swear. I just don't usually get to say these things out loud, if forum posts could be considered &quot;out loud&quot;. Thank you for the support, Brujah. You're always so nice to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe feelings and thoughts are still here. I'm still scared and I still can't sleep.<br /> <br /> I know I need help, but with every doctor I've ever had, it's either &quot;You have to take a proactive approach to your problems. Take these 9 different mood-altering medications and if you start seeing, hearing, feeling, thinking or saying anything unusual, we'll just hospitalize you.&quot; OR &quot;If you stop taking the pills and/or seeing your doctor, we'll just assume that you've overcome your lifelong disability and stop providing you with medical care and money to survive.&quot; So, either way, good deal, right? Right...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 01-17-2014, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T07:06:49-08:00","id":51597,"title":"","content":"Damned if you do/damned if you don't...I know how that feels. We are going to the stores today to pick up some stuff (running out of eggs badly) and I will pick up a Diet MD...been caffeine free for about a week and I am getting sleepy all the time to where Mom complains about it. Can't drink coffee because it makes me sick (even the smell of it brewing makes me gag). Probably run to the library (I want to get Outlander since Starz is making a series from it). Got to convince Mom to stay up Sunday night to watch Sherlock with me. Got my room reserved for Anime Overload and I am thinking of either volunteering for it or just buy the ticket for Elisabeth (I am still deciding whether or not to get a pass for myself). I always loved volunteering for OwlCon when I went to it in Houston and DragonCon one year in Atalanta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T07:37:48-08:00","id":51612,"title":"","content":"Azrael, I want you to know that we're here for you to vent to. But please go see someone. Please talk to a counselor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T10:59:58-08:00","id":51708,"title":"","content":"This is a bit awkward for me, especially given I haven't been around this community for very long, and some of you clearly have more serious issues. I have social phobia, and while being online helps, it sometimes still takes me a moment to calm myself and hit the post button on a forum (much less the other things I occasionally have to do just to function in public). This ended up blowing up in my face a while back, and I got help for it though initially they thought the problem was a really bad case of depression. So anyway, I got to the point I got a good enough handle on both of the issues that I was taken off the meds (which I would not-so- occasionally skip anyway, I hate taking pills). It's been a couple years since I've even seen the docs because there hasn't been a major issue.<br /> <br /> Which leads to the problem and question I am facing: I have recently started a new job, which has been an emotional roller coaster, but one I've been dealing with and keeping from flying off the tracks. The last couple days in particular has been increasingly hectic with me dealing with an increasing number of people I've never even heard of before in a very short order, some have been rather judgemental and condescending because I didn't meet some random criteria I'll never understand. So I'm having probably the highest level of anxiety I've felt in years and am wondering whether I need to go back to the docs and if I do how long should I wait to see if my normal coping mechanisms eventually work or not. It's only been a couple of days, so I'm hoping I just need a weekend to calm down, but part of me thinks that may just be a rationalization for not wanting to see a new doctor as the old doc is retired.<br /> <br /> I feel a bit better just typing all of it out...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T12:06:10-08:00","id":51768,"title":"","content":"No one will yell at you or tell you you have to wait in line to talk about your problems because your problems aren't serious enough (however you even determine the seriousness of a personal problem on a comparative scale anyway), Dairugger. Don't feel bad about speaking up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T12:43:23-08:00","id":51790,"title":"","content":"About social phobia, if you were to meet me in actuality I care not one fuck what you think of me. I'll say whatever pops in my head, however off-colour, offensive or rude. Not intentional, I just don't get social cues. But online I try to be the soul of politeness. Why is it I care more about what people I'll never meet think of me than someone in front of me who could potentially do me harm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T13:04:28-08:00","id":51812,"title":"","content":"No one can be as f*cked up as me. Bipolar, PTSD, BPD with fibromyalgia and a few more physical ailments. I do take pills, most of the time I am dull and lifeless unless someone gives me a bottle of Diet MD. Mom gets on my ass if I sleep too long (blame the pills...fibro requires Delta sleep in order for recovery to happen). I have been on a high for several years before I was finally DXed and it took a few more years to get the right cocktail to work. I had to deal with massive weight gain until one doctor discovered I had hypothyroidism and got me on meds for that (causing a loss of 76 pounds). I got a grown daughter who cosplay at cons. I am waiting until the 31st so I can volunteer at one so I can get my pass for free. I already got my room reserved.<br /> <br /> Got to excuse me...got a book to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T18:22:09-08:00","id":52032,"title":"","content":"I had about 6 or so paragraphs written about how I'm feeling, but twice in a row, I've written HUGE posts and after hitting Post Reply, they vanish. I give up. I'm not typing that goddamn novella all over again. I'm so fucking tired and frustrated and angry and upset and sad and I just want to be able to talk about this and I Can't. Forget it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 01-17-2014, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T18:33:59-08:00","id":52039,"title":"","content":"Just relax man and get some sleep. Mom has the TV on Transformers, being introduced to the works of Michael Bay. We got another cold front so I am hitting the cherry nyquil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T18:44:38-08:00","id":52047,"title":"","content":"Dairugger: I somewhat-recently found out that I have anxiety issues when I had to quit a job because I was having panic attacks just driving to work. Go to the doctor. If that's triggering your anxiety too, just break it down into smaller steps. It's okay.<br /> <br /> Azrael: :[ I wish I had more I could say, but have a sympathetic frowny face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T19:53:41-08:00","id":52093,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the frowny, tluthal<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> :dips the face in milk and eats it: I'm feeling a bit better right now. I'm kinda dopey on my meds, which is not good in itself, but is much more preferable to my former state.<br /> <br /> \u200bCurrent mood: <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dJxMAiRGg98\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dJxMAiRGg98</a><br /> <br /> \u200bIncidentally, also the setting of the VtM game I'm recruiting for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T22:27:21-08:00","id":52150,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T23:38:22-08:00","id":52186,"title":"","content":"I liked thanks better than likes, because I feel like if I click like on one of these posts, it seems that I like your problem. Thanks had no such issues because it could be &quot;thanks for sharing this personal thing with us&quot;. So instead, I'll say to you all, thanks for sharing these personal things with us. And thanks to others for listening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T01:01:43-08:00","id":52207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=52186#post52186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked thanks better than likes, because I feel like if I click like on one of these posts, it seems that I like your problem. Thanks had no such issues because it could be &quot;thanks for sharing this personal thing with us&quot;. So instead, I'll say to you all, thanks for sharing these personal things with us. And thanks to others for listening.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat Jedi said. Thanks, everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T02:01:36-08:00","id":52231,"title":"","content":"How are you doing now, man? Something told me to get up and check the forums...inner motherly thingie going, I guess...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T13:51:51-08:00","id":52741,"title":"","content":"I'm not great, nor even good, but I'm surviving and I'm doing my best to stabilize. Your Motherlythingyness is much appreciated, Jaded. &lt;3 I'm having a weird, bullshit day. I have a lot of conflicting thoughts that I need to work out with myself. I'm just trying to focus on my games and the people and positive things I DO have in my life. I'm glad to have a safe place to speak honestly, and awesome people (this means you, reading this right now) that make this forum seem like a second home. Actually, now that I just typed that, I realized I'm finally a fan of the new forums. Woo, I just knocked out my inner curmudgeon. Anyway, I've had a lot on my mind, some of it directly related to my mental health, some of it probably(?) unrelated.<br /> <br /> \u200boff to another thread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T14:39:56-08:00","id":52772,"title":"","content":"Just got back from a brush fire at my brother's place. A spark from the lawn mower muffler. Got a good portion of his property burnt, saving him from having to bushhog it and fertilizing it. He is planning to raise watermelons on the side to supplement the monies. Kept an eye on the kids while he, the neighbors and the fire department handled the mess. At last check, the big old dead tree was shooting up flames. Got my final Christmas gift...more crocheting hooks!<br /> <br /> I am so exhausted...just might eat and collapse in bed. At least no one was hurt and the dogs started digging in the ashes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T16:54:57-08:00","id":52855,"title":"","content":"Thanks all for the words of encouragement. My social phobia is a very general fear of social situations, especially with folks I don't know. By and large I have a handle on it, so long as I keep the sheer number of social situations down, I even deliberately worked retail as an attempt to learn to deal with it, how well it worked seemed to depend on what day of the weak it was. I'm much calmer now, and I called the docs and they said if the episode started be accompanied by more than a desire to hide under a desk, or simply started to become uncontrollable, it's probably not so bad as to require an actual visit. So basically the doc says unless the problem persists or gets worse, don't bother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T17:11:35-08:00","id":53564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3YxaaGgTQYM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3YxaaGgTQYM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3YxaaGgTQYM\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3YxaaGgTQYM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Describes me pretty much when I was first DXed...I ended up loving Amy Lee and started getting her CDs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T02:02:20-08:00","id":53829,"title":"","content":"I completely flaked on my friends today. I'm supposed to be trying to organize a Vampire: the Masquerade game that they want me to run (and that I've been saving for a special group ie. Them), but instead I secluded myself in my room until my sister came and took me to my grandparents house to clear my head. I'm trying so hard not to be a complete mess. The people around me deserve better than this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T15:56:26-08:00","id":54282,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">I finally made a call to my Mental Healthcare providers this morning and made an appointment with a therapist. I'm seeing him on the 12th of February. I'm hoping that's soon enough.<br /> <br /> I've sleeping a lot during the day. Fitful, restless sleep filled with half-formed nightmares. It seems like every abusive, stressful, negative situation in my life's history is on call for these little fright-sessions.<br /> <br /> Sleeping at night is requiring sedation. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T16:35:26-08:00","id":54311,"title":"","content":"I am seeing my p-doc on the 10th so we get to go over my mental state, drugs and who knows what else.<br /> <br /> Celebrate my niece's Hope birthday today...8yo. Got her some garnet earrings. Warm day today but getting back to low temps again starting tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T20:56:15-08:00","id":54460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=54282#post54282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I finally made a call to my Mental Healthcare providers this morning and made an appointment with a therapist. I'm seeing him on the 12th of February.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T01:13:15-08:00","id":54526,"title":"","content":"Lets us know what the therapist recommends. I am checking up on Elisabeth later today...she got her dragon scales Saturday so she was happy, free movie passes to an anime movie for Sunday and is looking for decent chainmail to put her scales on. She got put on Celexa so I want to see how she is reacting (besides wanting to kill the dogs for getting in the trash and wishing for a MacBook).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:59:44-08:00","id":55113,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T19:16:45-08:00","id":55125,"title":"","content":"Brohugs, 'killer. I have faith that this is a passing storm and that you are strong enough to overcome it.<br /> <br /> Not that you asked for advice (well, maybe by implication), but one trick that's been working well for me is something Ophidimancer said a long time ago: Observe your sadness as it passes through you. Don't hold onto it, don't feed it, and don't fight it. Just watch it while it stays, and watch it as it departs.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry about your friend, though I'm glad life has been going so well for you. Looking forward to going to work is a rare condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:05:09-08:00","id":56372,"title":"","content":"My mother's dementia is of course getting worse and she is sure she is getting better. Her roommate wants her to move out and she wants to move out because she is sure she is breathing in cat hair. And if I had one second to think about anything other than doctors, government run around, or the fifty thousand other things(including whatever I'm forgetting to get done) I think that would be just enough time to have a nervous break down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T16:07:04-08:00","id":56405,"title":"","content":"I hate being right. That's really all there is to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:21:11-08:00","id":56452,"title":"","content":"Mom is convinced that I am a zombie...must be from the drugs I take (getting up early and wanting a nap at 1 is not zombie-like behavior). I even passed up a chance to watch Resident Evil (marathon anyone?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T17:29:49-08:00","id":58413,"title":"","content":"Anyone else having strange sleeping habits? I take a sleep aid between 6 and 7 and suppose to go to bed afterwards but all it does is relax me. I read in bed (current book is Outlander, dealing with an accidental time travel in Scotland at a ruin to 1747 or 1745 and dealing with society of the people while avoiding the ancestor of her modern husband (the ancestor was a bastard Englishman who tries to subdue the Highlanders) and marrying one of her patients to keep her safe. Mom is reading a book I checked out that I don't have time to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T00:13:11-08:00","id":58560,"title":"","content":"I'm taking my medication. I'm trying to stay connected to friends (whom I am so grateful for) and family (whom I feel sorry for constantly, for having to deal with me), but it's hard for me to explain in words how broken and lost I feel. I have so many people I don't want to disappoint, and no love for myself left. I don't like who I am. I wish I could say that I'm ok with being me, but I'm not. <br /> <br /> \u200bLooking in the mirror disgusts me. I feel ugly, and worthless and angry, looking myself in the eyes like that. I can't shake the idea that the world would be better off without. Better that, than deal with the misery I bring and the joy I leave shattered in my wake. I need to be better. I can't keep being...this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T02:28:09-08:00","id":58594,"title":"","content":"Let me let you in on a little secret...I still get depressed but I do get hypomaniac moments...that is when I crochet like crazy. I got one afghan from hell because of the border. I got a few works in progress and I want to know how to knit. I collect recipes from FB to make (the shelf needs a notebook and plastic sleeves for the recipes). I even got a recipe for an apple pie with a bacon top crust.<br /> <br /> I take my pills daily. I got to see my NP on the 10th to discuss getting a new pill for my tremors. I am seeing a new GP for my main physical stuff and to get pain killers and possibly a back brace on the 30th. I hate to say it but the nerve burning in my lumbar section did not work. I don't know if I want to go through the mess again. I keep envisioning myself in a wheelchair...I don't want to go back to the chair. I don't want to be a cripple because of my body malfunctioning. My mind is driving me crazy with all of this mess. I need something to munch on, preferably something sweet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:22:21-08:00","id":59556,"title":"","content":"Knitting is super nice and actually really easy to learn. I tend to recommend continental or combination knitting because english knitting puts all the work on one hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T17:51:53-08:00","id":60263,"title":"","content":"Sorry for this, but I have to vent somehow and while lurking in the past I saw that this forum can be extremely helpful in dire moments. I will probably feel stupid about writing this and I probably will not have enough courage to show myself around here anymore, but I really have to put my thoughts on paper. My English will probably suck as well.<br /> <br /> I'm feeling bad right now. It's 3 AM around here and I just can't sleep because I'm panicking or depressed or something like that and I'm contemplating actions that would be drastically bad. While I realize that, there's not much I can do to stop that thoughts. My first and thus far only suicide attempt happened around ten years ago. I went out of a window and came close to jumping. If I'm not wrong, I was fourteen and even though the circumstances that brought me to do that are long gone and surpassed, I've always felt as if that day I opened a door that cannot ever be completely closed. When I feel sad, bad or messed up, somewhere in my head there's always this little voice telling me &quot;Perhaps you should kill yourself&quot;. I tend to dismiss it quite easily and the suicidal thoughts rarely get stronger than some sort of sick joke I tell myself to face the tension, but I'm aware that's not how things are supposed to work. Never talked to anybody about this.<br /> <br /> The fact is, today those feelings are quite strong and I feel I've never been as close to try that again.<br /> <br /> I have an exam on Thursday and I'm not going to pass. I know that because I've already tried it three times and I didn't ever came close to that. If I don't pass it, I can't accede several other exams and I'm basically stucked. And I keep trying and trying, but it's always worse: I have trouble sitting down and studying, I can't remember anything even after months spent working on this and all my &quot;crutches and tricks to memorize things&quot; jut disappear once I'm in front of my professor. If I not pass, I'll drag things further again and I can afford studying just because my family is doing lots of sacrifices that I, worthless piece of shit, cannot translate into results anymore. Lots of hard-earned money wasted. I can't tell my parents because I feel like I'm going to disappoint them again. The look of sadness I see in their eyes when I tell them that I've failed is not something I want to see again and, more importantly, I don't want to be a weight. And then there's my father, which is a good man, a great person all-around and I deeply love him but, goddamn, we really are yet another painfully common example of a &quot;complicated&quot; father-son relationship. The &quot;We can't have a conversation about something that's not the weather without arguing/If I ever try to answerm he feels like I don't respect him/Well Done, Son&quot; Guy&quot; sort. I can't exactly describe what I'm feeling right now, what I want to solve or avoid, but this whole exam mess combined with the whole pointlessness of what I am, the thought that I'm more a burden than anything to those around me and some assorted bad stuff and disappointments are getting me really close to the edge.<br /> <br /> Right now, I'm thinking of the methods, which I guess it's messed up as well. I don't want to do that at home because that would mean 1) Returning at home and facing my relatives after failing again and 2) Having them clean up the mess, something I don't want to happen. I've been thinking about jumping in front of the train on the way back home (and even then, I'm so stupid to feel sorry and think first those on the train and the fact I would probably ruin their day or make them late).<br /> <br /> I know there are worst situations out there, and that I'm just an egotistical entitled jerk and that my reasons are going to sound stupid and asinine, but I really can't help it. Thanks for having read this, people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-28-2014, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T18:13:08-08:00","id":60275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=60263#post60263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will probably feel stupid about writing this and I probably will not have enough courage to show myself around here anymore, but I really have to put my thoughts on paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no reason to. It is not shameful to feel bad, or to express your feelings, or to want or need help. You're okay, Cinder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=60263#post60263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always felt as if that day I opened a door that cannot ever be completely closed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever since my brush with suicide, I've felt that way too. You're not alone. I remember for the first year, maybe eighteen months, I felt <i>wrong</i>, like I was supposed to be dead and it was some enormous mistake that I was still drawing breath. I don't feel that way any more, but the specter of that moment is always there, just over my shoulder, a sadness that's only as loud as a whisper these days but that never goes away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=60263#post60263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there are worse situations out there[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry about that. It's not a contest, and no one is judging you for your reasons. I know someone who's in almost exactly the same situation you are right now, and he's taking it hard too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=60263#post60263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]and that I'm just an egotistical, entitled jerk, and that my reasons are going to sound stupid and asinine, but I really can't help it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right, you can't help it. It's not your fault. You are not egotistical, you are not entitled, you are not stupid, and you are not weak. You are someone who's in pain, and you matter to people. Don't sell yourself short, brother. Whatever burden you think you'd be to your family, it's one they'd happily bear compared to what you're considering.<br /> <br /> But look, I'm just a pedant with an internet connection. I can give you pep talks, but I can only help you so much. Talk to a professional; a suicide crisis hotline might have access to the support infrastructure you need not just to handle how you're feeling right now but also to handle your educational and financial situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T05:13:11-08:00","id":60643,"title":"","content":"Some useful stuff:<br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Befrienders Worldwide (operating in 39 countries): <a href=\"http://www.befrienders.org/\" target=\"_blank\">www.befrienders.org</a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">National Suicide Prevention Lifeline (USA): <a href=\"http://www.suicidepreventionlifeline.org/\" target=\"_blank\">www.suicidepreventionlifeline.org</a> 1-800-273-8255</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Samaritans (UK): <a href=\"http://www.samaritans.org/\" target=\"_blank\">www.samaritans.org</a> 08457 90 90 90</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lifeline (Australia): <a href=\"http://www.lifeline.org.au/\" target=\"_blank\">www.lifeline.org.au</a> 13 11 14</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T10:54:52-08:00","id":60919,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys. Really. It's weird, but just writing those things down and reading your answer helped me feel better. I'm still pretty down right now, but you really helped me.<br /> <br /> Thanks. I also guess it's time to seek some help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T17:41:40-08:00","id":61190,"title":"","content":"I'm having panic attacks there are too many people in the house and kids are screaming. I'm in my room but I feel very uncomfortable and I'm feeli g claustrophobic but I have no where to run too because its snowing, and my room is the only place I can be alone, and my medical attacks make moving difficult. But trying to drown out the stimulus I put on a jazz station and pumped up the earphones and all of a sudden I can breathe again. Is there any advice on this? All the stimuli feels like its seriously invading my personal space, but the non speech music seems like its creating a buffering or making personal space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T17:50:18-08:00","id":61194,"title":"","content":"Sorry I haven't been on this thread lately I've been mainly been using my phone to type. Cinder I hope you are feeling better. I'm sorry your having these grim feelings, but your not alone and I'm glad you are getting help. Please be well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T18:06:04-08:00","id":61197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=61190#post61190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having panic attacks there are too many people in the house and kids are screaming. I'm in my room but I feel very uncomfortable and I'm feeli g claustrophobic but I have no where to run too because its snowing, and my room is the only place I can be alone, and my medical attacks make moving difficult. But trying to drown out the stimulus I put on a jazz station and pumped up the earphones and all of a sudden I can breathe again. Is there any advice on this? All the stimuli feels like its seriously invading my personal space, but the non speech music seems like its creating a buffering or making personal space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only things I can suggest are what I've found effective when I have encountered similar feelings/reactions myself. <br /> <br /> <br /> Music can help as you've already discovered, something repetitive but upbeat. I tended to go for classical, but whatever works for you.<br /> <br /> Meditation. The simple way is to find a position in which your body has as little physical stress as possible and then focus on not thinking about anything. clear your mind of all thoughts. You don't have to ignore them, there will be time to think on them later, just put them aside as they come up and strive for the mental state of nothing. Picturing a gently moving beach or something similar may help. The idea is something simple and regularly repeating.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, cold air. I'd crack my window just enough that cold air could spill in and straight down onto my face. Warm body buried under blankets some cool air resulting from the cold air from outside mixing just a bit with the air of the room flowing straight down onto my face... relaxing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T20:25:19-08:00","id":61270,"title":"","content":"Something soft to hold onto can do wonders as well! Regulate your breathing. I also tend to use a trick to reset my adrenal response but given you have problems with cramps I'd worry about recommending it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T00:52:46-08:00","id":61370,"title":"","content":"Self hypnosis works for me at times...counting down from 300 and mentally relaxing your body at a certain point. I got this from a shrink when I was in the Army and was frozen from being away from home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T02:00:15-08:00","id":61398,"title":"","content":"It's hard to do calming things sometimes because I will feel a wave of pain any second that could cause me to jump to my feet to fight it. Does anyone else feel like a bad person when you suffer health problems? I know it's irrational but often I feel intense self loathing when my health gets bad, even though I know loved ones who were good people yet died in pain. I often feel like its trial and if I was a good person I would have triumphed over all adversity because I made promises to deceased loved ones I would, and I fail and ineptitude and incompetence somehow equals inequity. It doesn't help that family members essentially equated me as garbage for not being healthy like them. I know I shouldn't feel this way but I feel like I must be a monster and a bad person when everything wrong with me feels like a curse. Like if I was a good and worthy person then I would have loved ones who tell me they love me, give hugs and tell me everything is going to be okay. I mean I see friends that get this, and even lots of really bad people with this. I know people suffer regardless of their character but its hard to shake the feeling that if I'm suffering so bad I must be a bad person. And if I grew up with abusive monsters I must be a monster too because I'm broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T04:00:03-08:00","id":61447,"title":"","content":"Eldagusto, I often feel like a bad person for being sick. Granted, I don't have the physical ailments you do, but as a person suffering from multiple psychiatric disorders, I can empathize. I often feel like my suffering is dese<br /> rved, due to my being weak, lazy, unworthy, immoral, useless, whatever. A favorite saying in my family is &quot;God never gives us a cross that's too heavy to bear.&quot; I, for one, think that's total bullshit. I'm not ragging on religion here. I'm just saying that that particular phrase and others like it are just flashy ways of saying &quot;Suck it up/grin and bear it&quot;, and that type of unsupportive Shit gets old.<br /> <br /> \u200bChronic illness, regardless of kind, is a burden I wouldn't wish on anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":"01-30-2014, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T12:58:55-08:00","id":61686,"title":"","content":"Bad person? Broken? I'm going to say this as calmly and clearly as possible because right now the way you're talking makes me want to inflict bodily harm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Where do you draw the line? What constitutes &quot;broken&quot;? A broken thing is a thing that can't perform it's function. It's damaged goods. It's garbage.<br /> <br /> Is a man who loses his eyesight broken? Is the redneck guy who believes homosexuality is a disease you can catch broken? Shall we round them up and throw them on a compost heap?<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm looking at it from the wrong angle humm? Look to the people that are *not* broken and work from there? <br /> <br /> Well how about the brilliant scientists? They've done great things. Newton, Einstein and Hawking. Oh wait, the first was considered an abject failure by his family, the middle one broke wedding vows so blatantly it was hard work for the press to cover it up and the third managed to fuck around behind his wife even while being confined to a wheelchair (which takes some serious dedication by the way).<br /> <br /> Maybe not, how about the great humanitarians? Gandhi, Teresa, Mandela? Oh wait, they are recorded as a racist, embezzler and terrorist.<br /> <br /> <br /> What you are calling broken is inherent in every human. EVERY. SINGLE. PERSON. The word ceases to have meaning. Everyone has problems, issues and difficulties, to a greater or lesser extent. Everyone is deserving of positive human contact and is worth keeping alive as long is possible and they want it.<br /> <br /> If you grew up with horrible abusive people and live with unstable people that doesn't mean you are bad, wrong or broken, it means you had a shitty childhood and are in a really shitty spot in life. It means you'll have to *work* to develop understanding of how most people interact socially, because your perceptions on things are apt to be screwed up and likely tending towards expecting the worst... because that's what your brain was trained to expect. It means you have to work harder then others and will have issues that others do not. It does NOT mean that those issues can not be overcome, it does not make you inferior, unworthy or not welcome, and it sure as fuck doesn't make you broken.<br /> <br /> <br /> Calling someone, anyone broken is going seriously piss me off. It's a pointlessly negative one word summary that is simply writing something off as impossible to change or fix. Will you ever be perfect? No. Guess what? There are no perfect people, only people that pretend to be. And simply taking the time to do a mental inventory and assessment, to decide to work towards making yourself better in whatever ways you deem desirable, you will be ahead of a large portion of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T13:54:56-08:00","id":61727,"title":"","content":"Listen, I had an abusive dad but I loved him...he taught me to respect people and when I reach the point of not wanting to go to church, he let me stay home or we went fishing When I got hurt, he was the one I would run to because he knew I needed someone to cry to. I had an accident and cut my finger when I was 14, requiring stitches. He pulled the kit out and I got 4 stitches done...he was a LVN and a hospital corpsman when he was in the Navy. When he got Lyme and had to have double hernia surgery, I was the one who sat in his room, making sure he was okay. <br /> <br /> Years later I realized he was bipolar but it was not discussed. When he had his first stroke, he was put on SSI immediately (especially after 2 heart attacks). I could not stand to live with him because we would get into arguments which is why I moved down to Austin...I was able to live simply until I got insurance and had an infertility doctor check me for endo (severe case, stage 4). By then I was living with someone, working my ass off and enjoying $1 longneck nights at a metal bar (if not Bingo). Got pregnant on Beltane eve...damn longnecks and my roommie was enjoying it as well. I suffered from too many miscarriages so this one I kept...<br /> <br /> I don't know if I pissed the old man off for having a kid out of wedlock but he loved my daughter and did the same things that he did with me...including feeding the calves, fishing and who knows what else. When I started breaking down, he could not be there for me, but Mom rose to the bit and helped me out. I had another breakdown when he died...Mom held his memorial a year later, according to our Osage traditions.<br /> <br /> Now I live with Mom after my last breakdown/PTSD attack. I am getting excellent care from the local MHMR center. My daughter will be 19 come the 7th next week. We share the same likes (okay, so I won't cosplay) and I enjoy teasing her father about needing to keep winecoolers in the fridge for me. Elisabeth is getting help for her mood disorder after I told her that it is hereditary. The Celexa is working great for her and she is getting decent sleeping time. We got our hotel room reserved for Anime Overload this year and I am going to ask the main guy if I can volunteer for it. I did DragonCon one year and OwlCon 2 years...the most fun I ever had.<br /> <br /> Friends are needed to talk to. I am trying to deal with one friend who has depression and alcohol abuse. She wants the help but she needs to get rid of the alcohol and the &quot;friends&quot; who are enabling her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T10:42:42-08:00","id":62298,"title":"","content":"Got paid today, got some sodas for the Super Bowl dinner, ordered some slabs of ribs, paid rent so Mom could get her meds. Raided the bread store and their register was going through some trouble. Had to pay cash (I use my debit card for most everything). Pogo is paid for the year and got Dragonfly in Amber at the library.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T14:06:45-08:00","id":62454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=61686#post61686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad person? Broken? I'm going to say this as calmly and clearly as possible because right now the way you're talking makes me want to inflict bodily harm. Where do you draw the line? What constitutes &quot;broken&quot;? A broken thing is a thing that can't perform it's function. It's damaged goods. It's garbage. Is a man who loses his eyesight broken? Is the redneck guy who believes homosexuality is a disease you can catch broken? Shall we round them up and throw them on a compost heap? Maybe I'm looking at it from the wrong angle humm? Look to the people that are *not* broken and work from there? Well how about the brilliant scientists? They've done great things. Newton, Einstein and Hawking. Oh wait, the first was considered an abject failure by his family, the middle one broke wedding vows so blatantly it was hard work for the press to cover it up and the third managed to fuck around behind his wife even while being confined to a wheelchair (which takes some serious dedication by the way). Maybe not, how about the great humanitarians? Gandhi, Teresa, Mandela? Oh wait, they are recorded as a racist, embezzler and terrorist. What you are calling broken is inherent in every human. EVERY. SINGLE. PERSON. The word ceases to have meaning. Everyone has problems, issues and difficulties, to a greater or lesser extent. Everyone is deserving of positive human contact and is worth keeping alive as long is possible and they want it. If you grew up with horrible abusive people and live with unstable people that doesn't mean you are bad, wrong or broken, it means you had a shitty childhood and are in a really shitty spot in life. It means you'll have to *work* to develop understanding of how most people interact socially, because your perceptions on things are apt to be screwed up and likely tending towards expecting the worst... because that's what your brain was trained to expect. It means you have to work harder then others and will have issues that others do not. It does NOT mean that those issues can not be overcome, it does not make you inferior, unworthy or not welcome, and it sure as fuck doesn't make you broken. Calling someone, anyone broken is going seriously piss me off. It's a pointlessly negative one word summary that is simply writing something off as impossible to change or fix. Will you ever be perfect? No. Guess what? There are no perfect people, only people that pretend to be. And simply taking the time to do a mental inventory and assessment, to decide to work towards making yourself better in whatever ways you deem desirable, you will be ahead of a large portion of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div> Look I'm trying. I said its something I don't believe but it's something I feel. Saying stop feeling this way isn't really going to help. I know your not supposed to! I am already getting enough people getting pissed at me for not healing, or collapsing, or failing to get health care. You can't just order people to stop failing. I'm trying get up each time. Come on you can't disparage people for not comparing to hawkings and ghandi. I'm trying to not stay down, but I'm insulted for failing and not being functional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T15:03:54-08:00","id":62488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=62454#post62454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Look I'm trying. I said its something I don't believe but it's something I feel. Saying stop feeling this way isn't really going to help. I know your not supposed to! I am already getting enough people getting pissed at me for not healing, or collapsing, or failing to get health care. You can't just order people to stop failing. I'm trying get up each time. Come on you can't disparage people for not comparing to hawkings and ghandi. I'm trying to not stay down, but I'm insulted for failing and not being functional.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing the point. <br /> <br /> I'm not pissed because you try and fail. That's the whole point of my rant, EVERYONE fails, even the heroes of society. *you* are already doing a better job at picking yourself up than a lot of people I know.<br /> <br /> And *that* is why I'm pissed, because you're already doing a better job of making yourself better than most people ever do. <br /> <br /> And you consider that to be a failure.<br /> <br /> Fuck that noise, Eldagusto is doing a fantastic job with fixing his life, and I don't like you slamming the effort he's done.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T15:11:28-08:00","id":62495,"title":"","content":"TL;DR version<br /> <br /> Stop getting down on yourself, because we think you're cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T15:22:44-08:00","id":62504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd_Canuck is perfectly capable of speaking for himself, but in the interests of trying to calm down hurt feelings, let me take a run at it: I don't believe that's what he's doing. I believe he's saying, &quot;Here are reasons not to feel that way.&quot; He's trying to convince you, not to command you. He's saying you <i>do</i> compare to them. He's saying everyone is messed up, even our heroes and saints, so no one is irredeemable. Are you saying Odd_Canuck insulted you, or are you speaking more generally?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sorry if I misunderstood. It was coming off as anger directed at me. When he mentioned wanting to commit bodily harm I thought he was wanting to punch me. As I said I've been insulted directly for things like not being healed after leaving the ER, or not going out because of me trying to avoid an episode or even going out and having an episode. It feels everything I do is viewed as failing, and the only time it was okay was when I still had some savings so I could support myself for a bit. I was just cringing because I thought I was being told that I should be punched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T17:09:25-08:00","id":62582,"title":"","content":"All ERs do is just slap a band-aid on you and send you back out the door...it has happened to me when I could not keep anything down. 24 hours later, I was back in the ER, the EMS telling them that if the hospital does not take care of me, they would take me to a trauma center. I ended up in ICU dehydrated with IVs, getting antibiotics and who knows what else which vomiting anything that passed my lips. I know my potassium was low. I was sitting in a chair talking to one of the nurses when she handed me a soda, thinking I could keep that down. I could barely hold it because it fell out of my hand as I slip into a seizure. The hospital won't tell me what was wrong (Mom thinks I was at the beginning of sepsis which is rather nasty to have). That was when I started having intestinal trouble and trouble eating the foods I used to eat.<br /> <br /> We are avoiding the local ER because the way they treated our family, despite of Mom and Dad working there. My SIL nearly had a bursted appendix that they label as just an upset stomach. When Mom fell in May, all they did was splint her right leg (broken right fibula) and bandage her left ankle which was twisted. No pain medication. She was stuck in her chair for 2 months except when we took her to the bone doctor for her cast and walking boot. Medicare helped pay for a wheelchair but she had to use crutches to get to bed or the toilet. The ER did not notify her doctor that she was injured...I told him when I had to get some scripts one day. I had food poisoning one day and they kept giving me drugs that did not work. I told them Zofran several times...I know my body damn it. One hospital treated me for the flu (Tennessee before my hospitalization) and I started getting antsy, that wonderful itching feeling when you are reacting to a drug that you are allergic to.<br /> <br /> Most hospitals are not equipped to handle mental patients. Oh, they will admit them, get a sitter and pray that the state hospital gets a room open. If you take a closer look at mental patients in the state hospitals, they are the ones who slip through the cracks...no insurance, no Medicare so they are put in the nastiest 'dorms' where you have to guard your stuff from being stolen or have an elderly woman piss on the floor because she cannot make it to the bathroom (I learned to be a light sleeper during that time). The common area is co-ed but you have to watch yourself in case someone wants to know you better. I refused to be in any room by myself with any male, even the doctor. When they let us go to the basketball court, one guy kept bothering me. I told the attendant and he got the guy to leave me alone.<br /> <br /> I finally find a MHMR (who once rejected me) with the bipolar and PTSD diagnose from Tennessee in my hand and me telling them that I have to have treatment and I be damned if I go back to Terrell. The NP, caseworker and nurse worked with me and we finally find the right drug cocktail. Find the right doctor, Elgustado...if I knew where you are at, I could find a rheumy for you. Reapply for Medicaid. If the ER took x-rays, show up at a doctor's office saying this is necessary. That is how I found out that I have degenerative back problems (I overdid it again today...raking up the leaves from the trailer, making my lower back hurt again). If I could send you money, I would but I got bills and rent. All I can do is encourage you to be strong and fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T17:34:27-08:00","id":62602,"title":"","content":"Unless you have specific information about a particular emergency room being discussed, I do not think it is a good idea to discourage people from using an emergency resource. I'll grant that an ER is probably not the best specialized facility for someone suffering a psychiatric crisis, but it is a valid port in case of an emergent event, and it is the only place some people will have available to them due to location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T17:49:34-08:00","id":62609,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=62602#post62602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you have specific information about a particular emergency room being discussed, I do not think it is a good idea to discourage people from using an emergency resource. I'll grant that an ER is probably not the best specialized facility for someone suffering a psychiatric crisis, but it is a valid port in case of an emergent event, and it is the only place some people will have available to them due to location.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to point out that, on about 80% of the MANY occasions I have felt like a danger to myself, the ER was the most effective (and many times, ONLY) route to treatment and crisis management. Jim's point is more than valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 01-31-2014, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T09:50:14-08:00","id":62954,"title":"","content":"Today is a scary day. Nice temperature but it is raining mist. I do not like being out on the road when it is raining. Seen too many accidents happen because people don't slow down and follow the rules. I wanted to stay home, under the blankets but Mom made me get up and we went to Walmart. I was able to use the motorized shopping cart and I got lots of meat. The bread guy was there and handed me a swirl loaf of bread since it was on the top shelf. Got some fun size 3 Musketeers for my chocolate cravings. <br /> <br /> At times, I have to write down what I am doing. It settles my racing thoughts which is a part of being bipolar. If I do it on a forum, the thoughts go away, making me feel normal. Still does not stop the damn voices, but I do tell the voices to STFU half the time. Now if only the crazy dreams will stop...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T12:07:37-08:00","id":63039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JadedTrueBrujah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=62954#post62954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At times, I have to write down what I am doing. It settles my racing thoughts which is a part of being bipolar. If I do it on a forum, the thoughts go away, making me feel normal. Still does not stop the damn voices, but I do tell the voices to STFU half the time. Now if only the crazy dreams will stop...</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the racing, and the need to just Let Out whatever is in your head. A racing, confused mind can be unbearable.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy thoughts were decidedly dark last night. I managed to contemplate suicide multiple times, scare one of the few people that are nice enough to spend time with me, start an argument with my own mother over literally nothing, until finally just getting loaded (because it was either that, or &quot;Fuck it. It's been awhile since I've seen the Emergency Room. Let's try some self-harm!&quot;) and passing out.<br /> <br /> \u200bAccording to Wikipedia, I was experiencing this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wikipedia's entry for Bipolar Disorder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Mixed affective episodes</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">In the context of bipolar disorder, a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixed_state_(psychiatry)\" target=\"_blank\">mixed state</a> is a condition during which symptoms of mania and depression occur simultaneously. Typical examples include weeping during a manic episode or racing thoughts during a depressive episode. Individuals may also feel very frustrated in this state, for example thinking grandiose thoughts while at the same time feeling like a failure. Mixed states are often the most dangerous period of mood disorders, during which the risks of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Substance_abuse\" target=\"_blank\">substance abuse</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panic_disorder\" target=\"_blank\">panic disorder</a>, suicide attempts, and other complications increase greatly. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T16:48:12-08:00","id":63648,"title":"","content":"I have to be emotionless, especially around family. My niece was doing her cheer routine for us and I had to look away, tears in my eyes. I just sent an email to the volunteer coordinator for Anime Overload, asking to help out (free pass that way). Elisabeth has stripped her hair color and got it in a pretty chestnut color. Her MM piercing fell out and she can't get the back on it to stay put so she is going to let that heal. Her girlfriend's dad has to have a kidney transplant so I am worried about him. Her French girlfriend is sending her a special present for Elisabeth's birthday (I got her earrings). She has been responding great to the Celexa and is more uppity, feeling great. When I paid her Cricket bill Friday, the company texts her at 6:30am, waking her up and I get a call &quot;thanks for waking me up Mom!&quot; <br /> <br /> Do I have to be emotionless? I can't see my NP until the 10th. I could call to see the nurse on standby and let her know how I have been feeling. I don't feel suicidal, just not feeling anything. I am trying to watch the Super Bowl and all it has done is made me upset at Rameriz for hitting Manning in the head, allowing Seahawks to get a safety. I can't even watch it. I am not into Bruno Mars so the halftime show is going to be a bust. Pogo is not holding any interest for me, I am taking my pills as routine. I am tempted to put my headphones on and blast Evanessence again. I don't even feel like crocheting and that is what I use when I get down in the dumps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T22:15:47-08:00","id":64600,"title":"","content":"Hiding one's emotions is a coping mechanism that I know all too well. Numbing myself with substances or stimulation, whether pleasurable or painful,into emotionless oblivion is how I tend do it, when just faking it isn't enough. It's self destructive, but I'm doing my best to find other solutions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T10:59:12-08:00","id":64982,"title":"","content":"Went and got the bloodwork done for my depokate levels this morning. Now to wait and see what the NP says on Monday. Mom had to get bloodwork done too and an UA. Bought breakfast afterwards and saw the neurologist (ordering a special MRI for her).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T16:48:03-08:00","id":66842,"title":"","content":"I can barely get out of bed. If it weren't for WiFi, none would have heard from me for days....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T21:56:12-07:00","id":199667,"title":"","content":"I don't really feel safe posting this, and you don't want to read it. Oh well. Spoilers.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Tonight, for the first time, I was able to articulate what it's like to miss cutting.<br /> <br /> It's like I'm confused all the time, like I can't think straight and only barely have enough wherewithal to notice how confused I am, and I know that somehow, some way, the problem would be solved if I could just punish my flesh for whatever it is I'm too confused to figure out what I hate it for. Every day I wish I could just go to the bathroom and jam the narrow spire of a blade's point into the flesh of my left shoulder, because I think I'd honestly feel relief at the hot, ragged pain of my skin tearing as I pull the blade down my arm and seeing the red well up first in beads, then in lines running down my arm. I just know for a certainty that if I could just cut myself, I'd be able to think again; but I don't do it, because...I don't know why not. The reasons I can come up with--it's sick, it's a delusional idea, I could get caught, I could give myself a serious infection--are all weak and irrelevant, provoking no kind of concern or interest in me. I just don't do it because I have this confused, irrational feeling I shouldn't do it, and that feeling does not make sense to me, but I cling to it anyway for now. &quot;One more night, we'll see what happens,&quot; I keep saying to myself, vaguely aware that this is more or less what a drunk says about the bottle he wants to go buy.<br /> <br /> I don't want to go another night, though. I want to get the knife out of its hiding place and stop feeling so foggy in my head all the time. I won't do it because I know I'll disappoint and upset you guys and blah blah blah, but I really wish I could do it.<br /> <br /> That probably doesn't make sense to you. Sorry. I didn't say I was able to communicate it to you in a way you would understand, though. I said I could articulate it.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:34:56-07:00","id":199690,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry you're having these feelings Jim. I'm glad you're not going through with it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T02:14:27-07:00","id":199843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=199667#post199667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really feel safe posting this, and you don't want to read it. Oh well. Spoilers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a host of issues resulting from post-traumatic stress disorder as a result of a year long deployment in Afghanistan. Before then, I had frequent bouts of what was, admittedly self-diagnosed, depressive periods along with ideations of suicide that really only got worse after the military. Four of my friends from my unit have killed themselves since we came back. To make things even more potentially dangerous, I am an avid firearms enthusiast and have a few guns in my home and some of them are convenient enough to use that I could conceivably, comfortably shoot myself. In fact, I used to practice it.<br /> <br /> I spent a lot of time planning this, you see. It helped me feel calm knowing I had a way out and a plan to do it quick. I'd want to shoot myself in my bath tub because the drain's right there and it wouldn't stain the tile. Even if it did, tile's cheaper to replace than carpet, you see, and I wouldn't want to make a mess. I had a few notes written out. One I typed for legibility concerns but I thought that felt too clinical. I wrote a few of them out, a few in pen but the later ones in pencil because I wanted to get my word choice just right, and that requires the ability to erase clean. Eventually I got one that I liked and then went over the words in pen, but then realized I'd used notebook paper, and that felt like I'd been too hasty in my choice of paper and that I'd half-assed my last words. After I finally had the one I liked, I'd put the lid on the toilet down and set the note on it and then fuss over if it looked better askew or straight or what. I'd mess with the wash rags around my sink and tub, too, to make them look neat. I'd make sure my pets had food and water, and ways to get outside if no one came for them in time. I didn't want to leave a messy house or make my cats suffer.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'd empty my favorite pistol and look at myself in the mirror, barrel to my temple. Sometimes I'd experiment with where I held it, sometimes laying in the tub and seeing where the blood splatter would go, but usually it'd be against my temple. I'd keep my finger on the trigger and gently apply more and more pressure to really get a feel for how much I'd need to pull it, and I'd always jump nearly out of my skin when I'd hear the hammer drop and feel my gun rattle empty.<br /> <br /> The last night I did this ritual was when I'd heard my best friend from service had killed himself and at that point I felt like my misery had bottomed out, it couldn't get any worse, and that was the time to do it. I went through that ritual again, put a bullet in the chamber, got in the tub, put my pistol under my chin, and slowly put more pressure on the trigger until my senses came to me and I racked the slide before I could fire. I cried, I don't know for how long, got up, and went to bed, where I kept crying until I fell asleep. The next day I went to the VA to get help.<br /> <br /> This story scares me every time I tell it. It makes me feel like shit, it makes me want to cry, I don't ever want to revisit these emotions, but I do, regularly. Why? Because each time I tell this story, I feel a little less bad about it. Every time I tell people what I saw over there, what I did, what I've done since, it makes my burden feel lighter. I believe humans, as social creatures, benefit from a sense of community and camaraderie, and having a place where everyone can join you in mourning your problems, whatever they may be. I have my therapists, friends, and family to fall back on. If you know someone, or if you trust this community enough, do you think it'd help if you talked through your problems more with them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":77,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","user":"kongurous","date":". 07-17-2014, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:01:49-07:00","id":199974,"title":"","content":"kongurous, I liked your post to thank you for telling your story. It was a difficult story to read, but I appreciate your sharing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T07:28:14-07:00","id":199995,"title":"","content":"I am annoyed that the texts I intend to quote were pasted in an order different from the one I clicked the Quote buttons in, and I had to go back and manually fix them. I should bring this up in Trouble Tickets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=199974#post199974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">kongurous, I liked your post to thank you for telling your story. It was a difficult story to read, but I appreciate your sharing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said. I concur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=199843#post199843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd make sure my pets had food and water, and ways to get outside if no one came for them in time. I didn't want to leave a messy house or make my cats suffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a big part of my suicide plan, back in the day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=199843#post199843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe humans, as social creatures, benefit from a sense of community and camaraderie, and having a place where everyone can join you in mourning your problems, whatever they may be. I have my therapists, friends, and family to fall back on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T09:40:07-07:00","id":209374,"title":"","content":"wrote long post...laptop died unexpectedly before i could submit it....*sighs* I&quot;m ahving a shitty day started the morning a ball of anxiety freaking out over what turned out to be nothing. Vicodin makes me paranoid as shit on top of making me SUPER sleepy, but does jack shit for the pain. I really want to talk to my dad but cant bring myself to bother him with this, he has enough on his plate without worrying about me. almost a month ago without any warning he attempted suicide, but then again the warning should have been obvious i was well aware of his depression and suicidal thoughts we talked about them all the time since we share the same illness... The doctors told him looking at what he took and how much combined with alcohol, He should NOT still be alive and not just that he suffered NO Lasting damage. I dont believe in god...but someone was watching out for my dad. I've only talked to him once since the three days i spent with him in the hospital(anxiety about spending the night away from home? NOt a problem appearantly when my dad is not well, I was 45 minuets away from home with NO easy way back and was there 3 days, and guess what NOTHING bad happened at home while i was gone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> He told me what happened, and that he is in therapy, and all that, and wants to get better.<br /> <br /> THe worst part is he says he blames himself for my mental illness that its my fault i turned out like i did. I've tried to explain i was BORN with this and that nothing he did made it worse. Now i dont feel right talking to him about my issues untill he's more stable, i think he doesnt need to worry about me and my problems when he reallyh needs to deal with his own.<br /> <br /> i'm in a weird mood. PRobably cause of hte vicodin dunno<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT-oooooookkk then fell asleep when I got home, went to check my usual fourms, and see I posted in this thread this morning...yup dont remember doing that at all, probably didnt help that i was given 2 vicodin at the ER, then about 2 hours later when i finally got home i took 2 more and went to sleep. Most of my morning is foggy because I did that oops. as I said it doesnt help my pain one bit, but in large enough doses it knocks me out and makes me feel happy so its a rare treat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 07-26-2014, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T21:34:30-07:00","id":209810,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T23:04:37-07:00","id":209859,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Jack instead of beer. Don't talk to my dad. Cigarette burns, because cuts get my knives hidden from me, and I love weapons more than my own skin. <br /> <br /> Tomorrow I'll be chainsmoking and downing coffee like it's the antidote to a poison I've accidentally imbibed. Name's Joey. Azrael can't hang after that many shots. He's out for the night. He can stay that way. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T23:08:39-07:00","id":209861,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T23:32:35-07:00","id":209866,"title":"","content":"A few months ago, I could only drink beer and light mixed drinks. This many bottles in, I'm okay drinking it straight if I don't have a mixer. When I do, like now, I still make my drinks stiff enough to knock you out of your sneakers.<br /> <br /> Klonopin was unintentionally taken, because I'm not psychic and neighbors don't usually buy you a fifth of whiskey for helping them move furniture. So, those and my usual fucktons of weed are in the mix. I need more chemicals. I'm still typing in legible English.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T06:26:48-07:00","id":210073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=209810#post209810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whiny kid shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't, though. It's pain. It matters. I'm glad you're talking to us about it; I've missed you.<br /> <br /> Weren't you getting psychiatric help months ago? What happened with that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T06:41:08-07:00","id":210093,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T07:13:30-07:00","id":210132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=210093#post210093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My insurance decided randomly that my therapist wasn't qualified enough for their copay, so I had to start paying out of pocket. I can't afford $65/week so I go once a month now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you unwilling to find a new therapist because you've built a rapport with this one, or something?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=210093#post210093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really managed to do some damage to my arms last night with that knife but no one will see because I cut up near the shoulder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did it make you happy or feel better to do it? If not, I really hope you'll stop and maybe call your therapist about it. This behavior isn't healthy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=210093#post210093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't concerned about the safety of anyone I just watched it happen and had nearly no emotional response.</div> </div> </div> </div>And while you're on the phone, you might mention that too. I won't diagnose because I have no ability nor right, but I do care about you, 'killer, and this is worrying. It sounds like you are in a very dangerous place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T08:10:58-07:00","id":210206,"title":"","content":"I'm very sorry to hear your stories, Azrael and Cereal. I hope that you will start on the path to getting better soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T18:44:05-07:00","id":210693,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T18:58:42-07:00","id":210700,"title":"","content":"If you don't trust her to do what's right for you, 'killer, what's your rapport with your therapist based on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:45:09-07:00","id":210729,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T20:08:28-07:00","id":210758,"title":"","content":"'killer, I'm very worried for you. The things you describe, like the disinterest in anything around you, the muted emotional responses, the willful pursuit of your own pain, these are all extremely reminiscent of my own times being suicidal. These are things you need help with, and you are not getting the help you need. The last few months of silence have been frightening enough; please don't make me worry that the next silence is because you've killed yourself. I've tried to respect your privacy and your right to self-determination, and maybe that was a mistake on my part that sent an air of disinterest or apathy or something, but please talk to someone who can help you. I know that's hypocritical coming from me, but you're a good guy who deserves to not be in pain any more. Please let someone help you with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T20:14:31-07:00","id":210762,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T20:35:43-07:00","id":210797,"title":"","content":"I know how you feel. I've been wrestling too with the feeling that I don't belong here; that I'm only useful as a blunt instrument to be used as a weapon against those my friends disapprove of or else as a cautionary tale worthy of pity. It's still here, though. The spark, I mean. I won't go into why because it kind of involves be reverting to blunt instrument form for a while [cough], but for a while I was united with people. We didn't need to talk about it or plan it, we just did it. We fit together. It helped. It mattered. And I only know it happened because I kept trying with the community. I think it could happen for you, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T21:11:00-07:00","id":210832,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T21:17:27-07:00","id":210840,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't recommend it. If you can maintain the energy, then good for you, but personally, I find being the dick police exhausting. Those battles I fight these days I can only fight because I'm fueled by an intense burst of anger that burns hot and fast and leaves me emotionally weary bordering on despairing after. If that's the price of reclaiming a sense of community, then fuck it, I've got to let that sense of community go because it is poisonous.<br /> <br /> The common interest, the feeling of being in lockstep with people I've felt out of touch with for a while, the camaraderie: those are the things I took from the experience that I cherish. Those are the things I want, but in a different dynamic. I think they can happen, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T22:37:02-07:00","id":210883,"title":"","content":"This thread recently makes me sad. I care about all of you and hate the fact that you're suffering. Regardless of what happens to you guys know that I'm here and I care even when I don't post. Often I feel like anything I could say wouldn't be sufficient to express the depth of my empathy for your pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T03:12:50-07:00","id":211025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=210693#post210693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">baker acting me would be a terrible idea. I would fight them every step of the way and if I got away no one would ever hear from me again. Not because I would kill or harm myself but because I would constantly be in the noided stage where I think everyone and everything is trying to put me away.<br /> <br /> I don't know what it is but I want to self destruct. I can't destroy other things. Everyone is so possessive of their cars houses yards etc so myself becomes the target so that I harm no one else</div> </div> </div> </div> I now completely understand what you meant when you told me I reminded you of yourself a little. It's not a comforting feeling. <br /> <br /> ....Damn. I was almost chipper a few minutes ago. Now...<br /> <br /> I don't want to look in the mirror. I don't want to be ME. I'm so tired of all this pointless existing. WHAT am I even around for?!? I let the same person who called me a faggot, who I (pathetically enough) actually missed while they were away for a few days, slap me in the fucking face. I didn't even let my smile slip. I wasn't at a sit-in. I don't believe in a philosophy of non-violence.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe fact of the matter is: I don't give a flying Fuck anymore. I smoke all day. I get as loaded as possible, as often as possible, because I only seem to have some semblance of a conscience when I'm intoxicated. I might be acting like a prick or a one-man pity party while plastered, but at least I can almost feel my heart. Stone sober, I've walked out of my front door, carrying a very large knife, with the intention to kill someone because they bugged me. It was my mother putting her hand on my shoulder and BEGGING me to think clearly about what I was doing that stopped me. Part of me, a frighteningly large part, still feels that way. An even larger part of me truly believes that I'm a monster, and is starting to like that idea more than &quot;getting help&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T03:16:43-07:00","id":211027,"title":"","content":"I'm crying, but it's only my eyes. I feel hollow. I'm not sad. I'm....me. A shell filled with poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T03:25:14-07:00","id":211029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=210883#post210883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread recently makes me sad. I care about all of you and hate the fact that you're suffering. Regardless of what happens to you guys know that I'm here and I care even when I don't post. Often I feel like anything I could say wouldn't be sufficient to express the depth of my empathy for your pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, Jedi. I don't mean to add to anyone's sadness. I just don't think I want you to feel my pain, though, even if just through simple empathy. I want to swallow my pain until it either eats me from within or I become a friend to pain and horror, in which case I just need to be put down for good. I'm greedy like that. Old Yeller was a better man than me, and he was a dog. He also got a bullet in the head when it became necessary.<br /> <br /> Why does anyone even tolerate me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 07-28-2014, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T05:30:35-07:00","id":211111,"title":"","content":"Because having problems doesn't make you a bad person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T07:37:41-07:00","id":211202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=211111#post211111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because having problems doesn't make you a bad person.</div> </div> </div> </div>What he said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T07:54:33-07:00","id":211218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=211029#post211029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does anyone even tolerate me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've told you this before: because you're part of the tribe and we luv ya, ya mook!<br /> <br /> Now knock your silly shit off. When we're sick of ya, we'll let ya know. Until then, keep posting so we know you're still alive and kicking.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T11:01:36-07:00","id":211435,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Jim, Jeddy, PB and Thorbes. You guys are better than my blankie. ...Yes, I still need a blankie. Don't ask, unless you want to talk about Peanuts characters forever. That's what happens when people ask about my blankie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/4478-does-this-forum-make-my-butt-look-big-that-is-what-is-on-my-mind?p=211079#post211079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is slapping you and why, AzraelFirestorm?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the same friend girl that jokingly called him a faggot a few days ago and hurt his feelings. I really hope that wasn't her reaction at him telling that, that would be awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thorbes has the person right. It was my friend. The slap was for arguing with her. I don't even care. Slap me all you want. I never told her that my feelings were hurt. I was afraid to make her feel bad or sad. I was afraid she'd stop being my friend. I'll accept really any sort of treatment, so long as you show me even a glimmer of affection.<br /> One ex used me like an ashtray whenever she felt like it. She once tied me up and beat me so severely that my screams alarmed my roommate at the time (my sister) and they tried to literally break down the door to save me. I defended my girlfriend, and sent my sister away confused and worried. Apparently, I was so bruised up that my girlfriend was actually disgusted with herself. She turned on the shower and just sat in it, fully clothed and crying. I picked her up, helped her change like she was a small sleepy child and tucked her into bed with a back massage and assurances that I would love her forever, no matter what she did to me.<br /> I watch the Real Housewives of Wherever just about every day, just because my mom prefers to control the remote and I don't like being a bother. I cannot describe the palpable hatred I feel inside for those rich, spoiled, middle aged winos in cocktail dresses. I still memorized their basic personal histories, simply so I can conversate with my own mother without using the phrase, &quot;I dunno. i don't really pay attention to this boring, soul-numbing reality tv bullshit.&quot; Wouldn't want to upset her. Her life is hard as it is, with her nearly constant pain and accompanying symptoms of illness.<br /> I still hung out with that girl, by the way, in the rain, for hours after she slapped me.<br /> About a half hour after the rain stopped, my mom hobbled out for a cigarette (we don't smoke inside, because our cats are not furry little air filters) and gave her some very swanky boots that my shopaholic grandmother gave to my mom, but that would fit my friend better.<br /> \u200bThere's no point in saying anything. Her family is nice to me, and my mother likes them quite a lot. Better just to forgive quietly and keep marching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 07-28-2014, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T11:08:13-07:00","id":211457,"title":"","content":"Lately I've been seeing a meme make the rounds. I will provide it here as food for thought.<br /> <br /> &quot;If your friend talked to you the way you talk to yourself, would you let that person be your friend?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T12:27:26-07:00","id":211555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=211435#post211435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, Jim, Jeddy, PB and Thorbes. You guys are better than my blankie. ...Yes, I still need a blankie. Don't ask, unless you want to talk about Peanuts characters forever. That's what happens when people ask about my blankie.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what's up with the blankie, Linus?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T13:33:27-07:00","id":211604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=211555#post211555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what's up with the blankie, Linus?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://retrodecosettings.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/02/Linus-160x200.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Well, my blanket comforts me in troubled times, for starters. That's a blanket's primary job, before even preserving body heat or blanket-forts. It's a wonderful stand-in for a sympathetic ear when I need to vent to someone. It gives me hugs that don't make me feel ...weird... inside. In fact, it gives me hugs whenever I need them, which I can say about no other being in creation.<br /> <br /> AND, IF THAT WEREN'T ENOUGH, it's extremely versatile and useful:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Peanuts Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Uses</b><br /> <br /> Linus' blanket has the ability to be reshaped into nearly any form and be put to many different uses. These are:<br /> Linus uses his security blanket as a whip. security blanket (primary use), a stylish neck scarf, a quilt for <a href=\"http://peanuts.wikia.com/wiki/Lucy_van_Pelt\" target=\"_blank\">Lucy's</a> doll's bed (she cuts a square out from the middle of the blanket), various representational shapes for a &quot;flannelgraph&quot; (Lucy at work with her scissors), flannel squares to clean Linus' glasses (Lucy and her scissors), Lucy's kite, a penguin, a parachute, two sports coats (one for <a href=\"http://peanuts.wikia.com/wiki/Snoopy\" target=\"_blank\">Snoopy</a> and one for <a href=\"http://peanuts.wikia.com/wiki/Woodstock\" target=\"_blank\">Woodstock</a>), a hospital robe for <a href=\"http://peanuts.wikia.com/wiki/Spike\" target=\"_blank\">Spike</a>, a cowboy's neckerchief, a bullfighter's cape, a whip or insect swatter (&quot;fastest blanket in the West&quot;), a pool table felt, a hammock, a big bow tie, a slingshot, second base, Dracula's cape, a bunny, a monster that hisses at Lucy and attacks her (the blanket's own transformation), a &quot;paper&quot; airplane, and a cummerbund.<br /> In the world of the television specials, Linus most famously turns his blanket into a shepherd's headdress, in <i><a href=\"http://peanuts.wikia.com/wiki/A_Charlie_Brown_Christmas\" target=\"_blank\">A Charlie Brown Christmas</a>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>My blanket is more badass than vampire Chuck Norris after he learned V20 Celerity and some serious Obfuscate, then snuck up and diablerized vampire Bruce Lee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 07-28-2014, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T17:24:33-07:00","id":211842,"title":"","content":"meh i feel weird today...my mood for NO reason tanked to complete shit. I mean i've been cranky all day and in pain but still. Hubby went to his moms to go do laundry and here i am with a newly filled presccription of vicodin wondering what would happen if I took the whole thing. instead I took 3 and am waiting for it to kick in and put me to sleep for a bit. My moods go all over the place when i'm in pain, I was in a down mood before i got sick now...My back is on fire, my tummy is giving me trouble from the vicodin and zofran, and hten theres the pain that started it all, that stupid abcess. I was relived to find out its just a MRSA staph infection and that it seems to be getting better not worse but still...I&quot;m tired of laying in bed, my house is a fucking disaster and my husband wont lift a finger to help clean while i'm unable to walk. Well thats not true i CAN walk around a little bit but it hurts if my legs at all rub together, or if i put on pants, oh and then my back hurts and hurts even worse cause i have to walk funny to prevent the legs from touching..yeah...<br /> I know that when i'm well i'll be expected to clean up the house, and that includes his messes... All he does nowadays is play video games. Thats it. If I ask him to do anything with me he throws a fit over how i'm wasting his time blah blah. But then when he's not on the game hes at his moms, and gets mad that i dont want to go over there with him. *Shrugs* I wish i could make him see that he's hurting me. but he just says he wont talk to me about why he wont talk to me!? i'm so fucking lonely even when he's here, its a fight to just get his attention, I dont have anyone else in my life that i can talk to anymore, so all day I sit alone on my couch lately cause my back hurts to much to use my desk, not talking to anyone. I was fine with that untill hubby stopped talking to me except to mention role-playing or video games..or to ask when i'm cooking dinner or cleaning.<br /> <br /> I feel ugly and fat and lazy, i know the reason i got this abscess is cause my thighs rub when i walk around for to long and that causes a rash blah blah but not one of my doctors have had the balls to just say it &quot;you need to loose weight&quot;..i did get my nurse commenting on the fact i lost 2-3 pounds in the last 4 days(it may have been more, when she weighed me on friday i wasnt wearing heavy clothes, today i was, my scale says i've lost nearly 5lbs since thursday), which brightened my day up until i got home that is. and one of the rare times hubby said much to me lately was to comment on the fact my calfs and ankles are looking creepy thin. I havent been eating much at all lately. i just dont care to eat, food doesnt excite me, plus the more I eat the fatter and more lazy i'll get and I cant have that. Nope wont have that. (For the record &quot;Creepy thin&quot; to my husband is anything tiny...I'm fat,... He thinks my goal weight of 130 or a size 6-8 pants size is gross.(i'm 5'3 that is a perfectly healthy weight)..well i've politely told him its my body i'll do with it as I like. oN the upside its not like he's stopping me from dieting...though he has commented i need to eat more and is against my meal plan for next month, but has said himself its my choice. But beyond that i get NO support from him, he wont go on walks with me or do anything the takes away from &quot;His time&quot;...and talking is an annoyance, must just be with me though cause he talks up a storm to his mom and siblings damn near daily.<br /> <br /> His version of &quot;being there for me&quot; is to just hand me his debit card...we dont have alot of cash...but what little we have left after rent and bills he gives to me most of the time as a way to make me happy, funny how i just want to cry when he does that because though i love buying new things thats nto what i want, i want him to pay attention to me. Fuck I want him to see that i feel like i'm loosing it right now, but instead i'm alone, i'm having to deal with this all alone and that fucking sucks. I have TRIED to tell him, but its like talking to a wall, he laughs and doesnt take it seriously.<br /> <br /> I've been on the vicodin for about 5 days, and already i dont want to give it up(though i was given a fresh presciption today, 30 more pills yay.)...already i take more then i'm supposed to, not cause it helps the pain(ohh it really doesnt, not at all) but it makes me feel relaxed, calm and i can sleep, and as long as its in my system i'm perfectly fine with being ignored and treated like an object or servant,its also helping a ton with my diet I rarely got hungry before the vicodin and while on it im NEVER hungry i have to set an alarm on my laptop to accutally remind myself to eat...My doc wants to put me on Risperdal next week, as he says the psychatrsit is taking too long to get back to me,and he wants to get me on something before it gets any worse...i dont know i mean it was my idea but i hated the meds last time, they took away to much of 'me', i know it will help but at the same time...i would rather just let it get worse, maybe i just dont care if it gets worse this time. I dont know anymore.<br /> <br /> sometimes on days like this the only thing stopping me from doing something stupid is that I dont want to hurt my dad, because it would kill him if i did it. He already blames himself for how i turned out, i dont want him to blame himself for my death...and my cat, my poor cat would be heartbroken to loose her mommy...stupid i know...but really its all i have to hang on to..other then that I have nothing else no reason to even try, no reason to stop myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> i'm sorry for the wall of text dunno where else to put this, but i needed to get it out i needed SOMEONE ANYONE to see it so it would stop eating me, and i dont see my stupid therapist till later this week.....and i dont have any friends that ever get on g-talk or aim or whatnot anymore, cause they have lives now... Its just me always alone...no wonder i'm so fucking depressed again.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T17:34:39-07:00","id":211852,"title":"","content":"You don't have to be sorry. You didn't do anything wrong. That's what this thread is here for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T17:41:51-07:00","id":211856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=211852#post211852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to be sorry. You didn't do anything wrong. That's what this thread is here for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i always feel sorry when i post things like this ,cause i think &quot;oh maybe i shouldnt post this, its to much, i'm just rambling..etc&quot; or the worst one yhet &quot;why should i be burdening anyone elses minds with my shit? people have enough going on in their own lives without hearing about mine.&quot; blah.<br /> <br /> my mind works in weird ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":