be solved with an appropriate application of Tesla coils.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T10:19:44-07:00","id":220322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=220310#post220310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All problems can be solved with an appropriate application of Tesla coils.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need more Tesla coils in my house.<br /> <br /> No, wait, Littlest Baby Bear hacked her uncle's lock code for his iPhone...........I'd be worried what she would do with one of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T10:40:00-07:00","id":220327,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T10:54:55-07:00","id":220335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=219708#post219708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I beat myself up endlessly for every failure small and large; for instance, I still want to respond to the year-old failure of having reached across a dinner table for a pot of mayo rather than asking the person I reached over by inflicting physical pain upon myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps at all, apart from the inflicting physical pain part this is very very VERY common.... the whole beating yourself up over pointless mistakes and flaws. I had an issue with it years ago (still do to some extent)... mostly I worked on it by conditioning my brain that no, I'm going to make mistakes like everyone else and fuck it, they don't matter in the long run.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T18:34:45-07:00","id":220622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=220098#post220098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm alive. Hope you feel better and get the vertigo problem remedied, CK.<br /> Jim, I don't really know what to say, because I verbally abuse myself to the point that I genuinely daydream about the relief that a bullet blasting through my skull or falling on one of my own bowie knives would be. I'm glad you're trying something, and for me, I'd gladly sacrifice some objectivity for some love of self or some peace. Thanks for the encouragement, PB. And that was SUCH a sweet message, Scel.<br /> <br /> I'm ... not good.<br /> <br /> I'm going to go now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Az, I'm SO glad that you posted, I've been worried the last couple of days that something had happened to you, silly i know cause a couple days isnt that long but following that post of yours i've been concerned.<br /> <br /> I hope that you are getting help or taking the time to work on getting well, as always we're all here regardless!<br /> <br /> Take your time, but please dont be a stranger we'll worry our asses off if you just vanish!<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ ______________________________<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for me...blah. we're on day 2 of the Risperdal, VERY low dosage, half a miligram...but my god I slept through the ENTIRE night last night....I NEVER do that i usually wake up at least 4 times...That or i woke up and fell back asleep so quickly i dont remember. *shrugs* My brains a bit foggy and i'm still slightly sleepy all damn day, but I know in a week or two that should pass.... Dunno if its helping my moods, doc says it can take a week or two, and i see him again in 2 weeks, so he'll see if he needs to increase it at that point. Since this was an emergency prescription (my primary care doc prescribed it) I dont have the mood stablizer I should be on as my doc was not at all comfertable giving me that without me being under a physchatrists care..<br /> <br /> Still waiting to hear back on if I'm ever goign to get in to see one though, its been 2 months and a massive headache to even get an appointment(which i still dont have one and havent heard anything in weeks)<br /> <br /> I've been sorta sad and uninterested in much lately, though today i found myself drawing for the first time in weeks so thats got to be a good thing right?<br /> <br /> I'm smoking again sadly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I quit completely for a whole week...and them bam right back to full pack a day without even meaning to..I'll quit when i wont loose my mind from doing so. My leg itches, my entire left arm hurts from a fall in the shower 2 days ago(How the hell does it hurt worse 2 days after the fall then it did the day of!?)<br /> <br /> At least the icky thoughts have passed for now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 08-06-2014, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T16:57:04-07:00","id":221342,"title":"","content":"&quot;I love those who do not know how to live, except by going under, for they are those who cross over.<br /> <br /> I love the great despisers because they are the great reverers and arrows of longing for the other shore.<br /> <br /> I love those who do not first seek behind the stars for a reason to go under and be a sacrifice, but who sacrifice themselves for the earth, that the earth may some day become the overman's.<br /> <br /> I love him who lives to know, and who wants to know so that the overman may live some day. And thus he wants to go under.<br /> <br /> I love him who works and invents to build a house for the overman and to prepare earth, animal, and plant for him: for thus he wants to go under.<br /> <br /> I love him who loves his virtue, for virtue is the will to go under and an arrow of longing.<br /> <br /> I love him who does not hold back one drop of spirit for himself, but wants to be entirely the spirit of his virtue: thus he strides over the bridge as spirit.<br /> <br /> I love him who makes his virtue his addiction and his catastrophe: for his virtue's sake he wants to live on and to live no longer.<br /> <br /> I love him who does not want to have too many virtues. One virtue is more virtue than two, because it is more of a noose on which his catastrophe may hang.<br /> <br /> I love him whose soul squanders itself, who wants no thanks and returns none: for he always gives away and does not want to preserve himself.<br /> <br /> I love him who is abashed when the dice fall to make his fortune, and asks, 'Am I then a crooked gambler?' For he wants to perish.<br /> <br /> I love him who casts golden words before his deeds and always does even more than he promises: for he wants to go under.<br /> <br /> I love him who justifies future and redeems past generations: for he wants to perish of the present.<br /> <br /> I love him who chastens his god because he loves his god: for he must perish of the wrath of his god.<br /> <br /> I love him whose soul is deep, even in being wounded, and who can perish of a small experience: thus he goes gladly over the bridge.<br /> <br /> I love him whose soul is overfull so that he forgets himself, and all things are in him: thus all things spell his going under.<br /> <br /> I love him who has a free spirit and a free heart: thus his head is only the entrails of his heart, but his heart drives him to go under.<br /> <br /> I love all those who are as heavy drops, falling one by one out of the dark cloud that hangs over men: they herald the advent of lightning, and, as heralds, they perish.&quot;<br /> <br /> Friedrich Nietzsche, <i>Thus Spoke Zarathustra</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T00:25:43-07:00","id":221739,"title":"","content":"I am SO CONFUSED. Why is it the more depressed I get the easier it is for me to role-play or draw. Seriously all i want to do is role-play right now, i'm feeling creative...but at the same time I'm HORRIBLY depressed and lonely I dont understand. *slams face against desk* I think i'm craving human interaction, I need to VERBALLY speak to someone anyone, and it doesnt need to be serious conversation just IC chatter and OOC joking would be enough for me. I hardly talk at all nowadays, most of my human interaction is in the form of chat rooms and fourms which while great are not the best for my fucking sanity. I may claim to hate being around people but I think I'm just using that as an excuse to pull away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T08:06:25-07:00","id":222147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=221739#post221739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am SO CONFUSED. Why is it the more depressed I get the easier it is for me to role-play or draw.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've mentioned this one before, but have you ever been so drunk (or known someone who was) that they couldn't remember what they did? It's kind of like that.<br /> <br /> Your brain gets used to making certain connections when the chemicals/hormones are in a certain configuration. The memories of the drunken debacle are in there behind the wall of &quot;need more alcohol&quot; because that was the dominant influence on the brain at the time. In your case, you always feel like you're more creative because you're gotten some good material out of your head when depressed. The mental pathways are accustomed to heading for the creative places when running short of serotonin. It's not that you CAN'T be creative without being depressed, it's just the easier, established pathway. It's the Dark Side. (LUKE: <i>Is the dark side stronger</i>? YODA: <i>No, no, no. Quicker, easier, more seductive</i>.<br /> <br /> So, just try to take it easy, relax.....I know, easier said than done......and keep chatting with us for now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T10:11:34-07:00","id":222269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=222147#post222147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've mentioned this one before, but have you ever been so drunk (or known someone who was) that they couldn't remember what they did? It's kind of like that.<br /> <br /> Your brain gets used to making certain connections when the chemicals/hormones are in a certain configuration. The memories of the drunken debacle are in there behind the wall of &quot;need more alcohol&quot; because that was the dominant influence on the brain at the time. In your case, you always feel like you're more creative because you're gotten some good material out of your head when depressed. The mental pathways are accustomed to heading for the creative places when running short of serotonin. It's not that you CAN'T be creative without being depressed, it's just the easier, established pathway. It's the Dark Side. (LUKE: <i>Is the dark side stronger</i>? YODA: <i>No, no, no. Quicker, easier, more seductive</i>.<br /> <br /> So, just try to take it easy, relax.....I know, easier said than done......and keep chatting with us for now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> oh that makes a frightening amount of sense and makes me wish I could tell my brain to fuck off and stop being a dick cause I dont want to have to get all depressed to having my artwork come easily. (When i'm not depressed its SOOOO much harder to get any art out cause my brains all confused, and gets all &quot;ohhh no what are you doing this isnt when we do this, no you MUST wait all your good ideas will come later...&quot;<br /> <br /> So I guess i'll need to retrain my brain then? When i'm in a better mood if i'm not feeling creative I'll FORCE myself to draw or write and hopefully i'll trick my brain into accepting I can be creative anytime i want.<br /> <br /> (Its early I JSUT woke up, like 30 mineuts ago and it takes me like 2 hours to be &quot;awake and full coherent&quot; if the above doesnt make sense I applogize it makes sense in my own head)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T10:46:41-07:00","id":222293,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the more research you do on the brain, the more you realize that just about everyone has a little asshole riding around in their skull that gets it's jollies by fucking with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T10:53:27-07:00","id":222301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=222293#post222293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the more research you do on the brain, the more you realize that just about everyone has a little asshole riding around in their skull that gets it's jollies by fucking with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>HAH I love how you put that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T13:18:05-07:00","id":222410,"title":"","content":"If you want the negative side, think of how the brain is a collection of semi-specialized processing networks, all working together and yet all at the same time. And now consider the myriad range of effects and cross effects those sub networks have on each other, and how a simple chemical or associative change can cause all this other work and difficulty.<br /> <br /> Now remember that we're moving towards using this as a model to make self improving and replicating AI's which are expected to become reasonably sentient within our lifetimes. <br /> <br /> Imagine what would happen if the traffic control brain for a city got depressed and decided to take up the electronic version of drinking to feel better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:22:49-07:00","id":222510,"title":"","content":"The computers always have the advantage of &quot;yes&quot; or &quot;no&quot;, and never &quot;maybe&quot;. Hopefully, that will help keeping the traffic lights from getting depressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T20:32:56-07:00","id":222751,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T22:06:22-07:00","id":222791,"title":"","content":"I am exasusted mentally. I was not ready to go from ZERO human interaction to 5 hours of role-playing..my brain is mush, i'm so tired i'm barely able to stay awake and i feel drained. Thats not to say that I didnt enjoy it I totally did, in fact i was more active then i've ever been in an RPG, even attempted to take the leadership role that I normally shy away from cause I feel like i'm &quot;demanding the game go my way&quot;...I still feel that way, in fact MANY times tonight I had to tell myself that if I didnt take charge nothing would happen(the otehr two members of hte group are not the take charge type), and i got incredibly awkward during a short personal scene that just involved my character(each character had one of these, my characters just happened to be a bit dark)...I also think i'm going to ask the other players if they thought i was being to in charge, and ask that they step up more cause i personally find it rude for one player to lead and make the others just follow along.<br /> <br /> I do get a bit annoyed that my character has a detailed backstory that gets ignored 99% of the time(thats my spoiled brat side talking, i'm used to mostly solo games that are usually on a deep personal level that involves the characters backstory and such, i'll get over it), and a personality of her of own...and the ANNOYING amount of metagaming going on..i Dont think its okay for players to offer OOC ideas to another player whos trying to think of something IC, its fine if IC they want to bounce ideas of each other IC, but if that is PHYSICALLY impossible for the two characters (like they are not in the same room etc) I get irritated cause to me that takes away from the game, a player should be able to come up with plans on their own and if their plans fail then that can make an interesting story, but if players ooc throw shit around and dont give people a chance to think ,its beyond frustrating.<br /> <br /> And I swear to fucking god if my ST(Whos also my husband so yeah..) doesnt start paying attention when we are talking i'm going to punch him. our group had a detailed plan, that he asked us the time of day we were going, we REPEATEDLY said night, and then he sets the scene and tells us its daytime..when we point out this huge error on his part he tells us he already set the scene and cant undo it....and he got mad everytime I asked a question in regards to rules.Its been a while since i've read Orpheus so i'm rusty on a few things, never mind the fact i'm playing a goddamned Marrow, and am in NO WAY familar with their Horrors so I needed him to clairfy what I could do and he got pissy and told me to go get the book, adn when I did he got mad cause &quot;i wasnt paying attention cause i was reading&quot; *facepalms* ) oh and the joy of us MAKING A plan then him last minuet after its all set into motion saying &quot;oh wait you guys cant do this as none of you are the correct Shade...you'll need to recruit help.....grrr THAT is something you tell us first...luckily in that instance he handwaved and retroactivly said we had done that, but still he needs to pay more attention.<br /> <br /> I wish I had the courage to run a game, I've had ideas for games in my head, have so much stuff for games written down...but i'm so self concious I cant bring myself to do it. I'm okay with Owod and NWOD rules, and I knwo Exalted like the back of my hand and would KILL to run an exalted game...but i dont know how to do it. I'm afraid of how to balance NPCS, afraid i'll make one overpowered and tick people off etc...and I feel like an idiot if I screw up...Plus hubby is a rule nazi, if I decide to house rule shit for my game he'll get all pissy about it. (I know this cause i once asked him about it, and stated a few of my ideas for houserules)...<br /> <br /> Blah i'm in rant mode. /shutdown","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T11:17:47-07:00","id":224318,"title":"","content":"I'm so tired. I want to give up. I keep trying to find reasons to stay, and it's just getting harder to hold on to those reasons. I'm feeling suicidal, homicidal and destructive. Better to implode and harm myself than to explode and harm others, right? I should go to the hospital right now, but... I can't. I don't want to save myself anymore. I want to let go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:12:20-07:00","id":224344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=224318#post224318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so tired. I want to give up. I keep trying to find reasons to stay, and it's just getting harder to hold on to those reasons. I'm feeling suicidal, homicidal and destructive. Better to implode and harm myself than to explode and harm others, right? I should go to the hospital right now, but... I can't. I don't want to save myself anymore. I want to let go.</div> </div> </div> </div>*bear hugs* I'm gonna call you like 1000 times today if you dont reply &lt;3 It took me a ton of courage to call, cause maybe that wasnt its intended use, but i'm worried about you! Hopefully if you dont reply or answer your phone its cause you are at the hospital getting help, peoples will miss you if you go away forever <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:16:00-07:00","id":224350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=224318#post224318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to save myself anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to be the one to do it, though. I can and will cheer for you, but end of the day, you gotta be the one to do the heavy lifting. Talk to a medical professional, Az; this shit is getting out of hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T18:30:26-07:00","id":224730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=224350#post224350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talk to a medical professional, Az; this shit is getting out of hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been trying to, but the mental health care providers are swamped around here and some don't accept my insurance. if my current state of mind continues, I'll try to make it to the Emergency Room to be treated and likely admitted to the ward. I don't want to live right now... I don't. It hurts. I just don't want to hurt anyone else, either. I feel stuck. If I could wish myself from existence, so that nobody would miss me, I think I would do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T20:33:42-07:00","id":224798,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T22:25:34-07:00","id":224866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=224798#post224798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ive felt that way for about 15 years or so. Still not done anything. Im thinking of trying to join the 27 club. Im not famous but fuck it. 15 months is more than enough time to do serious damage</div> </div> </div> </div>I turn 27 in just about 3 months.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T23:22:23-07:00","id":224898,"title":"","content":"ah that fun moment when i'm in pain from yet another abcess, and start to get so terrified that by the time i see my doc it would be so much worse and that he'd have to numb it again to lance it that I decided to do it myself...it is infected, took 2 days to go from &quot;oh look a small painless bump great&quot; to &quot;fuck its red,larger, painfull and infected&quot;...I am so scared of my doctor that just the thought had my heart racing from anxiety....Took me 10 minuets to do it myself with a tiny ass needle, and hurt only a small bit but i helped make it easier on myself by taking a hot shower first and a swig of the vodka i was using to sterilize the needle and wound area and my hands. (If its MRSA like my doctor thinks i needed to be beyond fucking careful with making sure my hands were clean afterwards.)...I dont know what do to, if my self care didnt fix it, on tuesday when i see my doc i'm beyond terrified of what he's going to do...like to the point i'm not sure i'll be able to get myself to go... It hurts right now, and i'm scared. Its not fair. its fucking not fair. Just as i FINALLY start to get somewhat on track, this shit happens, i'm tired of being in pain, i can hardly walk without it hurting like hell, the last one thats still healing hurts still if i put pressure on it...and guess what i'm fat so my fucking thighs ALWAYS touch and when i walk well its painfull.<br /> <br /> I have to wear leggings damn near 24/7 now to prevent the skin from rubbing and getting irritated...I dont want to be in pain any more, 2 solid months with my inner thigh hurting. I've been trying to exersize every day and now its starting to look like i may have to stop again untill i heal due to this new abcesses location *Sighs* THIS is not good my mental health. I am doing EVERYTHING I can to get better mentally, taking my medication, exersizing daily, eating better drinking water and no caffiene...but this...this is making all of that hard. It makes me want to curl into a ball and die cause then I wouldnt have to go through that terrible procedure again, 3rd time is not a fucking charm its torture, I'd rather run ten miles then have any more needles shoved into my thigh.<br /> <br /> Perhaps i'm being dramatic, but pain is NOT something I handle well unless its in a sex game...and even then thats not like this...this is a constant pain thats not fun and is ruining my life. Its fucking hillariours to me that i'm actually considering self harm again after 2 years without because of the old &quot;pain stops pain&quot; thing... yano like if your back hurts and you kick something it stops hurting? But even i know thats only a temporary solution *sighs* I'm in a shitty mood.<br /> <br /> Hubby is sitting not 5 feet from me and has no idea. This makes me even more sad i cant bring myself to talk to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T07:17:07-07:00","id":225052,"title":"","content":"Pain is pain, Scel. It's not overly dramatic to voice complaints about suffering. <br /> <br /> I'm feeling a bit better today than yesterday. A very good friend managed to cheer me up some and take my mind off of things. <br /> <br /> I'm still having some scary thoughts, but I know they're rooted in depression, trauma and poor self-image, so I'm trying to ignore them. It's not easy. <br /> <br /> ...I was about to start apologizing for complaining about my pathetic struggle with mental illness, but then I remembered what thread this is.....<br /> <br /> Woke up in a daze (24+ MGs of Klonopin/Clonazepam just to calm myself enough to sleep) and realized I was grasping at a pillow and crying, &quot;Please, please don't leave! What did I do?!?&quot; My cheeks were tear-stained and wet. My heart was pounding and I felt like a lost child. Then, and only then, did I finally wake up enough to realize that I was crying to nobody at all. <br /> <br /> I don't know. I just want to feel better, or just feel nothing, as both would likely be similar. <br /> <br /> Bye for now, folks. I'm off to take my medication, like a good guinea pig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T07:29:54-07:00","id":225058,"title":"","content":"Cereal, please don't harm yourself. I care about your well being. I enjoy hearing from you. I'm sorry that you're hurting. I can't tell you that it'll get better, because I don't know if that's true. I will miss you if you die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T11:03:55-07:00","id":225168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=225058#post225058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cereal, please don't harm yourself. I care about your well being. I enjoy hearing from you. I'm sorry that you're hurting. I can't tell you that it'll get better, because I don't know if that's true. I will miss you if you die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded, and the same goes for, well, everyone else. I've pretty much run out of ways to ask people not to hurt themselves, so I've been keeping quiet while I try to think of some new combination of words that might do the magical trick of convincing people not to hurt themselves, but I'm glad Jeddy is taking up some of my slack there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T11:23:37-07:00","id":225177,"title":"","content":"My post was not meant to discount everyone else. Cereal seemed like he needed the most encouragement at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T11:57:04-07:00","id":225195,"title":"","content":"I didn't think it was, Jeddy, and I'm sure no one else did either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T19:39:13-07:00","id":226717,"title":"","content":"I'm freaking out a little bit. Not a lot, but a little. It's been happening to me more and more often lately. I keep getting nailed, transfixed, with this desire to just <i>go</i>. Go somewhere. Anywhere. Preferably somewhere I can't identify. Just get in my car with nothing but my keys and drive I know not where until I run out of gas, and then figure shit out from there but definitely not think about it. Just <i>go</i>.<br /> <br /> When I think about <i>going</i>, I don't plan anything except where I'll go (if I want to get lost, I need make only three turns, though admittedly those turns are separated by some miles, and then I won't know where or even what direction I'm going, especially at night) and calling my boss, maybe the next day or maybe in a week, and telling him I won't be coming in any more. That imaginary conversation always floods me with relief as I imagine the questions he might ask, like, &quot;Where are you?&quot; Or, &quot;What happened?&quot; And me being able to answer any or all of them, finally without any of the usual stoic lies, with, &quot;I don't know.&quot; Then maybe things would happen or maybe they wouldn't; maybe he'd call my emergency contacts or just fire me. I don't know or care how the fantasy ends. The part of <i>going</i> that inspires me is being able to just admit that I am not okay and I don't know what's happening.<br /> <br /> Oh, don't worry, I'm not going to do it. Not tonight, anyway, and probably not ever. I wouldn't be talking about it if I was going to do it. Talking is one of my ways of...I don't know, of diffusing the impact of my...things. My head stuff, whatever. It's working, too. Normally by this point my heart would be racing and I'd be stalking through the trailer like I'm trying to catch up with my blood-pump. I just...nraaaah. I want to <i>go</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T23:11:17-07:00","id":226814,"title":"","content":"It was nice to smile again...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T07:04:20-07:00","id":226994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=226717#post226717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm freaking out a little bit. Not a lot, but a little. It's been happening to me more and more often lately. I keep getting nailed, transfixed, with this desire to just <i>go</i>. Go somewhere. Anywhere. Preferably somewhere I can't identify. Just get in my car with nothing but my keys and drive I know not where until I run out of gas, and then figure shit out from there but definitely not think about it. Just <i>go</i>.<br /> <br /> When I think about <i>going</i>, I don't plan anything except where I'll go (if I want to get lost, I need make only three turns, though admittedly those turns are separated by some miles, and then I won't know where or even what direction I'm going, especially at night) and calling my boss, maybe the next day or maybe in a week, and telling him I won't be coming in any more. That imaginary conversation always floods me with relief as I imagine the questions he might ask, like, &quot;Where are you?&quot; Or, &quot;What happened?&quot; And me being able to answer any or all of them, finally without any of the usual stoic lies, with, &quot;I don't know.&quot; Then maybe things would happen or maybe they wouldn't; maybe he'd call my emergency contacts or just fire me. I don't know or care how the fantasy ends. The part of <i>going</i> that inspires me is being able to just admit that I am not okay and I don't know what's happening.<br /> <br /> Oh, don't worry, I'm not going to do it. Not tonight, anyway, and probably not ever. I wouldn't be talking about it if I was going to do it. Talking is one of my ways of...I don't know, of diffusing the impact of my...things. My head stuff, whatever. It's working, too. Normally by this point my heart would be racing and I'd be stalking through the trailer like I'm trying to catch up with my blood-pump. I just...nraaaah. I want to <i>go</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as I'm sure I've recommended in the past before, GO WEST, YOUNG MAN! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T08:08:54-07:00","id":227027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=226994#post226994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as I'm sure I've recommended in the past before, GO WEST, YOUNG MAN! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/cBsoNeRPDBs\" data-code=\"cBsoNeRPDBs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/cBsoNeRPDBs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T08:46:23-07:00","id":227059,"title":"","content":"And I always think of this.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M3K3Qcn5cYQ\" data-code=\"M3K3Qcn5cYQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/M3K3Qcn5cYQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.