asts forever if you want something to consider when contemplating such things. It may suck NOW but the one constant in life is change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T14:06:54-07:00","id":227331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=227328#post227328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good idea (not doing it again).<br /> <br /> Just remember that nothing bad or terrible lasts forever if you want something to consider when contemplating such things. It may suck NOW but the one constant in life is change.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, and i need tgo not make such descions when i havent had much sleep, me and sleep depravation make bad ideas and dont handle shit well.,,I'm just going to take it easy and when i see my therapist tommorow talk about it...maybe see if we can get me into that pyschatrist to get my medications so this doesnt happen again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T02:39:58-07:00","id":227721,"title":"","content":"Fuuuuucccckkk I cant sleep o0 I'm super tired right now(As in i'm nearly falling asleep in my chair), but i lay down and my mind wont shut the fuck up. I.cant.sit.still...I want to move move move ,run around, dance ,sing, talk, something anything but go to sleep....Its the stupid &quot;high&quot; after the massive low, Its been so long since i'd done that shit to myself that i'd forgotten about the upswing that always follows it usually within a day after....and laying down makes the killer heartburn i have right now so much worse. On the upside even if I get sleep deprived tonight I wont end up doing something stupid, cause I know my cycles and how they work, i'll probably be sleeping very little the next few days and just be bouncy, flouncy happy...Fuck me i see my therapist tommorow at 2...in my case &quot;super energetic&quot; does not mean &quot;i'm not fucking tired&quot; I'm also a massive bitch during this time cranky and demanding cause I want to be. I am fucking amazingly bored right now not even kidding, i'd call someone if it wasnt 2:30 in the damn morning and they are likely asleep...whhyyy must this happen!? It doesnt fucking help that I feel like i'm being watched right now, I had to close my blinds it didnt really help, i swear this place is haunted or something ;&gt;&gt; so everytime i lay down not only does my mind start racing, but the thoughts are something alng the lines of &quot;What was that noise?!&quot; &quot;whos watching me?&quot; asking outloud for it to go away and leave me alone.(it never does cause he is a prick and likes to play games with my mind...whispering from teh shadows in the room taunting me with words I cant clearly hear, laughing and going silent just long enough for me to get comferetable then BAM the whispers start up again tauntint taunting taunting ) FUcking damnit i feel like i'm going nuts(going? i am nuts...)<br /> <br /> I took my meds like a good little crazy girl tonight, and i'm giggling at nothing damnit, cat wont talk to me, I can hear the whispers right now, cause the room is dead silent...I need my music.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T12:18:03-07:00","id":228317,"title":"","content":"*curls up in the corner* I passed the fuck out around 6 or 7..nightmares had me waking up many times(i dont remember any of the nightmares but i do remember feeling immense fear and sorrow every time i woke up from one of them), and i woke up screaming around 11..the dream that woke me i dont understand why it scared me so much, i can clearly recall details which is rare for me and usually means its a message...gonna pull out my old dream interpritation book, cause i REALLY need to figure out what that dream meant.. Whatever he is trying to tell me I feel its important adn that dream that i can recal so vivdly is important.<br /> <br /> Thearpy today should be...interesting I feel weird.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T23:03:35-07:00","id":228833,"title":"","content":"My mind is eating itself. I'm cycling through bipolar moodswings in matters of minutes. it's like being in a jet-powered racecar with an angry driver going a few hundred miles above the speed limit, who just randomly stomps on the breaks to watch your head hit the dashboard. <br /> I don't want to be a bummer and suck all the happiness from the people I care about. I should just lock myself in my steamer trunk until this blows over. I'm no good for anyone like this.<br /> <br /> I don't want to be a burden on the people that care about me. I want to be strong for them. I want them to be able to count on me. I'm trying. I promise. I have a damn good reason to try. I have things to live for, people that matter, dreams to make realities. I can't let myself get sucked into my own bullshit again! I have too much to lose. I refuse to let the fucking demons and goblins in my head win.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T03:07:21-07:00","id":228927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=228833#post228833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mind is eating itself. I'm cycling through bipolar moodswings in matters of minutes. it's like being in a jet-powered racecar with an angry driver going a few hundred miles above the speed limit, who just randomly stomps on the breaks to watch your head hit the dashboard.<br /> I don't want to be a bummer and suck all the happiness from the people I care about. I should just lock myself in my steamer trunk until this blows over. I'm no good for anyone like this.<br /> <br /> I don't want to be a burden on the people that care about me. I want to be strong for them. I want them to be able to count on me. I'm trying. I promise. I have a damn good reason to try. I have things to live for, people that matter, dreams to make realities. I can't let myself get sucked into my own bullshit again! I have too much to lose. I refuse to let the fucking demons and goblins in my head win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just cause i feel like repeating myself!<br /> <br /> You are in no way a burden to anyone, you are allowed to have moments where you are not &quot;strong&quot; fuck i'd be worried if you didnt, geting better doesnt just happen overnight, there will be pit falls and slip ups and your brain being a dick(of course you already know this.) Also anyone who calls you a &quot;burden&quot; deserves a punch in the face(so please point me in their direction if someone says that to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) but thats just my opinion. You'll be fine, find ways to distract yourself, fuck if you cant i'm always around and will gladly spend 24/7 on the phone or skype or whatever to ensure you dont even have a chance to have a mood swing, and if you do, you can, if you feel like it, talk to me i will always listen, even if i may not always know what to say(And as you know like 95% of the time i have no words! *giggles* ) i can at least be an ear and a safe place for you to vent when you're upset, I dont judge no matter whats being said to me ever. Again i shall say it you are NOT a burden, and never be afraid to say whats on your mind, if your upset say something! I'd rather you say something then just let it fester and eat you alive. It wont bring me down, in fact i'd worry more if you dont say anything. (dont make me using my mind magic to make you talk hehe) It worried me to see this post cause my mind immidiatly jumped to some pretty dark places as to what &quot;mood swing&quot; may end up meaning for you, so please please please post here or pm or call me if you need to or feel like complete utter shit, or just want to chat about random nonsense all damn day, thats cool I dont care I love it, god knows i dont talk enough XD<br /> <br /> *hugs* be safe, take care and smile cause you are to awesome to not be happy! (moodswings be damned)<br /> <br /> <br /> (prolly shoulda pm'd this to lazy to actually &quot;click&quot; through to get to the page to PM XD its 3am clicking on PM would be far to much work, as it is i'm using voice control on my PC, and have yet to figure out how to get it to fucking click on PM no matter how many times i scream the words that eventually devole into me screaming &quot;fucking click on this&quot; or &quot;show the damn numbers&quot; it stares at me blankly as if taunting me...oh laziness thy name is Dana.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T03:47:32-07:00","id":228967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://namebrandlindsay.com/2014/08/12/why-some-peoples-minds-try-to-kill-them/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://namebrandlindsay.com/2014/08/12/why-some-peoples-minds-try-to-kill-them/\" target=\"_blank\"> Lindsay Ellis </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://namebrandlindsay.com/2014/08/12/why-some-peoples-minds-try-to-kill-them/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://namebrandlindsay.com/2014/08/12/why-some-peoples-minds-try-to-kill-them/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T06:59:12-07:00","id":229026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=228833#post228833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mind is eating itself. I'm cycling through bipolar moodswings in matters of minutes. it's like being in a jet-powered racecar with an angry driver going a few hundred miles above the speed limit, who just randomly stomps on the breaks to watch your head hit the dashboard.<br /> I don't want to be a bummer and suck all the happiness from the people I care about. I should just lock myself in my steamer trunk until this blows over. I'm no good for anyone like this.<br /> <br /> I don't want to be a burden on the people that care about me. I want to be strong for them. I want them to be able to count on me. I'm trying. I promise. I have a damn good reason to try. I have things to live for, people that matter, dreams to make realities. I can't let myself get sucked into my own bullshit again! I have too much to lose. I refuse to let the fucking demons and goblins in my head win.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be too little too late, but you can always try something (non-pharmaceutical) to calm yourself down. I know it's tough, but it never hurts to try. Despite what Yoda tells us, there is a try. <i>Try </i>or<i> try not</i>, if you don't try, you'll never get to <b>do</b>.<br /> <br /> Calm music, long boring documentaries on The History Channel, a couple of hours watching a bug zapper while contemplating what causes the bugs to be attracted to the light.....stupid shit, sure, but it derails the shit your mind it trying to beat you up with.<br /> <br /> And always come back to the same thing - it's your mind, you are the final judge on all this nonsense and you can tell that inner asshole to shut the fuck up. From experience, I will tell you that you will not always win every second of every day, but the more you work over that inner asshole with a few synaptic kidney punches, the more often he'll back down. I will also warn you now, he'll come back stronger for quite a few rounds. Eventually, you can wear him down enough that you'll win more than lose, but it takes time and a reason to fight.<br /> <br /> For myself, I had a hard time finding a reason to fight for a long time, until I just got pissed off enough to say, &quot;Fuck this! I'm not letting a 5 pound piece of meat that <b>I'M</b> in control of beat my ass at anything!!&quot; Yeah, I've got a serious amount of rage to tap into. If I ever got to close to a gamma bomb, there would be a big problem.<br /> <br /> But I digress.....first technique I tapped into was to derail the thoughts in the first place with other things. Give it a shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T13:43:50-07:00","id":229535,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to distract myself with music, as recommended. It's helping to drown out most of the intrusive and illogical thoughts I'm having. <br /> I must admit, though, that today has felt like a strong Datura Stramonium trip. I've gone onto the porch for a smoke a few times, and then proceeded to &quot;smoke&quot; a cigarette I haven't even taken out of the pack. I'm talking to people that aren't there. I know they're not there. Their voices are just echoing in my head from past trauma. I tell myself every day that this mind is my own, but chemistry can be a tough obstacle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T15:58:50-07:00","id":229651,"title":"","content":"What the actual fuck, i'm not feeling good(i think i caught a cold) found my nyquil and went &quot;oh hey i should drink whats left (half a bottle) r*rolls eyes* i Didnt, i just measured it out and took slightly more then the stanadard does snce this shit rarely works for me if i just take what it says to...i Dont get why my brain is all &quot;hey you know the medications meant to help you? yeahhh you should TAKE IT ALL!!!!!&quot; i Dont like being sick...i get grumpy...I reallllly need to see my doctor cause i think maybe the risperdal is fucking with my brain in bad ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:06:28-07:00","id":229662,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:58:34-07:00","id":229705,"title":"","content":"They care and are worried about you, 'killer. I know you said you'll never allow it and I'm not going to argue for it, but they're just doing the best they know how (which apparently isn't very good, but hey, points for effort) to express that they want to help you get better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T17:03:12-07:00","id":229720,"title":"","content":"I want to second what jimB said <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T01:45:18-07:00","id":230077,"title":"","content":"*curls up in ther corner* I didnt know I could be so worried about someone. Its beyond my own understanding. I HATE most people I can list on ONE HAND the people I care about enough to give two shits over and worry for their safety...and yet here i am worried sick about someone i've only known a short time, wondering if they are okay because my phone kept cutting out and i couldnt hear clearly enough to be sure that everything was fine...maybe i'm overreacting maybe i misunderstood what was being said to me, fuck i dont know, the fucking internet sucks for conveying tone and can make something innocent sound terribly dark...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 08-16-2014, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T17:15:11-07:00","id":230707,"title":"","content":"I forgot to take my medication last night...but holy shit i feel amazing...i wasnt tired when i woke up and it didnt take me as long to wake up as it does when i'm on it...i'm not taking it anymore. I see my doc on monday, i plan to ask him about an as needed medicine or just wait till i see a physchatrist cause my doc doesnt know what he's doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T19:56:35-07:00","id":230915,"title":"","content":"I don't know what I'm doing anymore. I'm so lost and scared and I wish there was something, someone who could make me feel safe. I feel like a failure in every aspect of my life. i don't have love. I don't have stability or peace of mind. I'm a mentally ill Neanderthal. I'm old fucking hardware, incompatible with anyone or anything. I'm obsolete. I don't want to be the way I am, but who am I when you strip the madness away? I don't know. I'm terrified that the answer will be a dead child, with tears dried on his cold cheeks. I don't want to feel dead inside. I don't want my story to be a tragedy. I'm afraid it will. I'm afraid I may be dead and already in Hell. I deserve it. I can't touch anything without damaging or tainting it. I'm dirty inside. I have a spoiled, rotten soul that's fit only to burn. I dreamed of damnation since childhood, and why? Because I'm damned. I'm in my own private hell and noone can save me. I don't care if I get hungry or thirsty or any of that bullshit. I'm tired of seeing the world. A few accurate pokes and gouges, I'll never have to see again. I'll feel so free. I wouldn't yearn for things I cannot have as much. I finally be blind to the suffering around me, knowing in my heart that I was meant to be a father and husband, not anyone's savior. I am trapped in a prison of my own making, my own weakness. I belong here. I wouldn't last outside this cage. People can be so cruel. The taunting, the judgment, the stares. I am ugly. I am fractured. I cannot find a way to change these things. I'm selfish.<br /> <br /> \u200b I should be worrying about the people around me, volunteering at the homeless shelter, the soup kitchen. I'm not doing those things. I'm not even caring for myself. I'm taking too many benzodiazepines, and I can't feel safe no matter what I do. I want a cigarette so badly, but I can't go outside yet. I'm having trouble breathing. I know it's psychological and I'm so sorry for complaining about my stupid bullshit problems! Why can't I just bottle it up and let it turn into a fucking brain tumor, like I'm supposed to. I feel like running at full speed off the highest cliff I can find, just to feel the illusion of the freedom of flight as my last clear sensation. I can't do that. I think. DO I EVEN BELONG TO MYSELF? Why is suicide illegal? Are you fuckers afraid I'll die in an inconvenient manner that might cost taxpayers?!? FUCK YOU. If I own nothing else, I own my body, my mind and my fucking soul. I just wish any of those things were worth having. nobody wants them. I'm going to shut up now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T06:10:48-07:00","id":231394,"title":"","content":"Az, can I ask what you're doing for your mental health? Are you seeing a doctor, getting medications, anything like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T10:46:33-07:00","id":231696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=231394#post231394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Az, can I ask what you're doing for your mental health? Are you seeing a doctor, getting medications, anything like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>- Seeing a psychiatrist, next appointment in a few days<br /> <br /> - On one medication (Clonazepam), because the mood stabilizer that I was also taking (Seroquel) made me feel dangerous to the public in such a way that I DEMANDED to be hospitalized.<br /> <br /> - I'm doing some RPG stuff to distract me, but nothing more taxing than planning one or two games per week. <br /> <br /> - Lots of music to drown out the bullshit that my mind enjoys screaming at me.<br /> <br /> - I've tried to meditate, and over the years, have discovered that it is Fucking Impossible for me to do it. Ditto for full body relaxation techniques. I'm a ball of stress and strained muscles.<br /> <br /> - Smoking pot. A lot. I know it's legal, but Christ, if I feel better, I'm too stoned to express it properly! I smoked 3 joints in a row just to maintain my emotional equilibrium enough to talk to my neighbor the other night.<br /> <br /> - Trying to avoid people, because I feel toxic. I even considered shutting down my Facebook and even my forum account. I'm not going to. I won't, because then I'll feel.... ready to... I don't know. <br /> <br /> I'm trying lots of things, and I'm still trying to get a real THERAPIST as well. So far, therapist #1 scared me for reasons I can't really explain, even to myself. Therapist #2, a renowned specialist in personality and mood disorders, kicked me out of his fucking office for &quot;arguing&quot; with him. I never raised my voice, and was only in that office long enough to finish filling out the paperwork.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo far, the 'finding therapy' thing is my biggest obstacle. And human interaction. And a broken heart. And intrusive thoughts about self-harm or suicide. And a looming sense of doom. That, and I'm out of my medication. Completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:12:41-07:00","id":236005,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:34:55-07:00","id":236026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=236005#post236005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Managing to crawl my way out of this pit without the help of my bullshit bitch cunt of a therapist. Issue made it sound urgent that I show up to a meeting on monday , no designated time just show up and shed be there to help me. She stood me up. Well yesterday I got sent home early from work because of my vertigo kick in my ass and me nearly getting crushed under and 200 lb grill. I showed up at 4:45 office closes at 5 she's already got and no one ks there. Today at my earliest convenience I shows up this time around 4:30 doors already locked. O caught her outside and yelled at her and screamed didn't call her any names but too her that she is a negligent bitch because if I had a patient in crisis mode who called a suicide hotline my ass would've dropped Shi and actually tried to get a hold of him and definitely not stood him up on the day she Tom me to show up. Fuck her. Im filing a complaint against her in office because this is bullshit. Im here for treatment not to be treated like a fucking child you can dismiss anytime he or she becomes too much of a burden for the time being</div> </div> </div> </div>Cereal, man, I hope things get better fast and this bullshit your DOCTOR is pulling stops post-haste. I hope you're feeling physically alright, as it sounds like you almost got horribly injured. Just know that, the heinous fuckery I've pulled with you put aside and hopefully forgiven, I'm here if you need to talk, vent, rant, whatever. I've been on the edge of ending it A Lot recently, and I'm doing my best to fight it. If I can help fight yours, you have my sword. I'm not fucking around. Pm me, you can have all my contact information and feel free to call me, e-mail, doesn't matter what time or for what reason. I'll be there. I'm not about letting good men fall, especially if I can fucking do something about it. You matter around here, and this wouldn't feel like home without cerealkiller. You matter to us. You don't deserve to be treated this way or suffer this much. I know that there are loads of people, many or most who know you far better than I, who would say the same.<br /> <br /> And yes, Fuck that dumbshit asshole douchenozzle fuck-knuckle thundercunt doctor! She deserves to be fucking reported, and you deserve better treatment! Period.<br /> <br /> \u200b*******************************<br /> <br /> I'm on my medication again as of an hour ago, and the doc added Gabapentin aka Neurontin to supplement the huge amount of Clonazepam I take. I'm doing okay. Got to see my Grandma, grabbed a pack of decent cigarettes (I'd been smoking the cheapest menthols I could find) and even got to talk to my absolute favorite person in the world for a while. =)<br /> <br /> Stressful day, but I can't call it bad. Today was a day. There will be more.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis might just be my new meds talking, but I'm kinda looking forward to tomorrow. How bout that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 08-20-2014, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T01:47:12-07:00","id":236294,"title":"","content":"edited for reasons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 08-21-2014, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T10:18:38-07:00","id":236645,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T13:52:56-07:00","id":236902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nc7c7Cdfjik\" data-code=\"nc7c7Cdfjik\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/nc7c7Cdfjik/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T01:06:44-07:00","id":238020,"title":"","content":"Tonight has been a fucking Sadness Extravaganza. I talk to a VERY good friend and make myself sad by being honest about myself with them and not realizing the gravity of what I was saying and what it said about my life. I go to another good friend to vent and end up just adding a sense of hopelessness to my sadness. Not their fault. I was just heading there already.<br /> <br /> THEN, my best friend from Junior High, who I haven't seen or heard from in 13 years, messages me out of nowhere and happily says that it's been awhile and he hopes to talk to me and hang out. He also asks how I've been since then.<br /> This guy watched my family crumble and witnessed my first breakdown that led to my first and second hospitalizations, and then soon thereafter moved away. He was my best and only friend. We smoked our first cigarettes together. We shot my first pellet gun together. I even took him on vacation with me and my family to Mexico, and he met my paternal grandfather, my aunts and uncles, my cousins (most of my dad's side of the family is still in Mexico) and now deceased grandmother, none of whom I've been able to visit since.<br /> <br /> He was family.<br /> <br /> I had to break it to him that I didn't get better. I only kept getting getting worse, and that now I'm disabled. I had to tell the guy I considered my brother, a guy I was planning to join the military with, and we were SERIOUS about it to the point that I tried getting into military school (He got in. I...just....), that I can't even function. I feel so helpless and pathetic and I'm too afraid to even look at his reply.<br /> <br /> I feel like a failure at life. I hope it's not all my fault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T06:17:23-07:00","id":238125,"title":"","content":"Fault isn't real. It's a trick you mind plays on you to get you accept its flagellation. Don't buy into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T12:18:22-07:00","id":238419,"title":"","content":"Ideleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T22:38:56-07:00","id":241100,"title":"","content":"Things are becoming terrifying. I'm getting worse and I don't know what to do. I'm sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T03:54:37-07:00","id":241206,"title":"","content":"Az, what happened?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T14:27:53-07:00","id":245652,"title":"","content":"I am very depressed and have been very depressed for the past week or two, I can't focus on things I like and I am constantly haunted by my childhood and my teenage years, both mistakes I have made and mistakes that were beyond my control.<br /> <br /> All I can think about is bad things from my past, and I tried to distract myself by coming up with an idea for a World of Darkness game that was anime-influenced and not traditional Gothic-Punk personal horror (as I like anime and generally prefer the more action-oriented &quot;Vampions&quot; style of gameplay, though personal horror is good for me in small doses and I can respect the tastes of others so long as they respect mine). Unfortunately, I proposed this on another forum and got bashed. Rather than do the mature thing and leave it alone, I got pissed and kept arguing back and forth for a few days, even lapsing into old habits from my days on the White Wolf forums (attacking the Goth subculture and the like).<br /> <br /> Combine this with my recent depression and constant haunting memories of my childhood and teenage years, and I in a fit of anger came up with a grimdark revenge-filled Werewolf chronicle (one that I wasn't even going to actually run) where the players would destroy my childhood past and erase all that bad mojo. It was supposed to be an exercise of catharsis but ended up making me even more angry and sad. So naturally, we argue back and forth on this board for a while and I bring up my Appalachian upbringing and bad memories related to it (Even though there were good memories too, I was just so focused on the negative that I left that behind and grew more upset) and it degenerates to more bickering and insults on both ends.<br /> <br /> After one shot of vodka and a bottle of Mountain Dew later (first time I have consumed alcohol in weeks, and don't worry, I drink responsibly and in small amounts), I am now realizing what I have done. I don't feel angry anymore, just really depressed and I kind of hate myself for letting myself relapse into old emotional habits, I feel really depressed, sad, and guilty over what I have done and I don't know what to do.<br /> <br /> I know most of you guys here on Onyx Path don't like me, but I wanted to say that I am sorry for all this chaos, whether it be on the old White Wolf Forums, on RPG.net's forums, or on /tg/. I am sorry for my ranting and raving on how I was wronged by goths in an old LARP group from years ago and how that festered into this mindset I had for a long time, one I thought I had gotten out of, but relapsed into recently.<br /> <br /> No matter what your tastes are, whether you be a goth or a metalhead, a punk or an anime otaku, or whatever, I am fine with what you like and whatever subculture you choose to identify with (if any), or however you play your games, WoD or otherwise. I just feel so bad about my past and haunted by all the things that I have done and I feel so fucking guilty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T14:43:55-07:00","id":245657,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T20:00:46-07:00","id":245782,"title":"","content":"Camilla and cerealkiller, I am sorry for the difficulties you are both going through. I wish I had something intelligent to say here, something that would make everything better, but that is not one of my skills, and the only thing I know how to do is to tell you I believe you are capable of getting through this. If there's anything more you need, please let me know what and I will try to offer it to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T20:05:45-07:00","id":245786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=245782#post245782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Camilla and cerealkiller, I am sorry for the difficulties you are both going through. I wish I had something intelligent to say here, something that would make everything better, but that is not one of my skills, and the only thing I know how to do is to tell you I believe you are capable of getting through this. If there's anything more you need, please let me know what and I will try to offer it to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your support, I do appreciate whatever support you can offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T00:26:54-07:00","id":245925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=241206#post241206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Az, what happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Suicidal ideation became a thing my brain wouldn't let go of, to the point that I was afraid I was going to do it the quick and messy way. I had a plan, the tools I'd need and even a secondary plan as a failsafe in case someone managed to call an ambulance before I could bleed out. I was terrified, and death itself wasn't nearly as scary as my mind had and has become.<br /> <br /> I'm really trying to cope and be productive and a boon to the people around me, instead of a burden, but part of me is just treating my efforts as a protracted prelude to checking out permanently. I just want to make someone happy, and know that I left the people I care about with some fond memories before I cash my chips in. That plan is still there, being polished to perfection by my own demons for the express purpose of ending my life. I want, no, I fucking NEED to get that idea in hand and push it from the forefront of my mind. I know it will hurt people, and I don't want to hurt anyone. I don't want to die without getting a chance to live first.<br /> <br /> I need to apologise to a few people in particular for my recent lapse into this downward spiral. They were in no way at fault for my weakness. Ive fucked some things up already because of this bullshit, and I'm so sorry that it's got me twisted up inside even more.<br /> <br /> Just let me tell one more good story and hear the words &quot;I love you&quot; from someone, even if they're lying. Let me survive this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-01-2014, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T06:36:14-07:00","id":246115,"title":"","content":"Joey, are you talking to your doctor about this shit? Because if you're still feeling like this despite all the meds you're on, I think something in your drug cocktail must need adjusting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T20:53:00-07:00","id":246605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=246115#post246115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Joey, are you talking to your doctor about this shit?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if you're still feeling like this despite all the meds you're on, I think something in your drug cocktail must need adjusting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. The Neurontin is either not helping or exacerbating my depression rather than easing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T21:04:35-07:00","id":246608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=246605#post246605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish you would.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T02:58:39-07:00","id":246729,"title":"","content":"Seconded. You should do it, buddy. Let people help you, that's not you it's chemicals playing dirty tricks on your mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:54:50-07:00","id":249367,"title":"","content":"I feel like a fuck up. I had a job interview today, I had applied at this game store months ago and had forgotten about it completely.They called today asked me to come in for the interview at 6, since i was sure it was part time work I said i'd be there. I get there and shes asking me the standard interview questions and I'm so fucking nervous I kept stuttering and tripping over my words like a fucking idiot. (Oh did i mention a majority of this job will be talking to people?) She asked for my resume and I totally wanted to smack myself as I FORGOT to print it, in fact i was so shocked by getting an interview my resume didnt even cross my mind *Sighs* So we finished up the interview and I promised to bring my resume in tommorow so she can review it...I'm not holding my breath that I'll get that job.. I looked incompetent and like I couldnt speak correctly...I wasnt looking for a job and yet i'm super pissed that I feel like I failed miserably. I hate my anxiety, I'm always nervous at job interviews but i've NEVER tanked one so badly...Why did I even go all it did was make me feel upset cause i'm a failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T07:00:37-07:00","id":249753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=249367#post249367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like a fuck up. I had a job interview today, I had applied at this game store months ago and had forgotten about it completely.They called today asked me to come in for the interview at 6, since i was sure it was part time work I said i'd be there. I get there and shes asking me the standard interview questions and I'm so fucking nervous I kept stuttering and tripping over my words like a fucking idiot. (Oh did i mention a majority of this job will be talking to people?) She asked for my resume and I totally wanted to smack myself as I FORGOT to print it, in fact i was so shocked by getting an interview my resume didnt even cross my mind *Sighs* So we finished up the interview and I promised to bring my resume in tommorow so she can review it...I'm not holding my breath that I'll get that job.. I looked incompetent and like I couldnt speak correctly...I wasnt looking for a job and yet i'm super pissed that I feel like I failed miserably. I hate my anxiety, I'm always nervous at job interviews but i've NEVER tanked one so badly...Why did I even go all it did was make me feel upset cause i'm a failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a few deep breaths and have a cup of Irish Coffee before you go back. Try to relax about it and take the opportunity to speak with the manager again when you take in the resume.<br /> <br /> And remember that it's a <b>game store</b>. Most of the staff probably has some kind of social anxiety/phobia/disorder. You'll be in good company.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And I'm fully aware that telling someone who has anxiety to calm down is a bit silly as it makes it seem simple. It's as simple as you make it, but I know it's not easy to make it simple. Savvy? Try anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 09-05-2014, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T07:06:37-07:00","id":249760,"title":"","content":"Papa Bear has good advice. Everyone screws up; hating yourself for screwing up is hating yourself for not being perfect, and while I can sympathize with it (because it's all I do all I day long), I can also testify it's a pretty great way to make oneself miserable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T13:18:26-07:00","id":250084,"title":"","content":"thanks papabear and jimb <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm feeling alot less shitty about it after some sleep, however now i'm having motivation issues in getting myself to get dressed and actally go turn the resume in..it 95 degrees outside and i'll have to walk a mile to go do it...that combined with my remaining anxiety over it is making it difficult for me to drag my ass off the couch get dressed and go. I dont handle the heat well, the walk isnt so bad i did it yesterday with no problems much to my surprise, but a long walk in long sleeves in this heat ew. I have to wear long sleeves cause I dont wish to possibly be turned down for a jbo cause of my obvious self harm scars (its happened before.) I could just carry the shirt with me and put it on before i go in but eh i'd still have to walk...<br /> <br /> This lack of motivation already doesnt bode well if I do get the job... maybe i should just wait untill i get back on my meds first after all i cant exactly work the first week i start new meds i'm usually unable to stay awake and cant even do anything for hte first week of new meds, and i start them in ten days*sighs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T15:18:43-07:00","id":250177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=250084#post250084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thanks papabear and jimb <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm feeling alot less shitty about it after some sleep, however now i'm having motivation issues in getting myself to get dressed and actally go turn the resume in..it 95 degrees outside and i'll have to walk a mile to go do it...that combined with my remaining anxiety over it is making it difficult for me to drag my ass off the couch get dressed and go. I dont handle the heat well, the walk isnt so bad i did it yesterday with no problems much to my surprise, but a long walk in long sleeves in this heat ew. I have to wear long sleeves cause I dont wish to possibly be turned down for a jbo cause of my obvious self harm scars (its happened before.) I could just carry the shirt with me and put it on before i go in but eh i'd still have to walk...<br /> <br /> This lack of motivation already doesnt bode well if I do get the job... maybe i should just wait untill i get back on my meds first after all i cant exactly work the first week i start new meds i'm usually unable to stay awake and cant even do anything for hte first week of new meds, and i start them in ten days*sighs*</div> </div> </div> </div>OR.....you could just get up and do it without the meds to show the docs you're not as messed up as they want to tell you that you are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Carry the shirt, wander on over there, throw on the shirt fast and walk in like you own the place. It's a GAME STORE. You've probably funded the place for a week by now. Goodness knows I've spent enough at my FLGS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 09-05-2014, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T15:45:05-07:00","id":250185,"title":"","content":"okay I was gonna edit my original post when i got back but someone replied lol so i'll say this anyways : Just woke up me is a complete total unmotivated mess and shouldnt be allowed to post...I just got home from taking in the resume. I couldnt find my long sleeve shirt so I said screw it and wore a sun dress so i wouldnt melt on the walk there. It wasnt SO bad a walk actually and felt really nice, the lady was busy so I just smiled kept my head high gave her my resume, thanked her for the opportunity and left.<br /> <br /> I soooo badly want to do this without meds i really do, I DO NOT want to go back on them if I can avoid it! And papa bear that is pretty much what I did, I got off the couch out the blue and went &quot;fuck this, i'm not going to pass on an oppertunity cause my brains being a dick to me, i'm doing this.&quot; got dressed and left without giving myself the chance to back out. <br /> <br /> I feel so happy I did it, i know if i hadnt regardless of if i get it or not i'd be pissed at myself for being such a lazy coward. <br /> <br /> <br /> Papabear, its not that kinda of game store sadly(I would kill to work in an RPG store, like seriously), just video games and magic cards, though they do have a bin of D-20s on the counter for sale(I need to buy some one of these days my cat lost all my d-20s x.x), but either way video games are not something i'm unfamilar with lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T16:03:13-07:00","id":255629,"title":"","content":"Increasingly feeling like suicide is the only rational solution.<br /> <br /> I'm 180 grand in debt thanks to medical school. I do pretty well when I'm seeing patients - I feel competent and able to make a contribution. But I'm currently four weeks into a six-week study period for a retake of a licensing exam, my performance is still shit no matter what I do, and unless I can figure out a way to pass I'll have no prospects.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T17:20:12-07:00","id":255675,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry things are so hard, Cielle, and if I had any experience with what you're going through, I'd offer the advice I had to give. Is there nothing in the way of, of coaching (I can't think of the word I want) to help you isolate what you're doing right when visiting patients and apply that to the areas where you need improvement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T17:58:13-07:00","id":255690,"title":"","content":"The stuff being tested is different. Let me see if I can explain by analogy.<br /> <br /> Do you remember when you were first learning to drive? If your state was like mine, the first step was getting a learner's permit through a written test. I still remember the tone of some of the questions - &quot;how much distance does it take for a truck to reach a complete stop&quot;, &quot;what reduction in speed is appropriate for a rainstorm&quot;, stuff like that. At this point driving is pretty much automatic for me, and I've managed to avoid any accidents. I don't remember any of the figures and numbers I memorized for that stupid test, though, because none of it turned out to be relevant. It's like that.<br /> <br /> So I'm infuriated that - having just spent the previous six weeks in a clinic seeing real patients - none of the stuff I actually needed to know is being measured. Everything I'm being asked is far more granular and far more difficult to remember and far less useful, and I need to pass this stupid fucking test, or else I'm going to be deep in debt with no prospects and I don't know what the hell I'm going to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T11:30:05-07:00","id":259068,"title":"","content":"So.Much.Anxiety. <br /> <br /> <br /> I need more vicodin....otherwise i'm not sure HOW i'm going to be able to shove the syringe into the tiny little hole in my gums caused by an abcess to flush it out 3-5 times a day. My dentist did it this mornign to show me how to do it, and oh my fucking god did it hurt.I hadnt taken my vicodin before i left for the emergency appointment and flat out refused to have a needle stuck in my mouth to numb me. (Just the thought of the needle nearly had me jumping from the chair and fleeing the office as quickly as i could) I'm super anxious....<br /> <br /> I dunno if the lamictal and vistaril are making this feeling worse...i just know the vistaril which is supposed to help with anxiety aint cutting it, the vicodin however if i take enough of it makes me not give a good goddamn enough i think i'll be able to do what needs to be done.<br /> <br /> My anxiety is at an all time high...I want to curl into a ball and cry I am so so sossos sick of abcesses and health problems at this point and am starting to get scared of seeing doctors unless there is painkiller being prescribed.... I'm tired of antibiotics and the nasuea they bring with them i'm tired of feeling run down or in pain with no explanations as to why this is happening.<br /> <br /> I'm supposed to be trying to get better mentally but for fucks sake how am i supposed to do that when as soon as one painful problem clears up another takes its place and makes me hate my life?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T03:07:34-07:00","id":262740,"title":"","content":"ceralkiller- I dont know you, but oi've seen your posts I just never knew what to say, otehrs said it all. I hoep that you are alright.<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ __________________________________________________ ___________________<br /> <br /> managed to stay awake for 14 hours straight today new record for the week! Between starting the lamictal and the vicodin(which i've been out of for 2 days but no longer need so yay!) I was sleeping most of the day and was mind numbingly tired to the point even staying awake 2 hours was an acomplisment.<br /> <br /> I have however been anything but plesant, to put it short I have been A TOTAL BITCH all day, and constantly picking fights cause i've been cranky, and nothing short of irrational(luckily that was a quick mood swing for hte most part) ;&gt;&gt; hopefully in a couple weeks this shit levels out cause my moods are bouncing around like crazy and I cant do much cause I cant focus worth shit, we tried gaming today and it went &quot;whats your character doing?&quot; *stares off into space while holding my mouse, and for a moment tries to minimize my living room cause i didnt find it an appealing window to look at,anymore.* Yeah caught myself on that and wondered if i'm spending to much time on my computer if i'm thinking i can ALT+tab reality haha...but the rest of the session i was so distraacted, EVERYTHING BUT THE GAME kept my attention, the cat, the shiny of the dice(which by the way i had to ut back in their bag so I could attempt to focus) the video game on my laptop...I can handle single player games but with other people I just cant do it, to many voices to much movement i just cant do that much right now.<br /> <br /> I cant read the book i've been wanting to read cause my mind wont let me focus on the words long enough or something distracts me *slams face against desk* <br /> <br /> I dunno it i like this new medication BUT i know its the &quot;adjustment phase&quot; and i juwst need to give it a few weeks.. blegh..<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">The only constant mood that hasnt left today is how misrable i feel....I feel like nothing ever changes..I will never change i will always be this bitch who hates everyone and yells and throws tauntrums over nothing get unreasonable and phsyically violent over NOTHING... I will never amount to anything, I cant get a job, i can barely leave my house...I will never be anything, I know i'm not alone but I feel like I should be i shouldnt be allowed to be around peole, I should not be allowed to have children as badly as i want them as I surely will fuck them up or damn them to live with this dreaded curse that runs in my family. HOW COULD I DO THAT TO A CHILD? How selfish does it make me to want to bring a child into this mess of my life? How dare i even allow myself to think I could be a good mother, a good wife, a decent person...I'm not those things. I'm fucking a waste of space doomed to drag everyone and everything I care about down with me...How is that Okay? Why do I hurt so bad? This isnt fair.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T20:57:12-07:00","id":279341,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to see the truth. It's terrifying, but I can't avoid it. I can't deny who and what I am. I can't save myself. I can't save those who will face me. I think Oppenheimer stood in both stark wonder and growing fear of his own impact as he quoted the Bhagavad Gita. I don't think I can be afraid of myself anymore. I don't matter. I'm not a person. I always doubt that someone could mistake me for one, but am continually surprised. I'm tired. I'm not playing anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T21:17:10-07:00","id":279369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=279341#post279341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to see the truth. It's terrifying, but I can't avoid it. I can't deny who and what I am. I can't save myself. I can't save those who will face me. I think Oppenheimer stood in both stark wonder and growing fear of his own impact as he quoted the Bhagavad Gita. I don't think I can be afraid of myself anymore. I don't matter. I'm not a person. I always doubt that someone could mistake me for one, but am continually surprised. I'm tired. I'm not playing anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joey, never, ever trust anyone who's trying to tell you what the truth is. That includes yourself. Anyone trying to tell you the truth is trying to get something out of you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T01:20:08-07:00","id":279444,"title":"","content":"why why is NOT smoking so hard? I quit for TWO WEEKS..then had to go visit my mom and grandparents yesterday and they smoke like chimeys and there was so much drama i got so stressed out I bummed 3 smokes off them while i was there(I had to...I was going to scream..I just wanted to go home and curl up there were ten people there and i'm NOT close to my mother or that side of my family so it was just plain uncomfortable for me....on top of that my sister was the one who gave me a ride and she and her friend fucking smoked pot WHILE DRIVING with the windows up and a BABY IN THE CAR wtf....then on the way home my sister whom threw a fit about having ot take me home(oh drama) had a couple drinks FIRST, drove 80-90 mph oh the freeway, and again smoked pot WHILE Driving and texting while taking me home... I have not been so freaked out in a while i saw cops on the freeway and kept PRAYING they'd pull us over cause i'd rather wait on the side of the road for my boyfriends mom to come get me then to have to sit in that car anymore....(She should be glad I Dont know her friends name it was her friends baby in the car with us my sisters baby was with its dad, or i'd call CPS cause that shit is WRONG...I dont care if you cracked the windows, i have no problem if you want to smoke pot but YOU DONT NOT DO IT WHILE DRIVING WITH A BABY IN THE CAR..i dont give a flying fuck if you &quot;Cracked the windows&quot; its not okay...and i swear if i go to my nieces birthday party and my sister picks me up and has my niece in the car and does that shit I WILL call CPS and report her ass, driving under the influence is illegal and i will not let a child suffer for her stupidity.)<br /> <br /> I&quot;m trying to find a polite way out of her daughters first birthday party cause my sister will be the one to come pick me up for it...and I do not want to get into a car with her again.... But no matter what I do I&quot;m going to come out the &quot;terrible sister who skips her nieces birthday party&quot; my family will be mad at me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I DONT WANT THIS STRESS IN MY LIFE... I wish I could just NOT be involved with that side of my family...But noooo they dont take hints...I RARELY call, make excuses to not go see them and yet still they dont get it. I dont feel like i belong, they dont &quot;get me&quot; they dont get I dont like family gatherings, small talk(Seriously i dont want to talk about the weather...and we share no interests so i have nothing to talk to them about), and being around people for hours at a time, adn would rather be at home. To them that is &quot;not normal&quot;.<br /> <br /> Today I bought a whole pack of smokes cause i'm still stressed out so badly. I Feel terrible cause i've smoked nearly all of it...I keep trying to tell myself &quot;Stop its not good for the baby&quot; then i end up smoking and getting all sad cause I cant fucking just put it down...<br /> <br /> I'm so emotional lately....more stable not as agressive(Which is a godsend ) but crying more and bouncing all over the place emotionally..<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T02:16:01-07:00","id":279461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=279341#post279341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to see the truth. It's terrifying, but I can't avoid it. I can't deny who and what I am. I can't save myself. I can't save those who will face me. I think Oppenheimer stood in both stark wonder and growing fear of his own impact as he quoted the Bhagavad Gita. I don't think I can be afraid of myself anymore. I don't matter. I'm not a person. I always doubt that someone could mistake me for one, but am continually surprised. I'm tired. I'm not playing anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are a person. A nice person on top of that. Everybody does wrong things from time to time or takes bad decissions that may hurt others, the difference being the intention. I don't, what's more I refuse to, believe you are consciously being malicious in any way to anyone. I'm not denying you are in a lot of emotional pain, but you have to understand is not your fault. You are not the one to blame.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to pretend to know what you are going through because that would be both a lie and presumptuous. I wish I could give you some place of comfort in this hard times, that is true. I will only say this, I consider you my friend and you can count on me giving you as much help as I can mustter. We care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T01:20:04-07:00","id":280713,"title":"","content":"I haven't posted in these forums much, mostly due to time constraints and not knowing anyone, but also a bit of unfriendliness from the old time White Wolf forums. I figured I'd make a post here though, since you guys all seem to be open and understanding. Give it a shot and all that. I feel like I'm hanging on by a fraying rope over a meat grinder that keeps taking off chunks of my wellbeing. Every time I get something figured out, another thing falls to shit. And some things, I never get a handle on. I am not trying to be melodramatic, this is how it's always been, it's just that usually, I don't talk about it because most people don't want to know that your life is a ruin. They want to chat about something asinine and then move on to their concerns, at least in my experience with real life socialization. I alternate between states of being these days, namely feeling hollowed out, or vibrant and full of life, or extremely sad. The main thing keeping me sane at this point is a combination of chain smoking and music. I have finally started to shake off and deal with my past, and now it looks like my future hangs by a mere thread. I have moved on from Montana where I grew up and had so many bad experiences to Washington state, but now am dealing with a string of shitty room mates and the potential of being homeless. I have no one to stay with if I should get evicted, which, we got our &quot;final warning letter&quot; today, because my current batch of room mates won't stop throwing loud parties every friday. I've tried talking to them and it's like the teacher voice in Charlie Brown to them. I don't currently have the money to move and even if I did, am in a year long lease agreement for this place. I've failed out of DigiPen so many times from depression, poor time management skills, and lack of tutoring that I have only one more semester to prove myself, at Bellevue Community College, or I lose my funding from Voc Rehab. I dreamt of being a game designer, but have yet to produce much of substance and seem to be unable to convince the design dept. at DigiPen that I can succeed. I've taken out many loans to get myself set up here, and am barely eking out a living on disability. I tried reaching out to the support groups on facebook for others with my conditions, namely schizoaffective and aspergers, but all I've gotten from that so far, for the most part, is disdain apathy or outright hostility. I have a support network, but only two of them are truly reliable, my best friend and my aunt. And they are both super busy, leaving me to mostly fend for myself these days. On the upside, I've done a lot of growing up in the last couple of years since hitting 30 and have more self awareness than I have in the past, as well as more self sufficiency. I am honestly trying my best, telling my room mates no more parties, getting a tutoring job in english to make ends meet, and &quot;putting myself out there&quot; socially though it is somewhat agonizing most of the time, to try and meet people and maybe even have a relationship. To paraphrase Sir Ken Robinson's Do Schools Kill Creativity?, I lived most of my life in my head and slightly to one side. I am now trying to round out my self and achieve my goals, but it never seems to be enough, like for every thing I do successfully four things go way out of wack. I don't know what to do a lot of the time, with my career goal, how to accomplish it. I am on meds with undesirable side effects, but no doctor trusts me to try tapering off of them. The worst though is the isolation, most people from any walk of life and with any world view that I've previously tried to establish rappoir with do one of three things: blow me off because I don't matter to them, look down on me or vilify me when I'm not around and make me a social pariah. I sometimes have trouble believing my life is anything more than a sick joke, with the punchline being when I die. It's been a rough couple of months, that's for sure, what with my &quot;friend&quot; from the aspie groups spewing hostility at me, my best friend being hostile and pissy, and smaller things have been eating away at what shaky peace of mind I have, like having a dream where I wanted to call my mom only to realize she'd been dead for almost two decades. I feel out of place in the world, almost constantly, and it seems what advice I can glean from other people has backfired in my face most of the time. Perhaps I should try meditation? I just don't know what to do, I think self reflection and discussion with others is a good start though. Sorry if this is TMI, please let me know and I'll delete it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T04:14:21-07:00","id":280820,"title":"","content":"[10/13/2014 3:10:24 PM] Kat(Not) Into Space: I already act as a prophet of Nasuverse at WoD forum and correct casuals<br /> [10/13/2014 3:10:41 PM] John Snow: Kat that's because you're insane<br /> [10/13/2014 3:10:54 PM] Kat(Not) Into Space: never denied I am<br /> <br /> Pretty much while I'm legit insane I embraced my condition and I'm happy about it. Just posting here to declare this. I'm not ashamed of my functional autism, workaholism, OCD tendencies and certain dose of overblown ego.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:45:56-07:00","id":281159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=280713#post280713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this is TMI, please let me know and I'll delete it.</div> </div> </div> </div>nah, there's very very little that most of the people around here consider TMI, no need to worry much about that. Some paragraph breaks would be a good thing though, wall-o-text is wall-o-text.<br /> <br /> Overall there's not a lot we can do but listen...which we are happy to do. I do think you're onto a good idea with meditation, I find it useful myself in dealing with issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T21:56:55-07:00","id":287253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=279461#post279461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice, supportive things! Hugs! Care and friendship! Did I mention I'm supportive and friendly? FEEL MY PALPABLE CARE FOR YOUR WELLBEING!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, buddy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was, and really still am, in a very dark place. I don't know if I should have posted at all while in that death-grip of emotion and fractured thought. I hope I didn't worry you. I am currently not a danger to myself or others, despite being in a loop of unwanted thoughts involving my violent demise and that of others. It's like I can't shut those thoughts out. I sicken myself.<br /> <br /> The more I fight the images and feelings filling my mind, the worse they get. I'm constantly on edge. I don't like being mean to people. I dislike human suffering as a rule. These are true statements. I thought about graphically murdering at least ten people today. I ran each scenario through my head until I was nauseated. I've cut most communication with people completely. I won't leave my house.<br /> <br /> I try so hard to be a kind person. I'm afraid of myself. What the fuck have I done to my soul that I'm thinking this way from morning to night and even onward until dawn?? Some part of me hopes to be shunned by humanity with such finality that I can walk away and forget that I once walked on two legs.<br /> I feel like I'm sinking into some atavistic survival mode.<br /> <br /> I wish killing myself wouldn't hurt my family and the people I care about. The world would be better off, and so would I. I genuinely feel that, in an almost overwhelming spiritual way. Is my mind being fucked by my unresolved childhood abuse issues and various chemical imbalances and/or deficits? Probably. That's what is keeping me alive: Doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 10-20-2014, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T02:15:48-07:00","id":287358,"title":"","content":"My knowledge about how medical care works where you live is pitifully meager, and specifically how to deal with mental health problems is even slimer. Isn't there some sort of treatment or medication they should be providing you? I'm afraid to know the answer and it makes me really mad when people are left in the mud because some swines want to fatten their wallets with a few more hundreds of bucks.<br /> <br /> Glad to know you are not endagering anyone and, most important, yourself. What you call doubt I'll call hope but as long as it's keeping you around semantics can go fuck themselves <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:24:34-07:00","id":287658,"title":"","content":"Hi people.<br /> <br /> I\u00b4ve read some of your posts. Many are sad, and seem really desperate.<br /> I\u00b4m not a pro in mental health. I have my own troubles with mental health from time to time.<br /> <br /> First off - I hope you all are able to see a doctor / therapist. If not I hope you are succesful soon. <br /> <br /> Many people I\u00b4ve read here are describing more or less severe of depression also many seem to have also a comorbidity with other illnesses like severe (social) anxiety.<br /> <br /> Second off - ackowledge that your sick and that is not your &quot;fault&quot;.<br /> <br /> One of the main issues of depression is the intersection of inabilty to act/demotivation/sadness and high moral standards / perfectionism. These two highly interact. &quot;I can\u00b4t reach my goals - I feel like scum because I\u00b4m a bad person, because of this I can\u00b4t be good person.&quot;<br /> <br /> You all are doing a great thing in articulating your pain - it does not matter if it\u00b4s here or with your diaries or a friend.<br /> Sickness taints your social/mental behaviour. That\u00b4s bad - but that\u00b4s also normal. I know it sounds like little relief. (Insert broken-leg-is-bad-for-running analogy) here.<br /> This means that thaughts like &quot;people hate me&quot; &quot;I\u00b4m a toxic person&quot; &quot;I\u00b4m unable to make friends&quot; are all symptons of sickness.<br /> <br /> Third off - Relax about the fact that your &quot;normal&quot; seeming family members / friends or even therapists are often unable to cope in depth with your sickness.<br /> Not all are able/willing to hear your story or the fill get &quot;fed up&quot; that you don\u00b4t &quot;get your act together&quot;. Many therapists are the same!<br /> <br /> Social Anxiety: You are role players!<br /> Play the situation! Like for real: Create an Alter Ego: &quot;Marc, who is capable of failing a test without making it himself failure.&quot; Alter Egos are powerfull tools of your personality and roleplaying made you a pro in fleshing out Alter Egos! Lady Gaga and others are good examples of this.<br /> <br /> When you are able to laugh - laugh! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Alsways Remember Folks: Depressed people have one of the best homoristic talents in the world.<br /> <br /> *Hugs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T12:43:30-07:00","id":287937,"title":"","content":"Ah, &quot;Fake it till you Make it&quot;, yeah, alter egos are great advice. Be careful, though and remeber to drop the act when is no longer neccesary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T23:16:37-07:00","id":288371,"title":"","content":"I'm taking the medications prescribed to me, though they seemingly have little to no effect. I see a psychiatrist once a month. The second to last time I saw my psychiatrist, I begged for some relief from my racing thoughts, and even said the words &quot;I don't want to be the next James Holmes! Some guy whose mind just breaks and then I hurt people that I care about or strangers...&quot; and he bumped up my dose of benzodiazepines and added Ambien to my nightly regimen.<br /> <br /> The next time I saw him, instead of his usual suit and striped tie, he was wearing a Hawaiian shirt and a pair of jeans. He informed me that he had been fired and that I would need a new doctor. He wrote some multiple-refill prescriptions for my medications and then I was out of there. I'm now looking for both a psychologist/psychoanalyst to reassess my mental health, a psychiatrist for my medication management, and a therapist for...well, therapy.<br /> <br /> The intrusive thoughts haven't been too bad today, but they're getting a bit more bothersome as it gets later... I want to be drunk right now. I want to just drown my mind in numbness. That feels cowardly to say, but it's honest. I'm stoned right now, as I seem to be most days and nights lately. It's just medicinal marijuana, but there lies the problem. It's not enough. It helps, but I'm still feel like I'm being torn apart inside.<br /> <br /> No mood stabilizer at this point. I tried two more, and they both made me feel like I was drunk or in the early stages of Alzheimer's disease. I quit smoking recently. I'm not sure how I feel about it yet, but we'll see. It's been about a week so far.<br /> <br /> \u200bThanks for caring. Really, thank you. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T02:04:21-07:00","id":288423,"title":"","content":"Well, what a mess. I thought they'll take this things more seriously, is not like you have a common cold for G+d's sake! Kudos on the quiting smoking, though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T09:14:26-07:00","id":290543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=288423#post288423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, what a mess. I thought they'll take this things more seriously, is not like you have a common cold for G+d's sake! Kudos on the quiting smoking, though!</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd think so, wouldn't you? But no, apparently telling my psychiatrist that I'm afraid of myself and directly referencing a recent mass murderer wasn't enough to worry him. I started smoking again for a day...or however long this pack lasts. After that, quitting again. I don't even enjoy cigarettes....it's just that my nervous system has felt so stripped down and raw that I needed a buffer.<br /> <br /> I'm still trying to find a new psychiatrist. I'm treating myself with street drugs and over-the-counter medications in near overdose amounts lately, and I'm scared. I'm scared to live as much as I'm scared to die.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T05:18:50-07:00","id":291204,"title":"","content":"I don't usually talk about my mental health any more than to be flippant about it... but I've slept 40 of the last 72 hours, and spent the rest on the verge of screaming and/or crying, so maybe it is time that I try something new.<br /> <br /> If only I knew where to start.<br /> <br /> It is very complex, but the short version is that I have a chronic pain condition (I don't know for sure which one, but I match the majority of symptoms of fibromyalgia) that has gone undiagnosed for over half my life because when I started to feel pain non-stop my parents told me it was normal, everyone feels pain and they just have to work through it, which at first made sense because I had suffered some injuries and those could have just been residual aches. But when I never stopped feeling pain, their constant &quot;it's normal. You're fine.&quot; and insistence that I didn't need to see a doctor left me feeling like they were telling the truth and I was just being a wimp and whining about nothing.<br /> <br /> That this is the short version has just become sad to me... anyways, I got heavy into drugs and alcohol so that I didn't have to feel the pain or sort out the feelings in regard to my parents' responses to my complaints. I've been clean and sober (excepting a few drunken nights here or there) for about 8 years now, and the pain has gotten worse and worse over those years, compounded by getting less active jobs because the pain made active jobs (which I had enjoyed the whole time I was strung out) too difficult, and then I gained weight, and the pain worsened, so I did less, gained more weight, and feel stuck because the pain is too much to push through in order to get some exercise and lose some weight to, hopefully, have less pain.<br /> <br /> Through all of that, I've also been diagnosed with bipolar disorder, though I tended to be more frequently manic, and I've avoided medicating because I don't like the person that I am on medication because, while it does take away the lows that I hate, it takes away the highs that I've come to enjoy... but even that is potentially just a side effect of the constant pain I am in, with my mania simply accompanying the days on which I am having less pain.<br /> <br /> And now, on to why I am currently locked in the lowest low that I've had for years:<br /> <br /> A few days ago my mother, who lives out of state but owns the house my girlfriend and I live in and keeps a room here so that she can have somewhere to stay when she comes to town and visits my sister, niece, and nephew, decided to express her concern for my current state - which she does every time she comes to visit, whether I want to talk or not - and the result was the two of us yelling at each other, ending the &quot;conversation&quot; in tears, and not having spoken to each other since.<br /> <br /> I expressed for the first time in my entire life the way that my mother makes me feel, which is to say that I feel like she has never believed a single word that I have ever said, including that she doesn't believe that I am even in any pain, and that the way she talks to me makes me feel like she thinks that I am just lazy and using any excuse I can to avoid basic responsibilities.<br /> <br /> I told her how her constant insistence of &quot;You are so stubborn, you never even try any suggestions that people give you,&quot; reinforces my belief that she doesn't believe anything I ever say, specifically that I <i>have</i> tried all of the suggestions that I am telling her didn't work (note: I've never said &quot;doing that <i>won't</i> help.&quot; but only ever &quot;doing that <i>didn't</i> help.&quot;) and she just isn't listening to me because she is too busy thinking of what she is going to say next to actually hear anything.<br /> <br /> I'm so fucked up about it all that I actually feel guilty for getting upset at her for the way she makes me feel.... meanwhile, she has had a nice chat with my girlfriend to clarify that my mom (and I guess my dad too, since the word used was &quot;we&quot; rather than &quot;I&quot;) isn't upset with her at all, <i>just me</i>.<br /> <br /> Because, you know, that's normal - be upset <i>at</i> your bipolar son that is telling you the reason that the house isn't quite as clean as you would like it is because it hurts just a little too fucking much to clean any more than he did.<br /> <br /> It won't bring him to tears. It won't make him want to yell so loud the walls rattle the next time he speaks to you. It won't at all cause any issue for you to be upset <i>at</i> him for not being the one in control of what he can, or cannot handle doing in a day.<br /> <br /> ...and yeah, that is the short version. I guess the shorter version is this: I am so fucking wrecked emotionally right now that I am considering rounding up all the booze in the house and having a one-man party morning, even though alcohol makes my pain dramatically worse once it wears off... the 2, maybe 3 hours of not having to fucking deal seems almost worth the 1 or 2 days of barely being able to stand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T19:12:14-07:00","id":293354,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> so many people i know are struggling in their lives, my dad told me he had another stint in the hospital he didnt hurt himself this time but was thinking about it and admited himself so he wouldnt...and a few of my friends are struggling in their lives as well and people i dont know well are hurting and it saddens me I cant do anything to make people not hurt...I just dont know what to say, or how to be supportive..I've never been good with people, all i can manage is to say i'm sorry, or that shit will get better or to just listen... It pisses me off that i dont have any skill with communicating enough to say something that may make someone feel better...but hten again expecting that I can magically make someone better with a few words is stupid...<br /> <br /> I sometimes hate that I secretly give a shit about people...(Outwardly in person i'm a world hating, selfish bitch who &quot;Cant stand anyone&quot; and barely speaks. but in private and online where i feel safe being myself i actually express i give a damn... well thats not entirely true a few rare people see i care in person but that list in TINY.)<br /> <br /> It stresses me out and makes me want to shut my internet down and pretend the world doesnt exsist so i dont have to see the suffering of others I cant help.<br /> <br /> This is entirely stupid isnt it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T19:42:40-07:00","id":293357,"title":"","content":"Nah, human nature. We're built to empathize and care about each other.<br /> <br /> It might not be the greatest of consolation, but things are at least looking up. Employment is slowly but steadily climbing in the US, and in terms of global conditions a higher percentage of the worlds people are getting the basic needs met than at any other time in recorded history.<br /> <br /> Things might get better for someone, they might not, but overall there are positive signs for the world. And if you don't accept the good things, and just focus on the negative you just end up in a never-ending spiral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T20:20:22-07:00","id":293367,"title":"","content":"I'm not up to date on current events so i wasnt aware things were getting better in the US so that at least is something..I just see the bad stuff on the news all the time hardly ever any good stuff. I try to see the good and just see shit, people treating others like shit for no reason, people dying unemployed homeless etc and its just so friggen sad to me. <br /> <br /> I just want people to be happy, but yes i am TRYING to see some positives but its difficult... I'm not usually this caught up about this kinda of stuff..but fuck I'm worried about people, the future, the state of the country(i dont follow politics but i hear things from time to time from people who do that scare me and make me wonder what kind of world i'm bringing my child into, or what his/her future could be like) I so badly want others to see the positives in life to cause even in the sadness their is something positive in that...but i'm always told by people close to me thats a stupid thing to say, that sadness is crap and shouldnt be considered a positive aspect of life. I'm fucking strange and i'm rambling, i'm in an odd mood right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T21:12:18-07:00","id":294511,"title":"","content":"Since my last post, things have gone from bad to worse...I am doing my best to rectify the situation but it doesn't seem to be enough. I've been having severe shoulder pain for about a week now, luckily am getting it checked out tomorrow, but between that and other shit my roommates have pulled(like locking both doors to the upstairs shower bathroom from the inside so I had to take off a doorknob just to take a shower, breaking various appliances in the house, eating my food and stealing construction signs to nail up in the living room), I'm nearing the end of my rope. I talked to some friends from facebook and they had me talk to the apartment manager, which went ok, except that I learned that to get away from these shitty roommates I have to have all 3 of them sign off on me leaving the lease, and I know they'll try and extort a bunch of utility money and stuff that I just don't have before they'll do that, not to mention that I don't know where to go...<br /> <br /> Because of all that, I missed the last few weeks of classes at Bellevue college. And am up to two packs a day. Then, I lend my best friend 100 through &quot;Walmart to Walmart&quot;, only to find that he's been charged with domestic violence and is in jail... He has been having anger problems but I've never seen him hit a woman. SO, he got out today and says that his gf made up the charge to get him arrested. Then I haven't heard from him since. So much stress. Just feel like collapsing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T07:07:48-07:00","id":294791,"title":"","content":"This is the FOURTH time I've tried to post this before accidentally erasing everything. Wish me luck?<br /> <br /> @Thorbes @Scelesta @JimB @PapaBear @Eldagusto @cerealkiller<br /> <br /> I'm checking myself into a residential psychiatric facility for a while (probably a few months or more) for my own safety and the safety of others. I need help. I still have to talk to a psychiatrist and my insurance provider, but it's happening. I won't be going for a few days to a week, so I'll try to message back and answer my phone until then. <br /> <br /> Phone: 1-505-316-0715<br /> Email addresses:<br /> <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#294048444d4c485d41594548404748474d5a404459454c694e44484045074a4644\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"a6cfc7cbc2c3c7d2ced6cac7cfc8c7c8c2d5cfcbd6cac3e6c1cbc7cfca88c5c9cb\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> <br /> <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#98f9e2eaf9fdf4fef1eafdebecf7eaf5d8f0f7ecf5f9f1f4b6fbf7f5\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"6e0f141c0f0b0208071c0b1d1a011c032e06011a030f0702400d0103\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a><br /> <br /> Skype: morningsidekiller1<br /> \u200bFacebook: Joey Polanco","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T09:01:51-07:00","id":294900,"title":"","content":"Thanks for letting us know, that's very considerate of you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> See, you are a nice person.<br /> <br /> I supose kudos are in order, though it seems strange to congratulate someone on being interned, but I'm glad to know you are on your way to get the help you deserve.<br /> <br /> I have abosultely no idea how the policies on contact are in those places, would you still be able to actually check on your mail from time to time?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T10:54:34-07:00","id":295001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=294900#post294900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have abosultely no idea how the policies on contact are in those places, would you still be able to actually check on your mail from time to time?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Contact with the outside world is generally very limited. Internet access isn't usually readily available. The same goes for telephone access. In most cases, one has to have previous written authorization from the patient for anyone to contact them.<br /> <br /> Basically, this means that if you might want to call me you'll have to let me know in advance and if you email or otherwise digitally message me, it will likely be read to me aloud while on the phone. Actual mail will be delivered as normal, but part of me wonders if the art of writing a letter is dead. I hope not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=294900#post294900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I supose kudos are in order, though it seems strange to congratulate someone on being interned,</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the second part of that sentence was the caring and positive part, but I just wanted to let you know that the mental image of me telling you that I'm committing myself to an institution <i>followed immediately by a mutually happy and enthusiastic jump-up-and-slap-skin High Five </i> made me smile. It's the little things that count. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, I've called my psychiatrist and my insurance company. Everything seems to be working as it should. I have an appointment with my doctor for a referral to a hospital in a few weeks, but I'm trying to expedite the process by directly contacting a few facilities and enquiring about possible openings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 10-28-2014, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T13:30:52-07:00","id":295147,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you're getting help, Joey. Seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T13:31:06-07:00","id":295149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=295001#post295001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I've called my psychiatrist and my insurance company. Everything seems to be working as it should. I have an appointment with my doctor for a referral to a hospital in a few weeks, but I'm trying to expedite the process by directly contacting a few facilities and enquiring about possible openings.</div> </div> </div> </div>A little suggestion from someone on the inside.....checking the facilities for empty beds, unless they' already told you which ones they might refer you to, could end up being a waste of time. Not all facilities will take all insurance companies, so someone that has an empty bed might not take your BlueCross and only take Aetna. I know it's a few weeks out, but expect to be given a (short) list of where you can go.<br /> <br /> Now, on the flip side, ask about the <i>entire program</i> when you're calling those places, not just whether they can get you in any time soon or not. Find out everything you can about how they do things, so when you go in, you can tell your doctor about some of the programs you're heard about that sound appealing to you. Do they have follow-up programs for out-patients? Do they have both behavioral health and chemical dependency programs? Dual diagnosis? Standard length of stay? 30 days? 60 days? Psychiatrists on staff or are they only there on certain days (which probably means they're on loan from somewhere else)? Are they going to start you off in the padded room for evaluation first or are you going straight into a regular patient room? Will you have to share the room?<br /> <br /> Lastly, keep use posted as best you can. Keep your cool. Listen to the docs and therapists. Learn from the other patients. Someone there is bound to be more screwed up than you..........no, really, there's always one. The sooner you learn to deal with it, the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T13:56:48-07:00","id":295173,"title":"","content":"I hope you do well, Azrael. God be with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T09:33:58-07:00","id":295931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=294511#post294511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since my last post, things have gone from bad to worse...I am doing my best to rectify the situation but it doesn't seem to be enough. I've been having severe shoulder pain for about a week now, luckily am getting it checked out tomorrow, but between that and other shit my roommates have pulled(like locking both doors to the upstairs shower bathroom from the inside so I had to take off a doorknob just to take a shower, breaking various appliances in the house, eating my food and stealing construction signs to nail up in the living room), I'm nearing the end of my rope. I talked to some friends from facebook and they had me talk to the apartment manager, which went ok, except that I learned that to get away from these shitty roommates I have to have all 3 of them sign off on me leaving the lease, and I know they'll try and extort a bunch of utility money and stuff that I just don't have before they'll do that, not to mention that I don't know where to go...<br /> <br /> Because of all that, I missed the last few weeks of classes at Bellevue college. And am up to two packs a day. Then, I lend my best friend 100 through &quot;Walmart to Walmart&quot;, only to find that he's been charged with domestic violence and is in jail... He has been having anger problems but I've never seen him hit a woman. SO, he got out today and says that his gf made up the charge to get him arrested. Then I haven't heard from him since. So much stress. Just feel like collapsing...</div> </div> </div> </div>I....don't really know what to say except hoping that the future will hold many good fortunes for you....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T11:15:10-07:00","id":296013,"title":"","content":"I think at the very least, you need to have a serious discussion with your doctor about the efficacy of your medicine, and to be extremely assertive in that conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T18:21:23-07:00","id":296359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=295149#post295149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A little suggestion from someone on the inside.....checking the facilities for empty beds, unless they' already told you which ones they might refer you to, could end up being a waste of time. Not all facilities will take all insurance companies, so someone that has an empty bed might not take your BlueCross and only take Aetna. I know it's a few weeks out, but expect to be given a (short) list of where you can go.<br /> <br /> Now, on the flip side, ask about the <i>entire program</i> when you're calling those places, not just whether they can get you in any time soon or not. Find out everything you can about how they do things, so when you go in, you can tell your doctor about some of the programs you're heard about that sound appealing to you. Do they have follow-up programs for out-patients? Do they have both behavioral health and chemical dependency programs? Dual diagnosis? Standard length of stay? 30 days? 60 days? Psychiatrists on staff or are they only there on certain days (which probably means they're on loan from somewhere else)? Are they going to start you off in the padded room for evaluation first or are you going straight into a regular patient room? Will you have to share the room?<br /> <br /> Lastly, keep use posted as best you can. Keep your cool. Listen to the docs and therapists. Learn from the other patients. Someone there is bound to be more screwed up than you..........no, really, there's always one. The sooner you learn to deal with it, the better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I was told this, not verbatim but close, by my mom this morning. More on this morning in another thread. Thanks for the helpful advice, PB. I haven't met my new psychiatrist yet (old one got fired), but if things get worse I'll do an emergency intake into the acute unit at the hospital. I'm not risking my life anymore. Fuck that. It wouldn't be the first padded room I had to stew in. Unless I'm an immediate risk, intake at the local hospital before transport to long-term is pretty easy. It's just a lot of waiting with your ass hanging out of a hospital gown while random security guards and nurses give you the Ol' Hairy Eyeball from time to time..<br /> <br /> I'll try to keep you, my friends, posted as well as I can. Feel free to contact me if you feel like talking, even if we don't know eachother too well, or at all. I could always use a new friend or two!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=295173#post295173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope you do well, Azrael. God be with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, man. Also, I totally forgot to include @Prometheus878 in the Keep In Touch, Please list. My bad!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 10-29-2014, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T13:04:11-07:00","id":298377,"title":"","content":"The person I know rants and raves at people a Skype chat over a fictional character he adores. I mean, it has gone more serious than mere waifuism, he really needs therapy or he will lose the grip on reality completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that ther