</div> </div> </div>Long story. I'm not suicidal. I might be psychotic, though. If that's the case, then I'm confused because <i> I thought people weren't able to tell when they themselves have gone crazy. </i><br /> <br /> I want to go away from this place. What's the world when every part of your being would rather be in another world with ostensibly much less hope?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T21:23:47-08:00","id":310870,"title":"","content":"I have been over-medicating with my benzodiazepines and diphenhydramine for a few weeks now, to blot out the hardest parts of the day with a blank spot of semiconscious nothing. I'm sleeping as much as possible, and in my head (lost in the Other, the place that isn't real to you) or just trying to keep it together.<br /> I don't know what to do. I notify my doctors, appropriate family members and friends that I NEED to be hospitalized and then.... they all just tell me to wait. Seriously, telling a doctor that I was having intrusive thoughts of violence and homicidal ideation didn't so much as raise an eyebrow. I've been retreating from the world and myself, and I'm not sure I can stop. They say that wherever you go, there you are. Fuck that. I can lose myself, and be free. So long as you're truly lost, you can never be found. Freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T08:34:31-08:00","id":311320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=310870#post310870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, telling a doctor that I was having intrusive thoughts of violence and homicidal ideation didn't so much as raise an eyebrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, your providers BLOW!<br /> <br /> That shit raises RED FLAGS around here and if they can't get someone in to a clinic ASAP, then they recommend going directly to the hospital. WTF!!???!!!?!?!?!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T09:20:10-08:00","id":311349,"title":"","content":"Seriously, Papa Bear has the right of this one. Unless you actually used the word &quot;ideation&quot; and they think you're faking it, but even then that's not an excuse so never mind. Go to the hospital. Let them sort it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T14:20:50-08:00","id":311649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=311320#post311320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, your providers BLOW!<br /> <br /> That shit raises RED FLAGS around here and if they can't get someone in to a clinic ASAP, then they recommend going directly to the hospital. WTF!!???!!!?!?!?!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hardly an expert but did live with someone with mental issues for a few years, and yes these are indeed the red-flag keywords that doctors, hospitals, police and others use for various effect. And while I personally think they a bad way of filtering the extremity of the various cases and reactions, it does sound like you need an independent evaluation. Purely opinion, YMMV, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T14:25:54-08:00","id":311651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=310870#post310870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been retreating from the world and myself, and I'm not sure I can stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a true story, though the timing is so convenient I won't blame you if you don't believe me.<br /> <br /> Today has been a bad day. The kind of bad where I'm thinking about all the reasons I should just be dead and I'm reaching for the knife in my car to start cutting myself, and only don't do it because the effort of opening its container seems too exhausting to follow through on. Doesn't matter; that's just background. The real story begins when I'm in the right-most of four lanes, waiting to make a right turn on an overpass. The stoplight is red, but there are trucks in the left two lanes that I can't see around, so I decide to just wait for the light to turn green.<br /> <br /> After a few seconds, I notice the guy behind me is gesturing angrily at me, which leads me to understand that sound I'd been hearing, which had been blending in with the brass section on a song on the radio, was actually his horn. I guess he could see around those trucks from behind and wanted me to go. I didn't feel very much like pulling into traffic on his say-so that things were okay, though, so I ignored him and just kept waiting until the light turned, which it did, as lights tend to do. I was only there for maybe half a minute.<br /> <br /> The third turn is mine, at a Chinese restaurant that used to be my favorite and that is now next to a Panda Express. I feel like supporting the Chinese restaurant, so that's where I go. The guy is following me, but nothing about that strikes me as worrisome or interesting, so I continue to ignore it. I find a parking spot, put on my jacket, get out of the car, and start walking up the parking aisle to find the guy has pulled around to where the aisle ends as is waiting for me with his window open.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're a fucking asshole,&quot; he says.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thank you,&quot; I tell him, and my voice expresses perfectly well how much I care about this wanker's opinion on anything as I keep walking toward him (or rather, toward the restaurant behind him).<br /> <br /> &quot;Man, I should get out of this car and whip your ass,&quot; he tells me.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am terribly sorry you had to spend thirty seconds of your fucking life sitting still in your warm car,&quot; I tell him, and he seems to take offense at this. Perhaps he could tell I was lying about being sorry and it upset him that I would lie to his face.<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't make me get out of this car and kick your fucking ass,&quot; he suggests, and at this point I am in the grip of conflicting emotions: one is a craven desire not to escalate things, and the other is a cold rage (those of you who've been around long enough know I am extremely impatient with bullshit) that knows full well anyone who has to threaten you twice doesn't have the balls to do anything.<br /> <br /> &quot;Either get out and do it or grow the fuck up,&quot; I advise him, still walking. I'm very near his passenger door now.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck you,&quot; he says, and drives off, still yelling things at me I can't hear because the wind catches most of them.<br /> <br /> I'm home now. It's twenty minutes later, and only now has my heart rate slowed down and my hands stopped shaking. It was a frightening experience, a potentially dangerous experience (he could have had a gun for all I know, and been evil enough to use it), and more, I deliberately tried to make it worse; but I enjoyed it so.<br /> <br /> Fucking.<br /> <br /> Much.<br /> <br /> Seriously. I can't tell you how much pleasure I took in this exchange. I stood up for myself to a bully, which is always nice, but I think the bigger part of it is that it got me out of my own head for thirty seconds and put me in the real world again.<br /> <br /> I can't recommend going out and picking fights with people the way I did, but seriously, I am riding high on the wave of what it feels like to get out of your own head, and if you can spare the time, I really recommend it. It's pretty fucking cherry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T20:14:58-08:00","id":311879,"title":"","content":"One of the triggers for my depression is exhaustion. I'm also an introvert, so social interaction exhausts me. I'm lucky enough to have a job that has me sleeping less than four hours a night and interacting with many, many people on a daily basis. But this is the only/best job I can find at the moment. I constantly feel like shit and there's nothing I can do about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T21:05:16-08:00","id":311912,"title":"","content":"What kind of job dictates your sleep schedule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T21:06:59-08:00","id":311915,"title":"","content":"A job in the hospitality industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T21:22:28-08:00","id":311932,"title":"","content":"I know nothing about the hospitality industry, and have only the most vague possible understanding of what it even is (either concierge or a euphemism for prostitution? Probably not that second thing, though), but even so, what resources does your job offer you in order to keep you at your best? Sleep deprivation leads to shoddy work in any field and from any person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T21:26:14-08:00","id":311935,"title":"","content":"The only resources that are offered would be polite scheduling (not scheduling me on a shift that gets me home at 11:45PM and has me waking up the next day at 5:00AM). Beyond that I just have to &quot;suck it up&quot;. And sleep deprivation? We're all supposed to be insane workaholics who never sleep and can only think about working more. Anything less is pure laziness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T21:50:22-08:00","id":311948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=311932#post311932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know nothing about the hospitality industry, and have only the most vague possible understanding of what it even is (either concierge or a euphemism for prostitution? Probably not that second thing, though), but even so, what resources does your job offer you in order to keep you at your best? Sleep deprivation leads to shoddy work in any field and from any person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally anything dealing with people from catering to hotel clerks to bank tellers to tour guides.<br /> <br /> And unfortunately while the number of jobs is going up in the US (and elsewhere) the quality of work available and pay is going down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T01:55:27-08:00","id":313568,"title":"","content":"....Stressed the fuck out.<br /> <br /> I have to learn to drive...not optional since we can only (hahahahhahahahhaha we really cant) afford one car it will need to be left at home with me so i can do stuff during the day like appointments, shopping etc... I dont know how we are going to manage that as the only person who has a car and could teach us is unreliable, and a TERRIBLE teacher(she panicks every two seconds, and thinks driving in circles in a parking lot while she plays on her cell phone not talking or instructing is perfectly okay, and if she does instruct its to freak out that you hit the breaks to fast or turned to sharply *Rolls eyes* and there is no fucking way we could afford drivers ed for both of us i looked the places out here want like 1500 bucks a person... Never mind the fact I have anxiety about driving like super bad anxiety to the point i'm not even sure I can learn to drive... Then theres the oh so lovely issue of money...always fucking money... money for the Learners Permits(for both of us), then money to take the drivers test, then money for the drivers licenses, and then the damn money for a reliable car that isnt going to break down and need a ton of work in a month.....and then finally car insurance...(we are not counting gas for each month either hahahaha) HOW are people who live pretty close to pay check to pay check supposed to do this shit? We simply dont have a choice anymore the person who usally gives us rides has become even more unreliable...We need to get a car because frankly i dont want to have to rely on her anymore, being able to get to my own appointments without freaking the fuck out cause she cant seem to ever show up on time isnt worth it anymore, that and she likes to drop a person off then &quot;forget&quot; to tell them she zero intention of picking them up till 2-3 hours after their appointment ended as &quot;She didnt feel like leaving the house untill she went to go get so and so from work&quot; WTF.<br /> <br /> Oh and then ON top of all this we need to come up with the money for a marriage licencse, and the money to pay some stupid court clerk to marry us(i'm not fucking wasting money on a wedding at this point i dont care that fucking much at this point pretty white dress and all that crap would be nice but its unrealistic when you're getting married JUST before a baby is born and have a limited income.) OH BUT WAIT cant do that untill like 2 weeks before the babys born(and then conviently forget to report the change in status to DHS till after the baby is born), cause any sooner and I will loose my health insurance and food stamps which we rely on to live... Fucking system sucks what makes them think calculating if we qualify by the money we make BEFORE taxes is realistic(they do realize that thanks to taxes we see so much less money each money and thus need assistance for food right? dumbasses)<br /> <br /> I dont like this...We need to get stuff for the baby and all this stuff which is expensive is popping up... I dont like this not at all. I hate this kind of stress, Can a nice car or van just please magically appear in my parking spot with a cute note saying its a gift as that is the most expensive thing i need to get...Maybe its time i find a part time job for a couple months cant get to many hours or yet again i'll loose my health insurance which i really need right now and even with a part time job couldnt afford even the cheapest plan if i dont qualify for the state insurance i am fucked... I just need to work a couple months (maybe 3-4 at most) to save up a bit of cash to buy a car then everything else can just happen. OH BUT wait cant do that till i shit money to replace my expired ID yano cause once its past its expiration date i'm no longer that person and it cant be used as legal ID (seriously what the hell is up with that?)<br /> <br /> RANT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T02:42:03-08:00","id":321603,"title":"","content":"I am somewhat looney disfunctional combat veteran. Yes, I have serious mental health issues and they are not getting better. I have been in therapy for 9 years. I take it one day at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1090-tobias","name":"Tobias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1090_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T05:21:10-08:00","id":321703,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your service, Tobias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T19:02:08-08:00","id":324948,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your support!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1090-tobias","name":"Tobias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1090_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T20:29:03-08:00","id":325023,"title":"","content":"Least I can do. I'm not a fighter, but I should respect the people who are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T06:48:16-08:00","id":325971,"title":"","content":"Grieving is hard <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My hamster died yesterday morning and while i knew it was coming eventually(she was old for her breed) I didnt realize how unprepared i was for it. I made her a coffin, burried her with her favorite treats...then went to the pet store..I know ot some that may seem...bad taste, but I had to, just seeing the empty cage, and siting in the living room and NOT hearing the small sounds of a hamster moving around that i was so used to hurt so bad i started crying everytime i noticed. <br /> <br /> The new hamster is a sweetheart, and a different breed then my last one...BUt she is not my Minipants, and while i already love my little Atti, it still hurt when i woke up this morning thinking yesterday had just been a bad dream and went to say good morning to my Mini, only to see a totally different hamster in her place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In order to lessen the pain I moved the cage from its old spot, but seeing the empty spot on the shelf saddens me even though I SEE The cage sitting on my coffe table now.<br /> <br /> Its been a long time since i'm lost a pet to death, and i'm hurting. My heart feels heavy and i have no idea how to get over the loss.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yes some people i know will say its stupid to be sad over something that when you got it you KNEW was going to die in a year or 2..but she was a family member to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T07:24:58-08:00","id":325998,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://cdn0.sbnation.com/imported_assets/1025947/cal_hobb-raccoon6.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Sorry, Scelesta. It just takes some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T01:58:33-08:00","id":332061,"title":"","content":"deleted for whininess","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 12-06-2014, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T01:23:51-08:00","id":333933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wWY69mTr5gM\" data-code=\"wWY69mTr5gM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wWY69mTr5gM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T15:15:11-08:00","id":334572,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T20:02:26-08:00","id":334772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=334572#post334572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It won't let me post a video for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure you need to delete the S at the end of https. Also, good to hear from you, man. How you been, apart from being blitzed?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T13:55:07-08:00","id":335453,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T14:39:42-08:00","id":335490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=335453#post335453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medical bills climbing faster than my student loans because the place I was Baker Acted into wont send the bill to the police department. I don't feel that I should be responsible for the amount seeing as I was forcibly interred.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sucks. I wish I had some insight on the money front, but I'm afraid I don't except to suggest you do what you've probably done already and call the hospital's social worker to ask about financial aid. On the health front, though, how are you feeling since your release?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T17:02:01-08:00","id":335585,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T17:51:05-08:00","id":335607,"title":"","content":"Kick ass! Sounds like things are going your way, at least in the long term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T17:56:25-08:00","id":335610,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T12:01:35-08:00","id":338231,"title":"","content":"Copy-pasted from my Facebook page, because JESUS CHRIST I DON'T WANT TO TYPE AGAIN FOR AT LEAST AN HOUR!:<br /> <br /> Wow. My new medications are genuinely giving me little bouts of fugue or something like amnesia. I've been told of conversations that I had TODAY that I genuinely don't remember. I've posted and said things to people recently that I don't even find out about til later! I feel like a blackout drunk, without any of the fun of merrily getting drunk. If I've sent a weird, overtly violent and/or sexual text, email, or the like in the last two weeks, lemme know. If it was before that, I probably did it on purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:16:13-08:00","id":338342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=338231#post338231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My new medications are genuinely giving me little bouts of fugue or something like amnesia. I've been told of conversations that I had TODAY that I genuinely don't remember. I've posted and said things to people recently that I don't even find out about til later!</div> </div> </div> </div>That uh, that seems troubling. Have you mentioned that to your doctor?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T15:17:52-08:00","id":338496,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Az, that is a really troubling side-effect. I second what Jim said, contact your doctor asap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T04:36:45-08:00","id":338932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=338496#post338496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Az, that is a really troubling side-effect. I second what Jim said, contact your doctor asap.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DlerL6y2h7c\" data-code=\"DlerL6y2h7c\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DlerL6y2h7c/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> My doctor has been notified, but hasn't discontinued the medications nor changed dosage. I have a history of sleepwalking, and the doctor along with my family seems to feel the same. I've been in a serious funk lately, beyond the memory blanks. I'm getting ready to play some VtM, and that's good, but when I'm away from my group and my hobby, I'm just in a haze.<br /> <br /> I daydream. I think obsessively about morbid scenarios. I'm hiding more and more behind chemicals. I've smoked marijuana every day for about the last ten years. I've been a smoker for half my life. It's sometimes the only balm for my pain. The only thing that works.<br /> These days, it's just an appetizer. It helps me wash down a mix of downers that I scrounge up to drop out of life for brief periods. I use booze when I can. I get less shit for drinking, and it's legal so people tolerate it to a point.<br /> My problem is that I just want to keep going. Buy another bottle? Why not?! I'm trying to live in a state of numbness, so I can smile and pretend I'm not broken. I say when I can, because I don't go out or drive, so my liquor is usually picked up for me. That tends to speed up people noticing you have a problem.<br /> Now my crutch has shifted to pills. Been forced to take the things all my life, so it's pathetically poetic. Benadryl, Valium, Klonopin. Over the counter or prescription, I'm starting to use pills for whatever whenever. I'm nodding as I type this, high on oxycontin. My left eye is drooping shut and I'm making a dopey face like a drunken duck. I might as well be on heroin.<br /> I'm intellectually aware of this. I don't know if it's morally wrong or right, a simple happy experience or simply a waste of time. Am I hurting someone? Am I hurting myself? Don't I own myself? Can't you do whatever you want with what belongs to you, so long as others aren't endangered?? People bungee jump. People drive cars. Am I just finding ways to excuse my behavior? I don't know. It's possible.<br /> <br /> I'm lonely. I feel like everything and everyone that I love is drifting away from me. I don't want to lose my best friend. I don't want to lose people that I would take a bullet for. I would. I would protect my gaming buddies with my life. They're my brothers and sisters. Gaming has saved me from a broken home, transformed a life of dysfunction into one where I can still dream. I want to hold you close, and be part of the story we're all living. Are you playing the way you expected? Do you feel cheated, or like you might be cheating? Who do YOU think is telling the Story? Is there a story here?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't that be fun..?<br /> <br /> Shout out to my peeps:<br /> <br /> JimB, the moogle with the mostest, may he be forever awesome<br /> Papa Bear, friend of lost cubs, may his heart, head and bear butt find peace and rest. May his cubs flourish.<br /> Scelesta, my friend and muse, who may yet find out where I left my heart<br /> Telgar, the best badger-friend I've ever had, necromancer and badass who makes pretty things.<br /> Prometheus878, my partner in a plot to take over north America and western Europe. Steal the flame! Freedom!<br /> Auron, the LightMaguz, my favorite person to argue with.<br /> Cadmiumcadamium, who is a kind heart, a generous soul and NOT NORWEGIAN. I have problems, bro. I know you're Swedish.<br /> Niza, my cool new ST and friend. DUDE, POST MORE!/<br /> DanielPLanman, for being himself. Dude, you're the best pain in the ass I've ever had. Second best was when I first really learned how to stimulate my prostate.<br /> cerealkiller, for being my long lost brother. Sasquatch might be solitary creatures, but drop me a fucking line, asshole! I really want to talk to you.<br /> <br /> This might be the weed and stuff talking, but FUCK do I hate being single!<br /> I tried getting a bit close with a friend in a romantic way, but that ended up in an odd place and I'd hate to have my unsatisfactory love-life on their shoulders. I need a damn significant other. Someone to flirt with, to be silly with, and occasionally get frisky with.<br /> <br /> I'm 27, light-skinned, six feet tall, chubby, short dark hair, brown-black eyes and a killer grin. I do lift weights and I tend to wear nondescript dark clothes with cargo pockets. I'm not exactly turned on by tattoos or piercings, but I never mind if my partner has a lot of them or none at all. It's just a non-issue. If you have interesting stories about them though, I'm all ears. I like chatting with my partner, but I can enjoy comfy silence with a good book or snuggling.<br /> I'm usually the type to lounge around, but I enjoy the outdoors and camping. I'll pretty much play anything with you on a tabletop, anytime, provided it's not a TERRIBLE game. Also, I don't mind long-distance romance if you don't. I would expect meeting each other in person would be part of the plan if things go well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I'm very giving when it comes to oral sex. No idea why. I just enjoy making my partner feel good. I'm a cuddler most of the time, but I enjoy alone time and don't mind a partner that enjoys the same. I don't mind smokers. I know it's unhealthy, but I sometimes just find the image and social dances that someone having a smoke sometimes exhibit to be sexy. If you don't smoke, I'll live. It's not important. I smoke a menthol from time to time and medicinal marijuana. That's it. I like horror movies, random cute stuff and being weird. I'm bisexual, and I don't really have a preferred physical type. I generally am attracted to personally more than simple physical appearance, but being cute doesn't hurt. I'm one of those people that can find beauty in nearly anyone, provided they have the heart to look into me and try to see the same.<br /> <br /> Am I selling myself like a television infomercial host? Apparently, but I never seem to approach dating the &quot;normal way&quot;. Oh well.<br /> \u200b<br /> If you want to try to take a shot at dating me, just let me know!<br /> <br /> You know a bunch about ME, so you have the advantage. You're a mystery to me.<br /> <br /> Would you try dating me?<br /> COULD you try dating me?<br /> <br /> Are you apprehensive? A bit leery? I understand.<br /> <br /> But you know me a little now. You know what's wrong with me. You know what small perks I come with. You know my policy on pleasuring my sexual partners.<br /> <br /> I dare you to message me.<br /> I dare you to hit on me earnestly.<br /> You might be surprised.<br /> <br /> You might like me.<br /> <br /> Skype: morningsidekiller1<br /> Email:<a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection\" class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"b4ddd5d9d0d1d5c0dcc4d8d5dddad5dad0c7ddd9c4d8d1f4d3d9d5ddd89ad7dbd9\">[email&#160;protected]</a><br /> 1-505-316-0715<br /> <br /> I believe in love. I believe in fidelity and loyalty. I believe that we deserve to find some happiness.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, I basically put a personal ad in the Mental Health thread, because it's my home. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 12-13-2014, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T15:15:24-08:00","id":339475,"title":"","content":"So, yeah. Sober now. <br /> <br /> How is everyone? *smiles awkwardly and shuffles out of sight*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:17:09-08:00","id":339656,"title":"","content":"Doin' fine. How're you, embarrassment aside?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T03:26:58-08:00","id":339913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=339656#post339656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doin' fine. How're you, embarrassment aside?</div> </div> </div> </div> Good. Um, me? I greened out* at some point this afternoon and woke up about an hour ago. It's the middle of the night. My head is spinning like one of those tops that shoot sparks when they spin fast enough. Water is my friend. I must drink my friend. <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*Green Out: When a pot smoker has smoked a lot of weed in a short amount of time, or taken large hits of very good bud and passes out. Vision gets blurry, loss of hearing, and your balance gets so out of whack you don't know which way is up. This can happen with both newbies &amp; long time smokers.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T04:47:17-08:00","id":340718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=339913#post339913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=339913#post339913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Water is my friend. I must drink my friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear it's important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T20:03:25-08:00","id":341478,"title":"","content":"I Have to go back on my meds..at least one of them, I've been cleared to take lamictal again as its &quot;Safe enough&quot; to take while pregnant. I attacked my fiance yesterday during a severe mood swing, i wanted a smoke we didnt have money blah blah, he took away my cell phone cause i wasnt paying attention when he was trying to explain WHY we couldnt get smokes, and I just snapped and started screaming mindlessly and clawing at him untill he gave it back, at which point i returned to my spot on the couch and didnt say a word really that i can recall for a little bit before he said something that set me off again, this time i didnt get up but i did threaten that if he dared to leave the house that day i would sell everything i could and destroy what i couldnt ;&gt;&gt; <br /> <br /> I hate myself...i hate that i do things like that and have NO CONTROL at all over rather or not i can stop, i really cant, even with the voice in the back on my head telling me to stop and that i'm being unresonable, the rage is so much stronger, and the only sure fire way to end said rage episode is to physically attack him at which point i calm down enough to at least talk and not rage out again though threats still happen...<br /> <br /> I see my psych on the 30th. I'm scared to go on medication while pregnant <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But i dont think i have a choice if i cant controll this without meds when i'm not a hormonal mess then its going to get worse. When i was on hormonal birthcontrol a couple years back,my violent rages got so bad and so frequent we had cops called etc Once i stopped it i went back to only having a violent fit a couple times a month rather then a few times a week...Its just scary to me that I could seriously hurt someone and at the time not care. <br /> <br /> And the worst part is I still cant appoligize for my actions verbally, I never can bring myself to say &quot;I'm sorry&quot; even the next day when i'm calm again and feel so much guilt, because to say out loud i'm sorry is admiting how bad a problem this is...and i jsut want to pretend i'm not a fucking mess.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T20:36:12-08:00","id":341499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=341478#post341478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the worst part is I still cant appoligize for my actions verbally, I never can bring myself to say &quot;I'm sorry&quot; even the next day when i'm calm again and feel so much guilt, because to say out loud i'm sorry is admiting how bad a problem this is...and i jsut want to pretend i'm not a fucking mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to pretend I have the faintest idea what it's like to be in your situation, because I don't, and to do so would be insulting to you. But if you have so much trouble verbally expressing yourself, have you considered maybe trying to express your regret another way? Like (and this is way off the top of my head, I'm sure you can come up with better), shouldering some extra responsibility you wouldn't otherwise, like a minor chore or something? Or buying your partner a kind of gift? Or maybe even just something like a hug or something?<br /> <br /> Obviously you're going to have to come up with your own ideas, only you know what you're capable of and your particular situation. Just a passing thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T10:23:33-08:00","id":342069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=341499#post341499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not going to pretend I have the faintest idea what it's like to be in your situation, because I don't, and to do so would be insulting to you. But if you have so much trouble verbally expressing yourself, have you considered maybe trying to express your regret another way? Like (and this is way off the top of my head, I'm sure you can come up with better), shouldering some extra responsibility you wouldn't otherwise, like a minor chore or something? Or buying your partner a kind of gift? Or maybe even just something like a hug or something?<br /> <br /> Obviously you're going to have to come up with your own ideas, only you know what you're capable of and your particular situation. Just a passing thought.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually that is a really good idea! And maybe eventually i can work my way into verbally appologizing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T05:30:47-08:00","id":344594,"title":"","content":"Today I reached the point when I acknowledged to myself I literally don't care about strangers or people who are in my way or in way of those few people I care about. Frankly, my amorality is liberating and gives me reason to persevere now even in my situation.<br /> <br /> I turned my mind to steel and forged my hatred of the country and of those who are assholes to me into something that gives me purpose.<br /> <br /> As a sidenote, I have such a disdain for my country that if somebody invaded it I would not even think about it and collaborate with invaders since in my honest opinion my country does not deserve independence and should be ruled by superior countries. It's not even betrayal in my mind, just a natural thing to do. If some country liberates my country or I have a chance to move out to another country for good I'll be fervently loyal to my new overlords just because of spite. I preferably I would move to UK, so God Save The Queen in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 12-19-2014, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T01:57:17-08:00","id":345578,"title":"","content":"&quot;I feel lethal, on the verge of Frenzy.&quot; - Patrick Bateman, American Psycho<br /> =D<br /> <br /> &quot;Some men just want to watch the world burn.&quot; - Alfred Pennyworth, The Dark Knight<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i7FHVa2KQlU\" data-code=\"i7FHVa2KQlU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/i7FHVa2KQlU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Why not, right? You only die once, might as well be now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T01:36:13-08:00","id":348121,"title":"","content":"Life is never going to get better.<br /> <br /> The world is never going to get better.<br /> <br /> I am honestly fluctuating between thoughts of homicide and suicide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T05:24:09-08:00","id":348193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=348121#post348121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life is never going to get better.<br /> <br /> The world is never going to get better.<br /> <br /> I am honestly fluctuating between thoughts of homicide and suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way of looking at it, I suppose, is that you posted here. Which means you think posting here will accomplish something, either providing a useful way to vent, or maybe you'll get to share your feelings with people you have something in common with (170+ posts implies at least a casual connection). So, if we go with that hypothesis for the moment, unproven though it is, that might indicate that you think the people here are worth talking to.<br /> <br /> So, you know, that's something? Even if it doesn't outweigh all the bad, which I have no doubt is significant, it's one positive thing.<br /> <br /> It's how I get through the day, anyway. Find one good thing, and cling to it (preferably something I haven't clung to in a while), doing my best to ignore the bad I can't fix, and using it as a sort of mental safety-catch to help deal with the parts I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T13:14:59-08:00","id":351932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TfDVLsBXYcM\" data-code=\"TfDVLsBXYcM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/TfDVLsBXYcM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v3ZA-_kWGGc\" data-code=\"v3ZA-_kWGGc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/v3ZA-_kWGGc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 12-27-2014, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T14:46:53-08:00","id":351984,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T14:49:33-08:00","id":351986,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T06:52:45-08:00","id":352625,"title":"","content":"I hear you, 'killer. It's a rotten time of year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T01:49:46-08:00","id":354580,"title":"","content":"I wish I knew what the hell to say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I feel like i fucked something up big time. A friendship that i treasure is now so fucking awkward to me i worry if i pick up my phone and call i'll say something that may sound misleading or give them a false hope that what we are will become something more then friends.I feel flustered not knowing how to respond to texts or start a conversation or to talk about my life without feeling guilty that perhaps i should be talking to this person about these things as it doesnt seem fair when i know how they feel towards me...<br /> <br /> *sighs* tonights one of those nights where i just sit and think...and wonder if I gave this person false hope, only to break their heart...I feel bad because it was never my intention to hurt someone nor mislead, but i was going through a confusing time in my life when we met and well shit got out of hand and things were said that perhaps I should have asked to not be said, and conversations had that perhaps i should have said were crossing a line...I didnt set boundries and now its just...fucking strange. I dont wish to loose a friend but I dont know what to do or how to handle things. When someone I care about as a close friend says they love me and i know damn well they dont mean in the &quot;like family&quot; sense, it makes me sad because i dont know how to respond to that, I should but i dont. I'm not the type of person to simply say &quot;please stop saying these things, you know i'm getting married, and i have a baby on the way, and that i dont plan to leave him for you.&quot; without sounding cruel and worrying they'll never want to speak to me again..but on the other hand i wonder if space would be a good thing, and then i realize thats dumb cause I dont like loosing people from my life at all.<br /> <br /> My hormones make me a fucking mess on top of yano my general moodswings...so its not like i feel comfertable getting on the phone and explaining this stuff or sending a personal message which I should but i wont...i'd rather stick to pretending they are not going to see this, when i know damn well they will.<br /> <br /> Am i being a total asshole in the way i'm handling this? cause i feel like i am...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T02:37:32-08:00","id":354629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=354580#post354580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish I knew what the hell to say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I feel like i fucked something up big time. A friendship that i treasure is now so fucking awkward to me i worry if i pick up my phone and call i'll say something that may sound misleading or give them a false hope that what we are will become something more then friends.I feel flustered not knowing how to respond to texts or start a conversation or to talk about my life without feeling guilty that perhaps i should be talking to this person about these things as it doesnt seem fair when i know how they feel towards me...<br /> <br /> *sighs* tonights one of those nights where i just sit and think...and wonder if I gave this person false hope, only to break their heart...I feel bad because it was never my intention to hurt someone nor mislead, but i was going through a confusing time in my life when we met and well shit got out of hand and things were said that perhaps I should have asked to not be said, and conversations had that perhaps i should have said were crossing a line...I didnt set boundries and now its just...fucking strange. I dont wish to loose a friend but I dont know what to do or how to handle things. When someone I care about as a close friend says they love me and i know damn well they dont mean in the &quot;like family&quot; sense, it makes me sad because i dont know how to respond to that, I should but i dont. I'm not the type of person to simply say &quot;please stop saying these things, you know i'm getting married, and i have a baby on the way, and that i dont plan to leave him for you.&quot; without sounding cruel and worrying they'll never want to speak to me again..but on the other hand i wonder if space would be a good thing, and then i realize thats dumb cause I dont like loosing people from my life at all.<br /> <br /> My hormones make me a fucking mess on top of yano my general moodswings...so its not like i feel comfertable getting on the phone and explaining this stuff or sending a personal message which I should but i wont...i'd rather stick to pretending they are not going to see this, when i know damn well they will.<br /> <br /> Am i being a total asshole in the way i'm handling this? cause i feel like i am...</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't do anything wrong .<br /> <br /> You'll never lose my friendship.<br /> <br /> I respect that you're building a family and that your child and your longtime partner are your priorities, and a good friend would wish you nothing but happiness, love and good health and wellbeing for you and yours. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T12:27:17-08:00","id":355008,"title":"","content":"uh wow this is awkward as shit. I dont remember posting this last night...nothing weirder then logging in in the morning and seeing posts and PM's you made/sent while super tired and near sleep...I guess super tired me had a bunch of shit on her mind she felt like getting out.<br /> <br /> Thanks Az <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm not sure what to say right now...so i'll respond to your PM as soon as i finish waking up/get back from my appointment","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T19:15:34-08:00","id":356173,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about hurting myself. I won't say I'm having the urge to self-injure, as it's much more like the desire to change, like cutting your hair differently or getting a piercing or tattoo. Specifically, I'm becoming very focused on and fascinated by the idea of castration and penectomy. <br /> Some part of me feels that these organs have no purpose in my life. Another part of me feels that they are impure and should be removed simply to separate their filth from my sense of self. Yet another part of me is drowning in tears now, hollering and screaming til he's hoarse as he bashes the walls with his fists, lamenting his belief that he will never be loved. That he will never be a father. <br /> Piece by piece, and bit by bit, I realize the ugly truth of my existence. I'm the problem. All I know how to be is screwed up. The only place I fit are those places in time and in the world that men look back at and call Hell. In a dark alley, the frozen corpses of the less fortunate glued to the pavement as I walk past looking for trouble. The psych ward, in the Safe Room, laughing while I'm still bleeding because the nurse is screaming. In a war zone, torn and twisted bodies lining the streets while smoke and the echoing of explosions blots out the intermittent yelling and clatter of gunfire, a big blade in my hand as I walk to my doom. That's where I belong.<br /> <br /> \u200bI was invited to my neighbor's house a bit ago. I turned them down as nicely as possible. It was better than explaining that it's a bad idea to let someone who's drinking and having psychotic thoughts into your house..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T20:21:38-08:00","id":356187,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T22:05:50-08:00","id":356269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=356187#post356187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hate new years. everyone either comes over or goes out. this year everyone came over. I want them to go away. I just want to be able to sit on the back porch alone and take it easy but instead I'm holed up in my room because I'm so fucking sick of seeing everyone every fucking day that its driving me crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall having what I think were similar feelings back when I was in college. Along with some rather dark thoughts related to the theoretical concept of eliminating the stress sources.<br /> <br /> I can't offer much, but I can tell you it got a lot better after I moved far enough away that I would only see the more annoying members of my family every few months. It got considerably better when the main stressful people died and I moved a couple thousand miles away... they both happened at the same time, so I can't really pin which effect on which event.<br /> <br /> Can't really offer a lot to you or anyone else (AzraelFirestorm I am looking in your direction here) except to say that things can and will get better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T06:21:27-08:00","id":356592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=356173#post356173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm becoming very focused on and fascinated by the idea of castration and penectomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are very permanent procedures. I'd be sure, if I were you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=356173#post356173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm the problem. All I know how to be is screwed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a way, that's true, but I don't think you're using it in the true way. I suspect you're using it as an excuse to torment yourself rather than to recognize that you just have special needs, a certain learning disability when it comes to how to manage and maintain your own happiness that can be overcome with the proper medical assistance and instruction. And don't get me wrong, it's okay to do that; we all need to wallow from time to time. The important thing is that you know you're being dishonest with yourself and that, when it's no longer time to wallow, you get back to work. It will be hard, and it will be slow going, and you will fail many times (and those last three statements apply to pretty much any endeavor ever), but you can do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T14:03:13-08:00","id":356876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=356173#post356173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Piece by piece, and bit by bit, I realize the ugly truth of my existence. I'm the problem. All I know how to be is screwed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered talking to a therapist about these feelings? Their job is to help people figure out how to be less screwed up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T14:32:14-08:00","id":356933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=356876#post356876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered talking to a therapist about these feelings? Their job is to help people figure out how to be less screwed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have considered that, many times, in fact. Unfortunately, my psychiatrist has told me, quite firmly, that I shouldn't even seek a therapist until I'm chemically stable. I'm not, sure, personally, why he thinks it's a bad idea, but I'm not a doctor. I've just decided that the long-term future holds very little for me. No children, no career or creative outlet to show to the world that my life was not a waste of oxygen, food and water. I'm likely going to check out at 30, unless I have acquired some genuinely good reason to continue this pain-in-the-ass existence. If you find suicide morally abhorrent or some other squeamish, can't-deal-with-reality belief system has a hold of you, my bad. <br /> Forgive me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T02:05:21-08:00","id":358156,"title":"","content":"I can't see any escape to this nightmare of a Universe, none but death and infinite void.<br /> There is nothing but pain here. Pain, fear and deep moral depravity. Disgusting beyond belief.<br /> <br /> I want to go to a world where there is more than pain, where the pain that there is serves a purpose. I want to live without fear. I want to be in a place where evil may never tread.<br /> <br /> I want to be God. To forge a perfect world, as this world is not. I want to have the power to make things better, for everyone that is worth saving.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think it's worth living, if I have to serve forever in this Hell. But I can never be God.<br /> The only freedom is suicide, or insanity.<br /> Nothing else is worth anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 01-03-2015, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T21:46:55-08:00","id":358816,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, Kleptomania. I wish I knew the words to say that would take the burden off you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T04:28:09-08:00","id":359010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=358816#post358816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, Kleptomania. I wish I knew the words to say that would take the burden off you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's anything that anyone can say to remove that burden-...<br /> <br /> I think -way- too much for my own good. And it is impossible for me to see past flaws in the world.<br /> But I don't think this world can be fixed, and I don't think there is any hope for its redemption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T07:06:22-08:00","id":359095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=359010#post359010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's anything that anyone can say to remove that burden.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least not anyone who isn't a trained professional, who doesn't have the length of a proper course of therapy to commit to saying it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=359010#post359010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is impossible for me to see past flaws in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't, though. Our perspective is inspired by a mixture of our hardwired factory settings, our experiences, and our choices. Regarding that last one, if you are seriously discussing suicide, then I tend to suspect you have a neurochemical imbalance which requires medication to correct and therefore isn't especially subject to just being wished away, but nevertheless, a choice to forge a new perspective through seeking new, positive experiences and medical assistance is the first step of the healing process. It's also a choice only you can make, so I urge you to make it for yourself rather than embrace nihilism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 01-04-2015, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T09:48:07-08:00","id":359244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=358156#post358156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see any escape to this nightmare of a Universe, none but death and infinite void.<br /> There is nothing but pain here. Pain, fear and deep moral depravity. Disgusting beyond belief.<br /> <br /> I want to go to a world where there is more than pain, where the pain that there is serves a purpose. I want to live without fear. I want to be in a place where evil may never tread.<br /> <br /> I want to be God. To forge a perfect world, as this world is not. I want to have the power to make things better, for everyone that is worth saving.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think it's worth living, if I have to serve forever in this Hell. But I can never be God.<br /> The only freedom is suicide, or insanity.<br /> Nothing else is worth anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is, in truth, the closest thing I've ever seen to my own feelings written by another hand. Except...<br /> <br /> Your assessment of the situation has an additional block that I've removed in my own analysis: The preconception that one, namely you or me, cannot BE God. Removing that single notion opens up the other, much more immediately useful notion that if the world's morality is, in its entirety, corrupt, then so may be the power behind it. A bigger notion still, is that perhaps we are meant to find and destroy whatever God there exists, if he/she/it does. The major problem with this last is obviously, Who then will be God?<br /> <br /> If it weren't for a few very influential sources, I would never have found a solution that seemed to make up for the power vacuum.<br /> <br /> The answer is simple: Whoever eats him first, in his truest and most concentrated form. Ein Soph. This may very well prove impossible, but if the ALL is quantifiable and touchable, then nobody is going to stop me from taking a bite.<br /> <br /> You are what you eat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and Jim is probably right about the neurochemical imbalance and medication. I still felt that I needed to encourage Theophagy before I seconded that...<br /> <br /> Am I insane? Of course not.<br /> <i><br /> Everybody else is!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T08:11:00-08:00","id":360213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=358156#post358156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see any escape to this nightmare of a Universe, none but death and infinite void.<br /> There is nothing but pain here. Pain, fear and deep moral depravity. Disgusting beyond belief.<br /> <br /> I want to go to a world where there is more than pain, where the pain that there is serves a purpose. I want to live without fear. I want to be in a place where evil may never tread.<br /> <br /> I want to be God. To forge a perfect world, as this world is not. I want to have the power to make things better, for everyone that is worth saving.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think it's worth living, if I have to serve forever in this Hell. But I can never be God.<br /> The only freedom is suicide, or insanity.<br /> Nothing else is worth anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You don't want to be god. It is an implausible concept which cannot exist in a confirmed universe.<br /> <br /> There is more than pain here. That's where the Buddhists take the wrong turn. Life is what you choose to make it. If you think it sucks, change your mind until it doesn't. It's only as hard as you make it, and believe me, I know it's hard. I fight it every day.<br /> <br /> Someone without fear is someone with nothing left to lose. Fear is nothing to be afraid of - fear is a superpower. Fear can make you faster and cleverer and stronger\u2026 Fear doesn\u2019t have to make you cruel or cowardly. Fear can make you kind. So listen. If you listen to nothing else, listen to this: you\u2019re always gonna be afraid, even if you learn to hide it. Fear is like a companion. A constant companion, always there. But that\u2019s okay. Because fear can bring us together. Fear can bring you home. Fear makes companions of us all. (Thank you, Doctor)<br /> <br /> Evil is perspective which can be changed. Things are usually never that black &amp; white. Our stories often are written as such because they are what we wish the world could be instead of what it is.<br /> <br /> Suicide is not freedom. That's an illusion. No life is not freedom, it is the total opposite. It is permanent transfixion within an inanimate state. That's like saying a rock is free. Life is the only freedom as it is the only state in which you have options.<br /> <br /> Insanity is also not a freedom and another illusion. That is allowing one part of your body to decide everything else that's going on, whether real or not. That's like letting your liver decide if you can see a tree in front of you. The Cartesian duality is insanity. It separates the whole person into discrete parts, ignoring the whole person.<br /> <br /> It's not insanity to acknowledge that the universe makes no sense. It is, in fact, perfect clarity. The universe only has natural forces interacting with each other. Any other sense, order or patterns are man-made. Human brains are hard-wired to make patterns where there are none. We crave it, we need it, we believe that we cannot live without it and, to a degree, we are correct. We mad little humans could not go on without getting over the hump of &quot;universal forces do not a patterned universe make&quot;. You can check out of life if you can't deal with it, but as I've already said, I don't recommend it. You can MAKE your own patterns, decide what is important to you and live that way. Or you can simply acknowledge the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Absurdism\" target=\"_blank\">absurdity of the universe</a>, have a good laugh about it, and move on with the business of living.<br /> <br /> <br /> And that's my brain dump for the day.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 01-05-2015, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T08:36:23-08:00","id":360222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=356933#post356933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have considered that, many times, in fact. Unfortunately, my psychiatrist has told me, quite firmly, that I shouldn't even seek a therapist until I'm chemically stable. I'm not, sure, personally, why he thinks it's a bad idea, but I'm not a doctor. I've just decided that the long-term future holds very little for me. No children, no career or creative outlet to show to the world that my life was not a waste of oxygen, food and water. I'm likely going to check out at 30, unless I have acquired some genuinely good reason to continue this pain-in-the-ass existence. If you find suicide morally abhorrent or some other squeamish, can't-deal-with-reality belief system has a hold of you, my bad.<br /> Forgive me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, have you told your psychiatrist about these feelings? Because I would think any mental health professional would want to see them dealt with.<br /> <br /> I don't find suicide morally abhorrent per se. My impression, however, is that your situation is not unsolvable yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T15:44:49-08:00","id":361655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=360222#post360222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, have you told your psychiatrist about these feelings? Because I would think any mental health professional would want to see them dealt with.</div> </div> </div> </div>YES, I have. And yeah, you'd think, wouldn't you? Reality vs. How Things Should Be. Reality: 1, other guy, 0.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=360222#post360222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't find suicide morally abhorrent per se. My impression, however, is that your situation is not unsolvable yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that I have a distinct, seemingly unsolvable problem. It's that existence holds very little enjoyment for me. I catch what pieces of happiness I can, but scraps aren't worth this. I find confusion and discomfort everywhere, and the only clarity I find is in daydreams of places and things that don't exist, or in hatred and violence against my brother. I figure that the nice and helpful thing would be to get off the ride <i>that I'm clearly not enjoying</i> and give someone else my spot.<br /> I'm eating food, drinking water and living a life that someone else could do more with, or better with. I'm not a martyr, so they can fucking wait until I'm ready to go and have enjoyed what I could, but when I'm done, I'm checking out and you people can turn my room into an office or a home gym or some shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v3ZA-_kWGGc\" data-code=\"v3ZA-_kWGGc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/v3ZA-_kWGGc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 01-06-2015, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T17:19:52-08:00","id":363935,"title":"","content":"blegh my pdoc LIED TO ME. Said the new med wouldnt make me tired, and well i havent gotten out of bed in two days, been awake maybe 12 hours in 2 days as well. I feel funny and i dont like it..oh and the monster headaches its giving me are JUST GREAT! I have enough on my plate with pregnancy i dont need this shit making things worse for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> yeah..i'm not taking it anymore...I have somethinking to do anyways about medications, since from what i understand i cant breastfeedd if i choose to go back on the cocktail that actually works for me...and the idea of that plus the adjustment period where I CANNOT function for like 2 weeks while i get used to the meds again may mean i just need to learn to manage without medications and pray that it works out...or take an as needed medication rather then a daily. I simply wont have the luxary of not getting out of bed for two weeks while i adjust to the meds...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T20:09:56-08:00","id":364049,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T02:19:09-08:00","id":364183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=364049#post364049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as needed typicall turned into daily for me but addictive personality and that. be care with as neededs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeah i plan to be, as needed for me also ends up daily unless i have someone monitoring me and controlling my acsess to the meds..i'm stilll not sure what i plan to do though i have some time to figure it out i guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T02:22:10-08:00","id":364184,"title":"","content":"I get what you mean, 'killer. My clonazepam was four pills maximum a day, as needed for anxiety. That turned into four pills every day just to feel like I wasn't going to snap. These days it's 4+ pills a day, plus whatever I can get to numb myself. I'm functioning as much or more than my new usual, but I'm in nearly constant emotional discomfort and psychological torment. It's starting to be like one of those injuries that didn't heal, but instead was compensated for by the sufferer while it became gangrenous.<br /> <br /> I'm doing alright. This is true.<br /> <br /> I'm not doing alright, and I live in fear, cowering in the dark corners of my own mind because every monster in the endless world inside my head is Me as much as I am, and if they get me, they'll BE me.<br /> <br /> This is also true.<br /> <br /> I don't have much, but I have myself. I won't lose that. I refuse to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T06:31:30-08:00","id":367291,"title":"","content":"I don't know what's wrong with me anymore. I just know that something is.<br /> <br /> I have been completely unable to even live in and interact with the world around me, because it disgusts me so much. I have been depressed for longer than I can remember, so in those days where it seems to have 'passed over', I don't know what to feel.<br /> Depressed or not, I am disgusted with the World; This doesn't appear to go away.<br /> Depressed or not, I am deeply and hopelessly lonely: It doesn't feel saddening in itself, just frustrating and empty. It also feels vaguely-... Petty and mundane, for lack of a better word.<br /> <br /> Being able to admit that loneliness to myself has helped out some. I don't actually think I have friends anywhere close to me anymore, only acquaintances: The only real friends I have are so very far away and can be difficult to get in touch with.<br /> So, I don't have any friends to interact with on this continent.<br /> Additionally, I feel like I have convinced my family to hate me, or at least my Grandparents: This-... This actually really hurts, I was trying not to feel the pain, but this really, really hurts. They can't seem to comprehend the viewpoints I approach things from, generally because they are things that would assuredly get me institutionalised if I were only a little bit more vocal with them: So, they might now think that I am either insane or morally disgusting. Both of which are quite likely to be accurate.<br /> My dog is dying, of course, so that certainly isn't helping my mental state.<br /> <br /> When I started out writing I was only feeling empty, now I feel pathetic and sad again. So pathetic: I feel like the stereotypical young man, all 'No one understands me!'. And I suppose that's because I am that stereotype, though I have not uttered those exact words: Nobody, in fact, does understand me, not even me.<br /> My mind is like a labyrinth, with myself as the sad and angry Minotaur at the centre and all my family and friends as-... Well sacrifices, I presume, certainly not Theseus, because he actually found his way through; this metaphor has fallen apart very quickly.<br /> <br /> Oh, my psychiatrist recommended I take medication. But honestly, I'm not sure how depressed I actually am. I mean, my mental state is definitely not normal and I am oftentimes morose, angry and melancholy, but I feel like I am right to feel this way. The World is a horrible, horrible place right now and somehow I am convinced that someone needs to fix it. I -should- be angry, I -should- be wrathful, I -should- want to break something: Because there are some eight billion things out there in need of breaking.<br /> But part of me just wants to be happy, quiet and content and small and stupid and mortal. And I wish that this part of me would shut up and die already, so I can actually strive to be more.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, I just want to cry, but there aren't any tears anymore. I used them all up over eighteen years of misery. And it's not because I'm depressed that I want to cry now, it's because all of that anger and hatred is -justified- and there is nothing I can do about it.<br /> <br /> I probably need to be medicated. I probably need to be institutionalised.<br /> Maybe I just want someone to talk to who won't judge me.<br /> Maybe I just want to be left alone.<br /> Maybe I want to stop disappointing everyone.<br /> I need to stop feeling the pain, without feeling like I've given up.<br /> <br /> Wow-... That was a wall of text I ended up typing-...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 01-12-2015, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T07:23:36-08:00","id":369728,"title":"","content":"I'm fucked up recently. I'm holding it together, but it's hard. I have been prescribed 150mg daily of Zoloft. About 2.5-3 months ago, I started feeling shitty on a regular basis. So, without consulting my doctor, I started taking 200mg daily. That helped for awhile, but then I started feeling shitty again. So I went to see the doctor on Monday. He was not happy that I'd upped my dosage without consulting him, but, as my counselor pointed out, that's what he would have done anyway. So on Monday he changed my prescription. I'm now prescribed 100mg Zoloft daily and 37.5mg Effexor (to be doubled in a week's time) and a multivitamin and vitamin d. (Yes, he prescribed me vitamins.) This week has been shitty. I feel like I'm being dragged along and I'm not sure I am holding my shit together. I'm pretending to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T09:08:48-08:00","id":369788,"title":"","content":"It's stupid, I know, and about the same thing I usually recommend.<br /> <br /> Change one thought from negative to positive. Just one. Start there. When that one works, try another. One at a time.<br /> <br /> MINOR RANT: Too many people, especially in this country/culture, expect things to get done in big, grand, sweeping gestures. They don't want to take the 1,000 steps in-between to get to the goal. <b>But it's how the world works.</b> Evolution took millions of years. There are no missing links because it was such a slow transition that there isn't a single creature that could be pointed to as the spot between this animal and that one. The continents drifted apart over millions of years in such tiny increments that there were certainly animals fording 50 foot wide streams to travel from the west coast of Africa to the east coast of South America. The first creatures that could be identified as &quot;human&quot; had a good 10,000 year run as nomadic hunters before someone finally complained so much about their feet hurting that someone else invented agriculture just to shut them up. Even after that, many of them kept going in a nomadic style before finally settling down either thru choice or necessity. It's only been in the past 150 years that things have really gone all that fast from a human perspective. Don't try to fight millions of years of inertia with silly human perceptions.<br /> <br /> Change takes time. Modern culture and technology has fooled you into thinking otherwise. Breathe. One step at a time. You <i>can </i>do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T13:06:25-08:00","id":370051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=369728#post369728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, he prescribed me vitamins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Papa Bear covered a lot of what I'd say, so I'll just say this: Vitamins can help. I don't know if your diet is as shitty as mine, but a lack of proper nutrition will absolutely contribute to a physical decline, and a physical decline will absolutely contribute to a mental decline as you have less energy and resources to muster in the battle. Throwing a bottle of Centrum-D at your mouth probably seems kind of sarcastic, but give it a shot.<br /> <br /> Actually, I lied. I'll also say that it's good to hear from you again and I missed you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T13:19:34-08:00","id":370075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=370051#post370051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Papa Bear covered a lot of what I'd say, so I'll just say this: Vitamins can help. I don't know if your diet is as shitty as mine, but a lack of proper nutrition will absolutely contribute to a physical decline, and a physical decline will absolutely contribute to a mental decline as you have less energy and resources to muster in the battle. Throwing a bottle of Centrum-D at your mouth probably seems kind of sarcastic, but give it a shot.<br /> <br /> Actually, I lied. I'll also say that it's good to hear from you again and I missed you.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I expect you to take this same advice next time you're feeling like that, little Moogle. Capisco? Verschten? Comprendo? Comprends? Don't make me get cosmopolitan on you!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T21:32:36-08:00","id":371816,"title":"","content":"I completely without professional training and such so take the suggestion for what it is, would recommend avoiding the news and things like tumblr or twitter if you get exposed to the depressing politics there.<br /> <br /> The amount of negative news that people are getting and are getting hammered with has been doing nothing but increase the last 50 years.... while horrible stuff going on has on the whole been going down. It may feel like sticking your head in the sand, but there's a lot that is overblown and/or that you can't do much if anything about... so don't dwell on it. This by itself isn't a solution, but it might help give you some mental space if you're not continually being bombarded with horror stories and terrible news played over and over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T21:59:06-08:00","id":371864,"title":"","content":"I've been avoiding the news for close on a decade now....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T06:53:51-08:00","id":372491,"title":"","content":"And just for those of you who think it can't be done and once you get &quot;there&quot;, it's done:<br /> <br /> On the way into work, I seriously contemplated driving my car into a telephone poll. I was yelling at myself about what an asshole I am because I was screaming at my Baby Bears for stupid, insignificant reasons. I was inflicting psychological trauma on little kids because I was worried I might be late to work and even that thought couldn't calm me down. I will be fighting this all damn day long.<br /> <br /> But I will still be here tomorrow because I fucking know better that these thoughts are as stupid as I think I am right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T12:25:18-08:00","id":372790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=372491#post372491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And just for those of you who think it can't be done and once you get &quot;there&quot;, it's done:<br /> <br /> On the way into work, I seriously contemplated driving my car into a telephone poll. I was yelling at myself about what an asshole I am because I was screaming at my Baby Bears for stupid, insignificant reasons. I was inflicting psychological trauma on little kids because I was worried I might be late to work and even that thought couldn't calm me down. I will be fighting this all damn day long.<br /> <br /> But I will still be here tomorrow because I fucking know better that these thoughts are as stupid as I think I am right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're a good man, Papa Bear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T13:36:12-08:00","id":372834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=372790#post372790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're a good man, Papa Bear.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's a good papa and a good bear, but I refuse to describe him as a good man. It comes off as speciesist.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, P-Bear, don't drive into a telephone pole. The whole &quot;no one is allowed to die&quot; rule you created applies to you too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T14:16:19-08:00","id":372869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=372834#post372834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's a good papa and a good bear, but I refuse to describe him as a good man. It comes off as speciesist.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, P-Bear, don't drive into a telephone pole. The whole &quot;no one is allowed to die&quot; rule you created applies to you too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, thank you for standing up for my species and for reminding me of my own no dying policy.<br /> <br /> I need these little reminders from time to time. Disadvantage of a mind that never stops.....it gets tired and forgetful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T19:21:48-08:00","id":373967,"title":"","content":"Silence.<br /> <br /> Maybe I just want - need - some silence.<br /> <br /> It might seem contradictory given my loneliness, but I feel like I'm never really alone. My family doesn't dare to give me even a day of peace.<br /> They're -always- with me, always around me, never giving me any privacy or time alone. They feel like prison wardens sometimes, albeit ones whom I'm most often friendly with and kind of care about.<br /> <br /> They're like shackles to the outside world, or an endless series of eyes always watching me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T16:35:58-08:00","id":374554,"title":"","content":"Kleptomania.<br /> <br /> I suffer from psychotic depression. I am prone to obsessive, delusional thinking and I hear voices. I'm also on bad days extremely suicidal and prone to psychotic episodes where I harm myself in the most violent way possible or try to at least. I perfectly understand your feelings. The world is absolute shit and people are going to destroy this world. Most days, I just feel like killing myself because I feel useless and unable to change anything. It's only with medications that I am able to function is a semi-coherent state of mind<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They can't seem to comprehend the viewpoints I approach things from, generally because they are things that would assuredly get me institutionalised if I were only a little bit more vocal with them </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> I specifically know these feelings. My parents do not understand, nor does my sister, my friends, or anyone else I happen to care about.<br /> <br /> I view the world as a massive shitball along with 95% of the world. I view the world as a world where Satan has won and all is lost. I'll also be completely honest in saying that I view hope as the most deluded emotion to possess and yet, I very much want it.<br /> <br /> When I try talking about these things, I do not get understanding. I do not get sympathy. I get bewildered looks, topic changes, and misunderstanding. I feel as though I am very lonely in feeling that the world is fallen and that hope is no more. I try to communicate, but when I try I feel as though my loved ones want to put me back in the hospital. But... depression is a mindset, and I try to communicate that if they at least tried to understand that I'd feel infinitely better. God knows I try to understand the violence, the oppression, the war but I don't. It's meaning eludes me, and all I see is our planet's death spiral and that makes me want to put lead in my skull because I feel so damn useless.<br /> <br /> Know that at least, you're not alone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T04:39:31-08:00","id":375137,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Pilgrim. It's been a sadness to me that I could not think of anything to say to Kleptomania, and I'm glad you could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T08:12:27-08:00","id":375264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pilgrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=374554#post374554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Know that at least, you're not alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I-... Thank you.<br /> It really does help. I oftentimes need to be reminded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T21:03:26-08:00","id":376896,"title":"","content":"There was this person today. I was minding my own business at the library reading a book about medieval Christian mystics. I get up from the seat and go grab a pencil so I can start writing notes and grab a drink. It was this younger lady about my age and she gave me this really dirty look. I sigh. I breath real deep. I go get a pencil from the reference desk and go to the vending machine.<br /> <br /> Then the violent fantasies start. I can't stop thinking about taking the pencil I just got and stabbing her repeatedly in the throat. I try meditating. &quot;god is love, I am love, all is love&quot; and then a voice says &quot;that won't work stupid shit. You know as well as I do, that God has damned you&quot;.<br /> <br /> I started balling really bad because I was conflicted between the urge to punish myself for my sinful thoughts and stabbing that woman.<br /> <br /> Man, things were going so good.Then this happens","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T03:54:44-08:00","id":380882,"title":"","content":"I'm not really a frequent poster so i feel kinda weird posting here but<br /> <br /> I've always known that I have very serious ADD, and it's been something I've dealt with my whole life. College has been an uphill battle for that reason, but one that for the most part has felt worth fighting. However, since summer of freshman year of college, I've known that I've inherited my mom's clinical depression. It's an issue that comes and goes but it's been a pretty steady drain on my health and grads over my last few years of school. In the past I've always been able to overcome my learning and focus issues because I've always had determination and enthusiasm, but depression pretty much sucks all the drive out of a person. Combined with ADD it's a pretty deadly combo.<br /> <br /> I honestly thought I was on the up-and-up this year. First quarter I powered through all of my classes just fine, and I'm living with dear and supportive friends who have really made life feel good again.<br /> <br /> This quarter, though, things haven't just relapsed, they've dipped down to a point I've never before encountered, as of just last night. The quarter went from normal and manageable to a nightmare in no time flat, and now as of just these two weeks I'm dealing with possibly failing out of my beloved major due to past mistakes when I was a freshman idiot, a missing wallet, a job that no longer supports me, looming deadlines, and minor sad social life events (a three year long campaign is just falling apart all of a sudden and i'm disproportionately sad) and honestly while I know in the logical part of me that all those things have hope of being resolved they've pretty much overloaded my system. I feel constantly dazed, I have trouble remembering things, i don't have the energy or number of fucks needed to feed or care for myself properly. I haven't finished a book for my own pleasure or spent any quality time outside in months if not almost a year, let alone do anything else i used to love doing other than pointlessly surfing the net to distract myself. I'm pretty sure I'm starving myself by forgetfulness and neglect but between appetite suppressant meds and depression it's hard to tell. All I know is today i took a shower to try and wake myself up and start my day moving and halfway through i just lost any will or desire to continue doing ANYTHING, let alone keep scrubbing. I pretty much just got out and lay on the floor until i was dry. I'm pretty sure i'm caught in a vicious cycle of depression, hunger, and physical fatigue but the scary thing is i don't think i have the energy needed to break out of it anymore. Or the hope.<br /> <br /> Idk I'm sorry, I don't really know where I'm going with this. I don't want to hurt myself or anything i just AM hurting myself by neglect and i don't know how to stop<br /> <br /> I want to live fully again and I want to think clearly again. The hardest part is remembering how bright and vibrant things felt just a few years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":4416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","user":"Heedra","date":". 01-25-2015, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T19:27:56-08:00","id":381512,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T10:32:30-08:00","id":382127,"title":"","content":"I am finding it supremely difficult to actually care about anything anymore. You would think it would be liberating, but it's mostly just-... Empty, I guess.<br /> My life has slowly been losing all meaning, while I've been losing all my tethers to sanity and the world.<br /> I want to make things better, but I can't. I feel like I've hit rock bottom-... I somehow doubt it.<br /> <br /> Fuck humanity, fuck mortality, fuck this horrible boring Universe. Why can't I just fucking escape already? My mind is ready, I want to see the walls of reality fall apart around me. I want my sanity to break apart, making me free again.<br /> But it's never going to happen. I've too much self-control.<br /> <br /> I need to get out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T11:34:40-08:00","id":399080,"title":"","content":"So I'm schizoaffective. Basically that means that I have some symptoms of schizophrenia along with the symptoms of major depressive disorder(in my case). That was a shock when I found out that I am a schizo, but it makes sense, because I sometimes hear voices and I get really paranoid. My doc and therapist also say that I am delusional, so there's probably something to the diagnosis.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T14:23:34-08:00","id":399327,"title":"","content":"So,as you mentioned both a doc and a therapist, are you managing it? You know, therapy, I don't know if medication (I'm awfully ignorant about this things but I think some forms of schizophrenia can be ameliorated by some chemicals?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T15:11:44-08:00","id":399401,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T19:03:12-08:00","id":399728,"title":"","content":"Hey, 'killer, good to hear from you again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T06:32:33-08:00","id":400227,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T10:20:58-08:00","id":400485,"title":"","content":"Well, my attempts to join the ranks of the medicated has turned out in a not wholly unexpected way.<br /> <br /> My psychiatrist insisted, despite my attempts to explain that it's a greater issue, upon starting me off on an anti-depressant. Now, at least she was smart enough to acknowledge that she was only 80% certain that was my problem and warned me what to watch out for if it was a greater issue. After three doses over three days, nearly those exact reactions she told me to be wary of occurred. I went from being kind of down to slightly relaxed to back where I was to a seething mountain of rage ready to unleash it upon the world in a glorious frenzy of destruction, blood and death.<br /> <br /> See, I wasn't quite able to explain to her properly that while I am prone to mild manias in which I have trouble sleeping and my mind races, it's not those states that I get the most nor are they the true danger of my existence. My &quot;mania&quot; expresses itself as <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>RAGE</b></span>, thus my choice of constant maniacal activity seems restricted to a small area of interest which usually involves WANTING TO HIT EVERYTHING AROUND ME!<br /> <br /> After leaving a few messages with her nurses, I was finally able to get the doctor's response, which was to wait for my next appointment, which is 3 weeks from now, and that I will be receiving no further medications until then.<br /> <br /> Since I work in behavioral health at my current job, I did not argue or fight or scream. I quietly, but very reluctantly, accepted that answer. I know what the problems are trying to get to see a psychiatrist these days are - too many people in need and not enough people willing to take the time, money and effort required to become a psychiatrist. It's insane amount of education and training required and they'll probably be facing a mid-life crisis not long after they finally get to <i>begin </i>their practice.<br /> <br /> So, now I wait and I do my best to maintain without. Which I used to be quite good at and now I can't seem to get a handle on things. Thus is the life of a man who's brain is working against him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:18:03-08:00","id":400756,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:07:04-08:00","id":400829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=400227#post400227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been really busy with work lately and just kind of been on autopilot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, I hear that. Still, it's good news that you're better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=400485#post400485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, my attempts to join the ranks of the medicated has turned out in a not wholly unexpected way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any chance of going to, say, an ER and getting a different result?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:04:42-08:00","id":400879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=400756#post400756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but I'm not really that upset by it. I half expected this. I work on the inside of mental health. I know what it's like around here, and we're supposed to be one of the BETTER providers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=400829#post400829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance of going to, say, an ER and getting a different result?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but it's hardly worth it. Maybe I'd get a small supply from them, a few days at the most, but it has the potential to be just as bad for me as what I was already given, and that's assuming they'd even admit me. I went off the meds I was given and will not take them again, so I'm not nearly the violence volcano I was on Friday. Also, it would be a great deal more expensive.<br /> <br /> I will bide my time and try something else when given the script. I'm fairly certain the doctor will listen this time as I was quite descriptive in my message to her since I was in the middle of one of these rage episode while leaving the message. The nurse was quite apologetic about not calling me back sooner based on that message. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T23:02:04-08:00","id":401481,"title":"","content":"Psychopharmaceuticals scare the crap outta me. Every one I've taken has hit me some major negatives. Most notably a couple of years ago when I was on Adderall. It induced mania and psychosis during a Changeling game I was in. Everyone but the ST didn't want me back after that. Stating that they didn't really wanna be around someone with mental illness.<br /> <br /> It still haunts me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T13:59:27-08:00","id":402377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=399327#post399327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So,as you mentioned both a doc and a therapist, are you managing it? You know, therapy, I don't know if medication (I'm awfully ignorant about this things but I think some forms of schizophrenia can be ameliorated by some chemicals?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm on Zoloft and Risperdal and I go to therapy. Therapist says I need to work on my black and white thinking and my incredibly negative thinking.(not my fault that the world is a steaming pile of shit that's on a mad death march<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=399401#post399401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently diagnosed with Bipolar Type II, Schizoaffective and Paranoid Personality Disordeer. Not trying to sound like one of those commercials but ask your doctor about seroquel. Shits worked well for me. I'm sure there are other options as well. Also, don't drink. It can make the auditory visual and sensational hallucinations worse and could push you to suicide. I know, its why I got baker acted in October. My hallucinations are typically audible voices but unintelligible and these weird fucking alien death spiders and centipedes crawling out of this nonexistent hole in the wall that kind of looked like the one from the movie Mama. I also have a big scar on my arm from where I peeled about a square inch of skin off trying to dig nonexistent bugs out of my skin. These were all made worse with drinking. Hang in there buddy. Just find the right meds and you'll feel better.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Risperdal is working for the most part. My hallucinations tend to be auditory, like I hear voices clear as day and they claim to be God, Satan, and angels and demons and I sometimes hear my family's voices say things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T12:47:41-08:00","id":404949,"title":"","content":"So my anxiety just is runining me right now.... i'm trying to breath and not panic but fuck.<br /> <br /> Onwards as to why!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I've been in pain from my tooth for weeks saw my dentist two weeks ago told i needed a root canal on the back top tooth, okay cool. Then last week the pain got worse and a bad taste in my mouth prompted me to get seen asap, saw the dentist this morning and that tooth and the one next to it are irrepairably damaged and infected and are getting pulled on monday as given they are causing pain and infected its to risky to just wait.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">however since i;m pregnant she is refusing to use nitrous okay i can handle that i guess barely(I plan to take a sedative at home before i go cause last time i had a tooth pullled, i nearly had a freak out and they used nitrous which helped a ton)...but then she added on saying that i can only take tylenol afterwards. Uh no just no. i had one tooth pulled last year and tylenol didnt work at all for the pain I had to have vicodin and that barely worked enough to not have me crying. (I dont handle pain well at all)..So i called my OB doctor and explained the situation his nurse said he should have no problem prescribing it for me as if its only taken for a couple days vicodin is fine. But then she calls back after talking to him and he says the dentist needs to prescribe it and that they can fax a letter to their office saying its okay.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I'm scared that my bitch of a dentist will still say no even with that. I CANNOT have two teeth pulled at one time and no painkiller afterwards <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm nearly having an axiety attack just at the thought of having the teeth pulled but its made worse KNOWING that afterwards i'll be in pain thanks to a horribly mean dentist who isnt listening/believeing me when i say tyenol doesnt work on me... My heart hasnt stopped racing since i found out about needing them pulled and its gotten worse finding out i may have to suffer afterwards. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I dont know what i'm going to do if even with my OB saying its okay my dentist refuses the pain meds... I may have to refuse to have them pulled because frankly i cant do it...i cannot do it knowing the amount of pain that will follow...infection and current pain be damned...</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T23:01:34-08:00","id":419867,"title":"","content":"I NEED to feel in control again...I'm loosing my shit here... my paranoia which i blamed on the vicodin(hoped it was the vicodin) hasnt gone away (and i havent taken any of the vicodin in days) It usually only gets this bad if i'm highly stressed out. though i dunno if its paranoia? does firmly believing theres something in the shadows lurking, watching me, whispering just loud enough to be heard but not enough ot be understood...count as paranoia or am i really fucking loosing it? I just want to cry and scream and hit things because everything is not okay and no one listens to me ..oh i get listened to in the sense it goes in on ear and out the other disregarded as &quot;hormonal rambling etc&quot;... I just badly need to be heard right now and well even my screaming gets ignored. Maybe i need to start seeing a therapist agian, but then again the last couple of times has just felt like a giant waste of time so i quit months ago..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T16:42:54-08:00","id":420825,"title":"","content":"That's paranoia Scelesta, it's a type of delusion. Have you talked to a pdoc or a psych nurse practitioner about it? I know those feels, and it didn't get better until I was open about feeling paranoid and hearing voices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:03:03-08:00","id":420928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pilgrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=420825#post420825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's paranoia Scelesta, it's a type of delusion. Have you talked to a pdoc or a psych nurse practitioner about it? I know those feels, and it didn't get better until I was open about feeling paranoid and hearing voices.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have, but they just want to give me medications which i'm flat out refusing to go on because of the risks being to high. So my only option really is to man up and get used to it and hope this passes on its own or i just stop being bothered by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T20:51:49-08:00","id":423783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=420928#post420928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have, but they just want to give me medications which i'm flat out refusing to go on because of the risks being to high. So my only option really is to man up and get used to it and hope this passes on its own or i just stop being bothered by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's more than meds you know. When I feel paranoid, one of the things I do is meditate or do breathing excercises and repeat something like &quot;no one is after me, and it's all in my head&quot;. I mean I'm not saying that what I say will work for you, but there are some good coping skills that don't rely on meds. Meds can only do so much anyway, like for my symptoms they only tone down the stuff I hear, my homocidal thoughts, and my paranoia, but it's on me to learn how to cope for the rest of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T14:24:10-08:00","id":424511,"title":"","content":"GODDAMN IT. I CAN'T EVEN SAY IT!!! I feel completely impotent and incapable of expressing myself in words and it's fucking killing me!!! I typed out what's bothering me three times! I can't stop erasing it and hiding like a fucking rat in the walls! Fuck","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T06:41:38-08:00","id":425113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=424511#post424511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GODDAMN IT. I CAN'T EVEN SAY IT!!! I feel completely impotent and incapable of expressing myself in words and it's fucking killing me!!! I typed out what's bothering me three times! I can't stop erasing it and hiding like a fucking rat in the walls! Fuck</div> </div> </div> </div>Send it PM to someone, just to get it out of your system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T07:03:02-08:00","id":425135,"title":"","content":"AzraelFirestorm - Don\u00b4t do that. It\u00b4s good that you can admit it to yourself.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have something remotely offtopic:<br /> As some people now I live in Germany and the clinical procedure seem really different:<br /> <br /> First off, I guess that most people here are located in the US and your pychotherapeutical-healthcare-systems seems horrid.<br /> Here you also need to wait (several months) to get to &quot;psychological Psychotherapist&quot;(The person who does the &quot;Freud&quot;) or psychiatrist (The MD who gives you drugs) (aren\u00b4t german expression neat? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> if you have express suicidal tendencies or are even trying to - you get a quicker application or if your so psychotic that they institutionalize you.<br /> Then you get 5 probatory session in which you decide if the therapist is to your liking and the therapist decides to keep you (and decide what and how should be treated) - or transfer you. <br /> Off course you can find a private therapist and throw your money at him/her...<br /> <br /> Don\u00b4t forget:<br /> <b>Depression lies. </b><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:05:32-08:00","id":425584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=425135#post425135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Depression lies. </b></div> </div> </div> </div>There really is nothing to add to this, but you know, ten character minimum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T01:56:47-08:00","id":426295,"title":"","content":"Depression lies. That I know, but the reminder is appreciated nonetheless as a totem of my connection to being a person. It's my mind playing tricks on me. I'm not evil. The intrusive and awful things that fill my my head are most likely a manifestation of Obsessive Compulsive Disorder, judging by their frequency and tendency to disturb me. I've had to drink a pint of 80 proof whiskey just to collect myself enough to type this. <br /> <br /> Do you believe in Hell? That's the crux of my existence.<br /> <br /> I want to go there. It's a delusional thought, to be sure. All the same, I want it.<br /> More specifically, I want a place where the commandments of the universe insist that I act as some puppeteer of intense pleasure and deepest sorrow as if it were something good and even saintly. Part of me wants to be a monster so bad I can almost smell the blood. <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I love humanity. It has an indescribable beauty. I would just thoroughly enjoy and be fulfilled by acting like fucking Pinhead and ripping, burning, chaining, flaying the damned both mentally and physically in a place and fashion that they could scarcely imagine. That's not normal. That's downright fucked up and evil. I know that. My emotions should match my logical conclusion that shit like this is not alright. <br /> \u200b<br /> Most days I spend writhing in the fetal position, fighting bloody battles against myself in mirror image who insist that whether I believe in God, Satan, Bigfoot or nothing at all, that I must be a thing that hurts. I want to be nice. I want to talk to people more than I talk to the bathroom mirror as if it were a different person. I'm neither of these things to myself, and in my mind, neither in general. People have told me otherwise. I don't believe them. <br /> <br /> If I sound crazy, well, maybe I am. Honestly, if I were confident and correct in my thinking, I would be living in some kind of terrible hellscape already.<br /> <br /> Maybe I just think too much about all the wrong things..<br /> <br /> I'm drinking the rest of this bottle. Don't include me in your prayers. I'm a fucking waste that's going to ignite and burn through existence. I'm not even here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T01:59:15-08:00","id":426299,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It was half a fifth, if anyone is doing their rough alcohol arithmetic. The other half is going to black me out harder than a baseball bat to the head. Blessed oblivion.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T08:14:45-08:00","id":426584,"title":"","content":"AzraelFirestorm.<br /> You know that alkohol doesn\u00b4t give oblivion. If it would work you weren\u00b4t in the need of this.<br /> But ask yourself if you want to feel better and actually allow it to yourself.<br /> <br /> I don\u00b4t believe hell, neither the heavens, nor purgatory and any other so called Afterlife. believe it or not this gives me a huge sense of freedom and the sentence: &quot;Life is without purpose.&quot; doesn\u00b4t frighten me - it gives me an intense feeling of hope. I`m alive and someday I will die.<br /> Imagine yourself - You are alive, I assume you have enough food and even have a steady internet connection. That\u00b4s good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T07:04:38-08:00","id":427689,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T13:17:13-08:00","id":428055,"title":"","content":"Everyone in the nation has a cold today, 'killer, and this is my second in one lunar cycle. There's just nasty shit going around. Try not to worry about it.<br /> <br /> The hallucinations, on the other hand, might be worth having a word with your doctor about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T11:46:38-08:00","id":429079,"title":"","content":"Well, it's official. I'm psychotic. Doc put me on abilify.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:30:09-08:00","id":429220,"title":"","content":"Ain't nothing but a word, brother. Hugs. Bear hugs, even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:39:18-08:00","id":429230,"title":"","content":"Oh, but it's GOOD NEWS. Now I can get one of these:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://rlv.zcache.com/i_am_handicapped_im_psychotic_the_poster_ii-rc9d1c519c91a440a9b3e16f94f71cdeb_w2q_8byvr_512.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:30:37-08:00","id":429304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=429079#post429079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's official. I'm psychotic. Doc put me on abilify.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anti-psychotics are used for more than just schizophrenia and other psychotic disorders. For example low doses of Latuda help with bipolar depression, risperdal is used for bipolar mood swings. So it might not be psychosis, it could other things. Like even though I'm schizoaffective, my risperdal is to help with my depressive mood swings too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T14:46:58-08:00","id":429314,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but...........<br /> <br /> The doctor did give it to me for depression and as a mood stabilizer......and because when she put me on Celexa I wanted to look up how to make a nuclear bomb and take out a major city.......for the fun of it.<br /> <br /> Yes, when my issues are out of control, I'm a super-villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T21:12:42-08:00","id":429787,"title":"","content":"O.o<br /> <br /> I can see the news now. Polar bear super villain confronted by Jesus freak rambo fanatic thing and the results are devastating.<br /> <br /> (&quot;Jesus freak rambo thing&quot; yes, you read that correctly, that's what I'm like when I'm unwell)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T21:39:04-08:00","id":429815,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:03:42-08:00","id":430224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=429815#post429815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if it makes you feel any better, they upped my dosage to 600 from 200 of seroquel and it swung me hard out of a very minor depressive bout ( I think of perfect harmoy as 0 -10 as crazy shit depression and 10 being fucking laughing maniacally like the joker)I shot from a -1 or -2 to a 6 in hours. I was on edge all day, biting peoples heads off. Hearing my name bothered me. I'm physically and mentally exhausted. I'm contemplating taking 450mg instead and bringing myself to that level. weird hallucinatory shit dropped in strength almost immediately though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'm really not having that much of a problem with the whole thing. I went into this knowing we're most likely be going someplace like that.<br /> <br /> Last time I was on meds in the psych ward, they had me on thorazine for about a week just to bring me down to a level they could reason with me. Then they dropped that and put me on an anti-depressant. This new stuff is supposed to help with both, plus a mood stabilizer. Doc acknowledged that sometimes the &quot;up&quot; portion of a bi-polar like disorder doesn't always result in a &quot;happy I can do anything&quot; kind of mood, it can also be &quot;angry I can KILL anything&quot;. 20+ years ago, they didn't know what to make of me. This time, sounds like they've got some new info to work with. We'll see how it goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:39:38-08:00","id":431656,"title":"","content":"I feel right now like it would better for me to never care about anyone because they will inevitably end up abandoning me leaving me more lonely than if they had never been there to begin with. <br /> <br /> Fuck it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:59:26-08:00","id":432065,"title":"","content":"What's up, Jeddy? Bad break-up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T00:08:36-08:00","id":432383,"title":"","content":"Heh. Well that's contributed to it. But that's not terribly recent. The specific thing that sparked this was the idea that one of my favorite roommates ever is probably going to move out.<br /> <br /> Spencer moved in last semester. So September. He's a wonderful human being; one of the best people I've ever known. At the beginning of this semester (January) Brandon moved in. Brandon is 21 and the rest of us are older. 25 or older. At the beginning of the semester, Brandon said, &quot;No offense, but I feel like I got a really old apartment.&quot; Brandon and Spencer hang out more than the rest of us. Today Spencer mentioned moving out with Brandon and living somewhere else. So basically Spencer is going to leave because he likes Brandon better than he likes us. Brandon doesn't like is because we're old. And that makes me feel really sad. <br /> <br /> This is the latest in what I feel is a long history of abandonments. It's exaggerated and it's the depression lying, but it got to me today; I spent about a half hour crying about it. That's when I made that post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T06:48:33-07:00","id":432584,"title":"","content":"Don't take it personal, Jeddy. When two guys want to move in together very, very much...........well, there's probably more to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T09:39:25-07:00","id":432675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=432383#post432383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. Well that's contributed to it. But that's not terribly recent. The specific thing that sparked this was the idea that one of my favorite roommates ever is probably going to move out.<br /> <br /> Spencer moved in last semester. So September. He's a wonderful human being; one of the best people I've ever known. At the beginning of this semester (January) Brandon moved in. Brandon is 21 and the rest of us are older. 25 or older. At the beginning of the semester, Brandon said, &quot;No offense, but I feel like I got a really old apartment.&quot; Brandon and Spencer hang out more than the rest of us. Today Spencer mentioned moving out with Brandon and living somewhere else. So basically Spencer is going to leave because he likes Brandon better than he likes us. Brandon doesn't like is because we're old. And that makes me feel really sad.<br /> <br /> This is the latest in what I feel is a long history of abandonments. It's exaggerated and it's the depression lying, but it got to me today; I spent about a half hour crying about it. That's when I made that post.</div> </div> </div> </div>TO be fair, I probably don't help the entire affair with Brandon.<br /> <br /> For those who don't know, Brandon is a really nice guy who never the less kind of favors all the things I don't, and visa versa. We get along, but there's no denying a tension between the two of us has been building. Brandon probably would stay if I would leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:45:17-07:00","id":432732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=432584#post432584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't take it personal, Jeddy. When two guys want to move in together very, very much...........well, there's probably more to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that you're intentionally implying that they're gay... I don't think so. Brandon I'd believe it. Several comments he has made this semester border really close to being flirtatious or turned on by men. I would not be surprised to find out that Brandon was gay. He's Mormon, so he's suppressing it, but he might be. Spencer, I would be very surprised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:48:58-07:00","id":432757,"title":"","content":"Oh and since Arcensean and I have pretty similar interests, I would much rather he stay than Brandon. Brandon kind of drives me batty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T18:42:09-07:00","id":433397,"title":"","content":"Does Thorin covet me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T02:25:38-07:00","id":442379,"title":"","content":"First off, I'm very, very, <i>very</i> aware that next to some, or even most, people on this thread, my &quot;problems&quot; are so tiny as to not really warrant the term. But I want to vent, and this seems a semi-appropriate venue. Also, this is more-or-less stream-of-consciousness, so coherency likely won't be high. I may go back and edit, see how I feel at the end.<br /> <br /> You know those situations you sometimes find yourself in where someone has clearly made a colossal mistake/is a giant idiot, but you honestly don't know who? That's increasingly becoming my default state. I've never been great with people at the best of times; between the increasingly-strong stress attacks I have when in a crowd, to having serious difficulty interacting with people due to knowing appropriate responses, and apparently my bizarre beliefs (I'm measuring this against the people I generally interact with. Imperfect metric, I know: they seem reasonable enough to me), it's just easier to stay at home and read or watch movies. I'm solitary by nature anyway, so that works out. But I think it's getting worse. I'm a research student in psychology, working on what will be my PhD project. However, I really have very little idea what I'm doing. I get the concepts I'm working with well enough, but I'm constantly feeling that it's a surface understanding, that I should have a better grasp of how they relate, the dynamics, and suchforth. Every other student I talk to at my level seems to have a pretty solid grasp of their concepts, whereas I feel like I'm mostly parroting and drawing tenuous links based on nothing. My supervisor <i>seems </i>OK with my progress, but it wouldn't be the first time I've catastrophically misread someone over an extended period of time. That, together with the fact that my last supervisor (different project) wanted as little to do with me as humanly possible, while apparently being great for all his other students, doesn't make me feel overly secure. Plus, I'm into the second year of a program that they're apparently enforcing a three-year limit on, and while I was on track in terms of time, I've hit a giant wall that I have no idea how to get around without a total redesign, which could easily take six months in itself (oh, by the way, I have like two weeks to do this, or I'll have to wait a year since my project is tied to the school year). I would ask my supervisor, but he's taken sick leave for at least a month. In combination, he was the convenor for the course I'm tutoring, and I keep getting this idea that the idea of having to see me more than once a month literally drove him away. I have no evidence for this, but it's in my brain and damn it I can't move it.<br /> <br /> At the same time I'm conducting interviews as part of a pilot study using the undergrad student pool, which is just reinforcing just how little I 'get' people. I mean, I know, thing about learning is you know how little you know, but most people seem to have this semi-intuitive grasp of how other people work, whereas I'm having to run entirely off half-baked academic theories and behavioural models. It's like how I play Go: I don't study or have much of a sense for the game, I've learned what little I have through trial-and-error. But in Go, I mess up, I lose a game and feel stupid. With people, I mess up, I screw up my one shot at my desired career and potentially worse. Plus, if I don't manage to pull out something meaningful from the data, then I will have that much more of a difficult time, administratively speaking, and so far I've got diddly. And not even useful diddly.<br /> <br /> So, I hear you say, why not talk to your friends? Well, I don't really have anyone I would call a friend. Oh, I have people I'm friendly with, a coffee every now and then, listen to them bitch about their boyfriend, but for me the title of friend implies a degree of reliability and reciprocity. I'm not expecting them to bend over backwards, or keep exact score of who owes who what, but literally every time I ask them to do something, from find something out for me to read a draft article I'm trying to publish to make sure it makes even a little bit of sense, inevitably they don't. Oh, they say they will, but nope, never follow through. Ever. I <i>sometimes</i> get a result if I nag, but I hate to nag, and even then it's not a great percentage. Plus, I am generally of the view that they have their own problems, listening to me whine about issues won't make my life any easier as it doesn't solve the problem, and may well make them more miserable. So, what's the point? Also, I'm kind of private. Not super-secretive, but I don't raise things about myself unless asked; just don't see it as any of their business (no, they don't ask). And yes, I see the contradiction: I like to keep things to myself, and I'm venting on a semi-public forum. Was it not clear this was a rant long on emotion and short on logic?<br /> <br /> So, overall, I'm pretty stressed. And when I get stressed, I get angry. Which normally isn't a problem, I'm used to having to control my temper, since it seems to be a bit more hair-trigger in me than in most. But the fact is that my willpower is not unlimited, and I'm pretty sure the anger is getting worse, and I can just see myself exploding all over something that is entirely stupid and a normal person would just laugh off or ignore. So, being the semi-intelligent person I like to think I am on my better days, I drew on my existing knowledge base and thought &quot;you know what? Buddhism has some pretty on-topic things to say about anger, maybe they can teach me something.&quot; So I go along to the local Buddhist temple. (This next part is going to sound really racist/xenophobic/generally nasty. Not intended, or at least not as nasty as it sounds.) Apparently, their grasp of the English language is, shall we say, limited? So, that wasn't any use, and my understanding of their perspective is purely academic, so limited ability to apply it in a useful fashion. And while I completely agree with the value of learning languages, I refuse to learn at least two languages to fluency to get feedback on a perspective which may or may not help, from people who live in a country where my first language is the dominant one. So, that didn't work out, and the fact that I live in a heavily Asian area (which is fine, lots of good Thai food) where only like 30% of the people speak English to any appreciable level (which is less fine, but understandable: my other languages aren't fantastic either), just makes it that much easier to form these associations between certain language/ethnic groups and irritation, which is really not a fine thing to do (have you ever tried to <i>not</i> form an association between paired stimuli? It's really hard).<br /> <br /> So, I'm lost, I'm stressed, I'm apparently alone and not in the way I like, and I'm constantly being shown that I'm even more stupid than I thought, or at least totally unable to apply my knowledge, which is basically the same thing in a practical sense. And I have no idea what I'm supposed to do, but I do know that if I don't do something then something really bad will happen.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. End rant. Like I said, I know full well that this doesn't even count as a problem, but it's irritating me, and hopefully venting will help. I very much doubt it, but it's not like I'm overly burdened with options here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T06:48:09-07:00","id":442470,"title":"","content":"It does look like a huge problem if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T05:28:27-07:00","id":445639,"title":"","content":"Not in comparison to others. I mean, we have people in this thread with psychosis, serious unipolar and bipolar depression, developmental issues and serious trauma. I'm just angry, stressed and confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T05:59:57-07:00","id":445684,"title":"","content":"Oh, of course, I dind't mean to make less of other's issues. What I meant was that particularly for you, given the career and study options you are seeking, it is a rather crippling problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:53:18-07:00","id":446504,"title":"","content":"son of a fucking bitch. So i as supposed to see my therapist today, its kinda fucking urgent as my anxiety is getting bad enough i'm having frequent panic attacks, i get there only to be told my appointment had been rescheduled for next month cause my therapist had jury duty. NO ONE CALLED TO TELL ME THIS!<br /> <br /> So i decide to go the fuck it route and schedule an appointment with my Pdoc,so you knowi can get on medications to help my crippling anxiety thats eating me alive, and the depression thats strongly creeping in... Soonest appointment? April fucking 15th.<br /> <br /> This isnt a joke, this is urgent i need to see a pdoc and get on meds NOW not in a month i dont know what to do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T19:39:33-07:00","id":446917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=445639#post445639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, we have people in this thread with psychosis, serious unipolar and bipolar depression, developmental issues and serious trauma. I'm just angry, stressed and confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am personally not interested in ranking mental and emotional problems, and I'm especially not interested in doing so if it makes someone feel he needs to apologize for having an issue. If something it bothering you, then it's a problem, and let no one prevent you from discussing it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T00:46:30-07:00","id":447329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=446917#post446917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am personally not interested in ranking mental and emotional problems, and I'm especially not interested in doing so if it makes someone feel he needs to apologize for having an issue. If something it bothering you, then it's a problem, and let no one prevent you from discussing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, as long as nobody thinks I'm belittling their (what I would call actual) problems with my comparatively petty ones.<br /> <br /> I suppose the biggest issue is that there doesn't seem to be any kind of solution that I can spot. I can hardly <i>make</i> my supervisor be not sick, and my inference of his &quot;motivations&quot; is entirely in my own head. Much though I'd like, I can't will myself to be more intelligent, or to have understanding I just don't have, and frankly if I don't have a base understanding of how people work by postgraduate psychology studies and half a lifetime of observation, I suspect I won't ever. Nor does any solution for my anger reaction to stress, or way of managing it better than I've currently found, seem to be available, either through my academic searches or more common-sense approaches.<br /> <br /> If I could find a solution, then I could work on it, and I wouldn't mind quite so much. But it seems I'm stuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T21:20:05-07:00","id":448814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=445639#post445639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not in comparison to others. I mean, we have people in this thread with psychosis, serious unipolar and bipolar depression, developmental issues and serious trauma. I'm just angry, stressed and confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can't even imagine your immense stress and bubbling anger, but just because I have psychosis and unipolar depression doesn't make your problems any less diminished because you don't have some of the issues, some of us have,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T13:06:26-07:00","id":449648,"title":"","content":"Dude, I whine about my problems all the time on here and I'm WAY not worse (apparently) that a lot of other folks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We're sharing, not balancing scales. No one's story has more weight than someone else's.<br /> <br /> Everyone's story is worth it's weight in gold to someone else.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I give example.<br /> <br /> I'm sitting here working in behavioral health scheduling. I'm getting calls ranging from parents trying to make little Johnny (who's 17) quit smoking pot (which is legal here in CO if not for their age, but no worse than the booze the parents were having when they were kids) up to the lady to called to cancel the appointment her husband had the next day because he committed suicide the previous day.<br /> <br /> The other day, I take this one call. This lady is going on about how she might be bi-polar and how she used to have it so together and then a bunch of stuff happened in her life and made her lose it. How she used to be so brave and now she was almost having an anxiety attack just trying to make the phone call to me. And how soothing and calm I sound and how much that helps and how I must have to be so together and right in the head to hear all these people's problems all day long. Meanwhile, I'm about to cry because she's telling MY story about how she feels right now and I had also just been diagnosed bi-polar and that my manic phases are RAGE-fuled and how I can fly off the handle over the stupidest shit.<br /> <br /> And that call helped us BOTH get a little bit better.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, never hide it. Tell your story, even if it bites you in the ass later (which mine has a lot lately). The more people QUIT hiding their mental problems like they're a wanted criminal, the more people get to NOT treat it like a horrible thing to be turned against you.<br /> <br /> K, done preaching, go about your business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 03-19-2015, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T23:43:14-07:00","id":450208,"title":"","content":"Thanks, everyone. Glad I didn't rub anyone the wrong way with my comparatively simple problems.<br /> <br /> I managed to get a meeting with my associate supervisor, who has a bit more experience dealing with schools and a more practical orientation than my principle (who's off sick), she really helped me get an idea of how to proceed with my project on a practical basis, and helped come up with some alternatives if for some reason that doesn't work out. Also she went over my timetable and pointed out that I'm not technically &quot;due&quot; to actually start data-gathering until June/July, which is a good couple months away, which I'd somehow missed. So, that was a big help.<br /> <br /> I still don't have any sense of people, and being in crowds still makes me have mini- or not-so-mini-freakouts, and I still don't have any better ways to address my stress levels or the resultant anger in the future, but even just being able to address one aspect, or even just have someone listen and try to help, even if it's only with one issue, has calmed the stress a bit. Which is something. If nothing else it's bought me time before I'm likely to explode over something irrelevant. Breathing room is good, as the drowning man would have said if he wasn't, you know, busy drowning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T10:49:31-07:00","id":459155,"title":"","content":"*hugs her new meds* Seriously Zoloft has been the best thing to ever be given to me. I was worried about the possibility of a manic episode but since its unclear if i am really bi-polar we took that risk. No manic episodes and its been almost two weeks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm feeling FAR less anxiety and my depression is lessening which is fucking amazing. I should have tried an anti depressant sooner cause wow. I'm actually getting out of bed every day at a resonable time, doing my chores, and smiling more. I'm even less grumpy overall, no extreme fits of murderous rage, or two hour long screaming fits over small shit. I think it helps to that I stick to a schedule, am drinking more water, and trying hard to get better for the sake of my child. I dont ever want her to see me crazy and that is enough to get me to go to therapy and take my meds and try HARD to get better.<br /> <br /> I know its not mania as its not crazy energy or rage filled outbursts. I just feel normal. Its a weird feeling and its taking adjusting to get used to feeling, well not crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T16:36:59-07:00","id":459481,"title":"","content":"Good to hear, Scelesta <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At the risk of revealing my own ignorance, I was under the impression that doctors were often reluctant to prescribe, well, anything, if you're pregnant? I guess either I was wrong, or you found one who recognise you needed the meds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T19:17:47-07:00","id":459595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=459481#post459481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good to hear, Scelesta <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At the risk of revealing my own ignorance, I was under the impression that doctors were often reluctant to prescribe, well, anything, if you're pregnant? I guess either I was wrong, or you found one who recognise you needed the meds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> oh no they are crazy reluctant to prescribe anything, but zoloft is one my doc usually gives to pregnant women for anxiety so he was okay with that...if I was trying to get on anything else it would be an argument over risk vs need lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T16:01:55-07:00","id":462763,"title":"","content":"deleted by the guy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 01-23-2018, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:41:48-07:00","id":462888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=462763#post462763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I'm going off the deep end. Yesterday I had a voice in my head, and it was my own. It compelled me to start writing about how I am a fractured human being. I specifically wrote about my various personalities. I've felt dreamy ever since. The problem I'm having is that my various personalities are almost entirely made up of lies. I lie to everyone about everything. I don't know the last time I told the truth except to my psychiatrist. I project a fake me everyday to deal with the world. I don't even know who I am or what I'm doing anymore. I was Joe yesterday, I think I'm neeto today, not CK, not Aaron, neeto. I have 2 fucking online personalities for fucks sake. Things are looking odd again, like I'm looking through a fish eye lense but at least I'm not viewing the world through that bizarre water filter like the other day. I'm having second thoughts of even publishing this. Its probably just grounds for ridicule. I already feel the anxiety of being mocked. fuck</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to mock you. /hug","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T03:18:52-07:00","id":472468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=462763#post462763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I'm going off the deep end. Yesterday I had a voice in my head, and it was my own. It compelled me to start writing about how I am a fractured human being. I specifically wrote about my various personalities. I've felt dreamy ever since. The problem I'm having is that my various personalities are almost entirely made up of lies. I lie to everyone about everything. I don't know the last time I told the truth except to my psychiatrist. I project a fake me everyday to deal with the world. I don't even know who I am or what I'm doing anymore. I was Joe yesterday, I think I'm neeto today, not CK, not Aaron, neeto. I have 2 fucking online personalities for fucks sake. Things are looking odd again, like I'm looking through a fish eye lense but at least I'm not viewing the world through that bizarre water filter like the other day. I'm having second thoughts of even publishing this. Its probably just grounds for ridicule. I already feel the anxiety of being mocked. fuck</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, there's a body of literature that suggests not only do we all tell lies to each other and ourselves to manage our lives and place in society, but that this is downright beneficial, and to not results in pretty serious issues for ourselves and others.<br /> <br /> What this means, I leave to you. Personally, I take from it that since stories are such a crucial aspect of the human psyche, and we use them to deal with and make meaning from our experiences, telling lies (which is really just another story) is a natural extension of that, with no more moral dimension than writing an e-mail. But then, my thesis is all about stories, so I would think that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T13:23:19-07:00","id":473279,"title":"","content":"So apparently I've been psychotic for a couple of weeks. I told my therapist about the voices I've been hearing lately, and admitted to her that they have suggested that others wanted to punish me and take away the voices from me. I told her about some of the weird hallucinations I've heard at work, and getting really paranoid there and on Easter too. She kind of hinted that I may need to go to the hospital, well she asked me if it was bad enough to warrant going. I said no, but I honestly don't think it's really in my hands. She just said ok, and wants me to write a list of reasons why I stayed away from my family on Easter to help me see what was psychotic and what was genuine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T21:20:57-07:00","id":477490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=462888#post462888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not going to mock you. /hug</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Promie is a good homie. -wipes a tear away to maintain his (questionable) masculine image-<br /> <br /> On that subject....are we ALL GOING CRAZY?? I don't mean to make assumptions about anyone's personal battles, but it seems like some sort of collective mental shit has hit a very large fan. Am I just being paranoid and connecting too many suppositional dots here? Maybe &quot;going crazy&quot; is too harsh a term....<br /> <br /> It just seems like more than a few of us have hit upon strange and difficult times....<br /> <br /> I just want you to know... if you consider me your friend here, then that means I'm your friend. Period. I don't have a life outside the walls I confine myself in, save for my interactions with all of you. I care, and I worry. I also ignore this place for periods of time while my mind crumbles into fragments...just like I do the world within these walls.<br /> <br /> If you'd like to talk to me and I haven't responded to a message, or haven't begun a dialogue myself, keep trying or give up, I suppose. It really depends on how much it matters to you. I'll make it easy. My number is 505-316-0715. Don't worry about my phone bill. I answer the phone as much as I can, text or voice.<br /> <br /> \u200bI was just about to wonder aloud(&quot;in text from&quot; doesn't quite have the same ring to it.) just why in the name of Bob I'd give out my number and invite everyone and anyone who wishes to contact me the power to easily do so on a most personal level. Then I remembered...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":".  NOW WITH CORRECT INFORMATION! 04-13-2015, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T13:11:53-07:00","id":478262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=477490#post477490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll make it easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're a good guy, Az.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:35:42-07:00","id":479072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=477490#post477490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Promie is a good homie. -wipes a tear away to maintain his (questionable) masculine image-<br /> <br /> On that subject....are we ALL GOING CRAZY?? I don't mean to make assumptions about anyone's personal battles, but it seems like some sort of collective mental shit has hit a very large fan. Am I just being paranoid and connecting too many suppositional dots here? Maybe &quot;going crazy&quot; is too harsh a term....<br /> <br /> It just seems like more than a few of us have hit upon strange and difficult times....<br /> <br /> I just want you to know... if you consider me your friend here, then that means I'm your friend. Period. I don't have a life outside the walls I confine myself in, save for my interactions with all of you. I care, and I worry. I also ignore this place for periods of time while my mind crumbles into fragments...just like I do the world within these walls.<br /> <br /> If you'd like to talk to me and I haven't responded to a message, or haven't begun a dialogue myself, keep trying or give up, I suppose. It really depends on how much it matters to you. I'll make it easy. My number is 504-316-0715. Don't worry about my phone bill. I answer the phone as much as I can, text or voice.<br /> <br /> \u200bI was just about to wonder aloud(&quot;in text from&quot; doesn't quite have the same ring to it.) just why in the name of Bob I'd give out my number and invite everyone and anyone who wishes to contact me the power to easily do so on a most personal level. Then I remembered...</div> </div> </div> </div>Better respond when I text, or I'll have to send the Brute Squad out after you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T12:18:36-07:00","id":479337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=479072#post479072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better respond when I text, or I'll have to send the Brute Squad out after you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I could totally use the exercise that said Brute Squad would help me with, I promise to answer, PB mein bro-ham. <br /> <br /> On that subject, I drunkenly fucked up my own area code in that post. Because I'm a winner. Edit time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T13:04:05-07:00","id":479377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=478262#post478262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're a good guy, Az.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. I wish I was, though. I hope that's helping me work my way toward one day being the real thing.<br /> <br /> Thanks, Jim. You're great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T13:13:49-07:00","id":479393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=479377#post479377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. I wish I was, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, yeah, go ahead and argue with me on this one. I know what I know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T09:55:04-07:00","id":488390,"title":"","content":"So this isn't much of a &quot;I'm freaking out and need to vent&quot; post but more of a... like, a realization, I guess. As a reminder for those of us who don't recall my last post here or don't know me (I don't blame you; I hardly ever post), I'm a veteran with... well, I was already depressive before I joined, and the myriad stresses of combat didn't help. I hesitate to say PTSD, but it probably is.<br /> <br /> There's one table I like to seat at in my university's food hall and that's because it's the only one where I can have my back to a non-reflective wall. Every other wall in the place is a window or a glass door to another room, and I just can't sit there without having something solid behind me. I've thought about making the complaint to the staff and while I still contemplate doing so, it isn't really something I can reasonably fault them for, because the vast majority of people aren't going to care, the people in charge of the layout and design of these buildings included. In all likelihood they're just not aware this is would ever be an issue. I know I wouldn't have thought about it before. Anyway, I guess the point of all of this is, like, mental health issues can make some of the littlest details into a big deal of personal comfort, and I wish I didn't have to deal with things like this every day. Life's hard enough, ya know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T11:01:49-07:00","id":488488,"title":"","content":"@kongurous I have the same problem with non-secure walls at my back. I'd much prefer something opaque, very solid and preferably reinforced. It's a hyper-awareness issue for me. I won't play amateur doctor and say that, like me, you have PTSD. I will say that it's one strong indicator, especially considering a combat background. I'll probably say more later, but my headache is making me nauseated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T12:37:08-07:00","id":488607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=488488#post488488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@kongurous I have the same problem with non-secure walls at my back. I'd much prefer something opaque, very solid and preferably reinforced. It's a hyper-awareness issue for me. I won't play amateur doctor and say that, like me, you have PTSD. I will say that it's one strong indicator, especially considering a combat background. I'll probably say more later, but my headache is making me nauseated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I appreciate your words anyway. Like it's nice to know I'm not alone and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T20:46:56-07:00","id":488998,"title":"","content":"You're not. I've never served in the military, and while I *can* sit at a window seat or one of the open ones, I really really really don't want to. And if I'm sitting next to a window I'm going to be continually watching the crowd on all sides of it, defeating most of the purpose of a wall. I... have some issues with crowds and people.<br /> <br /> Point is, you're not alone, and it's not just a PTSD thing, or a veteran thing. There are myriad reasons why someone does NOT want to be sitting in the open, and maybe letting the place know isn't a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T23:45:33-07:00","id":489115,"title":"","content":"Depression sucks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> all i've wanted to do lately is sleep, barely want to get out bed, i'm lonely and feel empty. I dont care about much of anything anymore, i hardly eat as my appitite is gone even though I KNOW I NEED to...My OB is gonna be mad at me. The only thing that makes me smile is when my little one moves around or kicks me..but then i'm reminded in a few weeks i'll be a mother and that makes me more depressed...I keep thinking i'm going to be a bad mother, i'm selfish, i hate anything that disrupts my precious routines...what if i hate my baby? What if i cant do this? I'm going to fuck my daughter up just like i am... I skipped my last psych appointment cause i was to depressed to get out of bed and go, my therapist is booked up full untill june so i'm shit out of luck on that one, cant see another either as their office is super busy and i cant go to another office cause the others are to far away and I KNOW i wont go if i have to take the bus cause fuck all if i'm getting on a bus when i piss my pants walking two blocks to the fucking store.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T00:05:52-07:00","id":489126,"title":"","content":"______________________________________","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":".  I'm sorry. Pain is no excuse. 04-23-2015, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T11:20:22-07:00","id":489669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=488998#post488998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not. I've never served in the military, and while I *can* sit at a window seat or one of the open ones, I really really really don't want to. And if I'm sitting next to a window I'm going to be continually watching the crowd on all sides of it, defeating most of the purpose of a wall. I... have some issues with crowds and people.<br /> <br /> Point is, you're not alone, and it's not just a PTSD thing, or a veteran thing. There are myriad reasons why someone does NOT want to be sitting in the open, and maybe letting the place know isn't a bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I didn't have this problem until I came back, so for me, it's probably a consequence of open spaces being dangerous, but I get that others will feel similarly for different reasons.<br /> <br /> (holy run on sentences batman)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T00:51:57-07:00","id":490291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=489126#post489126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">______________________________________</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's faintly ominious.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I should have said this earlier, but frankly I just don't really know what to say. I don't really know you so well, and while I've had my hard times, they don't even compare to your situation. I can say, however, that what little I've seen of you I've liked. You seem compassionate and open, willing to support others despite your own issues, and that really is a very rare quality. I know only a few people who will support someone else <i>at all</i>, and exactly zero people who are still willing to do it when they're even moderately stressed out.<br /> <br /> If more people were like you, then I truly believe the world would be a better place. That's really all I can say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T17:05:13-07:00","id":491082,"title":"","content":"...Thank you, Allan53. I want to say more. ....I want to learn how to be told something like that without my mind immediately screaming at me &quot;You show such a pretty mask. You're the ugliest soul to ever take a breath. If they saw you, everyone you know would flee screaming, if your bastard rage allows them the choice at all. You're a monster, you know that? If ever there was such a thing as so terrifyingly ugly and deadening that it was almost beautiful in its sheer viral tainting of the world around it, it'd be you. If you loved them, you'd stop existing.&quot; Those are just the ones that came to mind just now... that are comfortable enough to type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T20:47:05-07:00","id":491230,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't really know how to meaningfully respond to that. Personally, I take a view that a person is what that person does, so there's no such thing as being a bad person who just pretends to be good (assuming that 'pretence' happens all the time): if a person gives $100 to a charity, then that is a generous thing. I don't care if they're doing it out of altruism or self-glorification (of course, their subsequent actions are relevant as well: if they jump around saying &quot;look at me, look at me!&quot; then that's relevant too). But, from what very, very little I understand, these sorts of ideas don't really respond to rationality or evidence. So there's not much point in going down that line, because, well, first I'd just be repeating myself, and second, while I do believe it to be true (I am not a nice person, and don't say things I don't believe), I doubt your brain would 'accept' it, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> I will say, however, that what your brain says doesn't jibe with my, admittedly limited, observations, and I'm reasonably good at figuring out peoples motivations, and what I get from you is that you genuinely want to help people have a better life. Be that from a need to justify your existence or just being a good person, doesn't matter. My life is still better for it, and I'm not going to nitpick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T10:47:47-07:00","id":495004,"title":"","content":"I have a low opinion of myself. (Surprise, surprise.) This makes it hard to, say, make friends because I feel like I'm afflicting them with my presence; I feel like they'd rather I were not there. This comes up right now because I was just talking to a professor whom I am quite fond of and I believe, on some level, likes me. But I felt the intense urge to get out of his office as quickly as possible in order to let him be rid of my presence. That bothers me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T13:43:33-07:00","id":495140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=495004#post495004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a low opinion of myself. (Surprise, surprise.) This makes it hard to, say, make friends because I feel like I'm afflicting them with my presence; I feel like they'd rather I were not there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm right there with you, brother. I've been kind of using my dad's death as an excuse not to write e-mails to people I really need to write e-mails to so I can apologize to them for my behavior, which has been prompted by this belief that people are better off without me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:08:04-07:00","id":495253,"title":"","content":"For my silly little brothers here that think such bad things about themselves.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.imgion.com/images/01/Bear-Hug-.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 04-29-2015, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T06:19:27-07:00","id":496214,"title":"","content":"AzraelFirestorm you are a nice person. You are supportive of others and no matter what your mind says this is a fact. It takes a lot more than anger issues to bother me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T06:24:18-07:00","id":496216,"title":"","content":"Jim and brejedi26 low self esteem is not a good thing. I never feel like what I say is heard, but I know that it is. Both of you enrich others lives without knowing it. And yes I suffer from low self esteem, but I'm getting better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T09:53:32-07:00","id":500513,"title":"","content":"Yesterday I went to a therapist for the first time in four years. I talked to him about my symptoms of depression and low self-worth, and he responded with blunt talk and well-placed profanity. It was like getting psychiatric help from an octogenarian version of the dad from <i>That 70s Show</i>, complete with frequent use of the word &quot;dumbass.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> In other words: Dude was worth every penny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","user":"Daydreamer","date":". 05-02-2015, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T09:42:24-07:00","id":509061,"title":"","content":"Lately I've been cycling fast leaving me exhausted and cranky. I also started talking to a girl recently and fearing that she was intentionally ignoring me I called her. She was apparently with her boyfriend she never mentioned to me until that time. I feel like laughing at the fact that this has happened again to me mixed with the urge to beat myself to a pulp or just sit and cry. What I don't understand is why she would waiut until then to mention she has a boyfriend. She could've made things less awkward and I might would still be interested in hanging out with her regardless of that but using it as a bomb for when I finally got the courage up to call, I feel trampled.<br /> <br /> My arms are covered in blood again, I wasn't expecting anything like this on my vacation. I feel like just leaving running away from everything. I haven't enjoyed anything in months then this girl came out of no where and I was enjoying her company. tbh, I thought I had a chance. I should realize now that I'm going to live and die alone. Since thats the truth I would rather the death come now to put me out of my misery. I lament my every breath and wish for the swift hand of death to take me and end my suffering.<br /> <br /> I don't know how to describe how through I am with life. If a masked gunman showed up right now I would yell fuck you shoot me I dont give a fuck, I would probably help him. I don't wanna go back to the looney bin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","user":"cerealkiller","date":". 05-09-2015, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T12:57:22-07:00","id":509200,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Udf9NeXqkyA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Udf9NeXqkyA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Udf9NeXqkyA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/Udf9NeXqkyA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Listen to it.<br /> <br /> Text me, you morose motherfuckers. I love you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":".  Yeah. This is a sober editing of a drunk but heartfelt post. It happens. 05-10-2015, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T11:17:26-07:00","id":510900,"title":"","content":"So you're in the bowels of a depression or maybe it's just a bad case of self-pity, you're honestly not sure you can tell the difference between them any more, when you catch yourself tallying up all the friends and family members you have and mentally whining to yourself, <i>Why aren't they helping me?</i> There's more to that thought, something about how they're not helping you because even if they don't say it aloud or even realize it they secretly understand you're a lost cause, but you don't quite finish that thought because the part of your brain that gets outraged when it sees injustice heard that first sentence and has had enough of your crap. It won't let you tell yourself the hurtful yet comforting* lie that the people who matter to you have begun to hate you, because that's unfair to them. It demands that you accept they don't help you because you've been doing everything in your power to conceal what's been wrong with you and what you're going through, <i>and,</i> it continues with relentless, merciless logic, <i>this self-pity is a shield you use to deflect responsibility for your actions. You need to look at yourself and admit you're a bad person without trying to flagellate yourself as you do it, because let's face it, you're doing that so the pain will deflect your attention from the actual problems that you need to take steps to address but have not taken because you're afraid of failure and would rather provoke people into rejecting you than risk them rejecting you on their own terms.</i><br /> <br /> You can't un-hear some things once you've heard them, so you have to deal with what you now know about yourself. You take a step back and look at yourself, trying not to do the depression thing instead of using depression as an excuse to rub salt in your eyes until you're too blind to do a proper self-evaluation, and you realize that a lot of your pain and your issues are real--you're genuinely lonely to the point of heartbreak but you can't bring yourself to let anyone in because you're also genuinely terrified of humanity, convinced that they must see what an awful person you are and want to punish you for your evil as much as you do; you're not kidding when you think to yourself about how your death would only improve the general quality of the world--but both the real and the contrived issues are being used as smokescreens to conceal the long, hard work you need to do on yourself to be a better person. Somewhere along the way, you chose to wallow in your own failings because it's an easier route than self-improvement.<br /> <br /> The cold, clear truth is you're a weak person with a lot of room for, not to mention need of, improvement, and no amount of depression changes or really even excuses the fact. You have to pick yourself up, clean yourself off, and try to be better than you are not for the people you were unfairly maligning a few minutes ago (though certainly they deserve a better friend than the one you've been to them, and as you look back at the way you've treated them through without the filter of self-hate clouding your lens, you kind of despair of ever being able to pay them back what you owe them) but because the way you're living isn't right.<br /> <br /> You wonder if this might be that &quot;self-respect&quot; concept you've heard of but never in your thirty-six years of life really managed to comprehend.<br /> <br /> <br /> *That things can be comforting to you because they hurt you is something you try not to think about too much because the implications are kind of terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T13:36:50-07:00","id":511100,"title":"","content":"*doesn't know what to say, but wants to show support to his friends*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:29:05-07:00","id":511230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=511100#post511100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*doesn't know what to say, but wants to show support to his friends*</div> </div> </div> </div>Been there, Jeddy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T09:09:31-07:00","id":519644,"title":"","content":"I hate feeling like i'm no help...we were in a car accident yesterday. My fiance is learning to drive and was driving, pulled out into an intersection and didnt see an oncoming car, (both me and his mom, the person teaching him to drive, did but by the time we saw it, it was to late) He made a smart judgment call that likely saved us from getting hurt(Had he sped up the oncoming car would have hit my door, and i was in the back seat..), he hit the breaks rather then speed up to try to avoid the car. The other car took evasive action quick enough that it was a narrow miss in hitting us,however the other car ended up crashing into a light pole and another car. The car we were in was fine because of this, but one lady in the car hit by the other car hit her head on her window <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> He is so upset with himself and i dont know what to say to make him feel better, He got a ticket, but thats the least of the problem, he says because he failed to notice teh car he could have killed me nad the baby and now he doesnt want to drive anymore. <br /> <br /> I'm useless, the only thing i could figure out to say was that it was okay for him to take a step back and not drive again for a while. Car wrecks are scary and he needs time to calm down before trying again if he wants to, otherwise I will learn cause he doesnt have to always be strong and do everything. But, he's depressed, and i dont know how to help. <br /> <br /> I'm hiding a majority of my anxiety cause i cant bother him with it. I was so freaked out by the accident cause I saw how close it was. I didnt sleep well last night and i'm still shaken up over it, i can only imagine he doesnt feel any better either. For once i have to be the strong one because he needs me to be, but its not easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T12:11:50-07:00","id":530185,"title":"","content":"I decided to stop taking my antidepressants. I am experiencing negative side effects and I don't feel like they're helping that much. Over the past couple of weeks, I have been thinking about suicide a lot. So I figure if I'm having these thoughts anyway, and experiencing negative side effects, then may as well have the thoughts and not experience the negative side effects. I informed Arc of my decision last night and told him to keep an eye on me and if he thought things were getting out of hand to (metaphorically) slap me upside the head. So... yeah. We'll see how it goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T13:34:22-07:00","id":530268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=530185#post530185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I decided to stop taking my antidepressants. I am experiencing negative side effects and I don't feel like they're helping that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please stay on them until your doctor has created a step-down program for you. People's brains change when they just go cold turkey off their meds. Sometimes they don't change back.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T17:45:14-07:00","id":530444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=530268#post530268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please stay on them until your doctor has created a step-down program for you. People's brains change when they just go cold turkey off their meds. Sometimes they don't change back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going off cold turkey. I am stepping down over the course of two weeks. Started today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T09:35:19-07:00","id":535674,"title":"","content":"I know this is trival compared to others problems right now but hey..<br /> <br /> My anxiety is through the roof. Tommorow i'm being induced, bright an early i'll be at the hospital at 5:30 am induced around 6, then labor for however long it takes before she gets her butt out of me.<br /> I'm nervous...I have been for weeks but now that its less then a day away i cant think straight...I keep worrying about everything, I DONT like not having control of a situation and labor is IMPOSSIBLE to control, it goes on its own timeframe...If I end up needing a c-section god forbid i'm scared they wont put e to sleep first, if they dont I swear I will likely start screaming in terror as the whole idea fucking scares me enough as it is,being awake during it? OH fuck that...fuck that. I'm looking forward to having my body back, i really am, but....<br /> <br /> I cant wait to meet my little future gamer, but i'm also getting sad at the same time..I&quot;m going to miss laying in bed feeling her little kicks inside my tummy, knowing she is safe in there, protected from the world and its many hurts. I'm going into this knowing this is the closest i will ever be to her again knowing in a day or so she will own my heart for the rest of my life more then she already does..and then i worry that i'm going to fail as a mother, what if i cant handle this? I've wanted children since i was young, but dear god what if i cant do this? This little human will depend on me for everything for a long time, it will be my job to ensure she is fed, and loved, and cared for, what if i fuck up?<br /> <br /> Maybe i'm being stupid. I dont know...I wnt her to have a better life then i did, i want her to feel love and safety but i'm scared that when my hormones crash i'll crash, then what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T04:39:32-07:00","id":536803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=530185#post530185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I decided to stop taking my antidepressants. I am experiencing negative side effects and I don't feel like they're helping that much. Over the past couple of weeks, I have been thinking about suicide a lot. So I figure if I'm having these thoughts anyway, and experiencing negative side effects, then may as well have the thoughts and not experience the negative side effects. I informed Arc of my decision last night and told him to keep an eye on me and if he thought things were getting out of hand to (metaphorically) slap me upside the head. So... yeah. We'll see how it goes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't want to intrude on your decisions, Brjedi, but exactly how long have u been on therapy? Because in its first stages antidepressants will give you some energy back (so is a very,very delicate moment as the afflicted could have now the energy -and energy he/she didn't previously had, due to depression- to go for suicide) but their antidepressive effect will actually take from 2 to 3 weeks or so to kick in. Maybe the problem could be the dosification or even the antidepressant you're taking. It could also have to be something with your current ansiolitic. As i said, i don't want to intrude. Just coming here to let you a friendly &quot;hang in there mate&quot; and a cyberhug. How is the process going?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My anxiety is through the roof. Tommorow i'm being induced, bright an early i'll be at the hospital at 5:30 am induced around 6, then labor for however long it takes before she gets her butt out of me.<br /> I'm nervous...I have been for weeks but now that its less then a day away i cant think straight...I keep worrying about everything, I DONT like not having control of a situation and labor is IMPOSSIBLE to control, it goes on its own timeframe...If I end up needing a c-section god forbid i'm scared they wont put e to sleep first, if they dont I swear I will likely start screaming in terror as the whole idea fucking scares me enough as it is,being awake during it? OH fuck that...fuck that. I'm looking forward to having my body back, i really am, but....<br /> <br /> I cant wait to meet my little future gamer, but i'm also getting sad at the same time..I&quot;m going to miss laying in bed feeling her little kicks inside my tummy, knowing she is safe in there, protected from the world and its many hurts. I'm going into this knowing this is the closest i will ever be to her again knowing in a day or so she will own my heart for the rest of my life more then she already does..and then i worry that i'm going to fail as a mother, what if i cant handle this? I've wanted children since i was young, but dear god what if i cant do this? This little human will depend on me for everytthing for a long time, it will be my job to ensure she is fed, and loved, and cared for, what if i fuck up?<br /> <br /> Maybe i'm being stupid. I dont know...I wnt her to have a better life then i did, i want her to feel love and safety but i'm scared that when my hormones crash i'll crash, then what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anxiety is normal, as you say labor is almost impossible to control (doctors have a pair of tricks under the white coat: oxytocin is one of them). Worrying about c-section is very,very normal, but beyond its logical risks is a very safe (and tried-and-true) procedure. I know three friends of mine that went through it, and they are perfectly healthy now... and their babies aswell. Worrying about your future baby's life is normal. When your hormones crash you'll crash. But don't worry, you'll recover just like all those previous times. And don't worry: your baby won't be alone while you fightfor her and for yourself. She'll have friends, family and of course, you. And she will be strong aswell. Now, care only about your labor and the work is before you. Best of luck and strength to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T06:02:01-07:00","id":536893,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=536803#post536803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't want to intrude on your decisions, Brjedi, but exactly how long have u been on therapy?</div> </div> </div> </div>About two years. I've been on the current* regimen of pills for 4-5 months.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How is the process going? </div> </div> </div></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Seems to be going fine thus far.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">*&quot;current&quot; meaning what I was doing before I started the step-down process</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":1041,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","user":"brjedi26","date":". 06-02-2015, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T14:23:39-07:00","id":537425,"title":"","content":"I suffer from Bipolar II. I was diagnosed with Mild Depressive disorder in my early 20's and thought it was manageable. Then a couple years ago, I had a terrible breakdown...it was Diagnosed as extreme depressive disorder a year ago... then after Therapy and meeting with a Psychistrist and lots of observation, it was determined I have Bipolar II...<br /> <br /> So I was put on a mood stabilizer along with my anti-depressant. The results? Wonderful, I felt more in control of my life than ever before.<br /> <br /> Of course yesterday my Insurance was cancelled so I have no idea how I'm going to afford my medication. I'm trying to get it reinstated, so here's hoping! I really don't want to go off my pills since they've had such a positive effect on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T06:55:37-07:00","id":541098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=536893#post536893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About two years. I've been on the current* regimen of pills for 4-5 months.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that dissatisfaction with the pills effect has been present all the time, this last 4-5 months? Why the change from the previous ~1 year and a half regimen? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seems to be going fine thus far. </div> </div> </div>How are you feeling a week later from the start of the process? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:17:46-07:00","id":541137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=541098#post541098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that dissatisfaction with the pills effect has been present all the time, this last 4-5 months? Why the change from the previous ~1 year and a half regimen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was started out on Lexapro.* I was never really satisfied with it, but took it for 3-4 months because of the time delay in seeing any effect from the drugs. I started out on a lower dosage, and then later increased it. After I was still dissatisfied with the increased dosage, I was switched to Zoloft. The process to switch these took, I think, two weeks. (As a side note here, the times when I've changed drugs have been somewhat dictated by school semesters, as I/we have wanted to avoid changing the drugs during important times like finals because I/we want to avoid any unforeseen consequences affecting my performance in school. While the current drug may not be working, at least we know the way in which it is not working and can deal with it.) The Zoloft worked for awhile, but then I started feeling crappy again, so we increased the dosage. Iterate that again. Then we decide to reduce the Zoloft and start Effexor supplementally. Increase dosage of Effexor. That leads us to now.<br /> tl;dr<br /> Start Lexapro.<br /> Increase Lexapro.<br /> Switch from Lexapro to Zoloft.<br /> Increase Zoloft.<br /> Increase Zoloft.<br /> Decrease Zoloft, add Effexor.<br /> Increase Effexor.<br /> Now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How are you feeling a week later from the start of the process? </div> </div> </div>Still okay. Yesterday began the decreased dosage of Effexor. 8 days remain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*Any drugs mentioned, I have actually taken the generic replacement, but I find that name harder to remember so I don't bother.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T16:11:05-07:00","id":543183,"title":"","content":"I'm suprised, as Lexapro is considered highly succesful in the majority of patients (compares favorably, in fact, with Zoloft and Effexor), but then, we humans are complicated machines and there's always the exception. :S Keep us informed about the process, i hope everything will go fine... but check your state and take care, ^^ One cyberhugh for you. <br /> <br /> You too, by the way, Orphan81. I hope you'll manage to get your insurance reinstated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T16:51:01-07:00","id":543228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=543183#post543183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm suprised, as Lexapro is considered highly succesful in the majority of patients</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lexapro was not cut because it was failing to help with the depression, but rather because the doctor felt it was making me have more mood swings that were tending toward the angry and violent end of the spectrum. And it really fucked up my sleep. (If I took it in the evening, I couldn't sleep until 2am and if I took it in the morning, I fell asleep at 7pm. Theoretically I could have figured out the ideal time to take it, but then there was also the issue of mood swings.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T16:59:38-07:00","id":543233,"title":"","content":"I found Fetzima to be a miracle worker, after actual decades of dealing with other medications.<br /> <br /> There was only one side effect, excessive sweating. At random, as well as when doing anything physical, just wild pouring of sweat like I'd just ran a mile. It was ridiculous, but worth it, and the sweating went away after a month or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T18:51:48-07:00","id":543317,"title":"","content":"Excessive sweating is one of the major annoyances that I'm dealing with right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T15:47:02-07:00","id":549461,"title":"","content":"Back in my early or mid-twenties, when I first started seeing a doctor and getting medication for my depression, I tried to talk to my parents about it. I remember it was a car trip somewhere (probably to my gran's, but that's a guess rather than a memory) with just the three of us. I tried talking to them honestly about it, explaining how much I genuinely hated myself and how much everything I did seemed wrong and dirty and shameful; how deeply I believed I was incapable of doing good or being good or accomplishing anything that wasn't selfish and low. I don't remember Dad's reaction to this, but I know Mom started crying and most of the trip passed in silence, after which we never spoke of it again.<br /> <br /> I'd like to say that was the moment when I learned it's not okay to not be okay, just because it would be dramatically appropriate, but that's not when I learned that. The lesson is too deeply ingrained in me to be anything other than a response to a lifetime of messages that one mustn't ever be weak. This was nothing more than the time I learned I couldn't talk to my parents about it. Sorry, dramatic appropriateness.<br /> <br /> I hadn't thought of the incident in years. It just came to mind today for no particular reason, and I wanted to take a moment to tell all of you something:<br /> <br /> It's okay to not be okay.<br /> <br /> If that was on your mind at all, just saying, it's okay. You don't have to be okay all the time. It's alright not to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:50:30-07:00","id":553668,"title":"","content":"...Thanks, Jim. For sharing and letting me off my own guilt-hook. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T22:09:14-07:00","id":553885,"title":"","content":"Any time, Az.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"atta