sed on that statement, I'd say it's definitely time that you sought out a counselor. That sounds like depression speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T20:55:12-07:00","id":560304,"title":"","content":"PS: dealing with depression by drinking alcohol is a terrible idea. Alcohol will only make this worse. (At least that's my understanding.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T16:18:49-07:00","id":561313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=560304#post560304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alcohol will only make this worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's technically possible to go either way, but yeah, alcohol as a drug is categorized as a depressant and ought to be avoided by people with depression issues.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T21:12:06-07:00","id":561540,"title":"","content":"So, how do I go about this? Or go about paying for it?<br /> <br /> PS. Im here at work going about my assigned tasks fighting the urge to cry as I do. I dont know how much longer I can keep this up. Its been a while sice its gotten this bad....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 06-20-2015, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T22:01:39-07:00","id":561560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=561540#post561540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how do I go about this? Or go about paying for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've... got me there. My school provides free counseling for students so I've never had to worry about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> PS. Im here at work going about my assigned tasks fighting the urge to cry as I do. I dont know how much longer I can keep this up. Its been a while sice its gotten this bad.... </div> </div> </div>I know them feels. I ended up coming home today and crying myself to sleep repeatedly for several hours. Fortunately, I can afford to do this right now. I just have to make sure to get things done eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T14:59:33-07:00","id":563427,"title":"","content":"Well, looking into where to find help and already getting frustrated. Not seeing any listed on the site I found i think I can trust.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I may be getting worse. Dont feel as bad but finding I'm stsrying to take my problems out on my friend kaylee. And while I have explained my problem to her, she says I'm getting a bit too much to handle. So I need to get help soon. I dont want to drive off another friend....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T21:17:29-07:00","id":564980,"title":"","content":"I certainly hope you can find the help you need, Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T05:29:18-07:00","id":565258,"title":"","content":"There are lists of low-income mental health providers available online. I will look one up if I haven't heard from you by the time I get home, vampire hunter D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T15:39:05-07:00","id":565805,"title":"","content":"Here you go, vampire hunter D: <a href=\"http://www.mentalhealthamerica.net/finding-therapy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.mentalhealthamerica.net/finding-therapy</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T23:27:35-07:00","id":569995,"title":"","content":"My problems seem tribal compared to others so I feel an posting but whatever...<br /> <br /> I'm a mess. I'm feeling depressed north I gonna hurt myself or others kind though just a I don't wan/feel like I can't do this. Every night I'm the one who gets up and takes care of the baby so my fiance gets enough sleep to work. I take care of her every need all day. The brief moments where she doesn't wan me to hold her or feed her I spend cleaning the house which everyday manage to acquire an explosion of baby clothes etc that are a tripping hazard. I'm trying so hard to be strong but it's hard. It's selfish of me I know but I want to be able to take a bath when I want or play a sank video game or ducks go swimming but can't do this things cause even Inc my fiance gets home I get only a little bit of help and a assloaad of whining jaw hurting or that he's tired. Don't get wrong he does help an is a great dad but if he complains one more time I'm gonna deck him. I barely get much sleep, since he won't let me give her formula in force to breastfeed which means my own body isn't even mine and having someone come watch her so I can have some time.to myself.won't work. I cry everyday out of exhaustion an frustration. I want to curl up in my bed an not get up not have to deal with my crying daughter o th dirty house. My body aches from sitting in uncomfortable positions to feed or rock her. I'm constantly stressed over if she's eating enough or in pain from being gassy. I nerd a break or I'm going to loos my mind. <br /> <br /> This is probably uneasily posted I have a brutal headache an mad it works by having. Crying fit when she described used she didn't want to b put down yet again..her daddy has her now a I flat out refused to handle has I needed a bath to calm.this headache. I'm a Terri blel..mothrt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T20:06:38-07:00","id":575958,"title":"","content":"Don't worry Scelesta, I'm about to one-up you in the Complaining About Trivial Crap stakes. At least your issue has a legitimate stressor behind it (one of the main reasons I never want to have kids is to avoid exactly where you are now). And from what infinitesimal amount I've been able to glean, just being stressed out and wanting some time to yourself doesn't a bad parent make, it's what you do as a result. Hanging in there, taking care of the screaming brat as best you can, even when massively stressed? That makes a good parent. Although it does <i>sound </i>like your fiance could take a little more of the load, even if it's only handling the kid for a couple hours while you chill out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: Re-reading this, I don't know if I communicated my point properly. I did not mean to imply that your issue was trivial, it's really not. I cannot imagine dealing with that kind of ongoing stress day after day, constantly. </div> </div> </div>A while ago (a few weeks) I realised how cripplingly lonely I am. I won't go into details, but essentially barring a not-really-a-relationship when I was 17 (over 10 years ago), I've never had a serious girlfriend. This is hardly surprising; I'm reasonably intelligent and I do try to be friendly to everyone, but I've got the physical attractiveness and personality of a stump, my social abilities are near zero, and I'm fairly solitary by nature. Not surprising no woman is interested and that's perfectly all right. I wouldn't want to spend time with me either. But it does mean that this damn need goes unsatisfied, and I'm still trying to work out a way to deal with it beyond ignoring it or getting angry; one only lasts so long, and the other isn't constructive. I've managed to get a little distance from it, so it isn't occupying my every waking thought, by really knuckling down on my thesis, but, well, something more embarrassing has started happening.<br /> <br /> Whenever I watch/listen/experience something that elicits an emotional reaction from me, even if it's positive, I'm overcome with the urge to burst into tears. Even if I'm watching an early episode of Madoka Magica, which aren't really all that tragic and actually kind of heartwarming. I have to turn it off and just breathe for a goodly while. This is particularly troubling because my thesis, as with much of psychology, is at least partially guided by emotion; granted, mostly recognising it in my interviewees, but still. So having to take a Spock approach is really affecting me there as well, although I am making some progress.<br /> <br /> I've considered going and talking to a psychologist, but that requires me to get a referral from a GP (and apart from that being a gigantic pain in the neck, I don't want to go up to a stranger and say &quot;I'm being a giant cry-baby&quot;), or find a way to adjust the insurance to allow me to just go to them, but apparently unless you want to check yourself into a hospital they're no help. And yes, I'm well aware of how rare health insurance is in the US; chalk that up to a combination of me being really, really spoiled and it actually being kind-of common in Australia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 07-01-2015, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T20:24:59-07:00","id":579387,"title":"","content":"I just spent much of today crying. I couldnt stop. And worse, I dont even really know what I'm sad about.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T21:55:07-07:00","id":579448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=579387#post579387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just spent much of today crying. I couldn't stop. And worse, I don't even really know what I'm sad about.....</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone else demanded you justify your feelings, would you think that person is kind of a prick? If so, then don't treat yourself the way that guy would. There doesn't always need to be a reason. That's why sometimes there isn't one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T22:50:49-07:00","id":579488,"title":"","content":"I'm.... getting worse again. Long time without an update. I'm going manic and hard. The problem is, I started drinking again. which was really what caused all the problems I was having before. Its self medication to push me lower down on the 10 - -10 meter I use to express where I'm at. 10 is hellishly manic, I've never reached it but I'm an angry irritable pissed of man at 4 so I don't want to see 10. 0 is perfect. neither manic or depressive. I spend a lot of time near -4 (up from -7/-8 almost constantly thanks meds). I'm trying to push myself down, not to go bad but because I'm at a 5 right now and I do not do manic well. I'm aggressive, mean (like just up and saying mean things like they don't hurt other people or make them feel like I hate them) irritated at everything. I want to get closer to 0. Medicine alone isn't doing it. I've got a meeting with my psychiatrist this month so hopefully we can figure out why my brain is trying to kill me again. I did a solid 6 months on the wagon. Would prefer to be up there than down in the gutter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T07:28:56-07:00","id":579805,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you're taking steps with a professional, 'killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T08:19:09-07:00","id":579846,"title":"","content":"Yea, glad you can acknowledge things aren't going well and are going to talk to someone about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T15:44:38-07:00","id":597442,"title":"","content":"Why is it people who claim to be your friend talk down to you in a condescending manner, then get mad when you call them on it?<br /> <br /> Why is it people attsck you and make fun of you when you ask for help?<br /> <br /> Why is it some people seem to think you should be happy at all times, and get mad when you're not?<br /> <br /> Why can't I have even one good friend? Or any friends?<br /> <br /> Why.....i dunno anymore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T06:08:02-07:00","id":599281,"title":"","content":"It feels like the only reason I haven't killed myself is because of how it would destroy everyone I care about.<br /> <br /> I can't live for myself anymore, I don't even know if I know how.<br /> I have become obsessed with the problems of the world, as a way of finding some meaning for my existence. But that only makes me feel worse.<br /> <br /> It's gotten to the point where I just want it to end. I want everything to stop and for everything to be alright for just once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:41:43-07:00","id":599537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=597442#post597442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why...I dunno anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have any answers, but I suspect you weren't looking for answers in the first place. I am sorry you are experiencing difficulties in your personal life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=599281#post599281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like the only reason I haven't killed myself is because of how it would destroy everyone I care about.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a quite dangerous state to be in. If you have any medical professionals in your life at all, whether therapist or psychiatrist or general practitioner, please contact him immediately to discuss treatment options.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T19:51:41-07:00","id":600121,"title":"","content":"Blah blah something depression blah the pain <br /> <br /> Why do I bother with words? <br /> <br /> I'm empty. Please discard. Thank you. Have a nice day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T20:10:50-07:00","id":600140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=600121#post600121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blah blah something depression blah the pain<br /> <br /> Why do I bother with words?<br /> <br /> I'm empty. Please discard. Thank you. Have a nice day.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You are not a disposable thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T03:13:08-07:00","id":600303,"title":"","content":"Ditto!<br /> <br /> You happen to be the friend of some us, and we tend to value that a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T08:55:43-07:00","id":602971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=599537#post599537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a quite dangerous state to be in. If you have any medical professionals in your life at all, whether therapist or psychiatrist or general practitioner, please contact him immediately to discuss treatment options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I discuss it with them each and every time I go to see them, but nothing ever happens or changes.<br /> It's abominable and I think it's leading me into utter despair.<br /> <br /> Whenever I think I've hit rock bottom, I feel like I just sink deeper. I can't keep going on like this, but I don't think it will ever end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T18:11:59-07:00","id":603342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=602971#post602971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I discuss it with them each and every time I go to see them, but nothing ever happens or changes. It's abominable and I think it's leading me into utter despair.<br /> <br /> Whenever I think I've hit rock bottom, I feel like I just sink deeper. I can't keep going on like this, but I don't think it will ever end.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me you do not trust your health care providers. I don't want to treat you like a problem to be solved, or to invalidate what you're feeling, but please permit me to suggest it is time to change doctors (or therapists or whatever). The people who are paid to care for you should be doing a better job, but if they can't or won't, then you will have to take the initiative and find someone who will listen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T14:38:46-07:00","id":605947,"title":"","content":"That does it. I've had it. I think I'm almost done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T15:42:38-07:00","id":606015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=605947#post605947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does it. I've had it. I think I'm almost done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize. It was not my intent to be a straw on the camel's back. I will be silent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T18:06:15-07:00","id":606111,"title":"","content":"It wasnt you. Sorry<br /> <br /> Im just getting worse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T09:54:14-07:00","id":623413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=606111#post606111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasnt you. Sorry<br /> <br /> Im just getting worse</div> </div> </div> </div> I hope you're alright, D. It's been awhile since you've posted here.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going between an aggressive sort of positivity and a crushing sense of hopelessness, so at least I'm still bipolar. I'm not happy about it. I just fear change sometimes. Would've been kinda screwy if that just fell off or something.<br /> I'm coping...I think. I'm also starting arguments more often. Probably not a good thing. I'm an introvert, so I generally find people draining in social situations. It's a hurdle I've jumped before. <br /> High School theater? Who ELSE was going to play Eddie in our production of The Rocky Horror Picture Show, I ask you? Hot-patootee, I really loved that ridiculous, rather sexy costume. <br /> <br /> The problem right now is adjusting from one level of emotional stress to another. I can pump myself up so much I'd gladly hop up on stage and roast every person of note to ever live. I can also be too apathetic to heat up a cup of instant ramen. The transition, however, is still the rough spot:<br /> <br /> I was running through some written material. You know, reading aloud, adding conversational patter and my usual random tangents, walking the room as though it were a stage, etc. Yeah, I was basically walking around the room talking to myself...<i>but for work, you guys. So it's not weird..</i>..<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd finished doing that for the time being and wanted to watch some tv. (Toonami. It was Toonami. You know you wanted to ask.) I sat down to watch and...the word-vomit would NOT stop. I was <i>alone in the room </i>and just going OFF. My mind decided it would be helpful somehow to have me start passionately reciting some of William Forsythe's lines from The Devil's Rejects before jumping up to rant about religion. Not as William Forsythe, but still, that was weird too.<br /> <br /> \u200bI couldn't relax. I quit smoking awhile back, and I had to bum a few smokes and grab a drink before I could watch some damn Sword Art Online. Argh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T08:11:54-07:00","id":627613,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Im probably losing my job today. I've been in an extreme hypermanic stage (which would be rarer than if a doc were to find cancer on my lung). I'm off meds. If I lose this job even though I hate it I thought it might would be a good turning point but my family has a way of making everything hell for me. If I dolose the job, I'm either running or doing something dramatic. Either way I will keep you nposted. Stay safe stay on your meds and don't ever listen to anything from your family</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls r