title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T13:24:51-07:00","id":642016,"title":"","content":"So, I'm going to the doctor tomorrow to see if they derive me to the psychiatrist or psycologist. I sincerely don't know. Can't sleep, when I do I only have nightmares, constant dread and anxiety attacks, evryone that knows me thinks I might have depression. We'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T14:56:07-07:00","id":642114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=642016#post642016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm going to the doctor tomorrow to see if they derive me to the psychiatrist or psycologist. I sincerely don't know. Can't sleep, when I do I only have nightmares, constant dread and anxiety attacks, evryone that knows me thinks I might have depression. We'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or both.<br /> <br /> As I understand it, it is very common for a combination of both appropriate medication and therapy to be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:54:48-07:00","id":642161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=642114#post642114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or both.<br /> As I understand it, it is very common for a combination of both appropriate medication and therapy to be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, start with both. See what works best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T21:50:05-07:00","id":642587,"title":"","content":"So, this thread still viable, or do we need a new one?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T22:38:07-07:00","id":642619,"title":"","content":"Still viable in my book. Literally nothing that happened here had anything to do with Mental Health, unless you count people feeling bummed.<br /> <br /> I hope everything goes well, Thorbes. I can agree with pb and canuck on the combination of those two things are both likely and usually the most efficacious combination. As you probably know, I'm bipolar with ptsd, general anxiety and high functioning autism, so I've had to deal with both a LOT, separately and together.<br /> <br /> A nice simple antidepressant like Prozac and Klonopin, a benzodiazepine, for anxiety worked well enough to keep me alive until I discovered etheogens. Since then, I go back and forth every few years ony the subject. I've taken peyote, mushrooms, Zoloft, and Prozac for depression. All have had some effect, some far better than others.<br /> <br /> I've taken marijuana medically for almost ten years for my anxiety and occasional major depressive episodes. It's cut down on my self-harm to the point that adding more scars to my body seems genuinely silly, and I can say that, unlike the ten years before I started using it, I can't say that I've spent some part of every year in a hospital.<br /> <br /> I will add, though, that I've had a sporadic history of substance abuse throughout my life since adolescence. It has literally nothing to do with marijuana, though. I didn't even try pot until high school. I simply spent my childhood being fed psychotropic drugs, so at some point I started messing around with my own medication for fun. I'd tweak on my dexedrine (they thought I had ADD), I'd take a twelve hour nap on my anxiety medication.<br /> These are all things I've either eliminated from my life or am taking care of professionals because I have the mental stability that my federally illegal medicine gives me. <br /> I used to be afraid to talk. Now I'm talking for a living.<br /> <br /> Someone should legalize my medication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 08-28-2015, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T22:52:10-07:00","id":642623,"title":"","content":"I suppose the &quot;party&quot; mystique of the substance itself may be the most harmful aspect of its road to legalization. The issue honestly seems silly, though.<br /> <br /> You can get high on marijuana. You can then party/rap/get freaky/whatever while high.<br /> <br /> Last time I checked, that's true for EVERY intoxicant! It's just that nobody's figured out how to get a prescription for vodka yet. <br /> <br /> If your drug also doubles as a viable medicine for multiple illnesses and has few side effects, it's probably more a good medicine than a drug. Either way, big fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T23:50:46-07:00","id":642672,"title":"","content":"I dont know if i can do this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Putting her in her crib has my anxiety going so far through the roof its insane...but last night i came to bed and my fiance was out cold his back to her, half laying on the baby who was asleep face down in the matress. She was fine, and when i moved her actually got mad cause her daddy is a space heater and she was quite comfy, I however was not fine. I cuddled her in bed away from her daddy and laid awake while she slept as i couldnt sleep i was to scared. i decided its time she stop sleeping in bed with me. But this is hard. I have anxiety about her being in my bed, and anxiety about her sleeping in her crib alone. the cribs in our room right next to the bed so its not like she's in another room... I'm currently sitting in an armchair next to her crib on my laptop watching her sleep all safely swaddled up...I'm tired but cant sleep...If i do sleep it will likely be in this chair next to her crib.<br /> <br /> I dont see sleep coming easy. Anxiety is a nasty thing..my mind keeps going to horrible &quot;what ifs&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I wish i could have an anxiety med like you Az, but noooooo even though its legal here i'm not allowed to go near it cause if I smoke it I'm unable to care for baby girl (Seriously every time that shit knocks me out cold, it is THE best feeling in the world, no pain, no aches, no anxiety or depression just comfort, relaxation and the urge to curl up in a pile of blankets and sleep)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T02:42:51-07:00","id":642781,"title":"","content":"Today I got an appointment for the psychiatrist for Septemebr the 16th. They will tell if I can or not go to the psycologist in addition to, or instead of continue to go to psychiatrist. I also live in constant anger, so may that's something I should mention too. I feel quite immature for may own age too, though I wonder if being self aware of that means I'm wrong. The circular logic makes my head hurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T03:41:34-07:00","id":642810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=642781#post642781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today I got an appointment for the psychiatrist for Septemebr the 16th. They will tell if I can or not go to the psycologist in addition to, or instead of continue to go to psychiatrist. I also live in constant anger, so may that's something I should mention too. I feel quite immature for may own age too, though I wonder if being self aware of that means I'm wrong. The circular logic makes my head hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Being aware of a thought pattern usually doesn't just disprove that thought, but awareness of perceived immaturity is healthy. You can feel the rough patches that might need buffing. Being angry all day/week/month is something I deal with often. You definitely should talk about it with your psych professionals. It's uncomfortable, and it helps nada. Talking about your anger might feel awkward. It, oddly, might also make you angry just by talking about it. That's venting. It's ok. Talking helps, as does the right medication when needed.<br /> <br /> Love you, buddy.<br /> <br /> hope all goes well<br /> <br /> @scelesta The anxiety must be awful. Hopefully you can relax and sleep like a human being soon enough. *Hugs* <br /> <br /> You have at least three ways of making my phone make funny noises, so message me, would ya?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 08-28-2015, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T08:34:20-07:00","id":643025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=642623#post642623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time I checked, that's true for EVERY intoxicant! It's just that nobody's figured out how to get a prescription for vodka yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a point in the history of my homeland when it was the case. Granted that was almost a century ago now, during prohibition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T21:18:41-07:00","id":647646,"title":"","content":"Well, I spent the summer activly trying to take on my problems. And it seems all I've done is make them worse.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's time to try the other option","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T12:53:01-07:00","id":649223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=647646#post647646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I spent the summer activly trying to take on my problems. And it seems all I've done is make them worse.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's time to try the other option</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What's the &quot;other option&quot;? I don't mean to bother, but you can talk here. Are you going to be alright?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:52:46-07:00","id":649452,"title":"","content":"Probably not. sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T17:50:57-07:00","id":649568,"title":"","content":"Hm... is this the moment we start to panic for your welbeing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T23:28:34-07:00","id":649788,"title":"","content":"I need a break. A day a full day alone. No baby. No fiance...just me, a tv, a hot bath and a pack of my favorite cigs.<br /> <br /> I'm somewhere in the realm of beyond stressed. Trying to get her to sleep alone is proving so difficult...Tonight I went out my damn way to set up the crib in such a way to make it comfortable, and she was FINE in it for her nap but come bed time she raised so much hell, I nearly started sobbing because she wouldnt shut the fuck up and go to sleep. She wouldnt take her bottle, me holding her barely helped...I had to go give her to my fiance because I for a moment thought about throwing her across the room out of frustration. I asked him to take tommorow off but he wont cause it will cost us money...FUCK MONEY...I need rest. She's SOUND asleep in bed with her daddy, i'm not comfortable at all with that so she cant stay there long, and I cant sleep with her in the bed anymore as its putting my spine in so much pain its hurting to walk and sit... <br /> <br /> I'm sitting here now typing this trying not to start crying or screaming. I dont know why i want to scream i just do. I just want to not be in pain, i just need her to fucking sleep on her own. My sanity is suffering..my fiances bright suggestion? Just keep sleeping in the bed wiht her. FUCK WHY DIDNT I THINK OF THAT!? *sarcasm*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T05:02:07-07:00","id":649959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=649568#post649568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm... is this the moment we start to panic for your welbeing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. This is what I'm wondering too. <br /> Let us know how you're doing @vampire hunter d<br /> <br /> We're concerned. I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> Scelesta, we had a good talk, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Everything will work out.<br /> <br /> Much luv","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T08:03:27-07:00","id":650122,"title":"","content":"If it's really bothering everyone that much I'll just shut up<br /> <br /> It's what everyone else I know tells me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 09-03-2015, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T10:53:32-07:00","id":650308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=650122#post650122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's really bothering everyone that much I'll just shut up<br /> <br /> It's what everyone else I know tells me</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the exact reverse of what people are asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T11:17:18-07:00","id":650326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=650308#post650308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the exact reverse of what people are asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! You are in now way bothering anyone, we<u><b> dont</b></u> want you to shut up we want you to talk because it seems like you really need to.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T22:03:11-07:00","id":650912,"title":"","content":"Oh yay, depression rears its UGLY head...seriously why is my brain doing this to me? I havent felt like this in a long time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I keep looking at my baby girl and trying to remind myself i'm here for her, she cant have her mommy die..I would hate myself for dmaaging her like that. Its likely the only thing keeping me from doing something stupid. I'm having a hard time today just living...I dont want to do anything, forced myself to walk to the store, it didnt really help, forced my favorite foods down my facehole nothing. Nothing excites me, nothing interests me...I had a brief moment where I saw something that made me exited and happy but it vanished so fast. My little girls smiles and laughs make me smile but then i feel misrable because I KNOW that soon she will cry and I'll have to drop everything to go take care of it. If i sound bitter, I dont mean to, its just a matter of me not wanting to do ANYTHING. I made my fiance take a day off work today because I didnt feel I could take care of the baby alone today...I was met all day with a reminder of how i was selfish for costing us a full days worth of pay...<br /> <br /> Yeah....WAy to go dickhead, i'm depressed and asked for help and he's just going on about how selfish I am, how i need to man up and do my job. (job in this case means being a mom) and that i dont have the luxary of having mental breakdowns anymore. Oh. Well. Shit. I'll get right on that! Never mind I'm not on the meds that 100% work because we cant afford me to quit breastfeeding and forumla costs a fucking fortune, so i'm stuck on a medication that sorta works, but clearly isnt. (It may work better if I could remember to take it more then a couple times a week....)<br /> <br /> I may loose my health insurance which also means quitting my meds until we can figure out how the fuck we can afford to pay for health insurance, which means also figuring out how to afford copays and presription costs..I'm on state health insurance which is free, but our income is dangerously close to the cut off, and i think we may be over it...If I loose my meds I'm not sure how the hell i'm going to function, i'm BARELY functioning now. BUt htat is a problem for future me.<br /> <br /> Present me wants to curl into a ball and sob and scream and NOT adult anymore for a few days...cant afford to have him take tommorow off, no one can come over while he's at work to watch the baby while I lay in bed moping and wishing i was dead because I cant man the fuck up and realize I dont get to do this anymore its not my life that suffers if i act like this and cant control myself, my daughter needs me..But i'm failing her.<br /> <br /> I'm rambling. Likely cause I have no where else, no one else willing to listen...I feel terrifingly alone in this, and it hurts. I need to be a mom, I need to take care of my daughter but i can hardly care for myself right now... Why is this happening to me? I have zero reason to be this sad...My life is going well, its difficult but i shouldnt feel like this.<br /> <br /> /pointless rambling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T23:28:06-07:00","id":653535,"title":"","content":"I'm online because I'm genuinely not going to say aloud the phrase &quot;No, I'm not going to kill myself. I just can't stop thinking about it, worrying about not trusting myself and crying&quot; to anyone else for at least a solid decade. Sorry, confused lady on the crisis hotline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T23:48:18-07:00","id":653548,"title":"","content":"Scel... You're a strong person. You're my friend.<br /> <br /> There are certain people here that my head and heart have come to care about deeper than family. That includes you. You guys know who you are. Also Cerealkiller, who from what I'm told is leaving us permanently. If that's the case, I'm just glad I have his number. I'm tired of losing the little tastes of genuine goodness in my life. Tired of seeing people go. It's not that I'm bitter. I mean, I am bitter, but that's been since kindergarten or so. It's that I'm lonely of spirit. I need something to cling to, but everything hurts me.<br /> I promised myself I wouldn't mention Fight Club at all today. Well, fuck it.<br /> <br /> You know that scene where the main character/Tyler and Marla talk for the first time in whatever support group they didn't belong in? I'm living a life where people are talking, sometimes to me, and they're just waiting.<br /> Like carrion crows, I watch people wait for their turn to speak. Sometimes the cunts will hold their breath, like they're symbolically ignoring who they're talking to by pausing their own life processes. People say they want to listen.<br /> <br /> They want to be heard. Maybe it's the desire to be understood, recognized or wanted. I don't know. I'm no better. I'm a trained monkey on stage with an organ grinder and a hat to collect coins. I fucking brag about that, too. What kind of prick am I? My dad was an unadulterated cunt, but he's also a chef and I'm pretty sure he never fucking bragged about how good HIS stuff was. This might be a poor comparison, or I'm just hoping I faired better than him as a human being. Probably both.<br /> <br /> Sorry, anyway. Depression. It IS a bitch. It won't beat you. Pretty sure we spoke earlier, Scel, but just making sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-06-2015, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T19:29:36-07:00","id":655859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=653535#post653535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &amp;quot;No, I'm not going to kill myself. I just can't stop thinking about it, worrying about not trusting myself and crying&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That used to be my attitude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T12:10:17-07:00","id":656786,"title":"","content":"I lost my last refuge. The place I'd go to to try to get away from my problems is off limits to me now. So, I have no ither options. I'm cut off from the few people in real life who seemed to care enoigh to want to help. Snd I'm out of reasons to want to get better.<br /> <br /> Time to stsrt making plans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:09:12-07:00","id":656843,"title":"","content":"What happened? Have you been banned off the place or is a self-imposed exile due to some personal problems? You can still hang around here, with us. I know is a poor substitute for RL interaction but please don't give up on everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:42:53-07:00","id":656867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=656843#post656843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happened? Have you been banned off the place or is a self-imposed exile due to some personal problems? You can still hang around here, with us. I know is a poor substitute for RL interaction but please don't give up on everything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconded! You're more than welcome here. Struggling as it may be, there is some community. Some safety. Would you maybe please talk about it further?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:33:58-07:00","id":658336,"title":"","content":"has anyone called a crisis hotline? how good are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:38:00-07:00","id":658341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=658336#post658336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">has anyone called a crisis hotline? how good are they?</div> </div> </div> </div>depending on where you are they are pretty good. <br /> <br /> The one over here at least, send out a crisis team to come speak to me in person(it was offered and i accepted it they were NOT sent out without my permission), and the crisis lines are helpful if you need to talk, need resources to get help etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:45:10-07:00","id":658348,"title":"","content":"I'm just out of options. but don't really know if I want to go to teh 9mm solution......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:04:53-07:00","id":658369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=658348#post658348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just out of options. but don't really know if I want to go to teh 9mm solution......</div> </div> </div> </div>I wont claim to know your situation cause i dont. But there are always options, the fact that your are considering calling a crisis line is a good thing as it shows you still have some will in you to live and a desire to get help. please call them, let them at least give you soem resources to get help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:39:30-07:00","id":658391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=658348#post658348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just out of options. but don't really know if I want to go to teh 9mm solution......</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how you're feeling, but it doesn't <i>hurt</i> to contact them, and it may well <i>help</i>. They're free, and I'm told they can make a difference.<br /> <br /> I know I don't post on here much, mostly because my 'problems' are immensely petty, but I do watch, and I'm open to listen if you feel you need to talk to someone without judgement. (Also something the crisis line is good for, but that in no way negates the offer on my part.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T18:50:33-07:00","id":658756,"title":"","content":"I'm having the strong urge to harm myself. I'm not suicidal, I don't think. I just can't get the repetitive thought of slicing my wrist deeply open up to the elbow out of my head. I can't stop thinking it'd feel like lancing a boil, or unblocking a heart valve. Just let it out. I can't. I know I can't. I know my weird notion it being helpful is bullshit. I just want to punish myself. For not being strong enough, good enough, handsome enough, smart enough. For being me, the greatest sin. <br /> I want to bleed like I'm screaming &quot;FUCK YOU, WORLD! THE ONLY ONE WHO GETS TO HURT ME IS ME!!!&quot;. I know exactly what knife I'd do it with. Right there on my bookshelf. I'm not going to do it. I'm not. <br /> <br /> I just feel I should so strongly that I'm typing this on my kindle from the floor, where I'm curled up and can't seem to stop crying. It hurts inside and I want it to go away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T19:32:00-07:00","id":658809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=658756#post658756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having the strong urge to harm myself. I'm not suicidal, I don't think. I just can't get the repetitive thought of slicing my wrist deeply open up to the elbow out of my head. I can't stop thinking it'd feel like lancing a boil, or unblocking a heart valve. Just let it out. I can't. I know I can't. I know my weird notion it being helpful is bullshit. I just want to punish myself. For not being strong enough, good enough, handsome enough, smart enough. For being me, the greatest sin.<br /> I want to bleed like I'm screaming &quot;FUCK YOU, WORLD! THE ONLY ONE WHO GETS TO HURT ME IS ME!!!&quot;. I know exactly what knife I'd do it with. Right there on my bookshelf. I'm not going to do it. I'm not.<br /> <br /> I just feel I should so strongly that I'm typing this on my kindle from the floor, where I'm curled up and can't seem to stop crying. It hurts inside and I want it to go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Az, you know full well that that's not going to solve anything. You're stronger than this. You just to have to remember it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T19:40:29-07:00","id":658823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=658756#post658756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having the strong urge to harm myself. I'm not suicidal, I don't think. I just can't get the repetitive thought of slicing my wrist deeply open up to the elbow out of my head. I can't stop thinking it'd feel like lancing a boil, or unblocking a heart valve. Just let it out. I can't. I know I can't. I know my weird notion it being helpful is bullshit. I just want to punish myself. For not being strong enough, good enough, handsome enough, smart enough. For being me, the greatest sin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, first of all, quit being me. I'm me, and you're you, so quit being me. It's creepy that there's two mes.<br /> <br /> Second, as someone who's had and acted on exactly that urge, I can promise you whatever relief you think you'll feel, you won't. It will just hurt, and then you'll get to feel ashamed of yourself because you have to wear long sleeves from now on to keep people from not looking at your arm and not asking uncomfortable questions. Not worth it.<br /> <br /> Are you seeing anyone or receiving any kind of help? As much trouble as you're having lately, I feel like you must not be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T20:13:08-07:00","id":658852,"title":"","content":"Well, going into a fourth day of this bout. Is that normal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T20:45:30-07:00","id":658863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=658823#post658823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, as someone who's had and acted on exactly that urge, I can promise you whatever relief you think you'll feel, you won't. It will just hurt, and then you'll get to feel ashamed of yourself because you have to wear long sleeves from now on to keep people from not looking at your arm and not asking uncomfortable questions. Not worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've acted on it before. I'm not trying to find common ground with you. I've just told you this already. I already have a network of scars on my arms, chest, and abdomen. I have to wear long sleeves every time I'm meeting strangers. Are you telling ME, or answering &quot;I'm depressed. Would cutting myself help?&quot; on Yahoo answers? Did that come off as acidic? I apologize if it did.<br /> <br /> I know it's not worth it. I'm even considering hospitalization if this doesn't stop. I hope it stops, not only because I'm silently screaming like a man who just saw the face of God and it was just a pile of pulsing maggots singing Silent Night, Holy Night while it/they slowly digested human souls, but also because I'd be waiting in the Emergency Room at the hospital for a few hours just to tell a nurse exactly what I've already said in a post.<br /> <br /> I don't want to hurt myself. My brain is just torturing me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you seeing anyone or receiving any kind of help? As much trouble as you're having lately, I feel like you must not be. </div> </div> </div> In between doctors. Have medication and a therapist, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T21:22:42-07:00","id":658876,"title":"","content":"Sorry, Az.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T01:34:02-07:00","id":659105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=658876#post658876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, Az.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I should be the one apologizing. I was rude to you.<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely sorry, Jim. It was uncalled for, even considering my situation, and you're one of the last people that deserves that kind of treatment.<br /> <br /> Thank you for caring enough to even post a thing to me at all. <br /> You're a good guy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T05:43:15-07:00","id":659264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=659105#post659105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're one of the last people that deserves that kind of treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I appreciate that, what I deserve is irrelevant. For me to worry about what I deserve while you are in the state you're in would be an unforgivable display of egotism. What matters is whether I have the skills and abilities to help. I do not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T10:26:05-07:00","id":659503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=659264#post659264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What matters is whether I have the skills and abilities to help. I do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jim, sometimes you're surprisingly dense. *hugs* <br /> <br /> Ability: You talk to me.<br /> Skill: You're supportive and you care.<br /> How much that matters: a fucking LOT<br /> <br /> You underestimate your powers, bud. <br /> <br /> I hope you have as good a day as circumstance, other humans existing and brain chemistry allows. <br /> <br /> *walks away shaking his head &quot;That Jim. Fucking trip. Gotta love him&quot;*","signature":"<hr c