Well, I'm no longer sick.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T02:11:51-07:00","id":712093,"title":"","content":"I know this is a really, really petty thing to complain about, but it's really bothering me, and you guys haven't mine my whining in the past. So I guess I'll be asking you to indulge me one more time.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I'm just flat-out unlovable. People seem to like me well enough, for some reason, but nobody, ever, expresses any romantic interest in me, and when I try to express interest in people I'm rejected, no matter how I try to do it. I've tried in person, online dating, even an app where it helps people get together for hugs (just hugs. Explicitly non-sexual; even has a function where you can report someone if they try to do anything other than what has been agreed on) - nothing. Not a single, tiny, drop of a hint that someone might potentially look at me as a remote romantic possibility (and one quite clear explicit statement that nobody ever will, but I try not to give that undue weight). Now, I can't really blame anyone for this, I'm not really a catch. I'm not physically attractive, I'm kind-of clever but nothing out of the box, and my personality isn't anything to write home about. And it's not that I <i>need</i> to be in a relationship to be happy, but there's a big difference between not being in a relationship because you choose not to be, and not being even eligible because nobody would ever want you.<br /> <br /> I've tried raising this with my friends (god knows why, they're immensely self-interested and shy away from talking about anything of weight that does not immediately concern them), to no avail. Well, unless you count laughs like I'm joking 'avail'. Which I do not. So I try turning to the Internet... I'll leave that to your imagination how well <i>that</i> particular adventure went.<br /> <br /> Now, before anyone accuses me of being 'entitled to a relationship' or any of that bullshit (not that I think any of you guys would, but, well, it happens), I don't feel 'entitled'. I'm just really depressed that apparently I'm so low on the totem pole that people find the idea of me being in a relationship as being <i>funny</i>. And either ignore me, let me down easy (which I guess is a nice way to say no, but it's still no) or outright abuse me for daring to approach them.<br /> <br /> All I want is some tiny crumb of a hint that there might be some kind of value to my existence. Because, to be honest, I'm having trouble seeing any. My work is laughably irrelevant, both in topic and scope, I've made roughly 10% of the progress I'm supposed to have made, largely due to my own incompetence, and I'm fairly certain I'm a lousy tutor on top of it all (when my students are less engaged than those of my immensely self-absorbed and disorganised colleague, I'm in serious trouble).<br /> <br /> Just really, really frustrated with the world. And myself, because that <i>is</i> where the problem is. I've even considered hiring a prostitute to pretend to be interested in me for a night, just so I can delude myself for a second there's something about me <i>someone</i> might find desirable, even if it's just my money, except I'm sure I'd just feel worse after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T02:19:08-07:00","id":712098,"title":"","content":"Yay! Great news Prometheus!<br /> <br /> EDIT: because Allan53 posted while I wrote:<br /> <br /> That's far from being a petty concern, the feeling of belonging be it in a relationship or with a group of friends or at your job is an integral part of our needs as humans.<br /> It seems you are being refused any of it, which is more than enough to be pissed and worried.<br /> <br /> As my pal Az down here, I find the idea of someone being totally unlovable completly alien. I sincerely believe there's someone for everybody out there. Yeah it can be hell of a ride to find your particular someone, but they exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-21-2015, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T03:27:50-07:00","id":712136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=711583#post711583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> Wait, I never did tell you guys I was no longer sick, did I? Well, I'm no longer sick.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *does a celebratory Snoopy dance*<br /> <br /> Great to hear, Promie my homie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T03:51:34-07:00","id":712144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=712093#post712093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is a really, really petty thing to complain about, but it's really bothering me, and you guys haven't mine my whining in the past. So I guess I'll be asking you to indulge me one more time.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I'm just flat-out unlovable. People seem to like me well enough, for some reason, but nobody, ever, expresses any romantic interest in me, and when I try to express interest in people I'm rejected, no matter how I try to do it. I've tried in person, online dating, even an app where it helps people get together for hugs (just hugs. Explicitly non-sexual; even has a function where you can report someone if they try to do anything other than what has been agreed on) - nothing. Not a single, tiny, drop of a hint that someone might potentially look at me as a remote romantic possibility (and one quite clear explicit statement that nobody ever will, but I try not to give that undue weight). Now, I can't really blame anyone for this, I'm not really a catch. I'm not physically attractive, I'm kind-of clever but nothing out of the box, and my personality isn't anything to write home about. And it's not that I <i>need</i> to be in a relationship to be happy, but there's a big difference between not being in a relationship because you choose not to be, and not being even eligible because nobody would ever want you.<br /> <br /> I've tried raising this with my friends (god knows why, they're immensely self-interested and shy away from talking about anything of weight that does not immediately concern them), to no avail. Well, unless you count laughs like I'm joking 'avail'. Which I do not. So I try turning to the Internet... I'll leave that to your imagination how well <i>that</i> particular adventure went.<br /> <br /> Now, before anyone accuses me of being 'entitled to a relationship' or any of that bullshit (not that I think any of you guys would, but, well, it happens), I don't feel 'entitled'. I'm just really depressed that apparently I'm so low on the totem pole that people find the idea of me being in a relationship as being <i>funny</i>. And either ignore me, let me down easy (which I guess is a nice way to say no, but it's still no) or outright abuse me for daring to approach them.<br /> <br /> All I want is some tiny crumb of a hint that there might be some kind of value to my existence. Because, to be honest, I'm having trouble seeing any. My work is laughably irrelevant, both in topic and scope, I've made roughly 10% of the progress I'm supposed to have made, largely due to my own incompetence, and I'm fairly certain I'm a lousy tutor on top of it all (when my students are less engaged than those of my immensely self-absorbed and disorganised colleague, I'm in serious trouble).<br /> <br /> Just really, really frustrated with the world. And myself, because that <i>is</i> where the problem is. I've even considered hiring a prostitute to pretend to be interested in me for a night, just so I can delude myself for a second there's something about me <i>someone</i> might find desirable, even if it's just my money, except I'm sure I'd just feel worse after.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hate to be extremely lazy, but...ditto. Just include me in this as if me and Allan53 joined a support group for this in particular. I've already done the complaining part and gotten the comforting words part before, so leave that ALL for him. For both of us, though, especially me... Any idea on how to change this around? Giving off the wrong vibe? Making some sort of repeated gaffe that is going unnoticed by me/us? Should a new approach to romance be something to try? <br /> <br /> Allan, I can say with honesty that, even though I've met human beings that I actively dislike or downright hate (I'm not above hating a motherfucker. I'm less than a hundred thousand years from socially acceptable public cannibalism. I could be a bigger dick if I actually wanted to be), but I've never met a person I could call truly unlovable. A person's actions, those can be unloveable. <br /> An actual person, when stripped down to the basics and freed of societal construction as their measure of worth or goodness, is generally just as loveable as your favorite pet/best friend etc. In a vacuum, we're just social animals. I watched my cats beat the holy shit outta each other earlier today and then proceed to bathe/groom one another before cuddling together and falling asleep like a furry yin-yang. We're not so different.<br /> <br /> \u200bI DO completely understand the hurt and sadness that comes from FEELING unloved and unlovable though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh. And I've sequestered myself from the world. I haven't left the house all month and haven't had my phone on in two weeks. That's not going well. I'm not sleeping normally and I'm getting physically sick from the damage my lack of proper hydration, sleep and outside activity is causing. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:36:33-07:00","id":720197,"title":"","content":"This is not a joke.<br /> <br /> So, the backer pdf for Exalted came out yesterday, and a lot of people really like the art style.<br /> <br /> One look at that art style sent me into a depression cycle. I think I might even be feeling the first twinges of despair.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, I'm the only person who has reacted this way.<br /> <br /> ... I think there is something seriously wrong with me.<br /> <br /> Edit: Right now I feel on the verge of tears. I think there is <i>definitely</i> something wrong with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:44:33-07:00","id":720241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=720197#post720197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the backer pdf for Exalted came out yesterday, and a lot of people really like the art style.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's several threads complaining about the art, actually, and in particular the lack of people of color, or people of color depicted as white-ish. There's even implications, and possible evidence, of swiping and tracing. For what it's worth, I liked the cover.<br /> <br /> But maybe you should elaborate on <i>why </i>it's bringing you to tears, despair, and a depression cycle.<br /> <br /> I enjoyed your link, very apt about the white washing, with a nice humorous bent. I've never watched Yu-Gi-Oh but the abridged version looks worth viewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-23-2015, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:02:24-07:00","id":720297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=720241#post720241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's several threads complaining about the art, actually, and in particular the lack of people of color, or people of color depicted as white-ish. There's even implications, and possible evidence, of swiping and tracing. For what it's worth, I liked the cover.<br /> <br /> But maybe you should elaborate on <i>why </i>it's bringing you to tears, despair, and a depression cycle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know, I've participated in several of those threads. I can freely acknowledge that are pieces of art in that book that are genuinely great, but the whole book is...<br /> <br /> Alright, self analysis. I've waited for this book for three years. Exalted is my favorite RPG, so I had massively built up the hype in that time. Then, after all this waiting, I finally get to look at the finished product.<br /> <br /> And... I feel stupid when I unravel it like this. I don't like the new style they've gone with. I feel that the unique visual identity built up over previous editions had been lost in favor of &quot;generic asianness,&quot; if that makes sense. So I took a look to see what other people thought.<br /> <br /> Oh, other people had problems with specific pieces, to be sure. But the overall opinion towards the look of the new edition seemed to be positive. And I can see where they're coming from; it is technically very artistic. But the more and more I thought about it, the greater and greater a loss it seemed. And yet, when I expressed this opinion, only one or two people seemed to agree with me.<br /> <br /> Then I started thinking that, if the majority likes it, the more likely it would be that my opinion would be ignored, written off. I started thinking that maybe the problem was with me, and that <i>I</i> should change. And that made me feel very alone.<br /> <br /> God, this sounds so stupid. I'm sorry for wasting your time with this. It's just a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 10-23-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:11:34-07:00","id":720313,"title":"","content":"You're hardly wasting anyone's time. If you were, they could just skip your posts.<br /> <br /> I really don't think the overall opinion towards the art is favorable. My wife didn't like it at first sight, I like the cover, and I think the 'city' spread a few pages in but that's about it.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of people are on the opposite side of things as you. They've waited for it for years and are happy enough to get it that they'll dismiss flaws. But there's definitely people talking about not liking the art, and the problems with it, and there's already mentions of problems with specific artists and acknowledging the problem, so I don't think you should worry too much about your opinion being completely ignored.<br /> <br /> Still, right now, there's nothing we can do about the art except keep our opinions out there so they're noted for future books. Have you read the book itself? What did you think? I haven't gotten around to more than skimming, but everyone seems to really like the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:21:18-07:00","id":720358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=720313#post720313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're hardly wasting anyone's time. If you were, they could just skip your posts.<br /> <br /> I really don't think the overall opinion towards the art is favorable. My wife didn't like it at first sight, I like the cover, and I think the 'city' spread a few pages in but that's about it.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of people are on the opposite side of things as you. They've waited for it for years and are happy enough to get it that they'll dismiss flaws. But there's definitely people talking about not liking the art, and the problems with it, and there's already mentions of problems with specific artists and acknowledging the problem, so I don't think you should worry too much about your opinion being completely ignored.<br /> <br /> Still, right now, there's nothing we can do about the art except keep our opinions out there so they're noted for future books. Have you read the book itself? What did you think? I haven't gotten around to more than skimming, but everyone seems to really like the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I am reading through the book right now. The writing seems pretty darn good, and it's what brought me back. I'm diligently reading through it and noting typos and such, as we were asked to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T13:32:55-07:00","id":720413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=720358#post720358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I am reading through the book right now. The writing seems pretty darn good, and it's what brought me back. I'm diligently reading through it and noting typos and such, as we were asked to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No problem.<br /> <br /> I'm probably not going to be able to get time to read it until the weekend. But once I got to the end and saw Black Wind and the Volcano Cutter I knew I'd at least like some parts, even if not knowing the rest of the mechanics I'm taking it out of context. I've always loved weapons with special abilities, and there's even armor with it. And the Antagonists chapter is blessedly fat with ideas. Onyx Path seems to be finally coming around to placing an emphasis on helping Storytellers with putting baddies together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T00:19:38-07:00","id":722150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=720297#post720297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I know, I've participated in several of those threads. I can freely acknowledge that are pieces of art in that book that are genuinely great, but the whole book is...<br /> <br /> Alright, self analysis. I've waited for this book for three years. Exalted is my favorite RPG, so I had massively built up the hype in that time. Then, after all this waiting, I finally get to look at the finished product.<br /> <br /> And... I feel stupid when I unravel it like this. I don't like the new style they've gone with. I feel that the unique visual identity built up over previous editions had been lost in favor of &quot;generic asianness,&quot; if that makes sense. So I took a look to see what other people thought.<br /> <br /> Oh, other people had problems with specific pieces, to be sure. But the overall opinion towards the look of the new edition seemed to be positive. And I can see where they're coming from; it is technically very artistic. But the more and more I thought about it, the greater and greater a loss it seemed. And yet, when I expressed this opinion, only one or two people seemed to agree with me.<br /> <br /> Then I started thinking that, if the majority likes it, the more likely it would be that my opinion would be ignored, written off. I started thinking that maybe the problem was with me, and that <i>I</i> should change. And that made me feel very alone.<br /> <br /> God, this sounds so stupid. I'm sorry for wasting your time with this. It's just a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure everyone here will be happy to listen. Personally, I can hardly find fault: a while back (a month? Maybe 2? I get fuzzy with time) I was feeling pretty crappy; not depressed (at least not clinically), just really bad about the world generally. Even when I was feeling kind-of level, anything that elicited any kind of emotional reaction in me, positive or negative, brought me to within a hairs width of bursting into tears. I remember one time I tried to watch the first episode of Madoka Magica, an anime I thoroughly enjoy, and just the opening credits made me nearly cry.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. No judgement here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T22:28:25-07:00","id":740935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=712144#post712144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allan, I can say with honesty that, even though I've met human beings that I actively dislike or downright hate (I'm not above hating a motherfucker. I'm less than a hundred thousand years from socially acceptable public cannibalism. I could be a bigger dick if I actually wanted to be), but I've never met a person I could call truly unlovable. A person's actions, those can be unloveable.<br /> An actual person, when stripped down to the basics and freed of societal construction as their measure of worth or goodness, is generally just as loveable as your favorite pet/best friend etc. In a vacuum, we're just social animals. I watched my cats beat the holy shit outta each other earlier today and then proceed to bathe/groom one another before cuddling together and falling asleep like a furry yin-yang. We're not so different.<br /> <br /> \u200bI DO completely understand the hurt and sadness that comes from FEELING unloved and unlovable though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The intent is appreciated; really, it is. However, that logically leads me to the question of 'if I'm not unlovable, and I'm trying to give/find some kind of semblance of a sliver of <i>attention</i>, let alone love, without any success whatsoever, what's wrong with me?' Because it seems a lot more likely that the problem is with me rather than the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> I've been trying, I really have. I've tried to be kind, I've tried to be laid-back, more pushy, arrogant, to listen and talk, in combination. I've even said to people &quot;I know this is very forward, but I am feeling particularly lonely. Would you mind having a conversation with me?&quot; and gotten exactly nowhere, because god forbid someone give me the simple time of day.<br /> <br /> Oh, if I want people to scream at me, call me a Nazi because (when there <i>is</i> a reason) I don't understand their three-paragraph-long special-snowflake identity and this relates to me ordering an extra shot coffee in some weird way, I can get that easily. But that doesn't exactly fill me with joy to be alive, nor compassionate to my fellow humankind.<br /> <br /> (The following is <u>intended as illustrative only</u>, and not as any kind of forgiving or tolerating of violence in any way.)<br /> <br /> It kind of makes me sort-of understand why rape happens. Now, rape is a terrible, awful thing which should never be done to anyone by anyone ever, no matter what. But, yeah. You get lonely enough, the 'normal' ways of making some kind of remote connection don't work, I can see someone, in sheer desperation, turning to that kind of illusory connection, as horrible as it is. Particularly when, if you dare share these feelings with anyone outside of a very, very cool crowd (ie you guys), you literally get called an actual rapist anyway. So, why not (apart from the fact that it's terrible, awful and potentially actually, metaphysically, evil)?<br /> <br /> I'm doing another lot of data gathering at the moment, which involves me sitting in a room listening to undergrads whine about their lives. Oh, boo hoo, you and your boyfriend had a fight? Oh, wait, let me wipe your tears with my list of people who give a flying if I continue to exist or not - oh, wait, I can't, the list doesn't exist <i>because nobody does</i>. Well, except the electricity and gas companies. They care if I disappear - can't get my money if I'm gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T06:42:35-07:00","id":741652,"title":"","content":"Not to be an ass, but I think that's not usually the cause behind rape. Rape is an act of <i>violence through sex</i>, not sex through violence more often than not.<br /> <br /> I can see what you say happening, but I figure is rare.<br /> <br /> That said, people that lack some meanigful &quot;normal&quot; conection do usually seek it through alternative and often messed up ways. That's where you get abusive relationships and other terrible stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T08:16:39-07:00","id":741819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=741652#post741652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to be an ass, but I think that's not usually the cause behind rape. Rape is an act of <i>violence through sex</i>, not sex through violence more often than not.<br /> <br /> I can see what you say happening, but I figure is rare.<br /> <br /> That said, people that lack some meanigful &quot;normal&quot; conection do usually seek it through alternative and often messed up ways. That's where you get abusive relationships and other terrible stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're probably right.<br /> <br /> I stand by the overall sentiment, which you seem to have picked up on though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T22:24:56-08:00","id":761253,"title":"","content":"With all of !y current situations it seems suicide is one of the only options left. Thanks to those who supported me, sorry I'm not strong as others but I'm done. I can't take it anymore. Finances were the straw that broke the camels back and I'm so deeply indebt that ill never be able to climb out. I'm not sure when bit to those who care I'll keep you posted. Also don't try calling authorities or anything because I will choose to ngo pjut fguns blazing and I would rather I hurt myself and no others","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T00:08:19-08:00","id":761278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=761253#post761253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all of !y current situations it seems suicide is one of the only options left. Thanks to those who supported me, sorry I'm not strong as others but I'm done. I can't take it anymore. Finances were the straw that broke the camels back and I'm so deeply indebt that ill never be able to climb out. I'm not sure when bit to those who care I'll keep you posted. Also don't try calling authorities or anything because I will choose to ngo pjut fguns blazing and I would rather I hurt myself and no others</div> </div> </div> </div>I just sort of wandered into this topic while prodding around after work, so I won't pretend that I have any context for what's going on with you. But as a stranger off the street, I would be sad if you stopped existing. I am sad that you've come to feel so helpless and defenseless against the world. I wish I could say that fighting through it will make things better, just because I grappled with anxiety and suicidal thoughts in my life, but I know that my circumstances aren't yours. You might have a very long and painful road in front of you, but I hope that you'll find just enough strength to take a few more steps, and a few more past that. Without a traveler, the road is nothing. Without us living to behold it, this cold and strange cosmos may as well just be the stirring of starry ashes. You are the voice of the universe, and no mortal hardship can ever take that supreme importance from you. I hope that you choose to continue to discover yourself as a part of it.<br /> <br /> Be well, Cereal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2320-tilting-clock","name":"Tilting Clock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T00:08:35-08:00","id":762052,"title":"","content":"Ck, brother, please be alright. I haven't spoken much to anyone in awhile, but I need to know you're alright. Fuck! Message back, post back, something. I'm too drunk to panic properly, so I just fucking ran into three of my four bedroom walls on the way to rescue and hug you before realizing you don't live with me. Nigga, I'll kick your dead ass if you die. You are one of a handful of human beings that understands me, and I'll ritually sacrifice certain States or countries to get your wonderful ass back, so post something or message me before I fly to your home base and waterboard you with bong water until your survival instinct kicks in. I can't get all squishy and gay with you, your choice not mine, so it's man up motherfucker. You leave me behind, I'll kill myself just to follow you to hell and tell you off. Then, Scel will get mad at us and bring us back to life through black magic and shit will be out of our hands. Also, Thorbes will cry. Have you seen a Spaniard cry? Ok, maybe if you're picturing a conquistador crying, it's probably not that moving....but picture a young Antonio Banderas crying. Picture it. Don't make that cry. It hasn't been in films based on books I like yet. Moreover, ....dude..the fucking fuck? Don't kill yourself! You're younger than me and have purchased less useless shit, killer. Debt? It's an imaginary number made up by government you despise. Ignore it. Your life is worth more than a fucking number given to you by people we'd take out with machetes if we were fighting La Revoluc\u00ed\u00f3n! <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T11:52:48-08:00","id":762466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=761253#post761253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all of !y current situations it seems suicide is one of the only options left. Thanks to those who supported me, sorry I'm not strong as others but I'm done. I can't take it anymore. Finances were the straw that broke the camels back and I'm so deeply indebt that ill never be able to climb out. I'm not sure when bit to those who care I'll keep you posted. Also don't try calling authorities or anything because I will choose to ngo pjut fguns blazing and I would rather I hurt myself and no others</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoah don't listen to Azrael! From a guy that was in constant misery that became a hobo and is now rather happy don't let debt and what not bring you down. Things can be okay. I'm rather happy to just not be in constant misery all the time. Be alright!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T12:11:04-08:00","id":762488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=762466#post762466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoah don't listen to Azrael! From a guy that was in constant misery that became a hobo and is now rather happy don't let debt and what not bring you down. Things can be okay. I'm rather happy to just not be in constant misery all the time. Be alright!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically what Az said, in a rather ranty, drunk, rambly way that is his trademark. We love him for that. Or despite that, I'm not sure. We love him, period, that's the important part.<br /> <br /> So, CerealKiller, please stick around. Your life is really important and there's other ways out, as Eldagusto pointed out. Listen to them<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><