https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=767339#post767339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just been one of those years, I guess...</div> </div> </div> </div>A whole year? Want to talk about it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T04:28:23-08:00","id":767732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=767720#post767720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A whole year? Want to talk about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well..maybe not a whole year...but off and on the whole year..lol.<br /> <br /> And maybe...about to head to work, so I'll post or message you when I get some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T11:38:44-08:00","id":767974,"title":"","content":"So a couple weeks ago, I quit my job. As it turns out, I have an anxiety disorder and had been having regular panic attacks. After spending the night in Emergency, my boyfriend and family asked me to quit the job that was causing me a lot of stress. After talking a lot about the financial end of things, I agreed. I'm now jobless and on my first week of anti-anxiety medication which is making me feel <i>really</i> weird, but I know to expect that for the first few weeks until I get used to this stuff. I have to say, though, it's nice to not have my heart racing all the time. My chest no longer feels sore and the quality of my sleep is improving. I go back to see my new family doctor next week and at that time I would like to ask him to refer me to a therapist so I can begin CBT with the goal of re-entering the workforce in the new year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":438,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","user":"wulf","date":". 11-17-2015, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T14:17:37-08:00","id":768096,"title":"","content":"When you are dealing with something for a long time on daily basis, even if it is awful like anxiety, it does feel weird when its gone. It's been roughly a month since I started my treatment and I'm still getting acustomed to the lack of obsesive and depresive thoughts wandering in my head that was my former default.<br /> <br /> You'll get used to it, give it time. Also, kudos on finally puting a remedy to it. It's good to see the suport your family and boyfriend provided you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T15:57:29-08:00","id":768151,"title":"","content":"Thank you; it is very strange to not have such a worried mind. I used to worry all the time about accidents, doing or saying the wrong thing, not doing enough ... those worries are slowly evaporating and I'm not at all used to not having these constant worries running through my mind. I've spent probably a decade operating like that, I just got used to it. Now what? What do I fill my mind with? Should I fill it at all? Lots of questions, lots of possibility now. I'm curious to see what the future will hold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T23:44:35-08:00","id":768313,"title":"","content":"I've heard that some people, when they go on medication for the first time and their symptoms begin to dial back, they kind-of have a mini-freak out due to the change? I mean, I'd imagine depression and anxiety is awful, but similarly I can see the appeal of the familiar leading people to stop taking their meds?<br /> <br /> Is that a thing, or am I just mad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T00:13:48-08:00","id":768323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=768313#post768313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard that some people, when they go on medication for the first time and their symptoms begin to dial back, they kind-of have a mini-freak out due to the change? I mean, I'd imagine depression and anxiety is awful, but similarly I can see the appeal of the familiar leading people to stop taking their meds?<br /> <br /> Is that a thing, or am I just mad?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is VERY much a thing, For years I bounced on and off medications cause it made me feel well normal and fine, and THAT was such a weird and unsettling state to me that I'd take myself right off them because i was convinced that it was numbing who I was. (In reality it wasnt, it was doing its job I just was so unsettled by feeling happy and normal i didnt know how to handle it besides taking myself off the meds and going back to being my depressed angry self) I didnt know what to do with myself when i was on my meds back then, not sleeping all day? What does one do with their time? Do I go outside? talk to people? Try to make friends? Get a job? Nononono thats all wrong. I should be, laying in bed, moping, raging at the world. <br /> <br /> &quot;Normal&quot; Is WEIRD. I'm still adjusting to the new med I'm on, It kicked y anxiety so hard in the ass I'm surprised at how good I feel, and i hadnt realized how much anxiety I had going on till it was kicked down. I ALMOST stopped it cause again it feels weird. But I have to remind myself that so called weird feeling is &quot;normal&quot; and to just let it happen and to enjoy the new possibly better life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T04:37:44-08:00","id":768414,"title":"","content":"What Scelesta said. I also felt that &quot;are my emotions being supressed/numb bit&quot; and wondered if there was something wrong with me. Turns out that's just how a sane person feels <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T08:17:51-08:00","id":768517,"title":"","content":"A relief of long term depression can seem like mania to someone that is 1) not experienced with mania 2) forgot what it feels like to not be depressed. The thought of becoming manic is much more disturbing than depression to someone that suffers only from the latter. I imagine it would be less of a problem for someone that is aware they suffer from both. The loss of emotional range frequently associated with anti-depressants and mood stabilizers can also be unsettling. I think it is really hard to say that &quot;sane&quot; people feel that way most of the time. It would be more important to find a mental state that allows a person to avoid the problem symptoms while maintaining as much range of feelings as possible than to create a state like someone else. Sometimes a compromise must be made as to how much a person needs to feel and still be productive and safe. Often adjustments need to be made throughout a person's life. Mood disorders are treated or managed, never cured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T09:03:03-08:00","id":768546,"title":"","content":"I can feel that a part of me wants to freak out for not being so anxious about things - that I'm not concerned enough, that I'm not being prepared and I don't have the urgency I once did. I have to calmly remind myself those are learned anxious behaviors, not <i>good</i> or healthy behaviors. Yes, I'll admit, I got some use out of those behaviors - I would have things ready to go and in place <i>before</i> a problem came along and people would think I'm psychic (it also helps that I have the INTJ type personality, nicknamed <i>The Mastermind</i>). Now that I don't feel that constant sense of playing a game of chess with life itself ... it's strange. Very, very strange. I am comforted by the knowledge that I'm still capable of doing those things, I just no longer feel the need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T12:09:29-08:00","id":768644,"title":"","content":"... and today I'm struggling with feeling like a colossal loser. Here I am, applying for social assistance, while my boyfriend is at work. I know this program isn't just to pay the bills, it's to see if I can find a therapist to start CBT so I can get back to work but, I feel like a fraud doing this. We need to pay the bills and I need to get better, but I still feel like a piece of crap today. I'm choosing to interpret this as a good thing; I'm going to use it as motivation to get better. I just have to keep reminding myself of the plan: Get help, get better, get training, get a job. These things take time, they can't happen in just one week. At least I know I'm not lazy or complacent - I am actively doing something about this mess rather than wallowing in it or blaming others for this. I'm doing exactly what I should be doing - social assistance is nothing to be ashamed of, either. I've paid into this system with my tax dollars, I am allowed to take advantage of it now that I need it. Just keep focusing on the plan, wulf. Don't let this guilt swallow you, but don't ignore that motivation to do something about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T15:32:37-08:00","id":768750,"title":"","content":"That's the spirit!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T15:57:43-08:00","id":768763,"title":"","content":"To everyone in this thread who is suffering, I am sorry. I wish I had more to offer you than my sympathies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T00:52:31-08:00","id":769026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=768644#post768644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and today I'm struggling with feeling like a colossal loser. Here I am, applying for social assistance, while my boyfriend is at work. I know this program isn't just to pay the bills, it's to see if I can find a therapist to start CBT so I can get back to work but, I feel like a fraud doing this. We need to pay the bills and I need to get better, but I still feel like a piece of crap today. I'm choosing to interpret this as a good thing; I'm going to use it as motivation to get better. I just have to keep reminding myself of the plan: Get help, get better, get training, get a job. These things take time, they can't happen in just one week. At least I know I'm not lazy or complacent - I am actively doing something about this mess rather than wallowing in it or blaming others for this. I'm doing exactly what I should be doing - social assistance is nothing to be ashamed of, either. I've paid into this system with my tax dollars, I am allowed to take advantage of it now that I need it. Just keep focusing on the plan, wulf. Don't let this guilt swallow you, but don't ignore that motivation to do something about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing to be guilty about in your situation. I know you realise this intelectually, but it never hurts to have someone confirm that when your feelings don't align with your logic.<br /> <br /> I was on (the local equivalent of) social assistance for a full year while looking for a job. I hated it, hated that my gf left for work everyday and not me, hated having to little money to spend on anything else other than food and rend, and most of all, hated that what little money and financial confort came from public assistance and friends wishing to help. The last part was stupid as hell : I didn't choose to be in that situation, and I was actively job-hunting. Ignore that voice if you can. Get help, get better, get a job is a great plan, and those kind of plans are what social assistance is<i> for</i>.<br /> <br /> Vibes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T01:56:57-08:00","id":769047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=769026#post769026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was on (the local equivalent of) social assistance for a full year while looking for a job. I hated it, hated that my gf left for work everyday and not me, hated having to little money to spend on anything else other than food and <u><b>rend</b></u>, and most of all, hated that what little money and financial confort came from public assistance and friends wishing to help. The last part was stupid as hell : I didn't choose to be in that situation, and I was actively job-hunting. Ignore that voice if you can. Get help, get better, get a job is a great plan, and those kind of plans are what social assistance is<i> for</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, now I'm picturing a stand: &quot;$5 per rend&quot; and some poor sucker hanging by the wrists from a gibbet, huge cuts in his body...<br /> <br /> Horrific as I should find that image, it makes me chuckle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I would like to add my agreement: if you're feeling guilty, just keep in mind that you are trying to get <i>off</i> it as soon as possible, rather than bludging. Try to keep a mental checklist (or a physical one, if that helps) of the things you need to do in order to do so - the more detailed the better, so when you manage something you can check it off. Like (and this is totally pulled out of the air for sake of example, I have no idea if it's good or not) &quot;Go a week without having a stress attack&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> You know, unless that's a terrible, terrible idea. Then don't do it. I may be a psych postgrad, but my work is distinctly <i>not</i> clinical in focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T04:25:56-08:00","id":769100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=768763#post768763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To everyone in this thread who is suffering, I am sorry. I wish I had more to offer you than my sympathies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks man. Same here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:00:40-08:00","id":769249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=769026#post769026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing to be guilty about in your situation. I know you realise this intelectually, but it never hurts to have someone confirm that when your feelings don't align with your logic.<br /> <br /> I was on (the local equivalent of) social assistance for a full year while looking for a job. I hated it, hated that my gf left for work everyday and not me, hated having to little money to spend on anything else other than food and rend, and most of all, hated that what little money and financial confort came from public assistance and friends wishing to help. The last part was stupid as hell : I didn't choose to be in that situation, and I was actively job-hunting. Ignore that voice if you can. Get help, get better, get a job is a great plan, and those kind of plans are what social assistance is<i> for</i>.<br /> <br /> Vibes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for sharing your story with me, it really does help me to feel better about my situation. You're absolutely correct that it helps to have someone confirm my feelings. This kind of validation is a real comfort at this time. I feel good about cleaning up my home each day; it was something neither my boyfriend nor I had time for while we were both working full time. So it's really nice to have ways to keep busy and to accomplish things we both regretted we couldn't attend to as much as we wished. This also alleviates my feelings of not doing any work at all while my boyfriend goes out and works. It's not much, but it's something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T02:20:11-08:00","id":769826,"title":"","content":"I'm an addict. I didnt know I had a problem. Its not drugs or alcohol but spending. I HAVE to have stuff even if it puts us in debt. We had to cancel the power that was in my name and switch it to my fiances name because i kept making payment arangments so i could spend the bill money on stuff. I was up to 600 bucks behind on the bill. Now we're &quot;caught up&quot; because its in his name now, so my bill is in collections, same with our internet, did that last year...<br /> <br /> Tonight I came to the conclusion i have a problem. I dont know how to fix it. I dont know where to start. When i get told i cant have something I get mad, and upset. Not like a child throwing a tantrum. I just feel like If i dont get it and get it now then whats the point of money? I get so excited over buying new things, its like a drug to me. <br /> <br /> Its gotten worse since my daughter was born as it went from buying stuff for me, to wanting to buy a ton of stuff for her...I start therapy on the 3rd of december, seriously need to adress this i think, and figure out WHY i do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T02:28:24-08:00","id":769827,"title":"","content":"That's two steps in the right direction, Scel. You aknowleged the problem and have made some adjustments to deal with it. Keep us up on how therapy goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T18:53:02-08:00","id":770443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=769827#post769827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's two steps in the right direction, Scel. You aknowleged the problem and have made some adjustments to deal with it. Keep us up on how therapy goes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks thorbes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm trying. I posted on my facebook hoping my family would be supportive only to get surprisingly harsh responses about how its &quot;not an addiction and i just need to grow the fuck up and realize i'm an adult and cant spend money whenever i want&quot; Ummm seriously if it was that easy for me i'd do it but for me its a compulsion and such a strong need I cant seem to fight it and feel empty if i dont get what i feel I need. To me it is an addiction, it is something I feel i need to do to make myself happy and if i dont do it then i feel sad and upset. I dont know how to explain it in words that make sense, my brain sees it as an addiction, its just like smmoking to me something I cant seem to quit. <br /> <br /> It sucks when family who have history of addictions are being assholes to me for being open.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T04:40:29-08:00","id":770656,"title":"","content":"Shopping can be an addiction, as can gaming and countless other activities, so yeah. If you can't control it, freak out when you are forbidden to do it and is messing with your life, then it has all the signs of being an addiction. As I said, you've done the right thing. I'm sorry about the lack of support of your family, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T05:30:46-08:00","id":770672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=770656#post770656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shopping can be an addiction, as can gaming and countless other activities, so yeah. If you can't control it, freak out when you are forbidden to do it and is messing with your life, then it has all the signs of being an addiction. As I said, you've done the right thing. I'm sorry about the lack of support of your family, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! When I played world of warcrack, I was the same way i'd wake up get right on the game play 16 hours+ sleep repeat, wouldnt do anything else, no cleaning etc. I'd eat at my desk, get mad if i was asked to get off to do something else. I quit playing when i found a new obsession. Yay for addicitive personality? (I get hooked on things super easy...fucking family trait i sware.) Its why I refuse to drink, cause the one time i did I could see why I wouldnt mind doing it daily. Yup. No.<br /> <br /> Eh my family are assholes, I dont know why i expected any less, I deleted the post and called my dad instead cause he's not on facebook and is the most supportive family i have, I know for a fact he will understand. He's always supportive and as an addict(first drugs, got off that by switching to alchol and is now i think almost a year sober FINALLY!) himself(and also dealing with mental illness) we understand each other very well. Maybe its the xanax or the fact i'm tired but i miss my dad, and seriously want a hug from him right now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I dont get to see him much...<br /> <br /> I need to go the fuck to sleep..but we are expecting packages tommorow, and the excitment of getting them is keeping me awake. They were planned purchases in our budget but arrrgg I want to be the one to open the boxes and i know my husband will if i'm not awake when they get here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and i learned today i need to have my doc up my meds lol i took my normally spread every 8 hours xanax all at once cause i forgot to take it all day and shrugged and took it at one time cause i figured it would knock me out...I noticed it didnt make me tired BUT it did erase all my anxiety, the lower dose only slightly kicks it down..However given the above i dont think my doc would approve me taking this amount three times a day *Sighs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T15:20:57-08:00","id":770994,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry to hear you've been facing a lack of support for your issue Scelesta. The sad thing is many people have no clue when it comes to mental illness and addiction. They'll dismiss the seriousness of a condition and leave people without much needed support to pull themselves out of the rut they've found themselves in. As Thorbes said getting therapy and setting up and sticking to a budget are the right things to do. Turning to the family members that will support you is also the right thing to do. Keep at it and it will get easier over time as you make those good actions habits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T17:57:48-08:00","id":771092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=770672#post770672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and i learned today i need to have my doc up my meds lol i took my normally spread every 8 hours xanax all at once cause i forgot to take it all day and shrugged and took it at one time cause i figured it would knock me out...I noticed it didnt make me tired BUT it did erase all my anxiety, the lower dose only slightly kicks it down..However given the above i dont think my doc would approve me taking this amount three times a day *Sighs*</div> </div> </div> </div>Just out of curiousity, did you find it reduced your need to spend? Probably a terrible time-sample.<br /> <br /> Just curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T19:02:22-08:00","id":771130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=771092#post771092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiousity, did you find it reduced your need to spend? Probably a terrible time-sample.<br /> <br /> Just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interstingly yes now that i think about it, it took an hour then once it kicked in, I dont recall feeling like buying anything, or checking websites etc. The only thing I did was check the shipping status on teh stuff i was waiting to get here..then laid in bed for a fucking hour surfing the net while i waited for sleep to take me away and feeling slightly disoriented. (I was SUPER tired, add xanax in a dose i'm not used to on top of that, and just lifting my head of hte pillow made my head spin..In a good way, kinda like when i take narcotic pain killers, or smoke pot. <br /> <br /> I have considered talking to my doc about switching to pot as a treatment, as its safer in my mind then xanax and works just as well for me, but without my doc saying okay, my husband wont let me do it. (Its legal in my state, but still he says no <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T13:22:02-08:00","id":772487,"title":"","content":"Is it bad that something still bothers me months after it happens? I cant get things out of my head, at work I find my mind wandering to it a lot and I think it's making me worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T13:15:44-08:00","id":774224,"title":"","content":"The following is petty;<br /> <br /> I hate that i'm jealous of my younger sister.<br /> <br /> She's pregnant with baby number two. Just found out today. I congratulated her and am being supportive of her concerns etc about having two kids...But I'm deeply jealous, I tried for years to get pregnant, she gets pregnant by fucking accident...Now her baby is three, and I have my beautiful nearly 6 month old daughter...I want another baby <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have since before i found out she was pregnant, and now I just feel its so UNFAIR, she yet again accidentally gets pregnant, different baby daddy then her last one, no job... And me being the HORRIBLE person i am, am secretly wishing she looses the baby because she shouldnt have another child.<br /> <br /> WHAT THE FUCK KIND OF PERSON THINKS SHIT LIKE THAT?! If i had nuts i'd deserve a fucking kick in them for that shit. Its not okay for me to wish that on ANYONE..Yes she told me i should get an abortion and shouldnt have kids cause i have a mental illness but still not okay..not okay at all. NO i didnt say this to her, I WOULD NEVER do that to someone, nevver say that. But i'm still thinking it.<br /> <br /> I'm glad we are role playing tonight so I can loose myself for a bit...Maybe i'll feel less like a terrible person.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:18:11-08:00","id":774357,"title":"","content":"Everyone thinks stuff like that. When I'm in the passenger seat with my brother driving and he says something that annoys me, I have to suppress the urge to grab and wrench the wheel and crash us. When I'm teaching first years, and there's attractive women, I sometimes find it difficult to keep certain thoughts out of my head - not just sexual thoughts, but more explicit and violent ones.<br /> <br /> It's not the thoughts we have that define us. Jealousy, anger and such are every bit as human as compassion and altruism. Our moral standing is defined by the choices we make, and we often have little to no control over our thoughts, so they cannot have moral dimension. <br /> <br /> So, you're not a bad person for having those thoughts, you're just a human being <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:01:34-08:00","id":774389,"title":"","content":"I thought I had something to say about issues...but I'm tired of everything. I'm not suicidal. Just...tired of all this needless pain, my own and others. I hope you all have a good day/week/eternity. I guess I just quit for today. I'll be around. No worries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T00:37:48-08:00","id":774587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=774357#post774357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone thinks stuff like that. When I'm in the passenger seat with my brother driving and he says something that annoys me, I have to suppress the urge to grab and wrench the wheel and crash us. When I'm teaching first years, and there's attractive women, I sometimes find it difficult to keep certain thoughts out of my head - not just sexual thoughts, but more explicit and violent ones.<br /> <br /> It's not the thoughts we have that define us. Jealousy, anger and such are every bit as human as compassion and altruism. Our moral standing is defined by the choices we make, and we often have little to no control over our thoughts, so they cannot have moral dimension.<br /> <br /> So, you're not a bad person for having those thoughts, you're just a human being <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This makes me so happy, because i'm glad to know in this regard i'm just a fucking normal damn human. Its just thoughts not like i'm grabbing a coat hanger and chasing my sister down or anything. I have thoughts like this all the time, just thoughts always thought maybe that meant I was screwed up, guess not!<br /> <br /> Sitting here now i'm fine with it, i realized how petty i'm being and told my brain to knock it off and stop being a dick. (and took my xanax so maybe that helped ) I want to be happy for her, and my future niece or nephew not resentful and jealous. I still have many more years to have another kid x.x (PLus dear god as much as i want another cause i want a big family, the idea of two in diapers now that i've thought about it makes me cringe in horror. There would be a literal shit storm in my house. Thanks no thanks, this one poops enough as it is i dont need more...plus second kid is going to be the devil incarnate for sure since this kid i have now is the most relaxed baby fucking ever, hardly ever cries, easy to calm, sleeps perfectly, smiles at and loves just every fucking living being. I fear my second child will be a terror, never sleeps, always cries, wont calm down EVER and will cry if anyone but mommy holds him.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T06:52:24-08:00","id":775434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=774587#post774587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This makes me so happy, because i'm glad to know in this regard i'm just a fucking normal damn human. Its just thoughts not like i'm grabbing a coat hanger and chasing my sister down or anything. I have thoughts like this all the time, just thoughts always thought maybe that meant I was screwed up, guess not!<br /> <br /> Sitting here now i'm fine with it, i realized how petty i'm being and told my brain to knock it off and stop being a dick. (and took my xanax so maybe that helped ) I want to be happy for her, and my future niece or nephew not resentful and jealous. I still have many more years to have another kid x.x (PLus dear god as much as i want another cause i want a big family, the idea of two in diapers now that i've thought about it makes me cringe in horror. There would be a literal shit storm in my house. Thanks no thanks, this one poops enough as it is i dont need more...plus second kid is going to be the devil incarnate for sure since this kid i have now is the most relaxed baby fucking ever, hardly ever cries, easy to calm, sleeps perfectly, smiles at and loves just every fucking living being. I fear my second child will be a terror, never sleeps, always cries, wont calm down EVER and will cry if anyone but mommy holds him.)</div> </div> </div> </div> It's good that you realized that Scelesta. Knowing those thoughts are counterproductive and not acting on them is what defines you as a good person rather than the thoughts themselves. And as far as the baby is concerned wait until you get into the twos and threes. She won't stay quiet forever.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T14:41:21-08:00","id":777919,"title":"","content":"Strange how depression physically narrows field of vision. Driving home, couldn't tell was stopped too far away from next car at stoplight because hood was out of field of vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T14:48:27-08:00","id":777921,"title":"","content":"I had no idea. I did have problems focusing my sight sometimes, though.<br /> <br /> On other related news, yesterday I had an axiety attack after almost two months without any. It kind of made up for it because it literally dropped me to my knees and I didn't have the common sense of having my medication on me. Now I know better and always keep at least three pills close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T14:56:28-08:00","id":777924,"title":"","content":"The brain's pretty tricky. There was a problem with contrast sensitivity at night that caused a ton of car accidents, I think, in the 70s and earlier. Basically if you were driving straight down a road at night, and a semi-truck with trailer was ahead of you, perpendicular to you, blocking the entire road, a wildly surprising amount of people wouldn't really perceive it. So they'd just run into the trailer and get their heads smashed off or in. I think it was because most people focus on the area where their lights illuminate, and the darkness beyond that wasn't sufficiently broken by the trailer, so they would just understand it as part of the road ahead until it came into the light and it was, usually, too late to do anything about it.<br /> <br /> They added a reflective strip along the bottom, and now I think they've upgraded it to LEDs. They break up the darkness enough to poke your brain into awareness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-01-2015, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T09:11:18-08:00","id":778369,"title":"","content":"Things are most assuredly not going well. I've been alternating between fearing human contact to the point of visceral panic and loneliness that really can't be adequately described without lapsing into depressing poetry for more than a month or so. My best friends have been neglected, and I'm scared I might lose the only people who care about me.<br /> <br /> Has anyone heard from Cereal in the last five days??? His last message to me, found this morning but marked as sent six days ago, was overtly suicidal. Please be ok, ck. I'm sorry that I've been hiding from the world. If you're reading this, PLEASE don't hurt yourself. I don't know what I'm doing anymore and I'm terrified. Please don't be dead. I know I fucked up. I'm sorry! I don't mean to be this way. Please, be alright. I don't know what I'd do..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T13:56:21-08:00","id":778577,"title":"","content":"I also hope CK is alright, but what you have to have cristal clear is that whatever happens to him is not your fault. I can't remember him saying anything other that you are a good friend. And as far as I qualify as a friend (I hope) I'm still here for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T02:35:23-08:00","id":778873,"title":"","content":"Az, you'd actually have to try pretty damn hard to loose me as a friend <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I know you're going through a rough patch, to mean that doesnt mean you're ignoreing me, I'm well aware of not wanting to talk to anyone enough so its okay if you just need some time alone. I'll always be waiting though! I enjoy when I hear my skype notifications letting me know you sent a message! (even if they woke up my baby lol) <br /> So just to restate this: No matter what, no matter how long the silence I will be your friend. Friends dont give up on one another!<br /> <br /> Thorbes- Az told me he got a hold of CK and he's fine!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T03:46:56-08:00","id":778898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=778873#post778873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Az told me he got a hold of CK and he's fine!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very good to hear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T03:48:14-08:00","id":778899,"title":"","content":"Hello everybody.<br /> <br /> I've been lurking these forums for a long time but this thread is what made me create an account for the first time.<br /> <br /> A couple of years ago I lost my father. He died of cancer and I watched him slowly wither and die. I've lost my mother to cancer too 10 years ago so I was pretty close with my father.<br /> I was an only child and was always an overprotected kid, teen even adult. He tried to take care everything, all responsibilities were on him and the result was that when he was gone I was, and still am, lost.<br /> <br /> When he was gone I was devastated. The economic situation here in my country is pretty bad and the unemployment rates are high. I was one of the unemployed. Not that I cared at the moment. For the first time in my life I was living alone but that led to getting a cat that I love so much!<br /> Thankfully.my father had some money in our bank account. Money that started using to buy expensive stuff, and eat junk food everyday. These things were giving me temporary relief.<br /> <br /> After two years of living like this, I almost emptied the reserves of money I had and while I've always been heavyweight, now I'm straight up obese. Thankfully I've found a job but its really stressful and the payment is not good enough to be able to live decently but it's so really hard to find a job nowadays that I don't have the luxury to leave.<br /> <br /> During all that time, my only real escape was pnp RPGs. I'm socially awkward, terrible with other people and social situations but I'm blessed with a handful or really good friends. All the years that I've been playing RPGs I played exclusively with them, and the last few years were no exception.<br /> <br /> The problem now is that they started scattering all around, moving on with their lives. Some have already left for other towns or even countries for studies or work and the rest of them are planning to. We've stopped playing RPGs now and that hurts a lot. My social awkwardness makes it so hard to me to come close to new people at work and while I was always a recluse I'm so afraid of being all alone.<br /> <br /> I think that I'm depressed, but I really can't afford a therapist right now, but even when I could afford one, I didn't bother.<br /> <br /> Well, that's my situation, comparing to others here it sounds small but getting it of my chest for the first time feels good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10022-kalamaris","user":"Kalamaris","date":". 12-03-2015, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10022-kalamaris","name":"Kalamaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T04:16:48-08:00","id":778907,"title":"","content":"There's the things about problems: yes, everybody has them, and some may seem comparatively worse than others, but that is a trap. Your problems are the most important, because are yours,no matter others situation. Is nice and a sign of beig a good person to worry about others, but one also has to take care of themselves first if one is to help another person.<br /> <br /> So, what I'm trying to say, because I've seen it too many times already and I also fell into it, don't demean your own problems by comparing them to those of others. That's making yourself little favor.<br /> <br /> I'm really sorry about your parents and your current situation, Kalamaris. I'm glad you at least found a job, though. As for gaming, I'm sure you could find people here to at least playing online from time to time. Maybe the online medium would aleviate some of your social awkwarness problems when it comes to deal with new people.<br /> <br /> As for moral support, I've found this community to be not less than a second family at times. You are welcome to join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T04:29:37-08:00","id":778913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalamaris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=778899#post778899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's my situation, comparing to others here it sounds small but getting it of my chest for the first time feels good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes that's all you need - just to vent and be heard by a semi-sympathetic ear. I know a lot of my past and current issues can be traced to something similar.<br /> <br /> So, your situation has been heard, and I certainly see how it would be a rough one. Getting sympathy is likely hard due to people viewing you as &quot;blowing&quot; your chance, thus perceiving you as less deserving; a foolish position mayhap, but sometimes people aren't that sympathetic. Plus making any kind of connection can be <i>immensely</i> difficult, moreso if you're not a master of the downright bizarre social-fu that some people seem to pick up intuitively. Weirdos - do they get it like implanted at birth or something?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T22:34:12-08:00","id":780402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=778913#post778913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes that's all you need - just to vent and be heard by a semi-sympathetic ear. I know a lot of my past and current issues can be traced to something similar.<br /> <br /> So, your situation has been heard, and I certainly see how it would be a rough one. Getting sympathy is likely hard due to people viewing you as &quot;blowing&quot; your chance, thus perceiving you as less deserving; a foolish position mayhap, but sometimes people aren't that sympathetic. Plus making any kind of connection can be <i>immensely</i> difficult, moreso if you're not a master of the downright bizarre social-fu that some people seem to pick up intuitively. Weirdos - do they get it like implanted at birth or something?!</div> </div> </div> </div>@Kalamaris<br /> What Allan said. just mentally add the word fuck unnecessarily a few times for flavor.<br /> <br /> Also, welcome to the family! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> - Az<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar897_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"897\" data-vbnamecard=\"897\">Scelesta</a> Awwwwww love you guys *hugs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T22:52:05-08:00","id":780409,"title":"","content":"I'm having trouble sleeping. Today my sister blew up on me on facebook on my daughters fucking group page. I'm done. She made it public so i didnt hold back and kept it public so no one could fucking say i was in the wrong for what followed. She blocked me on facebook, I blocked my entire moms side of the family. They are all toxic gossip spewing harpies. I should have done this years ago, but i never had the courage, i wanted my family to be a family. Fuck that. I dont have to do this, idont have to be put down by them anymore or be a source for their gossip. I endured growing up with my mothers abuse, I endured all the times she guilted me into taking the bus out to see her. I endured my sisters HORRID comments about my pregnancy. But come at me on my daughters page? Expect me to bring my baby girl out in the cold on a long ass bus ride to please you all? NO. Fuck you all. If you wanted to see her or me so bad you'd make the effort, you'd find a way. <br /> <br /> My inlaws are amazing people, they took me in they gave me a chance, and its only been recently that i've really embraced them as my family and truely love them because they treat me like family should..., my husband is amazing. If my family cant see that well thats their problem not mine.<br /> <br /> and yet, i find myself wanting to cry as i'm mouring this. They will never know my daughter, they will never hear from me again. I will not answer their calls should they call. They are dead to me. I will not let my daughter be around toxic horrible people like this. I fucking refuse. It hurts to do this, but i know thats just hte part of me that wished so hard my mom and sister could change, that we could be a close family. I was wrong. Thats what i will have to tell myself remind myself. I wont cry, i refuse to cry anymore for them.<br /> <br /> I need a hug and everyones asleep <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T23:26:23-08:00","id":780418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=780409#post780409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> and yet, i find myself wanting to cry as i'm mouring this. They will never know my daughter, they will never hear from me again. I will not answer their calls should they call. They are dead to me. I will not let my daughter be around toxic horrible people like this. I fucking refuse. It hurts to do this, but i know thats just hte part of me that wished so hard my mom and sister could change, that we could be a close family. I was wrong. Thats what i will have to tell myself remind myself. I wont cry, i refuse to cry anymore for them.<br /> <br /> I need a hug and everyones asleep <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Although not nearly on the same level, I can sympathise at least a little. Even though we know, academically, that cutting ties is the best - or sometimes only <i>good</i> - option sometimes, it's still really, really hard to do, simply due to that degree of history. We're literally hardwired to attach to and stick with relationships, and cutting that link is never easy and always stinks. That tie being to actual blood-family would only make it harder by an order of magnitude, I'd imagine. From a certain perspective our identities are, in large part, made up of those relationships, and cutting them off is the emotional equivalent to hacking off a limb, and even people with gangrene and suchforth still get upset about losing a limb, even though they academically know that keeping it was a stupid bloody decision.<br /> <br /> I'm not there to give you a hug, obviously, but *wordhug* It was the right decision, even though it doesn't feel like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T18:56:39-08:00","id":783191,"title":"","content":"I feel ugly and unwanted. I feel useless, and tired in spirit. I feel these things despite reassurance that I'm mistaken in these feelings. <br /> <br /> I want to think that I matter in the long run, to someone. I don't think I do. <br /> <br /> I hope I'm wrong. <br /> <br /> Nothing is so commonplace as to wish to be remarkable...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T10:43:51-08:00","id":785464,"title":"","content":"This year, I promised myself that, one way or the other, I was not going to live this way (oppressed by my problems) anymore<br /> <br /> One Way crashed and burned. Total failure. And yet, here I am, 3 or 4 months later, and I'm still too much of a coward to do the other way<br /> <br /> I'm a loser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T11:22:33-08:00","id":785485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=785464#post785464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This year, I promised myself that, one way or the other, I was not going to live this way (oppressed by my problems) anymore<br /> <br /> One Way crashed and burned. Total failure. And yet, here I am, 3 or 4 months later, and I'm still too much of a coward to do the other way<br /> <br /> I'm a loser.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>What</b> crashed and burned? Uncertainty does not make you a coward or anything. We are here, so pour it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T19:26:03-08:00","id":785699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=785485#post785485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>What</b> crashed and burned? Uncertainty does not make you a coward or anything. We are here, so pour it out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconded. Say what you need to. We care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","