m.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T21:42:40-08:00","id":815248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=814848#post814848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just checking in, I hope your Okay D, and Azrael! I spent a year of Cloistered Hermitage working as much as I could after being a hobo for 7 months, and now this new Year I am going to be more sociable again and hang out with new friends and play video games again, and Exaaalted. My medical people have been good to me and I am happy. Aaaaalways love lost though. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Holy crap! I was just thinking about you the other day, I didnt want to sound like a creeper though and send a PM. Glad to hear you are doing better!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T22:52:45-08:00","id":826580,"title":"","content":"Its weird seeing a lot of you fellas with different Avatars. I feel like when I complete my repairing of my bodily chassis I would like to volunteer, like at my old Homeless Shelter. Man I really got to witness first hand mental Health at its nadir. I didn't realize how many Schizophrenics lived in my town. In a year I'll be able to Volunteer at the Shelter since I need to wait 2 years to do so. I need to write a letter of thanks to my caseworker and I enjoyed a lot of the staff particularly night staff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T21:13:18-08:00","id":838437,"title":"","content":"Looking around recently, really needed someone to talk to. Realized I have nofriends to talk to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T21:30:07-08:00","id":840382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=838437#post838437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking around recently, really needed someone to talk to. Realized I have nofriends to talk to</div> </div> </div> </div>Message me D! I've known you from Forums past and I'll listen to your troubles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T17:52:54-08:00","id":841615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=840382#post840382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Message me D! I've known you from Forums past and I'll listen to your troubles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconded.<br /> Seriously, you're a person I genuinely like. I'm here if you need to talk. Granted, I'm a natural Malkavian, so I might not be a great source of advice, but I'm willing to listen. Ask the people around here, I'm not bothered about giving the entirety of my contact info if I think you're a decent (or otherwise likeable) person. I don't offer friendship openly too often, but I'm Dean Martin drunk and I can't and won't ignore you.<br /> <br /> Know what? Fuck it. I'm technically a public figure, I guess.<br /> <br /> Email: <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#9adbe0e8fbfff6fcf3e8ffe9eef5e8f7daf2f5eef7fbf3f6b4f9f5f7\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"0b4a71796a6e676d62796e787f6479664b63647f666a626725686466\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a><br /> <br /> Skype: morningsidekiller1<br /> <br /> Snapchat: SlantyGrin<br /> <br /> Kik: NapalmChuckles<br /> <br /> Phone: 505-316-0715<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T01:18:56-08:00","id":842920,"title":"","content":"Dont k ow if this goes here or the drunk thread<br /> <br /> I went on as I always have. I cant anymore.<br /> <br /> I tried to change. I failed catastrophecly.<br /> <br /> I looked into help. I cant afford it.<br /> <br /> I tried to end it. I couldnt do it.<br /> <br /> I tried drinking. I hurt even more.<br /> <br /> I'm out of options<br /> <br /> What else is there?<br /> <br /> HELP! ME!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 03-06-2016, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T17:55:34-08:00","id":843219,"title":"","content":"I've been there, man. My advice, without knowing anything about your situation and based on my own experiences.<br /> <br /> 1. You are not a coward for not ending it. Living takes more courage than dying. <br /> 2. Drinking doesn't help. Alcohol is a depressant makes depression worse.<br /> 3. Just because other people have it worse doesn't mean you don't have a problem. Just because you don't have cancer doesn't mean you shouldn't see the doctor for a Sinus infection. Don't beat yourself up for feeling like this. There is a reason why depression is a mental illness. <br /> 4. You may not have the energy to find professional help, but it is worth it. Even though you read all the websites and books on therapy, having another person talk it out really helps. Check your government for free mental health services. If you are in the US, call 211 to get started. <br /> 5. Depression is a illness, but not an identity. Once I realized that I considered Depression as a part of who I am, I was able to disassociate myself from depression and see it as a illness that can be cured. <br /> 6. Life is a line graph of good and bad times. This is a bad time. Depression is evil because it keeps you from seeing the good times. Things can always get better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:50:13-07:00","id":857368,"title":"","content":"I'm still panicking every time I try to communicate with people. I can barely speak on the phone, and only when absolutely necessary, like bills and medical care. I hate everything about who I am, because I'm too weak to fight this. I can't give up. That's not anything but the hungry emptiness in me talking, refusing to let me rest. ..but it's enough to keep me alive, if not well. It always is.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry for being a bad friend. I was never very good at being close. Too bad.<br /> <br /> Hopefully I'll be back to my old self again...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:00:29-07:00","id":857457,"title":"","content":"I'm having a lot of problems. On Tuesday, the police came over after a friend contacted them, mentioning concern, but not really showing any. My psychatrist (seen on Thursday) said if they were worried at all, they should and would have taken me to the hospital. Which wasn't brought up or anything.<br /> <br /> I feel like I'm so depressed I'm very aggressive in my speech, even though I'm not trying to be, and that makes me feel even worse about myself. I just really have no one or thing to interact with face to face in a real positive way. I was having problems sleeping, but now I'm sleeping around 14 hours a day. Just not feeling good about anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T01:08:00-07:00","id":857574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=857368#post857368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still panicking every time I try to communicate with people. I can barely speak on the phone, and only when absolutely necessary, like bills and medical care. I hate everything about who I am, because I'm too weak to fight this. I can't give up. That's not anything but the hungry emptiness in me talking, refusing to let me rest. ..but it's enough to keep me alive, if not well. It always is.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry for being a bad friend. I was never very good at being close. Too bad.<br /> <br /> Hopefully I'll be back to my old self again...</div> </div> </div> </div>My sleep schedule has been all wonky! But golly when I am not unconscious I'll call you saturday or Sunday! I can officially join your supportnetwork! Well get through this my man, so say ELDAGUSTO!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T23:21:23-07:00","id":869970,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I should be posting this...but here goes.<br /> <br /> I have a hyper-phobia of death that has been following me every single day for eight years now. This is because I do not believe in gods or the after-life. Sometimes I wish they were real if only to prevent my consciousness and all the years within from being annihilated for all eternity. But then again, the mind control of Heaven and the tortures of Hell are both horrible to me. Reincarnation doesn't appeal to me either. I could be born with chronic illnesses, into an abusive family and many other painful circumstances. The concept of Nirvana or some other transcendental state that doesn't require the approval of a terrifying cosmic judge sounds decent, but I might be too weak and foolish to ever reach it.<br /> <br /> My whole life, everything I am and care about, it all feels like a frail soap bubble in a universe of needles. I try to enjoy activities for their own sake, live in the moment and minimize regrets, but it all amounts to an unfunny joke that no one is listening to.<br /> <br /> That being said, I really like these forums. There are a lot of great people here, and they seem to enjoy my posts. It makes me a little happier.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I also fear that I might turn into a paranoid utilitarian as a defense mechanism. I recently broke up with my first girlfriend in a really pathetic way, and it is bringing back my idiotic abandonment and self-esteem issues. I wonder everyday if the few true friends that are there for me to this day will get sick of my boring, whiny, repulsive face and leave. I wouldn't blame them. I expect it to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-21-2016, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T00:05:15-07:00","id":869995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=869970#post869970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I should be posting this...but here goes.<br /> <br /> I have a hyper-phobia of death that has been following me every single day for eight years now. This is because I do not believe in gods or the after-life. Sometimes I wish they were real if only to prevent my consciousness and all the years within from being annihilated for all eternity. But then again, the mind control of Heaven and the tortures of Hell are both horrible to me. Reincarnation doesn't appeal to me either. I could be born with chronic illnesses, into an abusive family and many other painful circumstances. The concept of Nirvana or some other transcendental state that doesn't require the approval of a terrifying cosmic judge sounds decent, but I might be too weak and foolish to ever reach it.<br /> <br /> My whole life, everything I am and care about, it all feels like a frail soap bubble in a universe of needles. I try to enjoy activities for their own sake, live in the moment and minimize regrets, but it all amounts to an unfunny joke that no one is listening to.<br /> <br /> That being said, I really like these forums. There are a lot of great people here, and they seem to enjoy my posts. It makes me a little happier.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I also fear that I might turn into a paranoid utilitarian as a defense mechanism. I recently broke up with my first girlfriend in a really pathetic way, and it is bringing back my idiotic abandonment and self-esteem issues. I wonder everyday if the few true friends that are there for me to this day will get sick of my boring, whiny, repulsive face and leave. I wouldn't blame them. I expect it to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First off: Post here all you want. Seriously. This is a non judgment thread!<br /> <br /> A fear of death is reasonable, i dont know if this will be helpful but here goes: Just because you die it doesnt mean you left NOTHING behind. Sure &quot;You&quot; as a flesh person are gone, but the people in your life(be it friends or family, or even a stranger on the street you saw once), the posts you make here or anywhere else, the things you may write on paper. ALL leave a mark in the world. No one is every truely forgotten, and bits of people rub off on each other, so personality to never is really gone its just out there in a different form. I like to believe no one every truly dies.<br /> <br /> I dont believe in an afterlife myself, i do believe in reincarnation, but life is life even if you are born in the next cycle in some painful circumstance its a lesson to learn, a life to lead. Challenges make us stronger and teach us and prepare us for the next cycle. (No i'm not tryign to make you believe what i do, i'm just saying this so I make some semblence of sense.) As for nirvana or transendace,etc I dont think personally you can fail that, but i also dont adhere to the beliefe that there are rules for such things. If they exsist, and that is what you want when you die THAT is what happens. The ONLY judge you have to deal with when you die is you, not cosmic being, just you. You decide where you go and what you want no one else.<br /> <br /> Your life, the things your care about, yes it is fragile, but THAT is what makes it beautiful and worth the journey however short it may be. Fuck the end point and whatever lies beyond. Regrets happen, happy things, sad things. All of that shapes who you are as a person, all of that if you look at it has made you who you are. Look at it this way, when the lights go out and its all over would you rather be stuck in the afterlife whatever it may be able to watch the world, and lament over the fact that you have to watch people suffer in their lives, or succede in things you did not? Or would you rather it just fade to black, and be content with knowing your actions and deeds left something in the world no matter how small?<br /> <br /> Life is a bizzare joke i admit...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T00:35:48-07:00","id":870002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=869995#post869995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off: Post here all you want. Seriously. This is a non judgment thread!<br /> <br /> A fear of death is reasonable, i dont know if this will be helpful but here goes: Just because you die it doesnt mean you left NOTHING behind. Sure &quot;You&quot; as a flesh person are gone, but the people in your life(be it friends or family, or even a stranger on the street you saw once), the posts you make here or anywhere else, the things you may write on paper. ALL leave a mark in the world. No one is every truely forgotten, and bits of people rub off on each other, so personality to never is really gone its just out there in a different form. I like to believe no one every truly dies.<br /> <br /> I dont believe in an afterlife myself, i do believe in reincarnation, but life is life even if you are born in the next cycle in some painful circumstance its a lesson to learn, a life to lead. Challenges make us stronger and teach us and prepare us for the next cycle. (No i'm not tryign to make you believe what i do, i'm just saying this so I make some semblence of sense.) As for nirvana or transendace,etc I dont think personally you can fail that, but i also dont adhere to the beliefe that there are rules for such things. If they exsist, and that is what you want when you die THAT is what happens. The ONLY judge you have to deal with when you die is you, not cosmic being, just you. You decide where you go and what you want no one else.<br /> <br /> Your life, the things your care about, yes it is fragile, but THAT is what makes it beautiful and worth the journey however short it may be. Fuck the end point and whatever lies beyond. Regrets happen, happy things, sad things. All of that shapes who you are as a person, all of that if you look at it has made you who you are. Look at it this way, when the lights go out and its all over would you rather be stuck in the afterlife whatever it may be able to watch the world, and lament over the fact that you have to watch people suffer in their lives, or succede in things you did not? Or would you rather it just fade to black, and be content with knowing your actions and deeds left something in the world no matter how small?<br /> <br /> Life is a bizzare joke i admit...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you...thank you so much. My eyes got all watery when I read your words, but in a good way. You reminded me of <b><a href=\"https://youtu.be/T6R_rRG_W4Q\" target=\"_blank\">this essay written by Roger Ebert and voiced by Roy Kelly.</a></b> I'll be leaving in a few hours on a short trip with my best friend, and you've inspired me to truly enjoy it and smile sincerely so my friend can enjoy it too. In fact, I'll even save your words on my folder for things that make me feel better and motivate me to improve myself. They will share a special place with the words of Mr. Rogers, Greek philosophers and other wise people. None too shabby, wouldn't you say? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would say God bless you if I had that sort of faith, but let me simply wish you a long and happy life instead. You deserve it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T07:16:06-07:00","id":870168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=869970#post869970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The concept of Nirvana or some other transcendental state that doesn't require the approval of a terrifying cosmic judge sounds decent, but I might be too weak and foolish to ever reach it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nyan, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pure_Land_Buddhism\" target=\"_blank\">Pure Land Buddhism </a>is pretty popular in my country, basically if you do good in life and call out to Amida Buddha or Guanyin when you die, then they escort you to the Pure Land and be your mentor on &quot;How to achieve Nirvana&quot; :3<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T15:10:16-07:00","id":870686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=870002#post870002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thank you...thank you so much. My eyes got all watery when I read your words, but in a good way. You reminded me of <b><a href=\"https://youtu.be/T6R_rRG_W4Q\" target=\"_blank\">this essay written by Roger Ebert and voiced by Roy Kelly.</a></b> I'll be leaving in a few hours on a short trip with my best friend, and you've inspired me to truly enjoy it and smile sincerely so my friend can enjoy it too. In fact, I'll even save your words on my folder for things that make me feel better and motivate me to improve myself. They will share a special place with the words of Mr. Rogers, Greek philosophers and other wise people. None too shabby, wouldn't you say? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would say God bless you if I had that sort of faith, but let me simply wish you a long and happy life instead. You deserve it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aw, i read this before i went to bed last night and it made my heart happy. I'm glad that you found my words helpful. I'm going to have to watch that video you shared as its likely something i'll enjoy. I consider it an honor to have my words saved by anyone. I dont consider myself wise haha<br /> <br /> And a long and happy life to you as well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:21:27-07:00","id":875128,"title":"","content":"Well I finally managed to get a diagnosis of ASD Level 1 or really Asperger's Syndrome. Nice to finally have official confirmation of something I've known for years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:18:26-07:00","id":875295,"title":"","content":"On Monday, I went for re-diagnosis testing (the first part) and had a very rough time, topped off by being told the Therapist I just was referred to because my other one was moving was going to have to refer me to another one after just a single session. So yeah... it was not a nice day when I already was having to force myself to go there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T04:25:46-07:00","id":876469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=875128#post875128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I finally managed to get a diagnosis of ASD Level 1 or really Asperger's Syndrome. Nice to finally have official confirmation of something I've known for years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually looking into that a while back - not sure if I am or not, but it'd be nice to get a semi-official word on it.<br /> <br /> Apparently it'd cost $600 which is not rebated. I don't need to know that badly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T05:02:49-07:00","id":877562,"title":"","content":"I'm into my sixth month of psychoanalytic treatment, after a year and a half of being pinned to the bed with crippling depression. Two weeks ago I had my first breakthrough, collapsing and crying during the session. My parents, especially my mother, were abusive, then I was bullied, then I was cheated on by several girlfriends and abandoned by my closest friends when the symptoms began manifesting.<br /> <br /> I've done some incredible progress, I've experienced some couples of days being entirely lucid and symptom-free (including my eating disorders which were under control during that time). The last three months were the toughest, I dropped out of my only college course (Calculus) because I couldn't get out of bed in the morning. My friends and family didn't make this any easier, saying I was being a loser that didn't want to face the facts of life and move on. I am not one to dismiss suggestions just because they sound like what an asshole would say, but the days I woke up trying to get the most things done ended up in disaster because failing to do even a couple of things from the total I had planned for that day was devastating.<br /> <br /> Now the battle against the symptoms always takes place on my turf and becomes manageable after an hour or two after waking up. Still, some memories and traumatic experiences that have resurfaced from the unconscious, linger around and I have to have a good crying/outburst session before I can get on with my day when I remember them. Mostly stuff about my mother and grandmother, who in their shared hatred of each other used me as cannon fodder, and my current partner's mother who hated me because of her own mental issues (she was the second child, her own family never accepted her or her life choices, so she now does the same to her daughter and <i>her</i> choices which included myself).<br /> <br /> Some days are truly great. I came back from a dark place I never thought possible to return without medication and on such a short time frame. Other days, the symptoms return like an itch I can't scratch unless I analyze myself.<br /> <br /> I am preparing a Vampire session that will include a Malkavian vampire &quot;treating&quot; a child that experienced trauma similar to mine. I feel excited for the opportunity to confront my past in such a way, although a little bit scared, as the &quot;treatment&quot; involves making the child relive the trauma until she finds the strength to stand up to the parents. If anyone's interested, I will post results (i.e. how I felt) after the session.<br /> <br /> Songs I listen to when I break down:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JJYh5k6jv8g\" target=\"_blank\">Memory Remains</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LGQTVNMXbLs\" target=\"_blank\">Gimme Shelter</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 04-29-2016, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:47:42-07:00","id":878231,"title":"","content":"Keep going, my friend. Every day you don't stay in bed is another day you give the figurative middle finger to the depression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T18:31:00-07:00","id":878304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=878231#post878231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep going, my friend. Every day you don't stay in bed is another day you give the figurative middle finger to the depression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I will try.<br /> <br /> My love and full-hearted support to all other forumites on this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T19:05:48-07:00","id":879167,"title":"","content":"I'm not dead. Good news, says the rational part of me. It rarely speaks for my benefit these days, so I don't know how to feel about that.<br /> I hope all is well, and that happiness is found by all who've hung their hat here even a moment.<br /> Gotta go.<br /> <br /> <br /> And thanks for trying, Elda. You're a pal.<br /> <br /> Bye for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:09:45-07:00","id":884214,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> So I've been working on my MPhil in psychology, with the intent to upgrade and complete a PhD. So I need a publication to upgrade. OK, good idea anyway, so I spend a few months gathering and analysing data and writing up an article. Then it got rejected, several times, the last fairly soundly. Fair enough, so I figured I'd finish the MPhil then apply to the PhD - inefficient, but it gets me there in the end. Then it turns out I need a publication to complete the MPhil.<br /> <br /> Then it turns out I can upgrade without a publication, but my supervisors don't want me to for no good reason, and I need their OK to do it. Instead, they want me to get the unpublished article published <i>and</i> write the last third of my 30,000 word thesis in 6 weeks - something they agree is impossible. Fine, I can do the thesis in that time, and I'll just do the best I can with the article. Now it turns out that my thesis is not 30,000 words as expected, but 50,000. (Oh, something to note: I present these as changes, but the administration insists at every point it's always been however it is at that moment.)<br /> <br /> While all this is going on, my social issues have been getting worse, so I finally decided I maybe should get checked for Aspergers (my mother who works with special needs kids, including autistics, insists I am, while I just say I'm an awkward jerk). So I look into that, and to get checked out as an adult will cost me between $600 and $1,500, with no government rebate. Meanwhile, I haven't been able to make much money from my usual source - share trading and investing - because I've been too busy with thesis stuff.<br /> <br /> In more minor news, I've been trying to lose weight, which means my diet has been weight-loss shakes and boiled vegetables. I recently started including more normal-person (yet throughly checked for healthiness and portion-controlled) food, and seems even that is sufficient to stop what small progress I had made so far. So it's back to boiled vegetables.<br /> <br /> Now, I am well aware that even with all this going on, my life is still really, really easy compared to a lot of you here. But seriously, I think I'm starting to approach my limit. What the hell am I supposed to do, when the world seems insistent on preventing any forward movement in any way, shape or form?<br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T07:12:38-07:00","id":885350,"title":"","content":"Also, after thinking over things for quite a while, I'm thinking that my psychiatrist is either burning out or just not wanting to see me at all. My problems get worse, but he wants to see me less often and there's just a number of things about his face/body language as well as vocal tells that speak to not being happy about the appointments with either me or at all. He's showing all the signs that preceded other ones leaving for private practice or whatever. This includes trying to find other diagnosis's (I've had one do a whole battery of blood tests, a different one wanting brain scans to look for tumors).<br /> <br /> I'm tired of having to start over with a new one every year or two. Especially when it seems there's no real movement forward. I keep hearing about how bipolar disorder is SUPPOSED to get better with age, but frankly, mine seems as severe as ever, with one thing... while I still have manic stuff going on, I don't get euphoria while on my meds. Which I wish I did. At least it'd be better than shades of depression with other dysphoria of a manic nature. It's just all very depressing on it's own even if I wasn't already severely depressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T22:06:29-07:00","id":890421,"title":"","content":"I've become the worst gamer ever. I can't interact. I can ramble, rant...but I'm cut off. I can make you laugh, but what do I do if you want to talk? I'm a monologue that fears your judgment, but I write and practice every day to make others laugh. Stupid personal revelations accompanied by tequila (Sauza, accept no alternatives) and a ridiculous, narcissistic worldview spewing from my lazily typing fingers is the norm, and that's goddamn annoying. I've annoyed myself.<br /> Unfortunately, I cannot duel myself. Well, kinda, but solo Russian Roulette isn't much of a duel. Thus, I must push forward, because Barbarella orgies followed by suicide booths isn't a cultural phenomenon yet. I accept that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, hope all is well.<br /> <br /> - Az","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T04:33:46-07:00","id":890540,"title":"","content":"I'm super great! My psychatrist basically told me my insomnia problems are all my fault and told me to just lay in bed 5-6 hours when I woke up. I had been getting up because the hallucinations get worse the longer I lay there, but he wouldn't listen and just kept telling me it was all my fault. It happened that way, then bam, all the euphoric mania! I've not had this in years while on my medications, just soul crushing depression and the upset/angry mania mixed in regularly. So I'm feeling REALLY GOOD.<br /> <br /> Had my psychologist appointment to rediagnose me. Basically decided I'm very intelligent, I guess. That I have bipolar/schizoaffective (which sounds like &quot;You have bipolar, but some symptoms we don't want to call bipolar, because they're uncommon in it, so we'll make up a term that means some blend of bipolar and schizophreia), some very, VERY mild borderline tendancies, but no where near meeting the criteria, and severe avoidance (in short, major fears or problems with lots of social things, so you just avoid it, in spite of wanting it very much). Of course, in the kind of state I'm in, the avoidance goes away. Euphoric mania, accept no substitute for confidence and feelings of self-awesomeness!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T03:41:55-07:00","id":897671,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone, I had posted only once here but now I want to share an update on how my analysis is going. It's been 7 months since I started psychoanalysis, despite having psychologists both in my family and in my group of friends who suggested CBT treatment (or even just Cognitive) and tried to prepare me for the possibility of medication (after I spent a year and a half in catatonic depression, plus an eating disorder lingering since I was 17, in which even outbursts like crying were difficult to muster).<br /> <br /> Today I'm on my third day in a row in which I wake up symptom-free. I had some days like these before, but none lasted for more than 24 hours and if you recall my earlier post, the most difficult part was waking up. I even recalled my dreams, which before I did not (perhaps repressing them?). I bought tickets and I'm finally visiting my parents again (after finding out they played a large part in planting the seeds of my symptoms, I avoided them).<br /> <br /> All this progress feels very organic, building upon earlier progress that now becomes more frequent and longer lasting, with no use of meds whatsoever. While I hope the three day streak lasts and starts a new chapter in my life, I no longer fear the return of my symptoms since it is now ridiculously obvious I can defeat them.<br /> <br /> Stay strong lovely people, I will be frequenting this thread more often now that I have my energy back, and offer all the advice I can. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T03:43:30-07:00","id":897672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=890540#post890540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm super great! My psychatrist basically told me my insomnia problems are all my fault and told me to just lay in bed 5-6 hours when I woke up. I had been getting up because the hallucinations get worse the longer I lay there, but he wouldn't listen and just kept telling me it was all my fault. It happened that way, then bam, all the euphoric mania! I've not had this in years while on my medications, just soul crushing depression and the upset/angry mania mixed in regularly. So I'm feeling REALLY GOOD.<br /> <br /> Had my psychologist appointment to rediagnose me. Basically decided I'm very intelligent, I guess. That I have bipolar/schizoaffective (which sounds like &quot;You have bipolar, but some symptoms we don't want to call bipolar, because they're uncommon in it, so we'll make up a term that means some blend of bipolar and schizophreia), some very, VERY mild borderline tendancies, but no where near meeting the criteria, and severe avoidance (in short, major fears or problems with lots of social things, so you just avoid it, in spite of wanting it very much). Of course, in the kind of state I'm in, the avoidance goes away. Euphoric mania, accept no substitute for confidence and feelings of self-awesomeness!</div> </div> </div> </div>Great to hear you're feeling well! Does this mean you feel better now without the meds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T08:27:33-07:00","id":897836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=897672#post897672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great to hear you're feeling well! Does this mean you feel better now without the meds?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, not at all. I mean, possible, but I'm still taking them. I'm just fairly sure they and other things have resulted in a strong manic episode unlike I've had in years. It's not to the REALLY crazy level, just staying in the... probably overspending, but generally super great, zone. I also have a follow up with the psychologist today for his formal findings/diagnosis. I had called to update the psychatrist about my state, and unsurprisingly to me, I got no response. I'm fairly sure I'm not a case he wants to deal with. I've seen a lot of them burn out, and he's going through all the signs. Sometimes there's no quick fix and doctors often seem to want something to get better, and when it doesn't... But doesn't bother me. I'm just enjoying life. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T19:33:19-07:00","id":898506,"title":"","content":"I'm bipolar with schizoaffective. It's hell on earth when it hits. Try suggesting seroquel (helps with insomnia, it's antipsychotic and helps manage bipolar to a degree). It didn't work out as much as I'd wished because I've been slipping from type 2 bipolar to rapidly cycling and all my psychotic issues occur during mania and mixed episodes. My current issue is I feel like I'm on the cusp of going from just bipolar with insomnia and schizoaffective to paranoid delusions that are kind of freaking my dpctor and family out (ie I'm quitting smoking tool left firearms to defend my family from what I perceive as the threat of severe civil unrest due to our political climate and the effects of the elections [Trump wins, civil war, Trump loses riots in the streets and yes I'm convinced of this 100%]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T19:52:35-07:00","id":898519,"title":"","content":"Just breathe, my friend. Long, slow breaths. In thru nose, out thru mouth.<br /> <br /> I'm bi-polar too and I've kept it in check with calming techniques way more than meds. Don't get me wrong, the meds help. I'm on a daily dose of nortriptlyne currently. Tried a dozen other meds before this one, and the doc was convinced it wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> People said there would be riots and civil war over Obama winning, too. Some of those nutters talk a WAY bigger game than what they'll actually do.<br /> <br /> So breathe, slow and deep and calm, and chant to yourself Om, om, omygodsomepeoplearesostupid, om.......","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T19:57:57-07:00","id":898521,"title":"","content":"And if those techniques don't work, there are ways of focusing and mentally going no-mind through activity... like people who just bike and bike, till they're not thinking. Not even about biking. It's happening without conscious thought. Also an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T20:03:36-07:00","id":898530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=898521#post898521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if those techniques don't work, there are ways of focusing and mentally going no-mind through activity... like people who just bike and bike, till they're not thinking. Not even about biking. It's happening without conscious thought. Also an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found that replaying video games I've played thru dozens of times is good for this, especially when I turn on god-mode so I don't die or have to stop until I clear the level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:58:17-07:00","id":900233,"title":"","content":"I don't know where I belong anymore. Have you ever felt that way? I'm going to assume that, to an extent, you have. I assume a lot. Sue me. Anyway, that's not feeling especially great. I'm less a free little dandelion fluffy and more a sentient severed limb as it kisses the sky following a violent and deadly explosion. Or a less violent metaphor. Maybe one involving baby birds. Terrified baby birds.<br /> <br /> I'm doing my best to keep myself going. I'm feeling damned broken inside. I'm finding myself confused about basic things often these days, and my doctors have no idea what's going on. I've recently started turning on my phone, which has resulted in very little actual human communication, but plenty of Twitter, because hope is just a manic fever-dream and God is a hungry, giant insect. I suppose everything is alright, though. I'm not fuck-the-toaster unhinged.<br /> Yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link