ng another breakdown building. Have been trying to find a term for this feeling bringing me down so bad, think I got it. Lonliness. Crushing lonlinesss....</div> </div> </div> </div>Best I can do over a computer:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://images2.fanpop.com/image/photos/8800000/Big-Bear-Hug-keep-smiling-8892466-400-378.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> You're not alone. We're here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T00:52:33-07:00","id":907021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=905744#post905744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not alone. We're here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn right.<br /> <br /> This is a community. A family for some. You're never alone. I've gotten through some terrible times with this place, and more importantly, the people in it. <br /> <br /> I'm not hard to reach. Unless you value punctuality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T23:54:49-07:00","id":912127,"title":"","content":"Why cant I get over something that happened months ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T09:38:17-07:00","id":912282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=912127#post912127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why cant I get over something that happened months ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the human mind is the only way to travel in time. It can conceive of time as a linear and progressive thing, then break that rule by remembering something. Sometimes, the brain is its own worst enemy. But forgetting what you've been thru doesn't help. You have to remember to know if you want to do that again or avoid it like a plague. <br /> <br /> tl;dr: acknowledge, giggle, move on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:01:49-07:00","id":912320,"title":"","content":"i can't.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T13:48:34-07:00","id":912414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=912320#post912320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i can't.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you can. Tell us the story and I'll help you find the giggle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T20:26:44-07:00","id":912605,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much I can say without revealing too much<br /> <br /> Besides, everyone always assumes I'm wrong. not matter what, everyone else is right, I'm wrong. no one will tell me why, or what I'm doing wrong. I just dont' get it. I don't get what I do wrong. Ido what I'm told is right, why am I the one who's wrong? is it because Ihave no friends to stick up for me?<br /> <br /> I've spent hte last week stayign ahead of a breakdown. I dont' knwo how much longer I can hold out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:05:42-07:00","id":914163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=912605#post912605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've spent hte last week stayign ahead of a breakdown. I dont' knwo how much longer I can hold out.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can relate, I've spent weeks and months like that before. Let it out and you'll fell better. It's not about us helping you with what you talk about. It's not about making sense of it. It's not about justifying your feelings or anyone else's.<br /> <br /> It's about getting it off your chest and out of your system. It's step one: admitting not only that you have a problem, but expressing it in whatever way makes sense for you. Sing a song, tell a story, draw/paint a picture, do free-style, whatever it takes to get it out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T21:05:55-07:00","id":918933,"title":"","content":"So for the past... year (wow. That's just sad.) I've been working on getting an article published based on my work, to no positive result. Which is depressing enough in itself, but I need to get the version deemed &quot;acceptable&quot; by my supervisors before I can submit it, and one keeps insisting I change things. It's starting to get to the point where there are two possibilities:<br /> <br /> 1. He's a douchebag who is actively trying to sabotage my career before it starts. If this is the case, then I'm screwed, because there's literally nothing I can do. If nothing else, none of the other supervisors have raised one hint of an objection.<br /> 2. I really am grossly incompetent and can't write a research article to save my life. Based on what is published, that sets the bar <i>really, really </i>low. If this is the case, then I have no business trying to do a job that I have enormous passion for.<br /> <br /> Combine that with the growing suspicion that my work, while interesting, isn't applicable, which means it doesn't gel with the existing climate of &quot;everything must have applications!&quot; in research. Which in itself says nothing about me, but since I want to do interesting work and not just &quot;applications&quot; which are ultimately reducing the potential sphere of human knowledge, maybe I should re-evaluate my direction anyway. But that then raises the question: if not this, then what? It's not like I'm particularly skilled, charming or knowledgeable. And I've seen enough evidence to convince me that if I was grossly inadequate, nobody would tell me. Actually they'd most likely react exactly the way I see people react.<br /> <br /> It's not that I mind hard work. But if the work I do is this bad...<br /> <br /> (Yes, I'm well aware of the level of awesomeness I statistically live with every day. Doesn't make this suck any less.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T11:24:15-07:00","id":919218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=918933#post918933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for the past... year (wow. That's just sad.) I've been working on getting an article published based on my work, to no positive result. Which is depressing enough in itself, but I need to get the version deemed &quot;acceptable&quot; by my supervisors before I can submit it, and one keeps insisting I change things. It's starting to get to the point where there are two possibilities:<br /> <br /> 1. He's a douchebag who is actively trying to sabotage my career before it starts. If this is the case, then I'm screwed, because there's literally nothing I can do. If nothing else, none of the other supervisors have raised one hint of an objection.<br /> 2. I really am grossly incompetent and can't write a research article to save my life. Based on what is published, that sets the bar <i>really, really </i>low. If this is the case, then I have no business trying to do a job that I have enormous passion for.<br /> <br /> Combine that with the growing suspicion that my work, while interesting, isn't applicable, which means it doesn't gel with the existing climate of &quot;everything must have applications!&quot; in research. Which in itself says nothing about me, but since I want to do interesting work and not just &quot;applications&quot; which are ultimately reducing the potential sphere of human knowledge, maybe I should re-evaluate my direction anyway. But that then raises the question: if not this, then what? It's not like I'm particularly skilled, charming or knowledgeable. And I've seen enough evidence to convince me that if I was grossly inadequate, nobody would tell me. Actually they'd most likely react exactly the way I see people react.<br /> <br /> It's not that I mind hard work. But if the work I do is this bad...<br /> <br /> (Yes, I'm well aware of the level of awesomeness I statistically live with every day. Doesn't make this suck any less.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I say, assume #1 and NEVER assume your degree is inapplicable. It's totally insane some of the things a degree can be applied to<br /> <br /> Did you know an archaeology degree can net you $100,000 a year? Why? Because places where they clear the land to build something have to be checked for ancient burial mounds, settlements, etc. They pay VERY WELL to make sure the findings are accurate and they won't get sued for disturbing the bones of someone's great-grandmother's great-grandmother's great-grandfather. People with psychology degrees are heading human resources departments because you have to understand how people think to do the job. Use some Google-fu and find out all the amazing things your degree could be applied to....unless it's Underwater Basket Weaving. That's still useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T16:05:56-07:00","id":919362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=919218#post919218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say, assume #1 and NEVER assume your degree is inapplicable. It's totally insane some of the things a degree can be applied to<br /> <br /> Did you know an archaeology degree can net you $100,000 a year? Why? Because places where they clear the land to build something have to be checked for ancient burial mounds, settlements, etc. They pay VERY WELL to make sure the findings are accurate and they won't get sued for disturbing the bones of someone's great-grandmother's great-grandmother's great-grandfather. People with psychology degrees are heading human resources departments because you have to understand how people think to do the job. Use some Google-fu and find out all the amazing things your degree could be applied to....unless it's Underwater Basket Weaving. That's still useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potentially a bad example, but I knew a guy with an archaeology degree that ended up having to totally change fields because there simply wasn't work because of the Australian government making/enabling end-runs around rules requiring checking, as well as universities cutting back because of the reduced demand.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, I <i>could</i> do HR work and stuff, except that's a whole other degree pathway. I'd need to go back and do either another Masters or a different PhD to work in organisations (since I don't have honours. It's a whole thing.). My studies up to this point have been pretty well aimed at research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T03:44:45-07:00","id":919628,"title":"","content":"WHO WANNA FUCK WIT THE MONKEY!?!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:50:18-07:00","id":919775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=919628#post919628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WHO WANNA FUCK WIT THE MONKEY!?!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I could make some jokes about spanking the monkey or shocking the monkey, but since that's just a few steps from beating a dead horse, I'll refrain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T11:57:42-07:00","id":919845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=919362#post919362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially a bad example, but I knew a guy with an archaeology degree that ended up having to totally change fields because there simply wasn't work because of the Australian government making/enabling end-runs around rules requiring checking, as well as universities cutting back because of the reduced demand.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, I <i>could</i> do HR work and stuff, except that's a whole other degree pathway. I'd need to go back and do either another Masters or a different PhD to work in organisations (since I don't have honours. It's a whole thing.). My studies up to this point have been pretty well aimed at research.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is remarkably difficult to get the exact job you want doing what you want.<br /> <br /> Out of college, I was trained and set up to become a network administrator with a side order of programming skills and delving into a layer of device integration... robotics and such.<br /> <br /> Where I ended up was software development with a focus on complex legacy systems and a semi-obscure language called Delphi.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:38:39-07:00","id":919918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=919845#post919845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is remarkably difficult to get the exact job you want doing what you want.<br /> <br /> Out of college, I was trained and set up to become a network administrator with a side order of programming skills and delving into a layer of device integration... robotics and such.<br /> <br /> Where I ended up was software development with a focus on complex legacy systems and a semi-obscure language called Delphi.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, and I wouldn't mind doing some other job that allows me to do research on the side, but due to regulatory crap and other such nonsense, psych is very... stratified? There's markedly different requirements for each broad field, and they don't really apply outside of that field. So if you start down one path, and turns out that's not going to work for whatever reason, you are profoundly screwed.<br /> <br /> But this is even broader than that. Research (I think generally, but I've only observed it in psychology) now has to solve problems, rather than answer questions, and those are very different goals. If my work solves problems, that's obviously great. And if people want to do work solving problems, that's fantastic too. But what I see as a problem - and I suspect this is a direct and inevitable result of this problem focus - is the active discouragement of curiousity and sense of exploration in researchers. I'm not naive; I know grants and that have always shaped research. But that was always viewed as a necessary evil, not an actively good thing. It's the difference between &quot;what is funded gets researched&quot; and &quot;what is funded is what <i>should</i> be researched&quot;. Not to toot my own horn, but I have more curiousity in my thumb than most of the research students I know, and I've faced nothing but strife for it because my work isn't directly, easily applied.<br /> <br /> Geez, I dunno. Maybe this isn't the career for me. But if it isn't, what is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:58:29-07:00","id":920427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=919918#post919918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that, and I wouldn't mind doing some other job that allows me to do research on the side, but due to regulatory crap and other such nonsense, psych is very... stratified? There's markedly different requirements for each broad field, and they don't really apply outside of that field. So if you start down one path, and turns out that's not going to work for whatever reason, you are profoundly screwed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Unless to transition to something else. Not as a single step, but as multiple. There are situations where you plan a career and might have 2-3 different jobs planned in a row to get to the position you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=919918#post919918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this is even broader than that. Research (I think generally, but I've only observed it in psychology) now has to solve problems, rather than answer questions, and those are very different goals. If my work solves problems, that's obviously great. And if people want to do work solving problems, that's fantastic too. But what I see as a problem - and I suspect this is a direct and inevitable result of this problem focus - is the active discouragement of curiousity and sense of exploration in researchers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeeh, yes and no. Research in pretty much all fields, is moving away from classical research and more into a development role. It's less &quot;discover how x works&quot; and more &quot;find a way to use y information about x to make something salable&quot;. The few things are are doing research are doing it with heavy grants and research in particular directions are encouraged.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=919918#post919918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not naive; I know grants and that have always shaped research. But that was always viewed as a necessary evil, not an actively good thing. It's the difference between &quot;what is funded gets researched&quot; and &quot;what is funded is what <i>should</i> be researched&quot;. Not to toot my own horn, but I have more curiousity in my thumb than most of the research students I know, and I've faced nothing but strife for it because my work isn't directly, easily applied.<br /> <br /> Geez, I dunno. Maybe this isn't the career for me. But if it isn't, what is?</div> </div> </div> </div> Research is a very idealistic and abstract thing. There *are* pure researchers out there, and there are some few that exist primarily on governmental funding rather than heavy corporate influence... but those are few and far between. Generally you need to be very unique in your skill sets to be able get in on them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T07:34:54-07:00","id":920948,"title":"","content":"I helped someone from the Homeless shelter and let them stay with me till they could get a sublet. But this person, who is twice my age, turned out to be much more mentally unbalanced. She believes she has a tracking device placed inside her by an ex husband. She refused to make an appointment to go to the Homeless shelter, and refused a sublet I found her because it doesn't have AC. Because of that I gave her a deadline of one week. She wasn't cooperating so I called the police. Now I have to get an eviction notice.<br /> <br /> I really really tried helping, but I screwed up and bit off more then I can chew. I didn't know the person I let into my abode was this unhinged. Her plan is to get the FBI to airlift her out of the state, because the local police aren't cooperating to her satisfaction, because she is irrational. She refers to everything as domestic abuse, even craigslisters not giving her subleases, or get police or government staff not being helpful. She doesn't understand why they banned her from the local women's shelter, even though her divorce was like a decade ago and I tried explaining they have their hands full with people that need immediate help from current situations.<br /> <br /> She believes I am a betrayer even though I let her use my small 1 bedroom apartment while I hide in my room and only cook meals on my days off. She is very clearly a hypocondriac and believes particles of Gluten will contaminate her food and make her sick if she doesn't hermetically seal anything she eats. Like she won't even eat rice I cook because gluten could be sneaking into the WASH AND COOKED RICE.<br /> <br /> Now I have to wait till monday to get an eviction notice. When the deadline expired she sat outside my door all night, and blamed me for not being a good friend.<br /> <br /> When I was sick nobody was ever this patient with me, so I really tried helping. But I failed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T07:56:39-07:00","id":920954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=920948#post920948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I helped someone from the Homeless shelter and let them stay with me till they could get a sublet. But this person, who is twice my age, turned out to be much more mentally unbalanced. She believes she has a tracking device placed inside her by an ex husband. She refused to make an appointment to go to the Homeless shelter, and refused a sublet I found her because it doesn't have AC. Because of that I gave her a deadline of one week. She wasn't cooperating so I called the police. Now I have to get an eviction notice.<br /> <br /> ..........<br /> <br /> When I was sick nobody was ever this patient with me, so I really tried helping. But I failed.</div> </div> </div> </div>/hugs<br /> <br /> Your heart, a big heart, was in the right place. Sometimes things don't work out the way you'd hope, but you made a real effort. I'm sorry it didn't work out, but that's not your fault in the least.<br /> <br /> Don't feel bad about trying to do good for someone. You said it yourself: nobody was ever that patient with you. You went above and beyond for her. I hope things smooth out as well as they can. <br /> <br /> May today and tomorrow be better than the days before them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T19:18:38-07:00","id":921291,"title":"","content":"I spent the day with a couple my friends, it made me feel better. Thanks for the Hug Az. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Some of my friends are or were staff the homeless shelter, they feel bad I got wrangled into this mess. On one hand she is irrational and mentally unbalanced, on the other hand she knows full well she took advantage of me because I was working on the honor system of if she says she needs help I would help her, and she took as much as I could have helped and when I did not want to help anymore she resorts to force. Not everyone was like that though, there were a rare few gems in the shelter that I know wouldn't do this if placed in similar situation. But I guess a lot would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T21:10:45-07:00","id":921840,"title":"","content":"Looking for a therapist. Once again being thwarted by the fact none lokk trustworthy or seem condescending.<br /> <br /> I may just give up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T01:53:43-07:00","id":921899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=921840#post921840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking for a therapist. Once again being thwarted by the fact none lokk trustworthy or seem condescending.<br /> <br /> I may just give up.</div> </div> </div> </div>There ARE so many psychotherapists that think they've found their master key to treatment, and quite many are just blowhard assholes who love a paycheck. But please, don't give up. I'm looking for better help myself. You matter to me. Forumites with a shred of honesty oftentimes can't be ignored by me. <br /> <br /> I don't recommend giving up. Life still has surprises for you.<br /> <br /> If you want a REALLY safe space, feel free to add me on Skype @ morningsidekiller1 or Twitter.@itsjoeypolanco <br /> <br /> I NEVER ignore messages and I'm online unless I'm asleep or on stage. You understand me, D? I'm here. This community, especially those who need support, matter to me the same as blood family.<br /> <br /> These people, around us, are family.<br /> Even through pm messages right here on opp, I'm there.<br /> <br /> My blood is mostly tequila right now, but know that I'll fight on the side of love and reason every time. I love you, because in the broad sense, you are my true family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T13:54:33-07:00","id":922830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=921840#post921840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking for a therapist. Once again being thwarted by the fact none lokk trustworthy or seem condescending.<br /> <br /> I may just give up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its always tough finding a therapist, because you kind of have to get lucky finding one that you feel comfortable with. You could perhaps find the number of your local university's social work program and they may have the numbers of alumni who became psychiatrists.<br /> <br /> The only therapist I trusted wasn't even a psychiatrist yet, she was a nurse practitioner so just under phd level but she was kind and helpful. I think it helped that she was my age. But everyone is different, I have found it easier for me to open up to females for instance.<br /> <br /> But many are condescending, I've found those who think they've seen it all can essentially roll their eyes at you, thinking they have more experience then they actually do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:03:04-07:00","id":922833,"title":"","content":"Got the actual eviction notice and served it to my guest yesterday. She was displeased and call the police telling them I can't give her the eviction it has to be false, she told the police officer I was breaking the law by not supplying her all the luxuries I used to supply her with. I talked to the officer and realized she mislead the policewoman into thinking she was fleeing a recent domestic abuse situation. I explained the situation she left from was a decade ago, and my guest refers to everything she doesn't like as domestic abuse, including craigslisters not responding to her. I explained that she was insane, which the police officer quickly realized when they argued for 10 minutes explaining to my guest that she didn't have a copyright on her name that prevented people from asking her if she needs mental help, which it turns out my guest just saw on an old episode of Three's company.<br /> <br /> So I basically just have to provide her the sofa with cushions to sleep on, and the bathroom and kitchen that is all.<br /> <br /> The police office told her she needs to take the eviction seriously because if she is still here after a month she will be physically removed. I told her that if she is here past a month I will follow up on the eviction and take her to court, to insentivize her to leave.<br /> <br /> I truly feel more and more that my guest has some form of Autism/aspergers syndrome. But she refuses all mental help.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does anyone here know much about eviction laws? Particularly in Michigan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:14:29-07:00","id":922842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=922833#post922833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone here know much about eviction laws? Particularly in Michigan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only that they vary widely state to state and province to province sometimes favoring the tenants sometimes the landlords.<br /> <br /> In your particular situation, I'm not even certain if she's a tenant or a guest.... the difference being if money changed hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:26:04-07:00","id":922847,"title":"","content":"There was no money, she was staying there for free, I only brought up charging her if she doesn't leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T12:38:34-07:00","id":925464,"title":"","content":"Had to run to the store today. While I was there I also bought a pack of razor blades.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T14:56:15-07:00","id":925510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=925464#post925464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had to run to the store today. While I was there I also bought a pack of razor blades.....</div> </div> </div> </div>What why?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T14:58:35-07:00","id":925513,"title":"","content":"I usually buy razors to shave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:34:51-07:00","id":925617,"title":"","content":"nevermind....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T23:10:45-07:00","id":925743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=925464#post925464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had to run to the store today. While I was there I also bought a pack of razor blades.....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vamp throw them away. Seriously they wont help at all. *hugs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T00:20:05-07:00","id":925772,"title":"","content":"Happy 4th of July Vamp, don't hurt your self. Vamp Firestorm be okay!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T07:43:03-07:00","id":925890,"title":"","content":"My job is giving me anxiety attacks...I'm pretty sure Hell is working in a call center for all eternity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T03:09:38-07:00","id":934975,"title":"","content":"So I had two appointments yesterday. Psych and therapist. The first went <b>REALLY BADLY</b>. I mean... ok, I described myself as being manic, because well... that's my current symptoms/mood, of a euphoric nature. And right off the bat he starts telling me how it isn't that, because only counts if you're hospitalized in his mind. Second, he starts blaming me for him not knowing I have hallucinations, even though all my previous ones knew, the psychologist I got my new diagnosis from knew, my therapist knew, and I'm sure I told him. Third, he starts tossing blame at the psychologist because I never got an ink blot, and he says he ordered it to be part of the whole thing. I'm 95% sure if that was to be part of it, I'd have had to run it. It just came off as really passing the buck, nothing is his fault, etc... and I can't get another option because there are no others. Sure, my case is tough. Medications aren't really working. But I'm putting real effort into my treatment, so blame-tossing at everyone else seems counterproductive.<br /> <br /> I'm kinda switching therapists for a while, because I'll be seeing a different one for... shit, now I can't think of what it's called. Some sort of therapy that uses stimuli to make it easier to talk/deal with while talking about past trauma. Like movement of hands, lights, stuff like that. And I really like my current one. After a month, we'll assess if I should see both. They are both nice, and I feel good about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:21:27-07:00","id":935260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=934975#post934975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda switching therapists for a while, because I'll be seeing a different one for... shit, now I can't think of what it's called. Some sort of therapy that uses stimuli to make it easier to talk/deal with while talking about past trauma. Like movement of hands, lights, stuff like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bio-feedback. Usually 4 or 5 sessions, you probably won't notice a thing after the first 2, but keep with it. It works in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T15:57:21-07:00","id":935317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=934975#post934975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, he starts tossing blame at the psychologist because I never got an ink blot, and he says he ordered it to be part of the whole thing. I'm 95% sure if that was to be part of it, I'd have had to run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm intensely stupid about the whole &quot;clinical&quot; side of things, but I was under the impression ink blots are rarely used these days, at least in a therapeutic context?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T16:02:14-07:00","id":935324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=935317#post935317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm intensely stupid about the whole &quot;clinical&quot; side of things, but I was under the impression ink blots are rarely used these days, at least in a therapeutic context?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I only know what he said to me. Edit: Also, did I mention he practically implied he thought I was addicted to drugs since he &quot;has never seen&quot; someone with tactile hallucinations unless they were going through withdrawl? Yeah... just...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 07-22-2016, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T05:46:04-07:00","id":941872,"title":"","content":"So over the last couple weeks I've been being evaluated to see if I'm on the autistic spectrum or not (for reference, I'm 29, if it matters). Not because I thought I was, per se, but the issues I've been having for, well, a really long time were starting to exceed my coping strategies and I just needed some kind of semi-definitive answer.<br /> <br /> So the guy doing the evaluation said to me at the end of the session today that while he doesn't want to be sure as yet, it's looking likely to him that I on indeed on the spectrum.<br /> <br /> Honestly not sure how I feel about that. On the one hand, it's not like it changes anything as such, I'm the same person I was yesterday. On the other...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:11:25-07:00","id":941957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=935324#post935324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I only know what he said to me. Edit: Also, did I mention he practically implied he thought I was addicted to drugs since he &quot;has never seen&quot; someone with tactile hallucinations unless they were going through withdrawl? Yeah... just...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a burn out. Might wanna switch doctors if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T08:51:40-07:00","id":941980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=941872#post941872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly not sure how I feel about that. On the one hand, it's not like it changes anything as such, I'm the same person I was yesterday. On the other...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah you do seem at least past the hardest part, the early developmental ages and public schools. Providing the diagnosis is accurate you have the ability and independence to look up methods to help yourself and enact the ones you feel appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:24:22-07:00","id":942003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=941957#post941957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a burn out. Might wanna switch doctors if possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's only one there till mid this month and it's him. I'll try and switch once she's in. I feel like men psych are... pretty bad. Like they feel burnt out or like they don't care or just... and I already have fears and such around white men to begin with (and all have been white except two who were/are hispanic). But that's because I'm probably in one of the whitest states.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:26:59-07:00","id":942007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=941980#post941980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah you do seem at least past the hardest part, the early developmental ages and public schools. Providing the diagnosis is accurate you have the ability and independence to look up methods to help yourself and enact the ones you feel appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which can be more valuable than anything......or totally useless.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/princess_bride/quotes/\" target=\"_blank\">Lemme esplain......there is no time, lemme sum up.</a><br /> <br /> When I was 17, they told me I had a &quot;bio-chemical imbalance&quot; and that there really wasn't much they could do but give me some meds to balance out parts of my brain. After less than a year on them, I started to figure out how to manage on my own without them. Now, at 42, they tell me I'm bi-polar 2, and NONE of the meds they've given me have done one bit of good. I'm now back on what I was taking at 17 and, while not perfect, is better than what they were giving me before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:39:32-07:00","id":942118,"title":"","content":"I had similar issues throughout my teen years.<br /> <br /> But still, in the end you've helped narrow down what was, if not perfect, then at least best for you of the available treatments you know about, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T21:23:47-07:00","id":942471,"title":"","content":"When I was a teen mymother would take me to therapists just tohave me diagnosed and treated for the latest disorder she read about. Never failed I always had what she thought about at the time.<br /> <br /> Why I dont trust them. <br /> <br /> Why I cant get help now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:22:36-07:00","id":943088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=942471#post942471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I was a teen mymother would take me to therapists just tohave me diagnosed and treated for the latest disorder she read about. Never failed I always had what she thought about at the time.<br /> <br /> Why I dont trust them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mother did something similar. But not trusting all of them because of a few probably isn't the way to go. Especially since they likely took a lot of what your mother said on her word, as being a parent they're believed to be around you and observe you more than a therapist might. Still, there's a lot of psychiatrists who are in it just to make a quick buck writing prescriptions from 'trusted' psychologists. I'm guessing you're an adult, so at this point in your life you could probably 'shop around' without your mother hanging over your shoulder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why I cant get help now </div> </div> </div>I've never heard of the APA banning someone. There's usually avenues to get help for those who need it. In some countries, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:56:08-07:00","id":943956,"title":"","content":"Had my first appointment with my alternate therapist for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_movement_desensitization_and_reprocessing\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_mo...d_reprocessing</a> so... yeah, that went well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T18:27:39-07:00","id":944047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=943956#post943956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had my first appointment with my alternate therapist for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_movement_desensitization_and_reprocessing\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_mo...d_reprocessing</a> so... yeah, that went well.</div> </div> </div> </div>'EMDR therapy is better than no treatment,' sounds like a ringing endorsement. Here's hoping it's considerably better than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T23:29:55-07:00","id":944153,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, talking with her connected some dots I never thought of before. Small things (there's a recurring element to my nightly dreams of endless hallways and doors that feel uncanny and wrong, and I used to get severe panic when traveling this stretch of road as a kid... which was a thick forest at night, and it hit me that it might seem not unlike a hallway in some ways) but ones that make me feel hopeful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:04:20-07:00","id":944480,"title":"","content":"It's started. I'm having another breakdown......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:53:36-07:00","id":944876,"title":"","content":"As someone who suffers from a multitude of mental disorders, I'm just now learning that some people in the industry are bothered when the terms &quot;madness&quot; or &quot;insanity&quot; is used in escapism; be it video games, rpg's, etc.<br /> <br /> I've had family members that have died in mental institutions, and to this day I suffer from numerous issues, but I've never been bothered by the use of those terms.<br /> <br /> I mean, who the hell am I to tell someone else what they're bothered by(I'm no one), but if I say something(or myself) is &quot;crazy&quot; or &quot;insane&quot; and you then call me &quot;ableist&quot; and follow it with insults, don't be surprised if I look like I want to drop you.<br /> <br /> If you're offended by something, cool. Just don't expect everyone on the fucking planet to have to subscribe to the same issues as you. So I'll keep using whatever terms I want to you, especially when talking about MYSELF, and you can worry about yourself and what bothers YOU.<br /> <br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wasn't sure if this belonged in the &quot;You Know What I Hate&quot; thread, or this one. I'm just having quite the crappy day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 08-06-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T20:22:21-07:00","id":945252,"title":"","content":"What was the quote? &quot;To say something is offensive starts a conversation. To say you are offended ends it&quot; or something? I could google it, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T22:52:36-07:00","id":945303,"title":"","content":"Once, i confessed to a friend how I felt. How much I hurt. And what I was considering doing to finally end my misery<br /> <br /> Others overheard. They complained about it. And my hurt was added to other, totally false, lies in order to punish me<br /> <br /> From how they put it though, almost feels like they're mad I didnt actually kill myself.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T17:44:07-07:00","id":957951,"title":"","content":"Tonight's episode of Steven Universe resonates particularly well with me and many of my issues.I just feel the need to present tonight's song with no additional comment beyond that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oHM8T2Gsciw\" data-code=\"oHM8T2Gsciw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/oHM8T2Gsciw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T22:58:45-07:00","id":958073,"title":"","content":"Im overwhelmed. I feel like i cant fucking do this, i can be pregnant, i cant have 2 children. Maybe tgis wouldnt feel so hard if i didnt feel like a burden to my husband. I get yelled at for using my morning sickness as an &quot;excuse to be lazy&quot;. I take care of our daughter while he is at work even when i feel like shit, i dont think its unreasonable to have him take over when he gets home so i can rest.<br /> <br /> But it is. Im having a hard time forming attachment to this pregnancy, and it makes my heart break. Its not fair to my son that i dont already love him as i dis gis sister at this point.<br /> <br /> Instead all i feel is this sickening feeling of doubt, the sickening feeling of wishing my birth control hadnt failed. I am against abortion but the thought has crossed my mind from time to time. I REFUSE to listen to it. I refuse to murder my child because i feel like a horrible parent unable to deal with the stress of a shit hole relationship and a one year old baby. Why.... do i feel like this. Hormones? Depresion? Fuck even i dont know why i feel this way. WHY don't i love this baby? I gave him a name hoping it would help me bond and nothing.i feel nothing.<br /> <br /> I have no one to talk to. My friends are away dealing with their own shit. My husband doesnt seem to give a shit so i dont talk to him... I had to put this somewhere it could be &quot;heard&quot;....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T01:45:23-07:00","id":958112,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm sorry, Scel. I think what you are going trough is the result of a bunch of stuff, all at once. Yeah, hormones could be part of it, but your husband surely isn't helping. Neither are we, for that matter and for that I apologize. If we could agree on a date and hour I will be there for you, even if only trough Skype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T09:08:53-07:00","id":958258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=958112#post958112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm sorry, Scel. I think what you are going trough is the result of a bunch of stuff, all at once. Yeah, hormones could be part of it, but your husband surely isn't helping. Neither are we, for that matter and for that I apologize. If we could agree on a date and hour I will be there for you, even if only trough Skype.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its okay, i honestly understand that my friends have their own lives and shit going on in them and cant always be on to listen to me complain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T09:19:13-07:00","id":958262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=958073#post958073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im overwhelmed. I feel like i cant fucking do this, i can be pregnant, i cant have 2 children. Maybe tgis wouldnt feel so hard if i didnt feel like a burden to my husband. I get yelled at for using my morning sickness as an &quot;excuse to be lazy&quot;. I take care of our daughter while he is at work even when i feel like shit, i dont think its unreasonable to have him take over when he gets home so i can rest.<br /> <br /> But it is. Im having a hard time forming attachment to this pregnancy, and it makes my heart break. Its not fair to my son that i dont already love him as i dis gis sister at this point.<br /> <br /> Instead all i feel is this sickening feeling of doubt, the sickening feeling of wishing my birth control hadnt failed. I am against abortion but the thought has crossed my mind from time to time. I REFUSE to listen to it. I refuse to murder my child because i feel like a horrible parent unable to deal with the stress of a shit hole relationship and a one year old baby. Why.... do i feel like this. Hormones? Depresion? Fuck even i dont know why i feel this way. WHY don't i love this baby? I gave him a name hoping it would help me bond and nothing.i feel nothing.<br /> <br /> I have no one to talk to. My friends are away dealing with their own shit. My husband doesnt seem to give a shit so i dont talk to him... I had to put this somewhere it could be &quot;heard&quot;....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it can be your hormones. Yes, it can be your depression. The two together will team up against you and try to kick your ass. Just remember, it's your brain, not theirs. Not always easy., but give it a shot.<br /> <br /> And tell your husband it's time to grow a pair, FUCKING MAN UP and help with the kid(s)! He helped bring them into the world, <b>he'd better help raise them</b>. I got 2 Baby Bears at home (6 &amp; 4) and I am on my feet all day for work, then get home, play with them for a bit (it would be longer if I didn't get home so late), help get their baths done, make sure they're in bed on time. In the morning, I'm getting them up, dressed and presentable to the world, fed well enough to keep them until snack time and off to school/daycare before getting myself ready and off to work. I am (multiple expletives) sick to death of overgrown boys (men know their duty to home &amp; hearth) playing this card of &quot;well, I had a hard day at work so I shouldn't have to deal with the kid(s).&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>BULLTSHIT!!!!!!!!! Man up and own your responsibility.</b> You think our ancestors just laid around the house. They busted their asses from dawn to dusk AND THEN HELPED WITH THE KIDS! This &quot;only women watch the kids&quot; shit didn't pop up until the INDUSTRIAL AGE! Y'know, that thing that happened only a century and a half ago!<br /> <br /> And I'm gonna stop here because this ain't the &quot;I Hate&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> Sorry, go back to your regularly scheduled program.<br /> <br /> <br /> ((can you tell one of my hot buttons just got pushed?))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 08-26-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:37:54-07:00","id":958389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=958262#post958262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it can be your hormones. Yes, it can be your depression. The two together will team up against you and try to kick your ass. Just remember, it's your brain, not theirs. Not always easy., but give it a shot.<br /> <br /> And tell your husband it's time to grow a pair, FUCKING MAN UP and help with the kid(s)! He helped bring them into the world, <b>he'd better help raise them</b>. I got 2 Baby Bears at home (6 &amp; 4) and I am on my feet all day for work, then get home, play with them for a bit (it would be longer if I didn't get home so late), help get their baths done, make sure they're in bed on time. In the morning, I'm getting them up, dressed and presentable to the world, fed well enough to keep them until snack time and off to school/daycare before getting myself ready and off to work. I am (multiple expletives) sick to death of overgrown boys (men know their duty to home &amp; hearth) playing this card of &quot;well, I had a hard day at work so I shouldn't have to deal with the kid(s).&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>BULLTSHIT!!!!!!!!! Man up and own your responsibility.</b> You think our ancestors just laid around the house. They busted their asses from dawn to dusk AND THEN HELPED WITH THE KIDS! This &quot;only women watch the kids&quot; shit didn't pop up until the INDUSTRIAL AGE! Y'know, that thing that happened only a century and a half ago!<br /> <br /> And I'm gonna stop here because this ain't the &quot;I Hate&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> Sorry, go back to your regularly scheduled program.<br /> <br /> <br /> ((can you tell one of my hot buttons just got pushed?))</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep getting double teamed by hormones and depression, sounds about right. I do remind myself its my brain, hence why I get up and do things like clean the house, because FUCK MY BRAIN.<br /> <br /> If I told him that he'd just throw a hissy fit about my nagging him. Dont get me wrong he DOES help with the baby when I ask, but NEVER without a huge fit, and guilt trip over how he never gets any time off blah blah cry me a river.<br /> <br /> I am a stay at home mom, so my &quot;work&quot; is taking care of the baby, and handling housework during the day. He doesnt consider that work so according to him he doesnt see why i should get time off when I dont work. He whines that I take a nap during the day saying its not fair cause he doesnt get to sleep at work. Uh, i'm not negelecting my &quot;work&quot; growing a human is tiring, so when my daughter naps I nap to sneak in some extra rest so i can contiune being able to care for her.<br /> <br /> He always wants to play video games, complains about how I never cook, and how he never gets a break and its not fair. Grrr. Whats not fair is being told what I do isnt equal to what he does, just because I dont bring in money doesnt make my job less important or not work. <br /> <br /> His childcare methods annoy me, he wont give her baths, gets frustrated at diaper changes(since she tries to run away andd it pisses him off), I cant really leave him with her ALL day as he also wont stick to her routine she's used to in regards to when she naps as he doesnt want to have to lay down in a dark room and be bored just so she can sleep. (She wont nap unless cuddled in a dark cold room.) 98% of the time I find out he forgot to make sure her sippy cup had water or juice in it, and she goes HOURS without anything to drink when he's watching her. So now before I go lay down i fill at least 2 sippy cups for her and make sure she knows where they are... <br /> <br /> I bust my ass taking care of her. Its not like I get free time much. during the day i'm lucky if I can get on my phone for a bit before she climbs onto me to try to steal it. My laptop is collecting dust at this point!<br /> <br /> Oh icing on the cake for this dickhead i'm married to? EVERYTHING i do is disgusting. I was throwing up and he had the nerve to tell me to hurry it up as it was grossing him out and that I had better clean it up. (I threw up on the living room floor, bathrooms upstairs and it came on so suddenly I KNEW i wouldnt make it to the bathroom, stairs are a bitch to clean so living room floor was the better option).<br /> I have shitty bladder control and its gotten worse since I got pregnant and got whooping cough 3 months ago.(Its gone, but the cough can take months to go away) I pee when I cough. he told me I need to stop cause its fucking disgusting to pee yourself. UH yes i'll get RIGHT on that, I cant control it AT ALL i've tried. I hate it its annoying but I live with it, it s a joyful side effect of pregnancy.<br /> He makes me feel like I'm disgusting for shit outside of my control.<br /> <br /> I&quot;M RANTING.<br /> <br /> But yes, men should 100% have equal part in child care. I hate the excuse that he worked all day and thus should get time off. Sorry dude it doesnt work that way. We have a kid, and another on the way. You cant OPT out of being a parent when its inconvient to you and what you want to do and only parent when its fun or not a burden. Its not unreasonable to offer to take over so your pregnant wife can get a little rest. To me that just seems like common curtosy. am I wrong in that??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:55:57-07:00","id":958721,"title":"","content":"Also, as someone who had a father who was abusive a lot, mixed with a bit of complete lack of consideration... it's better when a father cares. And taking time to do stuff with the kids shows them he cares about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:24:30-07:00","id":971804,"title":"","content":"I was in a car accident on the 14th. Rearended another car going 40mph. I DONT remember why i didnt see her slow, I'm thinking maybe it was the sun, but I just know one second i'm there next second i aware again and seeing the car in front of me had stopped. I hit my breaks, they slipped and didnt slow the car. I smashed into the back of her car. I dont recall details of the moment of the crash. I remember a LOUD sound, and getting hit with the air bag. I didnt pass out, but i was stunned for a moment. I turned off the car right htere in the road, got out, shaking and pulled my baby out of the car and walked to the side of the road holding her close and sobbing while she cried. A wonderful woman who lived in the house infront of the wreck, came out and talked to me, sat with me and helped me with freyja while I calmed down and called my husband at work to let him know what happened, and then to call my mother in law to come get the baby while i delt with the police and such. The women spent over a half an hour with me. Another BEAUTIFUL person that day was a man in a red shirt who lived down the street, he saw it happen, and hurried over to me, asking if we were okay, before asking if he could move the car somewhere safe. I didnt even hesitate to give him my keys, he moved the car, and came back up to us a few minuets later, he said there was a lot of smoke and he looked it over to be sure it wasnt on fire, removed the fuses, and disconnected the battery. He even got a pan to catch the leaking coolant. I thanked him so many times as he left. He came back out 10 minuets later with bottles of water for me, freyja and the kind woman who was sitting with me.<br /> <br /> The woman I hit, her car took ZERO damage somehow thankfully. She was so kind, and was more concerned for me and my daughters welfare then that of her car.<br /> <br /> All said and done the cop took down my info, me and the other driver exchanged info, and my mother in law took me and the baby home. I ended up going to the ER 2 hours after the accident at my doctors insistence. I was hurting. She was worried that the force could have hurt my unborn baby. I checked out fine, was given norco and sent home to rest. 2 days later the pain wasnt any better, doctor changed me to percocet. I've also been smoking ABSURD amounts of weed for the last 3 days as it helps the pain, and relaxes me so i dont freak out or panic. The accident scared me more then i've ever been scared. I've been high as a kite for the last 40 hours i think? As when it wears off, I smoke more.<br /> Husband stayed home from work the last three days to take care of the baby full time because i was high and couldnt take care of her. And even if i wasnt smoking the pot at the time, my percocet knocks me out flat cold, and makes me so loopy i dont feel safe carrying around a baby etc.<br /> <br /> tonights my last night of painkillers and weed I just needed a few days to heal physically and to destress mentally. I'm still scared, I still have the what if thoughts, what if i had done something different, WHY did i not see her slow down in time? I've never zoned out like that. What if freyja had been hurt? I havent seen the car since the accident. I dont think i want to. I couldnt imagine attempting to fix it i could NEVER drive it again, i'd shake everytime i drove it in fear. I'm afraid of that car now, afraid of the memory of the wreck.<br /> <br /> The car is destroyed. I have bruises on my chest and stomach from the seatbelts and airbags. Whiplash in my neck, and it aggrevated my back pain. freyja got crazy lucky, the only thing she had was a slight scrape from her car seat belt. No bruises, no residual pain the next morning.<br /> <br /> We are now trying to save up for a new car(Well new used car.) We have to have one its not optional, i have prenatal check ups, freyja has appointments, i have therapy to go to etc. I sucked it up and made a gofundme to share around my family, since we are not in any posistion to buy a new car, it could take us a year to save up enough on our own <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm dealing with so much. I'm battling depression, then this happens. Now i have high anxiety, and worry. I havent driven since the accident either, I'm afraid when we do get a car i wont be able to drive, what if i'm to anxious? I have never felt this kind of stress and fear, its differnet then anything i've felt before. It shook me to my core being in that accident.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> You can see the hood damage better in this one then the others. After the guy fixed it we were NOT able to open the hood again. Its stuck tight.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://s107.photobucket.com/user/Dana_Everett/media/car1_zps8p7lehyt.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i107.photobucket.com/albums/m314/Dana_Everett/car1_zps8p7lehyt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <br /> Front end damage, it cracked the radiator, folded the hood, likely damaged the engine.<br /> <a href=\"http://s107.photobucket.com/user/Dana_Everett/media/car4_zpsjllrz9ov.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i107.photobucket.com/albums/m314/Dana_Everett/car4_zpsjllrz9ov.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The white cloth on the dashboard in this picture are the air bags, both driver and passenger side went off. Windshield cracked from the impact.<br /> <a href=\"http://s107.photobucket.com/user/Dana_Everett/media/car2_zpsgs04i4pm.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i107.photobucket.com/albums/m314/Dana_Everett/car2_zpsgs04i4pm.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 09-18-2016, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T13:22:43-07:00","id":972094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=971804#post971804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I havent driven since the accident either, I'm afraid when we do get a car i wont be able to drive, what if i'm to anxious?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was in a series of car accidents over the course of a week that made my vehicle unusable about three months ago. One was very similar to yours - I was going about 70 on the freeway and rear-ended a truck in front of me because my brakes weren't responsive (actual impact was at about 30 MPH)<br /> <br /> I had a very, very similar feeling.<br /> <br /> I'm going to be honest: It changed how I act on the road entirely. For a couple of months, I was so paranoid and anxious driving that it was actually a detriment. I didn't really have a choice but to keep going, though, and the past month has been better. The past week especially - I've been able to drive without freaking out at all, although I'm still much more careful and wary of my surroundings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:18:11-07:00","id":974588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=971804#post971804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm dealing with so much. I'm battling depression, then this happens. Now i have high anxiety, and worry. I havent driven since the accident either, I'm afraid when we do get a car i wont be able to drive, what if i'm to anxious? I have never felt this kind of stress and fear, its differnet then anything i've felt before. It shook me to my core being in that accident.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite the rough story you got there, sorry to hear it. I was in a traffic accident a few years ago myself, long story short, I came close to being repsonsible for the death of my baby sister. <br /> <br /> I think an important part of my recovery was that I got back behind the wheel soon after my crash. I think it was the following day my parents forced me to take a drive in the countryside, just to &quot;Get back on the horse&quot;... <br /> <br /> Maybe you should considder getting some driving done, borrow someones car for a few hours, and drive a bit around outside the city where there aint a lot of traffic... If need be, go slow. If your really uneasy, book some lessons with a driving instructor. Everyone Ive ever met in this situation (Me included) agrees that the longer you wait, the harder it becomes to get back in the swing of things.<br /> <br /> I wont bother telling you to seek professional help; if your battleing depression, then your probably more or less in the same boat as me, and know everything I can tell you about professionals being there to help you... Even though they totally are there to help you, and anxierty can be overcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Then again, thats just my perspective. Wont pretend to know what works best for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Decent storyteller. Poor Banjo player.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12373-sarner","name":"Sarner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12373_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T15:03:24-07:00","id":974686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sarner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=974588#post974588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite the rough story you got there, sorry to hear it. I was in a traffic accident a few years ago myself, long story short, I came close to being repsonsible for the death of my baby sister. <br /> <br /> I think an important part of my recovery was that I got back behind the wheel soon after my crash. I think it was the following day my parents forced me to take a drive in the countryside, just to &amp;quot;Get back on the horse&amp;quot;... <br /> <br /> Maybe you should considder getting some driving done, borrow someones car for a few hours, and drive a bit around outside the city where there aint a lot of traffic... If need be, go slow. If your really uneasy, book some lessons with a driving instructor. Everyone Ive ever met in this situation (Me included) agrees that the longer you wait, the harder it becomes to get back in the swing of things.<br /> <br /> I wont bother telling you to seek professional help; if your battleing depression, then your probably more or less in the same boat as me, and know everything I can tell you about professionals being there to help you... Even though they totally are there to help you, and anxierty can be overcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Then again, thats just my perspective. Wont pretend to know what works best for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually thats exactly what i did. Grandpa got is a cheap used car a couple days ago and i immiditaly took it for a drive alone down the road i haf the accident on. I had to be sure i was okay and not be afraid of that road.<br /> <br /> I was fine. I agree waiting would have made it harder.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wish my one year had recovered as well. She used to love car rides and now she cries and freaks out if i even go near the car with het and its a fight to get her in. Poor thing has anxiety over it i think. But like myself i contiune to keep taking her with me. Life cant stop because of an accident.<br /> <br /> I talk calmly to her and offet her my phone to distract her and calm her. Im sure in time she wont even remeber this.<br /> <br /> Im surprised how easy it was to just drive again after a week. I thunk part of it is that for three days after the wreck i kept myself high as shit on my painkillers and weed and slept through the worst of my anxiety and fears. Then when it came time to do it i just went for it.<br /> <br /> Im in therapy! Its lame but required to get meds lol im used to the system it sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:49:30-07:00","id":978151,"title":"","content":"I'm on new mood stabilizers, after a few brief stays in the hospital, and I have no idea what my brain is doing.<br /> I'm in my head a lot. I'm finding myself trying to communicate in very specific, and sometimes contextually inappropriate, ways. Recent example: thinking and talking using paradigms and jargon from an rpg. I don't think I'm delusional, but I can'treally understand the world much except through this lens.<br /> Does this make any sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T23:05:43-07:00","id":978238,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't know the word for it <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar380_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"380\" data-vbnamecard=\"380\">AzraelFirestorm</a>, but sounds like perfect sense. First, game systems try and give a reality that makes sense internally, if not the same sort of sense as our world. It has rules that we know and can understand. Second, chances are you know those rules pretty well, so the fact your mind reaches for them when you're having problems communicating makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:13:19-07:00","id":978559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=978238#post978238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't know the word for it <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, but sounds like perfect sense. First, game systems try and give a reality that makes sense internally, if not the same sort of sense as our world. It has rules that we know and can understand. Second, chances are you know those rules pretty well, so the fact your mind reaches for them when you're having problems communicating makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. It's comforting to know I wasn't acting like a complete nut. The way you put it makes it fit more logically to me now. I'm having trouble with life, so I'm trying to use another set of life skills to get by internally. I suppose the worst immediate downside is just annoying people by talking in fluent VtM instead of English.<br /> Makes me wish I had a local WoD game I could plug myself into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:18:21-07:00","id":978697,"title":"","content":"Well, if you ever want, I know a pretty cool group of people on IRC and maybe you could drop by there (and there are games... though no WoD, just Exalted and Nobilis (I run the Nobilis).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:19:44-07:00","id":979977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=978697#post978697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you ever want, I know a pretty cool group of people on IRC and maybe you could drop by there (and there are games... though no WoD, just Exalted and Nobilis (I run the Nobilis).</div> </div> </div> </div>Your invitation is happily appreciated. <br /> Exalted is in my wheelhouse and I'm a curious enough squirrel to check out Nobilis. I don't use irc much, but I'll definitely give it some thought. <br /> Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar378_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"378\" data-vbnamecard=\"378\">haren</a> !<br /> Feel free to pm me if you ever feel like talking games or whatever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:24:11-07:00","id":979978,"title":"","content":"Anyway, as I was going to say before <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar378_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"378\" data-vbnamecard=\"378\">haren</a> was so nice:<br /> <br /> Today is frustrating and I feel sad and I want to blankity blankity blank until I can't even feel my blanks. That's blanked up, but I'm just tired of feeling blank.<br /> <br /> Angry song.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ha_F6HB3izI\" data-code=\"ha_F6HB3izI\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ha_F6HB3izI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:05:03-07:00","id":980244,"title":"","content":"I might just do that, but probably not today specifically. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T02:40:30-07:00","id":982027,"title":"","content":"I've been having strong suicidial feelings for the last few months and if anyone knows a good source of support or way to deal with them that would be nice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T04:50:26-07:00","id":982059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=982027#post982027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been having strong suicidial feelings for the last few months and if anyone knows a good source of support or way to deal with them that would be nice</div> </div> </div> </div>See a doctor or mental health specialist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T05:58:40-07:00","id":982083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=982027#post982027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been having strong suicidial feelings for the last few months and if anyone knows a good source of support or way to deal with them that would be nice</div> </div> </div> </div>Talk to a psychologist if they aren't too hideously expensive where you live.<br /> <br /> If you have any projects that take up a big part of your life right now, then drop them and hang out with people you value and talk to them about stuff you like.<br /> <br /> Not stuff you like in the sense of &quot;roleplaying games&quot; or &quot;running&quot;, but more like stuff you <i>really </i>like, such as when I talk to all my soulless lawyer friends about soulless lawyer things such as taking ridiculously much money from people and screwing them ov-<br /> <br /> Wait that wasn't supposed to come out.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that you should relax and do the stuff that you most enjoy.<br /> <br /> From personal experience, it tends to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:16:13-07:00","id":983804,"title":"","content":"I tried. It didn't. Tried to come back. I can't think of a better course of action. I'm never going to fit here, and that's just a microcrosm of how I'm never going to fit the world, and nothing I hope for or desire will never happen. I'll never live forever. I'll never have the body I want. Literally the only reason I'm still alive is fear of dying, and everyone tells me fear of dying is wrong. I don't know how to do it, though, but it can't be that hard. I don't know if I should leave a note and be dramatic, or just get it over with. I think, contrary to what everyone says, suicide is just the best option for some people. It was dealing with deathists that made me realize that suicide was the best option, but I realized that it isn't just because of them. It's bigger. Nature itself is why I want to die. The reason deathists bother me is that they, like almost everyone else, can't see the sheer awful horrible monstrous sickening inescapable hopeless awfulness of existence. Every single scientific principle and natural law disgusts me. Knowing that evolution and physics have us trapped in disgusting, decaying, oozing sacks of flesh on a dying inescapable rock prison in an inexorably fading universe makes me realize that there's no point in being alive. The only reasons I ever cared about humanity or the environment was because it was all we had. Fear of death was the only thing that ever motivated me. All I have to look forward to is fifty or so more years of misery and disappointment. Let the world and everything on it die, since everything dies and apparently that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> You know why I didn't kill myself already? Because I held out hope that I could live forever and escape my body. And it looks like neither will be possible. There's absolutely no fucking point.<br /> <br /> I really, really want to do something that will permanently destroy my body, though. I want it gone. If I can't escape it, at least I can destroy it. I wish there was some way I could get all the pictures of me destroyed. And I wish there was some way I could convince everyone who knew me that it was the fault of the universe itself and there was nothing they could have done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-08-2016, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:54:20-07:00","id":983953,"title":"","content":"That is... pretty dark. Believe me, I do am sorry that you feel that way, and you know you really got on my nerves to a point no one ever did, still I have no ill intent towards you and really wish you could be happy. <br /> I just don't know what to do or say to make it so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:11:19-07:00","id":984144,"title":"","content":"I got on your nerves more than anyone else? Jesus christ, the goddamn gall. You showed up in a homebrew thread to complain that I had said &quot;morality stat&quot; instead of &quot;integrity stat&quot;, and you continued to badger me about it even after I repeatedly explain that it was a mistake born out of force of habit. As much as I want to be gracious and say that this forum and community had nothing to do with it, I honestly can't say that I'm sure I would be here if I hadn't started spending time here or hadn't gotten into WoD/ChroD. The events here of the last few months were what brought me here, but I can at least say that I guess it isn't really their fault. The entire universe is set up to create a society and culture that validates their perspectives, and I know very well what it's like to have a hard time taking criticism. I spent the last few days trying to think of reasons not to kill myself, and I couldn't find any. I went back over everything- every conversation, everything I'd ever done, my life, my future- and there's no reason at all to keep going. The only hurdle remains my body. I guess I can always just ask for it to be cremated and the ashes to be flushed or something. If it bothers you, remind yourselves that as much as you'll feel obligated to say you're sorry that it happened, you'll still overall be better off and happier with me gone.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note done, got everything I need, ready. Death is great and nothing to be afraid of, based on what I've heard, so I guess it's time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-09-2016, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T23:42:41-07:00","id":984282,"title":"","content":"Later gator","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T01:13:01-07:00","id":984307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=984144#post984144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got on your nerves more than anyone else? Jesus christ, the goddamn gall. You showed up in a homebrew thread to complain that I had said &quot;morality stat&quot; instead of &quot;integrity stat&quot;, and you continued to badger me about it even after I repeatedly explain that it was a mistake born out of force of habit. As much as I want to be gracious and say that this forum and community had nothing to do with it, I honestly can't say that I'm sure I would be here if I hadn't started spending time here or hadn't gotten into WoD/ChroD. The events here of the last few months were what brought me here, but I can at least say that I guess it isn't really their fault. The entire universe is set up to create a society and culture that validates their perspectives, and I know very well what it's like to have a hard time taking criticism. I spent the last few days trying to think of reasons not to kill myself, and I couldn't find any. I went back over everything- every conversation, everything I'd ever done, my life, my future- and there's no reason at all to keep going. The only hurdle remains my body. I guess I can always just ask for it to be cremated and the ashes to be flushed or something. If it bothers you, remind yourselves that as much as you'll feel obligated to say you're sorry that it happened, you'll still overall be better off and happier with me gone.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note done, got everything I need, ready. Death is great and nothing to be afraid of, based on what I've heard, so I guess it's time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you're alright and today was a bit better than yesterday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T02:22:48-07:00","id":984323,"title":"","content":"Again, I don't feel obligated to do anything, much less feign caring if I did not. <br /> But I do. <br /> And I just was pointing out that despite having had issues in the past with you (even if you consider that it was only my fault) even then I still prefer to have you around. <br /> Death is not the answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T20:16:26-07:00","id":984728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=983804#post983804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried. It didn't. Tried to come back. I can't think of a better course of action. I'm never going to fit here, and that's just a microcrosm of how I'm never going to fit the world, and nothing I hope for or desire will never happen. I'll never live forever. I'll never have the body I want. Literally the only reason I'm still alive is fear of dying, and everyone tells me fear of dying is wrong. I don't know how to do it, though, but it can't be that hard. I don't know if I should leave a note and be dramatic, or just get it over with. I think, contrary to what everyone says, suicide is just the best option for some people. It was dealing with deathists that made me realize that suicide was the best option, but I realized that it isn't just because of them. It's bigger. Nature itself is why I want to die. The reason deathists bother me is that they, like almost everyone else, can't see the sheer awful horrible monstrous sickening inescapable hopeless awfulness of existence. Every single scientific principle and natural law disgusts me. Knowing that evolution and physics have us trapped in disgusting, decaying, oozing sacks of flesh on a dying inescapable rock prison in an inexorably fading universe makes me realize that there's no point in being alive. The only reasons I ever cared about humanity or the environment was because it was all we had. Fear of death was the only thing that ever motivated me. All I have to look forward to is fifty or so more years of misery and disappointment. Let the world and everything on it die, since everything dies and apparently that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> You know why I didn't kill myself already? Because I held out hope that I could live forever and escape my body. And it looks like neither will be possible. There's absolutely no fucking point.<br /> <br /> I really, really want to do something that will permanently destroy my body, though. I want it gone. If I can't escape it, at least I can destroy it. I wish there was some way I could get all the pictures of me destroyed. And I wish there was some way I could convince everyone who knew me that it was the fault of the universe itself and there was nothing they could have done.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I doubt this will exactly help because i know if someone gave me this advice when i was feeling similarly it wouldn't help me, but here's what i got.<br /> <br /> Step out. Stop pouring so much of yourself into rule books and text files where you try to make that one perfect game that you really really want to play out of the scraps of a game that doesn't quite measure up to your expectations. I had to remove myself from some things that I loved for almost two years, because i was putting too much of myself into gaming and it was throwing off my mental balance. Find something you can put your mental focus on and invest your health in and build yourself up. Look for support groups that you can share your issues with.<br /> <br /> I got a cactus, cause it doesn't mind not being watered when you're trapped in your own head for a week. I took up watercoloring and i have a bunch of shitty watercolors of my cactus now, they liven up my walls. Now i have a dog, and she does wonders for getting my head unkinked when I'm in a bad place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:10:39-07:00","id":985137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=984144#post984144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I spent the last few days trying to think of reasons not to kill myself, and I couldn't find any.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop right there.<br /> <br /> You have people here saying that they <i>don't want you to die</i>, persisting in thinking that they want you to die is the voice of defeatism. Don't go there, because it's not a question that you'll ever find an answer to, it's infinitely more easy to find answers to why one should kill oneself than why one should stay alive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=984144#post984144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went back over everything- every conversation, everything I'd ever done, my life, my future- and there's no reason at all to keep going. The only hurdle remains my body. I guess I can always just ask for it to be cremated and the ashes to be flushed or something. If it bothers you, remind yourselves that as much as you'll feel obligated to say you're sorry that it happened, you'll still overall be better off and happier with me gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fuck no.<br /> <br /> Every time I see that &quot;Forget it&quot; quote in your signature, I wince slightly, because it's just such a different attitude to what you opened up with. You used to crack jokes and have plenty of ideas and talk about how cool the games you played were, and while I disagreed with you, I disagreed with you as a fellow forumite, just like I disagree with other fellow forumites. But please, fucking <i>please</i> don't go this road.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=984144#post984144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Note done, got everything I need, ready. Death is great and nothing to be afraid of, based on what I've heard, so I guess it's time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a successful life.<br /> <br /> I'm a lawyer, I work hard, I have a lot of money and I have a nice house (okay, it's a large apartment but I have a car to go with it, so it's a nice house). <br /> <br /> I have an intelligent and beautiful girlfriend from Syria that I can geek out over games and discuss law with.<br /> <br /> I have a lot of RPG books and a loyal group of players that I gather with every saturday evening and together we tell the story of an Amalgam of Technocrats desperately fighting against the dark.<br /> <br /> It is good.<br /> <br /> But it isn't all that.<br /> <br /> My body feels like a cage, it's lungs are diseased and weak. My mind cannot help but think in order and patterns and I have alienated several potential friends with my demands for hierarchy and control, I'm afraid of time to a degree that the mere exploration of concepts such as the end of the world can send me into a panic and accelerate my heart rate. <br /> <br /> My country is in the hands of a bumbling incompetent and the local equivalent of National Front who constantly devise new laws that tear apart <i>everything</i> that this country stands for, and it may soon be called into question whether my girlfriend can even fucking stay here.<br /> <br /> My best friend of ten years was killed in the Ferguson riots, and everyone hates him for being a police officer who only did his job.<br /> <br /> My life was literally fucking shit, and this was only two years ago.<br /> <br /> I fucking considered the suicide option, I really did.<br /> <br /> And you know what? I was too fucking chickenshit to do it, and I couldn't even kill myself.<br /> <br /> And I do not regret that fear.<br /> <br /> Because, if I hadn't chosen to live there, there would be countless of nice people I would never have met.<br /> <br /> So I implore you, do not think &quot;is there anything worth living for?&quot;, ask yourself &quot;could there be anything worth living for?&quot;<br /> <br /> I really hope this helped.<br /> <br /> I really do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:50:21-07:00","id":985162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=984282#post984282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Later gator</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">This is absolutely unacceptable as a response to someone struggling with thoughts of suicide.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T00:31:48-07:00","id":985305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=984144#post984144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got on your nerves more than anyone else? Jesus christ, the goddamn gall. You showed up in a homebrew thread to complain that I had said &quot;morality stat&quot; instead of &quot;integrity stat&quot;, and you continued to badger me about it even after I repeatedly explain that it was a mistake born out of force of habit. As much as I want to be gracious and say that this forum and community had nothing to do with it, I honestly can't say that I'm sure I would be here if I hadn't started spending time here or hadn't gotten into WoD/ChroD. The events here of the last few months were what brought me here, but I can at least say that I guess it isn't really their fault. The entire universe is set up to create a society and culture that validates their perspectives, and I know very well what it's like to have a hard time taking criticism. I spent the last few days trying to think of reasons not to kill myself, and I couldn't find any. I went back over everything- every conversation, everything I'd ever done, my life, my future- and there's no reason at all to keep going. The only hurdle remains my body. I guess I can always just ask for it to be cremated and the ashes to be flushed or something. If it bothers you, remind yourselves that as much as you'll feel obligated to say you're sorry that it happened, you'll still overall be better off and happier with me gone.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note done, got everything I need, ready. Death is great and nothing to be afraid of, based on what I've heard, so I guess it's time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I dont know you, I tend to lurk, and hide here in off topic.<br /> <br /> However, I do agree with you suicide IS an option, but I feel like it isnt the ONLY option. especially in your case. <br /> <br /> Things suck I get that, but it wont always. Life takes work, you are really the only person who can take their life and make it count. Dont let your negative thoughts destroy that. <br /> <br /> When you looked back at your past and saw things you didnt like you jumped to use that to make sure your choice to end your llife was right. Maybe try looking at those things in the past you didnt like, examine them, WHAT in them did you not like, what can you change. Use your past to learn and grow, try not to let your past consume you in any form. Getting stuck on something you said or did in the past is common, take that step to use your experience to better yourself.<br /> <br /> If you dont like therapy, maybe reach out to some friends, if you dont feel comfortable talking to friends about things like this. Post here, vent anything, seriously. Just getting it out can be so helpful. Or (And as always this applies to ANYONE here on OPP) if you badly need an ear NOW, and cant wait for a slow fourm reply, and need another person but find the crisis hotlines uncomfortable. Text me, I can easily text most hours of the day, hell I can even accept a call if its an emergency. 503-840-5311. <br /> I will glady be an ear to listen, no matter how stupid you think whatever is bothering you is, etc. I'm NOT easily offended, I DONT judge, I am just a person who cares about the well being of others, even those I dont know. <br /> <br /> I hope that you decided against suicide. I truly do. Please be well, and take care of yourself. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:05:45-07:00","id":985519,"title":"","content":"And just remember a few things: the best day dead still is worse than the worst day of living. Why? Because dead means there's no other options. Life means you still have choices. Pain is part of life. The only things that feel no pain are dead things. What is good is easy to get, and <i>what is terrible is easy to endure</i> (Epicurus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:18:14-07:00","id":985532,"title":"","content":"I support everything that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar897_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"897\" data-vbnamecard=\"897\">Scelesta</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar375_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"375\" data-vbnamecard=\"375\">Papa Bear</a> just said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:21:02-07:00","id":985675,"title":"","content":"Anyone has a way to reach Gecko and make sure they are ok?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T22:21:33-07:00","id":985949,"title":"","content":"If anyone here knows Gecko, or has been in touch with Gecko, please message me. I got to this forum by searching their tumblr url and they're not picking up on skype or coming online.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I don't even go here.<br /> (I check my inbox in the morning and in the afternoon)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12533-littlewords","name":"Littlewords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T23:26:55-07:00","id":985966,"title":"","content":"The most recent activity on Gecko's Tumblr was on Sunday, and it was an announcement that they had finished the note and a goodbye. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12533-littlewords\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12533\" data-vbnamecard=\"12533\">Littlewords</a> here said they haven't been online on Skype since then either. If anyone knows any other way of contacting them, please let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-12-2016, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T07:31:33-07:00","id":986119,"title":"","content":"Fucking damnit there are no ways to find someone's email on tumblr or here, so I can't try and do that.<br /> <br /> Fucking damnit I feel so fucking useless right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:26:25-07:00","id":986149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=985966#post985966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most recent activity on Gecko's Tumblr was on Sunday, and it was an announcement that they had finished the note and a goodbye. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12533-littlewords\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12533\" data-vbnamecard=\"12533\">Littlewords</a> here said they haven't been online on Skype since then either. If anyone knows any other way of contacting them, please let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have a general idea of location, which should be something an admin can find, you may be able to check the IP and then contact what would be the nearest law enforcement office. If they didn't go through with it and decided to take a break they may still get baker acted but its better than a corpse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:16:14-07:00","id":986233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=983804#post983804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm never going to fit here, and that's just a microcrosm of how I'm never going to fit the world, and nothing I hope for or desire will never happen. I'll never live forever. I'll never have the body I want. Nature itself is why I want to die. Every single scientific principle and natural law disgusts me. Knowing that evolution and physics have us trapped in disgusting, decaying, oozing sacks of flesh on a dying inescapable rock prison in an inexorably fading universe makes me realize that there's no point in being alive. The only reasons I ever cared about humanity or the environment was because it was all we had. All I have to look forward to is fifty or so more years of misery and disappointment. Let the world and everything on it die, since everything dies and apparently that's a good thing.I really, really want to do something that will permanently destroy my body, though. I want it gone. If I can't escape it, at least I can destroy it. And I wish there was some way I could convince everyone who knew me that it was the fault of the universe itself and there was nothing they could have done.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what my problem with your dismissal of deathists is?<br /> <br /> I live my life haunted by the certainty of all that. I live my life in defiance of that certainty. I live my life knowing I'll lose in the face of that certainty.<br /> <br /> Whether you live or die, come back here or find somewhere else to be, that's your choice. You handle that spectre how you will. But if you catch this and wanna talk about it, I'm willing.<br /> <br /> PS to others: Yes, I am aware of the situation, yes, this is how I decided to respond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T03:58:30-07:00","id":986666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=986233#post986233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether you live or die</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this an attempt at possible internet necromancy?<br /> <br /> Internecromancy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:33:56-07:00","id":986835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=986666#post986666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this an attempt at possible internet necromancy?<br /> <br /> Internecromancy?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's called respecting her choices, even if I disagree with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:52:38-07:00","id":986846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=986835#post986835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's called respecting her choices, even if I disagree with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;it's called&quot; part is unnecessary and comes off as condescending.<br /> <br /> I am very well aware of how one respects another person's choices, I was mostly cracking a joke to distract myself from the sadness I feel every time I look at this thread, which may be a sign that I shouldn't look at it in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:05:25-07:00","id":986851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=986846#post986846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;it's called&quot; part is unnecessary and comes off as condescending.<br /> <br /> I am very well aware of how one respects another person's choices, I was mostly cracking a joke to distract myself from the sadness I feel every time I look at this thread, which may be a sign that I shouldn't look at it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have a better sense of what to crack jokes about. That said, I do apologize.<br /> <br /> And sadness is good for the soul. Keeps us empathetic and thinking beyond ourselves. It hurts, but I'd encourage you to keep your eyes here.<br /> <br /> The weeping in the world will not decrease if we do not weep together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:41:38-07:00","id":986864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=985966#post985966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most recent activity on Gecko's Tumblr was on Sunday, and it was an announcement that they had finished the note and a goodbye. <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> here said they haven't been online on Skype since then either. If anyone knows any other way of contacting them, please let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are the only two contacts I have with them, and I hadn't seen that last chain of posts on their tumblr.<br /> <br /> Fuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:13:13-07:00","id":986883,"title":"","content":"I don't have much to say. I know dealing with Gecko on the forums was frustrating to me, but I also hope they spoke with someone and got the help they needed, whatever it is or was. I've been in similar mental knots about things where ending my life seemed like the only way to resolve things satisfactorily. I know that when my family spoke with me and said &quot;it's only a permanent solution to a temporary problem&quot; I would sigh and agree with them because not lying to them and telling them that I really felt that my death would make so many things better for everyone long term would just upset them.<br /> <br /> I still think that if I had gone through with it when I was 16, they would have recovered some time in the last 17 years. They'd still be sad if they thought of me, but they'd be better able to live their lives.<br /> <br /> IDK, it's just something I have to grapple with all the time I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:13:44-07:00","id":986911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=986851#post986851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you have a better sense of what to crack jokes about. That said, I do apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, jokes and scathing sarcasm are my primary coping methods, but I'll attempt not to bring any more of it in here, unless asked to.<br /> <br /> And thanks for the apology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=986851#post986851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sadness is good for the soul. Keeps us empathetic and thinking beyond ourselves. It hurts, but I'd encourage you to keep your eyes here.<br /> <br /> The weeping in the world will not decrease if we do not weep together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I have enough sadness in my life right now, especially pertaining to suicide.<br /> <br /> One of my clients killed herself with arsenic today and my country feels like it's falling apart as politicians who are either too blind or too opportunistic use the xenophobia and fear to funnel more and more money into their pockets and pass more and more restrictive laws.<br /> <br /> And I can't even be angry because I'm the target of those laws, hell I stand to <i>benefit</i> from them.<br /> <br /> And there's absolutely fucking nothing I can do except lend my voice to the choir.<br /> <br /> But I think, I'll add your quote about weeping to my signature. It's a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:03:58-07:00","id":988162,"title":"","content":"It's quite a thing to attempt suicide several times over the course of weeks, try to get myself together, try to self-reflect while I'm lying there healing various self-inflicted wounds, finally come back, look at the messages people have sent, and then hit a screeching halt when you see that one of the people who tried to help you unironically uses the term &quot;tumblrina&quot;, and then wanting to throw it all away and give suicide another try. I wish I could stride triumphantly back like the wounded but victorious hero to tell you all the epiphanies I've had and my newfound appreciation for life, but the truth is that I'm only here because trying to kill myself ended up being yet another failed strategy. I've come up with nothing to refute my earlier conclusions, and I do think it's gratifying to, for once, really know that I'm absolutely right about something: killing myself was the best approach, I just couldn't do it. <br /> <br /> You know what's hilarious? Dwight stalked me to my tumblr to encourage me to kill myself there, and it's funny because it's the most fucking ignorant, incompetent jab at me imaginable. People like him have told me to kill myself before, and it isn't because of their opinions I wanted to die. Realizing that people I liked and admired held ideals that I find terrifying, incomprehensible, and harmful is a lot worse than random people telling me to kill myself, and I just so happened to find myself in the middle of an absolute goldmine of disturbing revelations about people I used to trust. <br /> <br /> I've fought hard to get out of my New Atheist phase, but I do have to say this. Though I'm realizing that I really do hate religious people, I really hate anyone who peddles optimism, even if they're completely secular. Because they're lying. Here's a fun game: if someone tells you that people are essentially good, that life has meaning, or that the world is a good place, they're either lying to you or to themselves. I'm autistic, and that might be the issue. Maybe normal people just automatically pick up that all the &quot;life has meaning&quot; and &quot;people are good&quot; stuff is bullshit they need to play along with, the way they pick up other unwritten social rules, but I never did. I went into life trying to tell myself that somehow all that was true, I believed it, and here I am. <br /> <br /> I wish those hippie chickenshits at Unitarian sunday school had just told me: &quot;Eddie Guerrero's catchphrase has more valuable insights into how to live than anything Jesus ever said&quot;. Dear god, how I fucking wish someone had told me, and kept telling me, that the only way to be happy in life, and I mean literally the only fucking way, is to learn how to lie to and manipulate yourself and others. That's something I've only just fully realized and accepted recently, and god would it have been nice to get it over with earlier. <br /> <br /> I guess those arguments about mortality on these forums finally bore fruit, in that now I have started to actively hate myself for my current inability to die, and I'm ending this desperately wishing I could honestly assure you that this time I would do it, but knowing, deep down, that I'm too scared of death, too weak, too much of a shit to probably ever be able to do it. One more try? &quot;I'm such a loser I even failed at killing myself&quot; seems like it should be my takeaway here, but in a way I feel better about myself than I ever have before: I've begun to grasp, to the extent that it's possible for humans to grasp, just how incomprehensibly awful humanity, nature, the world, the universe, and reality itself are, and I feel like much less of a failure knowing that all of my faults multiplied a trillionfold would not even come near to equaling the tiniest fraction of the tiniest fraction of the merest iota of the absolute horror that is existence. I wish I could say with certainty that I'm about to kill myself, but my track record on that isn't very good. Goodbye again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-16-2016, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:45:25-07:00","id":988172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ez1rWBPznEc\" data-code=\"ez1rWBPznEc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ez1rWBPznEc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T04:03:34-07:00","id":988200,"title":"","content":"I am glad that you are not dead. I hope, with time, you could heal. I am not only talking about the physical wounds, is the other ones wich last longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:36:21-07:00","id":988281,"title":"","content":"Very relieved to see you're alive. Sorry to hear you've come to hate humanity so much. Have you looked into existentialist philosophy at all? It's founded on similar conclusions - life is essentially meaningless, people are not inherently good, and existence is horrifying. But, it also makes the best it can out of those understandings. Might be helpful to you, might not, but it couldn't hurt to look into. Either way, I hope things can improve for you in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T10:24:31-07:00","id":988301,"title":"","content":"Relieved you're alive, but sorry that you're hating humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T17:44:48-07:00","id":988535,"title":"","content":"I'm not good at saying the right thing, but <a href=\"https://scholar.google.com.au/citations?view_op=view_citation&amp;hl=en&amp;user=d5TrVQMAAAAJ&amp;citation_for_view=d5TrVQMAAAAJ:roLk4NBRz8UC\" target=\"_blank\">apparently</a> <a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/David_Dunning2/publication/21194651_Depression_Realism_and_the_Overconfidence_Effect_Are_the_Sadder_Wiser_When_Predicting_Future_Actions_and_Events/links/55ef042d08ae199d47bff2e7.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">depressed </a>individuals are more overconfident and less accurate than non-depressed individuals when predicting the future in their personal social worlds. So although it looks bad, your evaluation is probably incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:06:02-07:00","id":988542,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog/hide-and-seek/201206/depressive-realism\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog...essive-realism</a> Oh look, I found an article saying the opposite in a few seconds, so maybe consider shoving it. <br /> <br /> I can say with the utmost confidence that humanity, the world, the universe, and reality itself are all unremittingly awful. The laws of thermodynamics are undeniable facts. If you accept those yet still think the universe is a good place, you are deceiving yourself. <br /> <br /> I am starting to accept that my inability to kill myself is a flaw. Killing myself would be by far the best approach for me to take, I just don't think I can do it. I am instead forced to deal with working out how to live with that knowledge. So if you're worried I'll kill myself (even though most of you would be much happier if I were gone and there was no one around to criticize things you liked), you can stop worrying/pretending to worry about it, because I don't think I can do with it. <br /> <br /> Unless your advice relates to how I can live as enjoyable and fulfilling a life as possible with the knowledge that I should kill myself but can't, your advice is useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:38:14-07:00","id":988558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=988542#post988542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog/hide-and-seek/201206/depressive-realism\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog...essive-realism</a> Oh look, I found an article saying the opposite in a few seconds, so maybe consider shoving it.<br /> <br /> I can say with the utmost confidence that humanity, the world, the universe, and reality itself are all unremittingly awful. The laws of thermodynamics are undeniable facts. If you accept those yet still think the universe is a good place, you are deceiving yourself.<br /> <br /> I am starting to accept that my inability to kill myself is a flaw. Killing myself would be by far the best approach for me to take, I just don't think I can do it. I am instead forced to deal with working out how to live with that knowledge. So if you're worried I'll kill myself (even though most of you would be much happier if I were gone and there was no one around to criticize things you liked), you can stop worrying/pretending to worry about it, because I don't think I can do with it.<br /> <br /> Unless your advice relates to how I can live as enjoyable and fulfilling a life as possible with the knowledge that I should kill myself but can't, your advice is useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I for one <i>love</i> people criticizing things I like. It gives me an excuse to strike up a conversation about how much I disagree with them.<br /> <br /> Saying it out loud I realize that that might be a character flaw of mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:42:07-07:00","id":988560,"title":"","content":"The universe is not a good place. The universe is not a bad place. The universe is a place. We exist in it and then we don't. Might as well enjoy the time that we do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:43:35-07:00","id":988561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=988542#post988542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog/hide-and-seek/201206/depressive-realism\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.psychologytoday.com/blog...essive-realism</a> Oh look, I found an article saying the opposite in a few seconds, so maybe consider shoving it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two are actually talking about two different things. Yours is talking about the comparatively lesser effect illusory superiority seems to play in depressed people (a phenomenon which is still being investigated to properly understand the mechanics behind it). Mine is talking about predictions of the future and people's actions.<br /> <br /> Also, and I don't want to get into a pissing contest, your work is basically a summary/opinion piece written for lay people. Mine is an actual quasi-experimental study.<br /> <br /> The reason I shared it is because it relates to the idea of &quot;things will never change and people will always be awful&quot; you seem to be putting out, when your judgement would seem to be compromised. As a result, getting help and talking to a professional to help clear your head is probably a good idea: it subjectively appears that these things are obvious, but that is not necessarily an accurate evaluation.<br /> <br /> By &quot;the laws of thermodynamics&quot; I presume you're referring to entropy? Sure, you could view that as an inevitable force for degradation, or you could view it as an inevitable tendency towards change. It explains the phenomenon just as accurately. Yes, it tends to go to lower energy states, but that in no way corresponds to &quot;badness&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if you're worried I'll kill myself (even though most of you would be much happier if I were gone and there was no one around to criticize things you liked), you can stop worrying/pretending to worry about it, because I don't think I can do with it. </div> </div> </div>If most people would be happier if you died, then why did lots of people get really upset at the idea that you might have? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar378_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"378\" data-vbnamecard=\"378\">haren</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2456_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2456\" data-vbnamecard=\"2456\">zeroninja</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7195_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7195\" data-vbnamecard=\"7195\">TidyGamer</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6042_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6042\" data-vbnamecard=\"6042\">ManusDomine</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar897_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"897\" data-vbnamecard=\"897\">Scelesta</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar375_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"375\" data-vbnamecard=\"375\">Papa Bear</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12533-littlewords\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12533\" data-vbnamecard=\"12533\">Littlewords</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar372_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"372\" data-vbnamecard=\"372\">cerealkiller</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> all tried to get in contact with you and expressed sadness at your sadness, along with either implicit or explicit sadness at your attempt. Is that behaviour consistent with being happy at you potentially being gone? Yeah, there are toolbags in the world, but there's good people too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:48:27-07:00","id":988566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=988558#post988558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I for one <i>love</i> people criticizing things I like. It gives me an excuse to strike up a conversation about how much I disagree with them.<br /> <br /> Saying it out loud I realize that that might be a character flaw of mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not alone in this. We're the sort of people the culture of online forums attracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:49:13-07:00","id":988567,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't really care even if your study has issued forth from the mighty asshole of Einstein itself. It doesn't change the undeniable truth that killing myself would be the best course of action. Of the people you listed, I'm quite sure that at least a few of them would be happier if they didn't have to deal with me. <br /> <br /> Again, you don't have to talk me out of killing myself. I'm too chickenshit to do that. <br /> <br /> And regardless of what you think, I think entropy is a bad thing. Anything that guarantees the inevitability of death and decay is a bad thing. Entropy isn't even exactly &quot;change&quot;, because the inevitable end of entropy is essentially a universe of nothingness. Charlaquin contradicted herself. The fact that &quot;we exist in it and then we don't&quot; makes it a bad place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:55:45-07:00","id":988573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=988567#post988567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't really care even if your study has issued forth from the mighty asshole of Einstein itself. It doesn't change the undeniable truth that killing myself would be the best course of action. Of the people you listed, I'm quite sure that at least a few of them would be happier if they didn't have to deal with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in other words, you don't care if the study suggesting that your judgement is compromised is accurate, your judgement isn't compromised? You see the contradiction there, right?<br /> <br /> And why would they be happier if they didn't have to deal with you, and then try to deal with you in a way which is totally voluntary? Again, contradiction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":"10-16-2016, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:57:03-07:00","id":988575,"title":"","content":"Nonexistence isn't bad. No existence isn't good. Nonexistence isn't anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T18:58:51-07:00","id":988576,"title":"","content":"I'm not picking goddamn lottery numbers, take off the fedora. I know much better than you do whether or not my death would be the best approach for me to take. And I'm also quite certain that, say, Captain Nun or Snake would have been happier without having to deal with me. <br /> <br /> No, nonexistence is bad. If you can't say that irrevocable cessation of existence is a bad thing, then you can't say that anything is bad. For example, if you don't think death is bad, than you can't say that murder is bad, for one. And if you don't think death is bad, you have no reason to try to persuade me not to loll myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:08:06-07:00","id":988582,"title":"","content":"Murder is bad because the murderer removes agency from the victim. The victim might not have wanted to die. And probably didn't, after all, life can be quite an enjoyable experience at times. And I don't want you to die because death doesn't occur in a vacuum. Your death would impact the lives of other people, and contrary to what you may believe in your currently depressed state, it would have a greater negative impact on people's lives than a positive one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:09:49-07:00","id":988583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=988576#post988576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not picking goddamn lottery numbers, take off the fedora. I know much better than you do whether or not my death would be the best approach for me to take. And I'm also quite certain that, say, Captain Nun or Snake would have been happier without having to deal with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't give a flying about your thoughts about your death. I don't know your situation. What I do care about is the fact that you're <i>suffering</i>, and your reluctance to try to alleviate that suffering seems to be a major contributing factor in that suffering continuing. There are ways which can help that don't involve hiding or dying, and regardless of your thoughts about nonexistence you'd have to concede that barring a dramatic misunderstanding on our part, it tends toward the irrevocable. Which means it shouldn't be done lightly, ie by ruling out alternatives.<br /> <br /> And even if we take that off the table, there are ways to reduce suffering. If we define suffering as <i>bad</i>, which is reasonably inarguable I think, at least barring some compensation (e.g. surgery hurts for a little, but can drastically improve functioning in the long run), then that should be something that we should at least try to alleviate. If you're going to stick around (a good thing, in my book), then you may as well make it somewhat tolerable. Otherwise you're just being an idiot.<br /> <br /> Let me be absolutely clear here: I do not want you to suffer. I don't want anyone to suffer. I don't pretend it's within my power to stop everyone suffering, but I will do what I can. If there's the slightest change I can push you to seek the help you need to stop suffering, even if I have to hound you and make you hate me and annoy you into it, I will do so, and I'll sleep no worse than usual at night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:22:17-07:00","id":988594,"title":"","content":"I made a very good potato soup today. It wasn't anything fancy, just a 99\u00a2 creamy potato soup in a box, with a chopped up red pepper, a chopped up potato, a little extra garlic and some butter and some milk. If I had killed myself half my life ago, I would never have made it.<br /> <br /> Does it make up for the suffering I went through for last 15-17 years of my life? <i>Hardly</i>. I'm still glad I made the soup tonight.<br /> <br /> There's no meaning to life, except what meaning you make for yourself. Even if tonight's meaning is &quot;mmm that was good soup&quot;,<i> that's still meaning.</i><br /> <br /> I don't <i>hate</i> you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5358_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5358\" data-vbnamecard=\"5358\">Geckopirateship</a> I just disagree with you on some aspects of an imaginary game. I wouldn't want anyone to die because I disagree with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:27:07-07:00","id":988597,"title":"","content":"If murder is bad because it removes agency from the victim, so is mortality and entropy. <br /> <br /> If I could alleviate my suffering, I fucking would. You seem to be making the common mistake of seeing someone suffering and thinking that they're only suffering because they want to be. I can't stop myself from suffering. I have tried. It has not worked. I have sought out therapy, it hasn't worked. Making Mage: The Transgression and TLC was an attempt to alleviate suffering. That didn't work either. Killing myself was an attempt to alleviate suffering. That also didn't work. If I knew how to alleviate my own suffering, I would fucking do it.<br /> <br /> And no, I never said you hate me. I said that if I left, or had never existed, your life would overall be happier, even if you don't accept it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:30:17-07:00","id":988598,"title":"","content":"I don't really know why folks are trying to debate down someone who's suffering, and I know for a fact that when I was suicidal it all felt trite as fuck. Nobody is going to argue down someone else's illness using fucking citations on an internet message board.<br /> <br /> Gecko, I'm glad you're still alive for now. I hope you can find some reason to keep going, and would be pretty goddamn bummed if the world didn't have you in it tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:37:30-07:00","id":988604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=988597#post988597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I could alleviate my suffering, I fucking would. You seem to be making the common mistake of seeing someone suffering and thinking that they're only suffering because they want to be. I can't stop myself from suffering. I have tried. It has not worked. I have sought out therapy, it hasn't worked. Making Mage: The Transgression and TLC was an attempt to alleviate suffering. That didn't work either. Killing myself was an attempt to alleviate suffering. That also didn't work. If I knew how to alleviate my own suffering, I would fucking do it.<br /> <br /> And no, I never said you hate me. I said that if I left, or had never existed, your life would overall be happier, even if you don't accept it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So try again. And again. And again. Find a better therapist, or one with a better fit for you. Perhaps try some medication - that can work for some people, provided you can afford it. Or a support group. Obviously this is not something that can be beaten on your own, by your own experience. Therefore, if it can be beaten, you need help. And since you've already said that you're not going to kill yourself, you may as well do something else in the meantime. Just sitting and suffering without trying to stop it just because past attempts have failed is just downright silly. Some therapists are, unfortunately, idiots. Some aren't. My own experience has been mixed. If you roll badly on one check, do you stop rolling altogether? No (usually). You try again, possibly accepting a -1 penalty, or try to shape the situation to give yourself better modifiers. Maybe try to get another PC involved so you can get some teamwork going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:45:05-07:00","id":988613,"title":"","content":"I've seen multiple therapists. I've taken medication. I don't have the time or the money to send myself to fucking Switzerland for a buffet of every therapist and medication available. No pill is going to make Promethean 2e not have those pissy little jabs at anyone who thinks it's ridiculous for a game about change and growth to be defined by a single rigidly enforced endpoint. No therapist can fix entropy or mortality. I've told you the conclusion I've drawn, and nothing has come up to change my mind. <br /> <br /> The problem is, I'm not a good fit for humanity or this universe, but unlike with a tabletop game I have no options. I can't hack it. I can't play something else. I can't even find a community- I can't move to some town where everyone dislikes children too and agrees with me that popular culture is fucking insufferable when it comes to the raging hate-on it has for immortality and transhumanism. I can't go anywhere. I just have to except that the world and body and species I'm stuck in fucking sucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:01:11-07:00","id":988633,"title":"","content":"If I'm doing more harm than good then I'll stop. I apologise for being superior and preachy, it was not my intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:32:39-07:00","id":988657,"title":"","content":"Anyway, guess what's the best show ever:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_whfpCOFM6E\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_whfpCOFM6E\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_whfpCOFM6E\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/_whfpCOFM6E </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hamlet can get fucked, BoJack Horseman is the most accurate portrayal of depression ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:35:42-07:00","id":988659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=988657#post988657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, guess what's the best show ever:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_whfpCOFM6E\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_whfpCOFM6E\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_whfpCOFM6E\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/_whfpCOFM6E </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hamlet can get fucked, BoJack Horseman is the most accurate portrayal of depression ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Mister Peanutbutter is such a <i>hunk~</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:58:19-07:00","id":988669,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you're still alive, Gecko. I doubt I've ever replied to you before, but seeing what you attempted to do was still painful. Getting definite news about it would be even worse. So I'm relieved that you're physically recovering.<br /> <br /> I've battled depression for quite some time. It's extremely tiring, but I've managed this far and I hope I'll get an even better handle on it in the future. Unfortunately I don't always have that attitude. During my bad periods (especially back during my suicidal periods) I simply can't motivate myself to go on the same way that I do when I feel better. The way I've described it to my therapist is that I practically become a different person when I'm sad and frustrated. Things I love don't cheer me up anymore, and the reasons I have to go on and to live just seem like bullshit in comparison to how much I hate my living situation, my diagnoses, and how much I am a social fuckup. But then when I get those feelings out of my system I have a hard time understanding how I could even feel that way. I'm not bipolar, but that's how drastic the difference is for me. Right now when I'm writing I certainly feel a lot of frustration with my life as it is right now, but I can still enjoy the good parts of my life. RPGs, TV series, bad horror movies (especially this month) and so on. Not a particularly meaningful existence, perhaps, but I'm managing.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to convey is that what you're feeling right now might not actually represent what you'd feel once you've started on your mental recovery. It seems really fucking hopeless right now and I doubt you'll see it this way right now, but I'm glad I never carried through with any of my plans (though it certainly was close a few times).<br /> <br /> I don't know what you're going to do now, Gecko, or what you should do in your particular situation, but I hope it works out for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T21:02:42-07:00","id":988672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=988597#post988597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, I never said you hate me. I said that if I left, or had never existed, your life would overall be happier, even if you don't accept it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have not had a measurable impact on the happiness level of my life, for good or ill. You're just someone I've argued with on the internet.<br /> <br /> You may or may not find it difficult to believe, but that isn't an<i> uncommon</i> description on the internet.<br /> <br /> It's clear you are suffering. I hope that you are able to eventually understand that there are people out there who don't want that to be true.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T21:04:42-07:00","id":988673,"title":"","content":"Edit: Removed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-18-2016, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:10:23-07:00","id":988906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=988542#post988542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless your advice relates to how I can live as enjoyable and fulfilling a life as possible with the knowledge that I should kill myself but can't, your advice is useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did already, but I can lay some more on ya.<br /> <br /> First, to reiterate: What is good is easy to get, and <i>what is terrible is easy to endure</i> (Epicurus). This is not a platitude, but simple adjustment of perspective. By simple, though, I do not mean easily attained as it can take constant reassurance and redundant recitation to remain within one's perspective. It is simple in that it's not complex, which means it's easier to repeat as necessary. <b>&quot;What is good is easy to get.&quot;</b> There are many things in life that are good: breathing is good, eating is good, laughing is good, crying is good, walking is good. We take so many things for granted, and these simplicites of life are missed for their innate pleasure. Try taking a few deep breaths while stretching. Focus on the feeling of the air filling your lungs. Think about how amazing all those little capillaries are, sucking the useful ingredients from the air to keep you going. Feel the tension in your muscles and how nice it feels to release it. Not your thing? how about food? Make yourself a peanut better &amp; jelly sandwich (unless you're allergic to peanuts, because then we're back to the suicide thing). Simple food that can be wonderful. Feel the textures in your mouth. Roll it around a bit. Get all the flavor out of it. Nuts and fruits squashed into paste, do you know how much work that takes? Someone went thru a lot of trouble to make that just so you can shove it in your mouth and swallow. Enjoy and appreciate the effort they put into it. <b> &quot;What is terrible is easy to endure&quot;</b>. Once again, it's a shift in perspective. Name me something that can happen to you in life that cannot be endured, overcome or adapted to. Go on, I'll wait. Loss of occupation? Loss of house/home? Loss of transportation? All can be replaced with a little work or adapted to if long term. Loss of limb or family? Endured and adapted to as well. Depression, even when it's strictly a matter of biology, has methods for enduring and adapting. Loss of life? Ah, there's the one. Only life has potential to persevere. Early and unnatural cessation of said life consequently snuffs out that potential.<br /> <br /> Now, I should state that what you are asking above is nearly impossible. <i>Someone else</i> cannot make your life appear enjoyable or fulfilling for you. There's only one thing in the world you are actually in control of: how you react to everything around you. If you choose not to find enjoyment and fulfillment in your life, and you also choose not to change the circumstances of your life or the perspective you have on it, then it's never going to change. But if you make the decision to change things in your head, then that's your first step on the 1,000 mile journey.<br /> <br /> And if you think any of this cannot be done, I'll refer you to not just several people who post on this thread regularly, but feel free to message me personally and I'll tell you all about my fun times living with bi-polar 2 while on and off meds.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:14:45-07:00","id":988939,"title":"","content":"Edit: Removed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-18-2016, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T14:22:49-07:00","id":989019,"title":"","content":"Edit: Removed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-18-2016, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T14:35:43-07:00","id":989026,"title":"","content":"Edit: Removed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-18-2016, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:53:08-07:00","id":989053,"title":"","content":"<i>Sigh.</i><br /> <br /> I hate to be the bearer of bad news, and I hate to be a dick about it, but it's really<i> really</i> bad form to fill the thread where people who are already struggling with brain issues and who have repeatedly tried to reason with you to try various things to improve your quality of life with requests for suicide methods.<br /> <br /> I urge you, with the greatest compassion, to seek professional help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:14:50-07:00","id":989334,"title":"","content":"I'm willing to give the benefit of the doubt. I've been around people with suicidal tendencies and have in fact lost two friends to suicide.<br /> <br /> I have also known several people who made light of those deaths by using it as a stick to ward off criticism way too much. I have personally had my losses be disrespected by people who think threats of suicide are &quot;Get out of jail free&quot; cards.<br /> <br /> I am not saying it is wrong to talk about these feelings, how overwhelming they are and how powerless we can feel to them. We need to talk about them in order to cope, to hang on, to find meaning.<br /> <br /> But I've been around people who are working to get better, who are trying to handle it, who are seeking help, and I know what that conversation sounds and looks like.<br /> <br /> If you're going to talk about suicidal feelings, make sure you know what you are doing when you do so and why, lest you come across as offending those who have lost people to suicide. We know the difference between people who will do it without help and those who are just wanting to be excused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T18:55:40-07:00","id":989657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=989334#post989334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have also known several people who made light of those deaths by using it as a stick to ward off criticism way too much. I have personally had my losses be disrespected by people who think threats of suicide are &quot;Get out of jail free&quot; cards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm dense: could you explain what you mean a bit more? Something along the lines of<br /> <br /> A: You're being unpleasant.<br /> B: Then I guess I'll just go kill myself!<br /> <br /> ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T19:07:27-07:00","id":989665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=989657#post989657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I'm dense: could you explain what you mean a bit more? Something along the lines of<br /> <br /> A: You're being unpleasant.<br /> B: Then I guess I'll just go kill myself!<br /> <br /> ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:30:23-07:00","id":991014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=985305#post985305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I dont know you, I tend to lurk, and hide here in off topic.<br /> <br /> However, I do agree with you suicide IS an option, but I feel like it isnt the ONLY option. especially in your case.<br /> <br /> Things suck I get that, but it wont always. Life takes work, you are really the only person who can take their life and make it count. Dont let your negative thoughts destroy that.<br /> <br /> When you looked back at your past and saw things you didnt like you jumped to use that to make sure your choice to end your llife was right. Maybe try looking at those things in the past you didnt like, examine them, WHAT in them did you not like, what can you change. Use your past to learn and grow, try not to let your past consume you in any form. Getting stuck on something you said or did in the past is common, take that step to use your experience to better yourself.<br /> <br /> If you dont like therapy, maybe reach out to some friends, if you dont feel comfortable talking to friends about things like this. Post here, vent anything, seriously. Just getting it out can be so helpful. Or (And as always this applies to ANYONE here on OPP) if you badly need an ear NOW, and cant wait for a slow fourm reply, and need another person but find the crisis hotlines uncomfortable. Text me, I can easily text most hours of the day, hell I can even accept a call if its an emergency. 503-840-5311.<br /> I will glady be an ear to listen, no matter how stupid you think whatever is bothering you is, etc. I'm NOT easily offended, I DONT judge, I am just a person who cares about the well being of others, even those I dont know.<br /> <br /> I hope that you decided against suicide. I truly do. Please be well, and take care of yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the best response in the entire thread IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:35:26-07:00","id":991019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=988561#post988561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two are actually talking about two different things. Yours is talking about the comparatively lesser effect illusory superiority seems to play in depressed people (a phenomenon which is still being investigated to properly understand the mechanics behind it). Mine is talking about predictions of the future and people's actions.<br /> <br /> Also, and I don't want to get into a pissing contest, your work is basically a summary/opinion piece written for lay people. Mine is an actual quasi-experimental study.<br /> <br /> The reason I shared it is because it relates to the idea of &quot;things will never change and people will always be awful&quot; you seem to be putting out, when your judgement would seem to be compromised. As a result, getting help and talking to a professional to help clear your head is probably a good idea: it subjectively appears that these things are obvious, but that is not necessarily an accurate evaluation.<br /> <br /> By &quot;the laws of thermodynamics&quot; I presume you're referring to entropy? Sure, you could view that as an inevitable force for degradation, or you could view it as an inevitable tendency towards change. It explains the phenomenon just as accurately. Yes, it tends to go to lower energy states, but that in no way corresponds to &quot;badness&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If most people would be happier if you died, then why did lots of people get really upset at the idea that you might have? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar378_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"378\" data-vbnamecard=\"378\">haren</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2456_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2456\" data-vbnamecard=\"2456\">zeroninja</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7195_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7195\" data-vbnamecard=\"7195\">TidyGamer</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6042_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6042\" data-vbnamecard=\"6042\">ManusDomine</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar897_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"897\" data-vbnamecard=\"897\">Scelesta</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar375_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"375\" data-vbnamecard=\"375\">Papa Bear</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12533-littlewords\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12533\" data-vbnamecard=\"12533\">Littlewords</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar372_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"372\" data-vbnamecard=\"372\">cerealkiller</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> all tried to get in contact with you and expressed sadness at your sadness, along with either implicit or explicit sadness at your attempt. Is that behaviour consistent with being happy at you potentially being gone? Yeah, there are toolbags in the world, but there's good people too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Truth be told, I think about it all the time, and each day's tragedies or travesties (personal or otherwise) make it seem more tempting. The reason I don't? Because I feel it's necessary to &quot;give it my all&quot; before giving up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:58:44-07:00","id":991886,"title":"","content":"I'm in a pretty bad place... I'm out of a med, and the psych refused to refill it because I refuse to schedule an appointment with someone I trust -10%. I put in a request for a transfer at the very start of September (checking the calendar, literally the 1st day) , but it's not been looked at (in spite of being #1 on the list) yet and won't be till Tuesday. The soonest I can get them looking at the meds (by the nurses since they admit, this kinda is their fault for putting off the meeting they have to do for this stuff for two months)...<br /> <br /> And things have been rough generally, and I can tell I'm not in a good place. I'm really depressed and angry at everything... I'm always angry, but it's usually a minor baseline. This is a fuming toxic state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:15:08-07:00","id":992050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=991886#post991886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in a pretty bad place... I'm out of a med, and the psych refused to refill it because I refuse to schedule an appointment with someone I trust -10%. I put in a request for a transfer at the very start of September (checking the calendar, literally the 1st day) , but it's not been looked at (in spite of being #1 on the list) yet and won't be till Tuesday. The soonest I can get them looking at the meds (by the nurses since they admit, this kinda is their fault for putting off the meeting they have to do for this stuff for two months)...<br /> <br /> And things have been rough generally, and I can tell I'm not in a good place. I'm really depressed and angry at everything... I'm always angry, but it's usually a minor baseline. This is a fuming toxic state.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the meds often have terrible withdrawal symptoms. I hope you can get your prescription filled ASAP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:09:23-07:00","id":992085,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm definitely not in a stable location... it's a wild difference from yesterday. And it's far more dramatic than usual (and those swings are not great as is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:10:53-07:00","id":993274,"title":"","content":"Just to stipulate: I know my problems don't measure up to you guys', even a little bit. Not even on the same order of magnitude, and nothing I say after this is intended to indicate anything else. OK? OK.<br /> <br /> Periodically I get kind of... crappy feeling. I don't think it's depression <i>per se</i>, probably closer to just usual feeling down than anything clinically significant. But it suck unbelievably - a week or two pretending even harder that people make sense to me, that my life is in some bizarre way net positive, and that my work is worth even doing, let alone reading. I used to put this on being stressed, but I can feel myself going into that kind of mood again, and since I submitted my thesis a few weeks ago, I'm less stressed and better rested than I have been in a long time. I hate feeling this way, and not just because I'm pretty sure it's actually just an accurate evaluation of my life.<br /> <br /> So, given that you guys deal with issues far worse than this every day, how do you deal? I know the usual advice is to go see someone, but that's not on the cards for two main reasons. First, it's really expensive, and I'm pretty short on cash these days. I'm not in immediate danger of eviction or starving, but optional expenses are certainly on the &quot;not right now&quot; list. Second, I really, really hate talking about myself. It took me 29 years to get evaluated for Aspergers, and the issues related to that are chronic and have far more impact on my life - going and wasting a therapists time talking about how I feel kind of crappy and am increasingly sure that I am literally more useful dead than alive (I've run the numbers. That's not a depressive thing, that's just the kind of person I am), when they could be helping people with <i>actual</i> problems? Urgh.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I know this is really stupid, but any advice for stopping a spiral before I end up sitting in a room staring at the wall?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:30:45-07:00","id":993280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=993274#post993274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to stipulate: I know my problems don't measure up to you guys', even a little bit. Not even on the same order of magnitude, and nothing I say after this is intended to indicate anything else. OK? OK.<br /> <br /> Periodically I get kind of... crappy feeling. I don't think it's depression <i>per se</i>, probably closer to just usual feeling down than anything clinically significant. But it suck unbelievably - a week or two pretending even harder that people make sense to me, that my life is in some bizarre way net positive, and that my work is worth even doing, let alone reading. I used to put this on being stressed, but I can feel myself going into that kind of mood again, and since I submitted my thesis a few weeks ago, I'm less stressed and better rested than I have been in a long time. I hate feeling this way, and not just because I'm pretty sure it's actually just an accurate evaluation of my life.<br /> <br /> So, given that you guys deal with issues far worse than this every day, how do you deal? I know the usual advice is to go see someone, but that's not on the cards for two main reasons. First, it's really expensive, and I'm pretty short on cash these days. I'm not in immediate danger of eviction or starving, but optional expenses are certainly on the &amp;quot;not right now&amp;quot; list. Second, I really, really hate talking about myself. It took me 29 years to get evaluated for Aspergers, and the issues related to that are chronic and have far more impact on my life - going and wasting a therapists time talking about how I feel kind of crappy and am increasingly sure that I am literally more useful dead than alive (I've run the numbers. That's not a depressive thing, that's just the kind of person I am), when they could be helping people with <i>actual</i> problems? Urgh.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I know this is really stupid, but any advice for stopping a spiral before I end up sitting in a room staring at the wall?</div> </div> </div> </div>Friend, if you can't find motivation to do things, think you'd be better dead than alive, and are constantly downplaying your own struggles... that's depression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:54:08-07:00","id":993290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=993274#post993274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to stipulate: I know my problems don't measure up to you guys', even a little bit. Not even on the same order of magnitude, and nothing I say after this is intended to indicate anything else. OK? OK.<br /> <br /> Periodically I get kind of... crappy feeling. I don't think it's depression <i>per se</i>, probably closer to just usual feeling down than anything clinically significant. But it suck unbelievably - a week or two pretending even harder that people make sense to me, that my life is in some bizarre way net positive, and that my work is worth even doing, let alone reading. I used to put this on being stressed, but I can feel myself going into that kind of mood again, and since I submitted my thesis a few weeks ago, I'm less stressed and better rested than I have been in a long time. I hate feeling this way, and not just because I'm pretty sure it's actually just an accurate evaluation of my life.<br /> <br /> So, given that you guys deal with issues far worse than this every day, how do you deal? I know the usual advice is to go see someone, but that's not on the cards for two main reasons. First, it's really expensive, and I'm pretty short on cash these days. I'm not in immediate danger of eviction or starving, but optional expenses are certainly on the &quot;not right now&quot; list. Second, I really, really hate talking about myself. It took me 29 years to get evaluated for Aspergers, and the issues related to that are chronic and have far more impact on my life - going and wasting a therapists time talking about how I feel kind of crappy and am increasingly sure that I am literally more useful dead than alive (I've run the numbers. That's not a depressive thing, that's just the kind of person I am), when they could be helping people with <i>actual</i> problems? Urgh.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I know this is really stupid, but any advice for stopping a spiral before I end up sitting in a room staring at the wall?</div> </div> </div> </div>well its not a pissing or dickwaving contest so don't worry about your problems not measuring up. I would try to answer how I deal with that but I don't have any healthy coping mechanisms. Last time I was going to a therapist for any length of time they managed to get me just comfortable enough to let my guard down then after removing my old coping mechanisms and before we could replace them properly the office decided to just stop seeing me completely. I fell into drugs and alcohol pretty hard. I can't be a good influence or give good advice for this but what I can do is be a bad example so that you can have something to try and not be.<br /> <br /> ~4 months ago I left my job at walmart after 4 years for something I was hoping would be a great new job opportunity. I was supposed to be going into a small company and be a manager. They lied during my interviews and I was going to be a door to door salesman. They fired me after I called out a week and a half in due to my sister getting in a car accident. I was trying to find something else for work and fell even further down the drugs and alcohol hole and ended up attempting suicide around this time in July. I only survived because my dad found me completely unresponsive in the bathroom covered in blood after ingesting 2 LD50 doses of sedatives. I've been living like a hikikomori neet for the last 3 months. I've not gone outside much, I don't interact with people much. I sit around doing nothing but watching anime and building models. Not that you expressed the direct urge to kill yourself but suicide isn't that great of an option. My reasoning being that someone will find you and either stop you, interfere or save you. Its also incredibly embarrassing afterwards. So yeah, look at this and realize how shitty of an example I am so you can better yourself, so you don't end up like me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:58:55-07:00","id":993292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=993280#post993280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Friend, if you can't find motivation to do things, think you'd be better dead than alive, and are constantly downplaying your own struggles... that's depression.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much that I'm downplaying my struggles as recognising the clearly more onerous issues of the people on this thread. We have people who have made multiple suicide attempts - my feeling kind of crappy for a couple weeks periodically isn't really on the same level, and I wanted to acknowledge that rather than risk belittling their experiences.<br /> <br /> As for the better dead than alive thing, again, that's just a numbers thing. According to some estimations, a life can be saved from <a href=\"http://www.givewell.org/charities/against-malaria-foundation#Cost_per_life_saved\" target=\"_blank\">malaria for $3,500</a>. Given my age and career direction, I can estimate to give <i>maybe</i> a half-million to charity over my life, and that will only become less &quot;efficient&quot; (pardon the term) over time. Or, I can get a life insurance policy, wait out the 13 month exclusion period, then no matter what I do that will give a potentially much greater sum immediately, saving potentially hundreds of lives, as well as protecting thousands of people, mostly children, from non-fatal infections, which can seriously mess you up in the long term. Even if my work becomes far more influential and useful than I can imagine, I wouldn't have nearly that impact with my life. (Um, not saying that suicide is good. It isn't. Obviously. Just saying that the argument is not without merit.)<br /> <br /> And the motivation thing... I got nothing clever there. I would say I'm lazy, but there's evidence against that that would take some pretty serious mind-bending to discredit. But by itself it's hardly definitive.<br /> <br /> But this is all beside the point. I'm happy to stipulate that feeling this way is, at the very least, unpleasant. The question is, how do I stop or manage it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:32:21-07:00","id":993329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=993292#post993292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not so much that I'm downplaying my struggles as recognising the clearly more onerous issues of the people on this thread.<b> We have people who have made multiple suicide attempts - my feeling kind of crappy for a couple weeks periodically isn't really on the same level, and I wanted to acknowledge that rather than risk belittling their experiences.</b><br /> <br /> But this is all beside the point. I'm happy to stipulate that feeling this way is, at the very least, unpleasant. The question is, how do I stop or manage it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolded is important. <br /> <br /> Yes there are a few of us who have had suicide attempts, but that doesnt mean your problems mean any less in anyway.<br /> Funny thing about those many suicide attempts? MANY of us likely started with the same feelings you have now, and we let it consume us, or we couldnt ask for help for various reasons, or we didnt know HOW to fight it. What i'm saying is that you sound depressed, but you realized one method of help already, You reached out to talk. <br /> <br /> So therapy isnt an option? Not a problem at all. I can do some digging for you and pull up some websites with GREAT ways to manage depression, healthy coping methods etc for you to give a try. You are also more then welcome to vent here, or message me through pm.<br /> <br /> But first my personal methods i've found that work for me, ymmv:<br /> <br /> Music. LOUD music, dont just listen to it, LISTEN to it focus on the lyrics, try to spin a story in your mind around the song, or find its meaning or what it means to you. <br /> <br /> Going for a walk outside. Depression can easily get worse if you lock yourself away, you'd be surprised how refreshing just going outside for a few minuets can be mentally.<br /> <br /> ALWAYS get a good night of sleep every night. Go to bed on time, and get at least 7-8 hours of sleep, dont let yourself sleep in force yourself to get out of bed. The forcing part is hard, if you have to drink a HUGE glass of water in the middle of the night to ensure you have to pee first thing upon waking, then you dont have any choice but to get up.<br /> <br /> When you find a negative thought, Stop, acknoledge it to yourself its a valid thought ignoring your thoughts is just bottling those thoghts up. After you allow yourself to give that thought its attention. Take a deep breath in and out. Then think of it again, but this time from a different perspective, Think &quot;How can i turn this into something positive&quot; For example: say i find myself thinking &quot;I'm useless, I should just die.&quot; I'd do the above, then maybe spin that thought into something like: &quot;I'm not useless, I'm a good mother, whose daughter clearly loves and finds her useful.&quot;<br /> <br /> If its just an emotion not a thought, breath, focus on it, focus on WHY you feel that way. You may not know, it may not even have a reason. If you find a reason for it, what is that reason? Once you find it, think of ways to spin it to something postive. Like: Say i'm feeling angry after a long day. I dont know why i'm mad, so i focus on it, I realize i'm mad because nothings gone right all day.&quot; Well shit cant have that. PROVE it wrong. Such as &quot;Actually, I did get to my appointment on time, and am healthy. I didnt burn dinner. &quot; etc in that case find all the reasons as to why that statement was a lie.<br /> <br /> Learn your emotions. Put words to them so you can better counter them. Not sure what you are feeling? <a href=\"http://copyranger.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/Emotional-Copywriting-Words1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://copyranger.com/wp-content/upl...ing-Words1.jpg</a><br /> That site can help you identify your emotions<br /> <br /> Meditation!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T23:48:50-07:00","id":993354,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's something that I've already mentioned offhandedly once:<br /> <br /> So, as you may know, I work as a lawyer, which is usually not the most traumatizing job in the world (oh no, a copyright infringement case, I have been wounded inside!), but for about sixteen days ago, something happened.<br /> <br /> I had recently participated as the defendant in the trial of a woman suspected for the murder of a man, she had a history of having been poorly represented in court before, and had been in prison twice before, though only for a month at most. I was to defend her in court, which in this case basically meant that I had to defend her in an already skeptical court.<br /> <br /> I lost it, and she stood to face twelve years in prison.<br /> <br /> Three days later, she called me in the morning and informed me she had taken arsenic and would die in about fifteen minutes, she thanked me for my defense and told me that at least I tried and that she didn't blame me for losing.<br /> <br /> Then she hung up and died in her home.<br /> <br /> I've been feeling like shit ever since. I've been having nightmares, and I sometimes hear her voice when I close my eyes, no medication has been helping and visiting her grave only makes me more sad.<br /> <br /> I tried using as much of my salary (which is pretty fucking much if you're a successful lawyer in Denmark) to buy flowers for her family as I could, but the result was simply that her family had a bunch of flowers, and that I had less money.<br /> <br /> Please, fucking help me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T01:08:31-07:00","id":993372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=993354#post993354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here's something that I've already mentioned offhandedly once:<br /> <br /> So, as you may know, I work as a lawyer, which is usually not the most traumatizing job in the world (oh no, a copyright infringement case, I have been wounded inside!), but for about sixteen days ago, something happened.<br /> <br /> I had recently participated as the defendant in the trial of a woman suspected for the murder of a man, she had a history of having been poorly represented in court before, and had been in prison twice before, though only for a month at most. I was to defend her in court, which in this case basically meant that I had to defend her in an already skeptical court.<br /> <br /> I lost it, and she stood to face twelve years in prison.<br /> <br /> Three days later, she called me in the morning and informed me she had taken arsenic and would die in about fifteen minutes, she thanked me for my defense and told me that at least I tried and that she didn't blame me for losing.<br /> <br /> Then she hung up and died in her home.<br /> <br /> I've been feeling like shit ever since. I've been having nightmares, and I sometimes hear her voice when I close my eyes, no medication has been helping and visiting her grave only makes me more sad.<br /> <br /> I tried using as much of my salary (which is pretty fucking much if you're a successful lawyer in Denmark) to buy flowers for her family as I could, but the result was simply that her family had a bunch of flowers, and that I had less money.<br /> <br /> Please, fucking help me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, have you considdered seeking professional help? <br /> As a skizophrenic Ive seen my fair share of unplesantry (even if its just in my own head) But even so... It helps a lot just to have someone to talk with, even just to get the things said out loud to someone who knows what questions to ask to really get it out of your system. <br /> <br /> If youve burned all your income on flowers, then it might help to know that some &quot;indboforsikring&quot; (Home insurance) covers counseling in some cases... Dont know, might be worth checking up on? <br /> <br /> Holler if you need to talk<br /> Stay strong!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Decent storyteller. Poor Banjo player.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12373-sarner","name":"Sarner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12373_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:33:41-07:00","id":993409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=993354#post993354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been feeling like shit ever since. I've been having nightmares, and I sometimes hear her voice when I close my eyes, no medication has been helping and visiting her grave only makes me more sad.<br /> <br /> I tried using as much of my salary (which is pretty fucking much if you're a successful lawyer in Denmark) to buy flowers for her family as I could, but the result was simply that her family had a bunch of flowers, and that I had less money.<br /> <br /> Please, fucking help me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be slightly inappropriate. If so, I apologise, just ignore me.<br /> <br /> To my reading, it looks like you're upset that there's nothing you can do outside of empty, ultimately meaningless gestures? I'm going to proceed under the assumption that that reading is correct - again, if I'm wrong, ignore me.<br /> <br /> Have you considered investigating initiatives that help prevent suicide? I'm not from Denmark, nor do I speak Danish, so I'm limited on knowledge and ability to get more, but I think the general principle is sound. You say that as a lawyer you make a pretty decent wage. Have you considered donating a portion of that to well-chosen initiatives? Apparently the Danish government has <a href=\"http://cphpost.dk/news/national/danish-government-proposes-more-cuts-to-suicide-prevention.html\" target=\"_blank\">cut funding</a> to suicide preventing programs, which means they would be desperate for more funding, and many of them willingly accept donations. Or if they don't, maybe you can volunteer your skills? I don't know suicide hotlines specifically, but I'd imagine any organisation would love to get some free legal services.<br /> <br /> The broad idea is maybe doing something directly might make you feel like you're honouring the memory of your client? Given that it seems that the usual socially mandated option isn't working for you?<br /> <br /> Again, if this comes off as predatory in any way, I deeply apologise - that is not my intent in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:56:59-07:00","id":993415,"title":"","content":"Not a bad thought, Allan53... Im a volunteer worker myself (And as a dane I can confirm that there are plenty of suicide prevention communities that need all the help they can get) Personally I find doing some active good does a lot to raise spirits when times are tough.<br /> <br /> I dont think its predatory as such. Its an option worth considdering. Might not be the right soloution for everyone, but there is no harm in being aware of ones options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Decent storyteller. Poor Banjo player.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12373-sarner","name":"Sarner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12373_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:05:45-07:00","id":993755,"title":"","content":"If you want something more concrete in addition to helping with suicide prevention through donations, you can probably get in contact with whatever your local mental health or homeless services are and ask them about donating personal hygiene products. Feminine Hygine products, no-rince shampoos, hand sanitizer, dental products and underwear are all things that can be difficult to budget for when someone is low income, but having them can do wonders for their mental health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:52:30-07:00","id":995305,"title":"","content":"I figure this is as good a place as any to vent a bit and hopefully find my mood some measure of improved.<br /> <br /> However, what I need to vent about kind of necessitates some establishment of history if I want to even imagine that anyone will understand where I am at right now. So here's the shortest version: I've had bipolar depression for as long as I can remember, but I didn't know what how I have always been was called until about a decade ago. My parents got me help because I was living with them again after about a decade living apart and they realized that it wasn't &quot;just normal teenager stuff&quot; that I was shutting myself away in a darkened room and seemingly flip-flopping between sleeping all day and not sleeping at all for days at a time. The medication I got onto evened out my activity cycle, and it did even out my mood too - but it did so too strongly, and my friends, girlfriend, and family had to tell me to stop taking it because I didn't even notice that I didn't give a shit about anything anymore (no anger, no irritation, no excitement, no laughter, nothing).<br /> <br /> I decided at the time that I would just continue on as I always had, dealing with the lows and channeling the highs into something productive.<br /> <br /> It turns out that I've also had fibromyalgia since my early teen years, and was not in fact a &quot;wimp&quot; that couldn't handle the normal pain that everyone goes through as my ill-informed father had convinced me. Only very recently, within the last year, has this been confirmed as well as can be by medical professionals and treated with medication.<br /> <br /> So that gets to the part I need to vent about - I lucked out big time; the first medication my doctor picked for me to try out to see how it would help (chosen because it is alphabetically first on the list of medications she put together that both might be helpful to me and will only cost me $4 a month) has worked wonderfully. I no longer spend every day dreading the pain of simple things like taking a shower, or getting into and out of a car so I can go places a person needs to go. I still have pain, but it's a tiny fraction of what I used to feel all day everyday, and it's also entirely explainable by the fact that I am significantly out of shape from all of avoiding the pain I started doing once I stopped self-medicating with marijuana, alcohol, and any opiate I could get in my body without a needle.<br /> <br /> The medication, an antidepressant by design that incidentally has been found to help some people with fibromyalgia, also manages - the absolute miracle drug I lucked into it being - to help keep my activity cycle more even.<br /> <br /> But now I don't know how to live. By which I mean I don't how to get shit done, not that I've considered ceasing to be alive (which hasn't crossed my mind in nearly 20 years, and I am thankful for that fact). I sleep more than I have ever slept - I'm used to being able to function on like 4 hours of sleep a day, and now if I sleep 4 hours and then wake up to take the wife to work, I get home from dropping her off and sleep another 6 hours. And if it rains, I'm useless with how tired I get. We had a couple days back to back last week of light rain, and I think I was sleeping 10 hours at night and still drifting off into an 2-4 hour afternoon nap.<br /> <br /> And my moods still have highs and lows like before, but I think the lows are getting worse, or maybe I'm still just adjusting to life on medication and my irritation at loss of my &quot;super powers&quot; that were my manic periods is compounded into making the lows seem worse. The point being that I fucking hate some shit now that wasn't such a big deal to me before. I'm straight up pissed off to the point of thinking insults at myself that I haven't been able to get on top of house work, and that I haven't started making progress at getting back in shape, because my old excuse of the pain being too much to bear is gone and what is left is what feels like bullshit to me even as I sit here literally struggling not to dose off at my desk typing of &quot;I'm too tired right now.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I've been angry. Like I'll ask the wife &quot;What do you want for dinner?&quot; and she'll ask me &quot;Do you want to fix something at home, or pick something up?&quot; which I know logically isn't a problem because she is participating in the process of us figuring out what our dinner will be, but it isn't actually an answer to my question. And that's a common thing she'll do where she won't actually answer the question I've asked, and it seems to me like she's trying to give me the answer I want to hear. And I've mentioned in the past that I don't like people trying to tell me what they think I want to hear, I just want them to answer the questions I've actually asked (I've got a think about power dynamics - I hate people putting themselves under me, but I also hate feeling like people don't listen when I speak to them, so it's kind of a double-dose of &quot;ugh&quot; when someone tries to put their own opinion below mine in importance by not actually answering the question I asked). But lately when she does that I have the urge to scream. I try not to raise my voice too much - I don't give in to the urge to scream - but I do raise my voice because I can't keep the frustration bottled up inside.<br /> <br /> I know it's not her fault, and I know that I'm not the only one suffering from my affliction - it's hard on her too, seeing me in the dumps starting to lose my shit. But I can't stop myself feeling the way I feel in an instant, and I can't help but to be frustrated and to feel like when she comes to tears because she feels bad about me feeling bad she is taking something away from me - because I'm not expressing my sadness/frustration/whatever and receiving comfort or support from her, I'm <i>giving</i> the comfort and support and she is the one that gets to cry it out. And no, I really can't figure out why we can't just both cry it out and be giving support to each other in doing so together - the instant the first tear streaks down her cheek, all the things I was wanting to let out and be comforted in regard to turn into the hurt and anger that is the feeling that she just took away my right to be the one needing a shoulder to cry on.<br /> <br /> Through all of this, there is one other thing. Fear. I'm scared shitless that this is just how life on this medication is going to be from here on out, and similarly terrified that if I ask my doctor to switch me to another medication that I'll go through the shit my sister has gone through where she is on something new every few months and dealing with a new shit-show of side effects or things just not helping at all because the only thing she's been on so far that has actually help and not had unbearable side-effects are the narcotics that her doctor doesn't want to leave her on long-term because of their addictive nature - so I kind of feel like I don't even know what the fuck I want in this whole ordeal, and that makes me angry too.<br /> <br /> I don't even have enough give-a-fuck left in my tank right now to go back and read this post to make sure it is intelligible, so sorry if it isn't. But hey, maybe I got something out of me. Maybe after a shower and a nap I won't be quite as pissed off at everything and nothing as I was before I started typing.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll make it through this weekend's trip to the grocery store without becoming that guy that's clearly losing his temper about trivial shit in public - because I fucking hate that guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:21:44-07:00","id":995619,"title":"","content":"A couple of tips from one semi-medicated bipolar sucker to another:<br /> <br /> Maybe the doctor mentioned it, maybe not, but sometimes those manic phases can come out as anger instead of boundless energy, especially while on certain medications. Also, caffiene can cause those anger phases to come quicker and easier on those same medications. My doctor this time said that wasn't a problem, but I remeber it being an issue when I was on the same stuff as a kid. I cut out caffiene and I feel like I have more energy and have less rage issues.<br /> <br /> Get a punchng bag in your home. When the anger comes, go hit, yell, kick and scream at it. When fatigued, strap on the gloves and take some swings at it. Take a bit of self-dicipline to do it, probably sting more with your other issues, but getting the heart rate up pushes that fatigue away. When you get up to take your wife to work, make sure you put on something to work out in, but that might bug you if you tried tosleep in it. I found these work out shirts that are very good for letting air thru, but the collars are too tight and it would drive me nuts trying to sleep in it.<br /> <br /> We've all seen it and heard about it before, but it's still often dismissed easily: autumn and winter can make someone who's already down feel worse. I've had a hell of a time doing my own exercises, skipped it for two weeks now using excuses like &quot;I'm too busy.&quot; and &quot;I'm too tired.&quot;. Tomorrow, hell or high water will not stop me. I'm tired of my own excuses. Sometimes, you can channel that anger into getting mad at yourself for not doing what you know you should be doing. Just don't let it go too far or you'll be back into the depression spiral.<br /> <br /> Anger turned inwards is depression. Anger turned sideways is humor. Watch some 3 Stooges, listen to Christopher Titus (a comedian who uses some very messed up things in his life). Whatever you find funny, go for it. The Addams Family is great if you're already in a dark mood. They are right there with you. Robin Williams always worked blue, but his later stuff revealed just how hard a time he was having. He truned his open heart surgery into some really funny shit.<br /> <br /> I cannot emphasize this one enough: TALK ABOUT IT! Don't hide your moods. Don't be afraid of your problems. Tell everyone. My employer company has both of your conditions listed as legitimate disabilities. I have to put down being bipolar for any changes I make in my employment status, and they have to accommodate me. And, of course, you always have us here.<br /> <br /> Try it out, let us know, stick around and keep talking to us. Good luck, my friend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T10:26:05-07:00","id":995700,"title":"","content":"Of course, coffee may affect you differently. My grandmother and I have an odd reaction to it. We'd sometimes share a pot or two before bed because other than needing to bio in the night, we'd sleep better. I find it calming (but I avoid drinking often... just some now and then if I'm going through a state where I'm super unrationally angry to bring my levels down to normal raging baseline. Like I'm doing now.) Biology is weird like that. From what I understand, it is the same sort of reason people who have ADD take stimulants to focus. It acts as a calming agent, rather than ramping them up more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:05:30-07:00","id":995712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=995700#post995700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, coffee may affect you differently. My grandmother and I have an odd reaction to it. We'd sometimes share a pot or two before bed because other than needing to bio in the night, we'd sleep better. I find it calming (but I avoid drinking often... just some now and then if I'm going through a state where I'm super unrationally angry to bring my levels down to normal raging baseline. Like I'm doing now.) Biology is weird like that. From what I understand, it is the same sort of reason people who have ADD take stimulants to focus. It acts as a calming agent, rather than ramping them up more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Substances and habits can also cause weird effects due to association. For example, coffee used to stimulate and energize me, but in college I would play Vampire LARP until midnight when the campus rec center kicked us out, then we'd all go to a diner after and I'd down a pot of coffee before going home and going to sleep. Now coffee makes me tired. Not caffeine, mind - I can still get a pick-me-up from tea or energy drinks. Just coffee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-30-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:15:57-07:00","id":995773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=995712#post995712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Substances and habits can also cause weird effects due to association. For example, coffee used to stimulate and energize me, but in college I would play Vampire LARP until midnight when the campus rec center kicked us out, then we'd all go to a diner after and I'd down a pot of coffee before going home and going to sleep. Now coffee makes me tired. Not caffeine, mind - I can still get a pick-me-up from tea or energy drinks. Just coffee.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had considered that, since as a child I'd drink coffee on my grandmother's lap, sharing hers. But other drinks with caffiene do it also. Anyways, the short version of this, is pay attention to how things affect you, and take that into consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T22:28:54-07:00","id":995966,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Papa Bear, I hadn't thought about manic phases manifesting as anger or caffeine potentially exacerbating things. I'll try cutting it, drop my 2 pots of coffee on game night habit for a while, and see how things shake out.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Haren, my wife is the same with coffee - knocks her right out most times.<br /> <br /> Also, after ranting here the other day I sat with the wife and talked all the same stuff out with her. I'm not used to sharing my problems like that, because the way I was raised fooled me into believing my problems were insignificant and I was just bad at handling what everyone has to handle, but it really helped. I'm still down, but I'm not so down that I feel like one more let down would start me crying.<br /> <br /> And lastly, for now at least because I've got some delicious tacos from a local bar to go eat while watching some TV with the wife and a buddy, I kinda feel like &quot;Der&quot; because I didn't think of channeling my current anger into physical activity like a punching bag. When I was much younger and had seriously bad times with anger issues (like throwing another person 8 feet into the steel post holding up a basketball hoop because he ripped my shirt and trash talked me instead of apologizing), I used to do just that sort of thing - though more often it was doing demolition work like smashing down old fences so new ones could be built in their place, rather than a punching bag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:17:51-07:00","id":997446,"title":"","content":"Seeing signs of ADHD in my kid. Hope schools and public are more accepting now than they were when I was a kid. I know, at least, we'll be better parents about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T20:09:19-07:00","id":997522,"title":"","content":"My fiance is nagging me to get a new prescription for Adhd medication. About six years ago, I've tried Adderall and Vyvanse. It worked fine for six months and then the side effects overcome the benefits. I had no appetite, rage issues, and suicidal thoughts. Also, it kills my creativity. <br /> <br /> Has then been any medical advances in the past six years? Right now I am taking omega 3 and self medicating with caffeine. But my caffeine tolerance is going up. I've heard about an anti depressant that has been prescribed for adhd, but my last doctor hadn't had any good experiences with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T22:00:34-07:00","id":997550,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's been any advances particular to ADHD medications. There are more medications available than you were prescribed, however. Adderall (and Vyvanse, which is Adderall with a clever time-release design to foil abuse) is just one option, and the other stimulants might not have such harsh effects for you.<br /> <br /> I wasn't on Adderall for even a full month, as it caused intense TMJ pain. Ritalin was better but not by a lot since the generic the pharmacy gave me was not very good. I used to self-medicate with ephedra but it had to go and become illegal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T22:07:33-07:00","id":997553,"title":"","content":"I couldn't say, they started treatment in the 80s with Ritalin and I think something else later on but it's been a long time. During the mid-90s other problems came up and I haven't been treated for it since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T00:16:54-08:00","id":1000640,"title":"","content":"I feel like any and all movement forward for me was destroyed in a single night. I'm in a deep despair and suicidal, and frankly... I just feel terrified about the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T00:31:03-08:00","id":1000645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1000640#post1000640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like any and all movement forward for me was destroyed in a single night. I'm in a deep despair and suicidal, and frankly... I just feel terrified about the future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel you. I'm living in the deep south and I am terrified for what the future holds. My faith in humanity lies dead at the bottom of my soul; and, the only thing I have now is my love for my friends. That's what will keep me from suicide, personally. I'm disassociating pretty hard myself right now.<br /> <br /> I am not good at helping people with this sort of thing, but if there's anything I can do please tell me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T00:52:42-08:00","id":1000652,"title":"","content":"I'm in North Dakota, and I'm suspecting we hear similar things from locals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,