:"In that case it is rather effective yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:37:24-08:00","id":1000748,"title":"","content":"I'm not feeling very confident in my survival within the next four years right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T08:30:36-08:00","id":1000806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1000748#post1000748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not feeling very confident in my survival within the next four years right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wish that I could help you somehow.<br /> <br /> I really do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T08:46:13-08:00","id":1000816,"title":"","content":"I'm a future educator, and on Thursday I'll have to go into my super-diverse practicum class of immigrants (I'm in Canada) and try and explain why their parents are so afraid. I don't know how I can face them.<br /> <br /> I was raised Catholic, but I don't know what I am now. Haven't sincerely participated in a service in years.<br /> <br /> I prayed today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:02:55-08:00","id":1000823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1000806#post1000806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really wish that I could help you somehow.<br /> <br /> I really do.</div> </div> </div> </div>A big part of that is that I live near enough to a military base so that if (<i>god forbid</i>) there's a nuclear exchange, I very likely won't be surviving it. There's other reasons, but right now that's the biggest one hanging over my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:29:14-08:00","id":1000841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1000717#post1000717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they meant other people hating on minorities bringing people together who are, or want to not see minorities hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he's kept one campaign promise so far. He sure as hell brought people together....in hate. Now he's doing it again with the people who hate the people who hate with him.<br /> <br /> But I'm not going to be one of them. I'm going to follow the advice of Master Yoda. Fear leads to anger. Anger leads to hate. Hate leads to the Dark Side. I'm not letting Darth Hater turn me into a Sith. I won't go so far as to say I will love my xenophobic neighbor. I'm not a saint or a Jedi Master. But I'm sure as hell not going to let them change me into something I'm not. It is easy to be angry. I refuse to make this easy for anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T10:45:32-08:00","id":1000878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1000841#post1000841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm not going to be one of them. I'm going to follow the advice of Master Yoda. Fear leads to anger. Anger leads to hate. Hate leads to the Dark Side. I'm not letting Darth Hater turn me into a Sith. I won't go so far as to say I will love my xenophobic neighbor. I'm not a saint or a Jedi Master. But I'm sure as hell not going to let them change me into something I'm not. It is easy to be angry. I refuse to make this easy for anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm right there with you.<br /> <br /> The kind words and suggestions of folks in this thread about a week-and-a-half ago helped me get on a good path, thanks for that by the way, and I am happier with myself today than I was then. I'm not letting anything take that from me.<br /> <br /> Not the governmental system I've been against since learning how it functions, not the president elect being a hate-monger, biggot, and generally out of touch imbicile, and not that I feel like I got the shit kicked out of me last night when the reality is that all I did was a few loads of dishes, hauled some trash out, and took a shower - all things I mean to repeat today, pushing through the pain, because I need to get my house in order and the pain should subside as my terribly out of shape body gets used to being a human being again.<br /> <br /> I believe it was Winston Churchill who said, &quot;If you're going through hell, keep going.&quot; I mean to do just that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:06:01-08:00","id":1000891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1000841#post1000841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, he's kept one campaign promise so far. He sure as hell brought people together....in hate. Now he's doing it again with the people who hate the people who hate with him.<br /> <br /> But I'm not going to be one of them. I'm going to follow the advice of Master Yoda. Fear leads to anger. Anger leads to hate. Hate leads to the Dark Side. I'm not letting Darth Hater turn me into a Sith. I won't go so far as to say I will love my xenophobic neighbor. I'm not a saint or a Jedi Master. But I'm sure as hell not going to let them change me into something I'm not. It is easy to be angry. I refuse to make this easy for anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're a better Jedi than I am. Because right now all I want to do is<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6dyUYjH8AnY\" data-code=\"6dyUYjH8AnY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6dyUYjH8AnY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-09-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:13:10-08:00","id":1000896,"title":"","content":"Good on you Drake! Keep pushing through.<br /> <br /> Today I got genuinely <i>angry </i>for the first time in a long time. I've been annoyed and frustrated before, but this was the first time in years I managed to summon enough emotional vitriol. I didn't think I <i>could </i>get angry anymore just because of the sheer emotional weight of anxiety and depression. I actually managed to scream, which I haven't be able to do outside of martial arts for years. I don't want to give in to anger and hate, but I'm glad I'm feeling it. Fully plan on using it as motivation in the coming weeks.<br /> <br /> As an aside, a geeky friend of mine posted a speech Steve Rogers made in Captain America I feel is relevant to today.<br /> <br /> <i>Doesn't matter what the press says. Doesn't matter what the politicians or the mobs say. Doesn't matter if the whole </i>country<i> decides that something </i>wrong<i> is something </i>right<i>. This nation was founded on one principle above all else: the requirement that we stand up for what we believe, no matter the odds or the consequences. When the mob and the press and the whole </i>world<i> tell you to move, your job is to plant yourself like a tree beside the river of truth, and tell the whole world \u2014 No, </i><b><i>you</i></b><i> move.&quot;</i><br /> \u2014 <i>Amazing Spider-Man</i>, #537<br /> <br /> At this point, I'm planning on digging my heels and not giving an inch. I'm training to be a teacher, I have a responsibility to make the world a better place. Like <i>hell </i>am I going to let an entire generation of civil rights go down the tube.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:25:18-08:00","id":1001058,"title":"","content":"Captain America is good for quotes like that. I particularly like this one from Avengers (vol 5) #34:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>You people telling me how I just don't <b>understand?</b> When it's <b>you</b> people-- you <b>clever</b> people-- who don't get it. I don't let people die because it's the lesser of two evils, or expedient, or because it serves the greater good... I don't compare the act against something else-- I see someone who needs help... <b>And I help.</b>You think it's a weakness. You think it's simple... But you're wrong. It's what makes us human... Which is exactly what we're supposed to be fighting for. I know who I am. I rescue the helpless. I raise up the hopeless. I don't measure people's lives... <b>I save them. </b></i> </div> </div> </div>I like it because it says that none of the divisions, be they political, racial, religious, social or otherwise, matter. We're all human, and we all owe each other a basic measure of respect and compassion. You might disagree with someone, even strongly. You might even be forced to move against them. But none of that negates this basic level of respect and compassion that we are required, by dint of being <i>human</i>, to show for each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 11-09-2016, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:21:19-08:00","id":1001087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1001058#post1001058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Captain America is good for quotes like that. I particularly like this one from Avengers (vol 5) #34:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I like it because it says that none of the divisions, be they political, racial, religious, social or otherwise, matter. We're all human, and we all owe each other a basic measure of respect and compassion. You might disagree with someone, even strongly. You might even be forced to move against them. But none of that negates this basic level of respect and compassion that we are required, by dint of being <i>human</i>, to show for each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I don't know that it does... It doesn't say he saves people regardless of race, religion, class, or politics. It says he saves people who are in immediate danger regardless of long-term consequences. This says he is either shortsighted or (more likely, from the context) unwilling to make the kind of decisions someone in power needs to be able to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T20:40:19-08:00","id":1001172,"title":"","content":"That part is most clearly said by the &quot;<i>I don't measure people's lives... I save them.</i>&quot; part. It means that regardless of your &quot;value&quot;, you get saved. It doesn't matter who you are, you get saved.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>I don't let people die because it's the lesser of two evils, or expedient, or because it serves the greater good</i>.&quot; Letting someone die is bad. Letting someone be hurt is bad. Hurting someone is bad. Saving people is good. At no point in there does someones opinion on lettuce tariffs become relevant.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm reading a bit into it. But it's a really short speech, I think you can forgive me a few liberties <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't think anyone can really accuse Captain America of being unwilling to make hard decisions, or being short sighted, or being unable to handle power well. Unless Mark Millar is writing him, but, well, that's Mark Millar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T22:29:55-08:00","id":1001201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1001172#post1001172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That part is most clearly said by the &amp;quot;<i>I don't measure people's lives... I save them.</i>&amp;quot; part. It means that regardless of your &amp;quot;value&amp;quot;, you get saved. It doesn't matter who you are, you get saved.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that reads to me like saying it doesn't matter if saving you will mean more people may die, you get saved. He's not going to weigh the value of your life against the value of the lives of the people who might be saved by letting you die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1001172#post1001172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;<i>I don't let people die because it's the lesser of two evils, or expedient, or because it serves the greater good</i>.&amp;quot; Letting someone die is bad. Letting someone be hurt is bad. Hurting someone is bad. Saving people is good. At no point in there does someones opinion on lettuce tariffs become relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but none of that is really a profound statement. Of course suffering is bad and preventing suffering is good. But it doesn't seem like the statement quoted is talking about lettuce tariffs, it's talking about not sacrificing individuals for the greater good. He's saying the needs of the many don't outweigh the needs of the few, the needs of those in immediate danger outweigh the needs of those in future danger. If he can save you now, he will, and he'll deal with the consequences later.<br /> <br /> To be fair, this isn't exactly an attitude unique to Cap. It's very common among superheroes. And it's a much more defensible when you have superhuman abilities and a massive support network like most superheroes do, it's pretty reasonable to focus on the immediate danger, because there's a pretty good chance that when the future danger comes, you'll be able to handle that too. But it's one of those fiction tropes that has always bugged me, because it sounds all honorable and inspiring in fiction where author fiat can insure the consequences are circumvented, or at least swept under the rug. But in real life it's just not that simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1001172#post1001172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm reading a bit into it. But it's a really short speech, I think you can forgive me a few liberties <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool. We all interpret these things in our own ways <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1001172#post1001172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone can really accuse Captain America of being unwilling to make hard decisions, or being short sighted, or being unable to handle power well. Unless Mark Millar is writing him, but, well, that's Mark Millar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't know, I'm not much of a comic book girl. But, as a casual enjoyer of superhero media, I've never cared much for Captain America. Spierman has always been my Marvel hero of choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T09:43:21-08:00","id":1001386,"title":"","content":"I'm seeing my psychiatrist today. It's not much beyond a refill prescription and some chatting, but I'm nervous as hell anyway. Why? No idea. Maybe cumulative stress? All I know is that I'm edgy and uncomfortable. I'm supposed to go shopping for some games afterwards with family and, while normally that'd be great, I'm tempted to &quot;conveniently'&quot; lose a few fingers to a blender mishap just to get out of it. Ugh.<br /> Ok, I guess I'm done bitching for now. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T09:51:00-08:00","id":1001388,"title":"","content":"I'm getting a referral tomorrow, suppose I should start getting things in order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T05:11:20-08:00","id":1001716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1001058#post1001058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>You people telling me how I just don't <b>understand?</b> When it's <b>you</b> people-- you <b>clever</b> people-- who don't get it. I don't let people die because it's the lesser of two evils, or expedient, or because it serves the greater good... I don't compare the act against something else-- I see someone who needs help... <b>And I help.</b>You think it's a weakness. You think it's simple... But you're wrong. It's what makes us human... Which is exactly what we're supposed to be fighting for. I know who I am. I rescue the helpless. I raise up the hopeless. I don't measure people's lives... <b>I save them. </b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>He sounds like a privileged straight white cis male who is smugly explaining to a minority about how he doesn't see race/sexuality/religion/etc.... in everything. Basically an #AllLiveMatter guy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T05:34:36-08:00","id":1001720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1001716#post1001716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He sounds like a privileged straight white cis male who is smugly explaining to a minority about how he doesn't see race/sexuality/religion/etc.... in everything. Basically an #AllLiveMatter guy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I must admit that I lost the capability to take you seriously when you had to mention his race, gender and sexual orientation.<br /> <br /> Why couldn't it just be &quot;a privileged person who is smugly explaining to a minority&quot;.<br /> <br /> I must also admit that some of this annoyance may come from the fact that I am:<br /> a): Privileged as hell.<br /> b): White.<br /> c): Cis.<br /> d): Male.<br /> <br /> (I'm not straight though, I am both completely asexual and aromantic.)<br /> <br /> But I basically feel excluded from any feminist or anti-racist communities, because I keep getting hit with &quot;white people do X&quot; or &quot;white people be like Y&quot;, and I honestly feel rather annoyed at this given that I spend my entire work, speaking for those who can't speak up themselves (I'm trying to make a habit of volunteering my services as a lawyer relatively cheaply or even free for some cases if I sympathize with my client. It's wonderful to be able to do that.), yet none of that fucking matters because I'm just a white cis male who should check his privilege and shut up.<br /> <br /> I mean, what does it fucking matter that I literally live in an apartment when I could have bought a fucking <i>mansion</i> instead because I could have simply have chosen not to throw exorbitant amounts of money in charity?<br /> <br /> So maybe I should just start abusing the fact that I <i>have </i>privilege and that I could buy a car more expensive than some people have houses.<br /> <br /> Sorry if this comes off as against you directly, but I hope you can understand my frustration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T06:55:20-08:00","id":1001739,"title":"","content":"Yeah, being generalized like that does make you feel really crappy :'0<br /> <br /> I wish I would have been there when you heard those &quot;white people do X&quot; phrase to tell you that you are awesome and a good person (uuuu, I have to re-type this sentence a dozen time but it still sounds so love confession-ly)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T11:48:05-08:00","id":1002288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1001739#post1001739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, being generalized like that does make you feel really crappy :'0<br /> <br /> I wish I would have been there when you heard those &quot;white people do X&quot; phrase to tell you that you are awesome and a good person (uuuu, I have to re-type this sentence a dozen time but it still sounds so love confession-ly)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a nice and wonderful thing to be told.<br /> <br /> But really though, I live in a pretty low-class apartment and my car is laughable comparable to my colleagues. The only expensive things I have are my computer, my suits and my RPG books (of which I have been buying significantly less as of recently), so being told that I only have my job due to white privilege when I attended a pretty shitty school and only managed to drag myself out of &quot;will probably end as a gang member&quot; through sheer studying and desire for something else, is pretty annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T11:58:32-08:00","id":1002292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1002288#post1002288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is a nice and wonderful thing to be told.<br /> <br /> But really though, I live in a pretty low-class apartment and my car is laughable comparable to my colleagues. The only expensive things I have are my computer, my suits and my RPG books (of which I have been buying significantly less as of recently), so being told that I only have my job due to white privilege when I attended a pretty shitty school and only managed to drag myself out of &amp;quot;will probably end as a gang member&amp;quot; through sheer studying and desire for something else, is pretty annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that you or me have what we do only through white privilege, but that we have/had an easier time getting even what little we have. I work for a smidge over minimum wage, but even that is something I have a better shot at getting as a white person who looks male with a 'normal' name over a black girl with a 'weird' name well before the resume comes out or the imterview starts. White privilege isn't saying white people get everything handed to them on a silver platter, but acknowledging the very real bias in our favor in the Western world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T12:28:36-08:00","id":1002307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1002292#post1002292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not that you or me have what we do only through white privilege, but that we have/had an easier time getting even what little we have. I work for a smidge over minimum wage, but even that is something I have a better shot at getting as a white person who looks male with a 'normal' name over a black girl with a 'weird' name well before the resume comes out or the imterview starts. White privilege isn't saying white people get everything handed to them on a silver platter, but acknowledging the very real bias in our favor in the Western world.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I never claimed that it was.<br /> <br /> There certainly is a very real bias and privilege towards people who are white, but this doesn't really change my situation does it? I mean, I'm still being accused of having had a huge advantage over everyone else due to my white skin colour, I'm still being put into a huge box of &quot;white people&quot; and I'm still being told that my opinions don't count because I'm actually comfortable with being cisgender.<br /> <br /> But I still agree with the feminist and LGBTQIA agendas! I really just needed to vent up there, because I sure as hell won't let a few idiots who ruin an otherwise beautiful message ruin it for me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:54:36-08:00","id":1002344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1002307#post1002307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I never claimed that it was.<br /> <br /> There certainly is a very real bias and privilege towards people who are white, but this doesn't really change my situation does it? I mean, I'm still being accused of having had a huge advantage over everyone else due to my white skin colour,</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept itself only says that you had an advantage over a hypothetical person who was in the same situation, but black, or apparently female, or otherwise lacking in the benefits of the systemic bias. If people are explicitly claiming you only have what you have as a direct result of those advantages, they're misunderstanding the concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1002307#post1002307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still being put into a huge box of &quot;white people&quot; and I'm still being told that my opinions don't count because I'm actually comfortable with being cisgender.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is unfortunate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1002307#post1002307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I still agree with the feminist and LGBTQIA agendas! I really just needed to vent up there, because I sure as hell won't let a few idiots who ruin an otherwise beautiful message ruin it for me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And your support is appreciated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:02:56-08:00","id":1002347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1002344#post1002344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The concept itself only says that you had an advantage over a hypothetical person who was in the same situation, but black, or apparently female, or otherwise lacking in the benefits of the systemic bias. If people are explicitly claiming you only have what you have as a direct result of those advantages, they're misunderstanding the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>And see, I understand this. But that doesn't make it less of an annoying thing to be told, *especially* when I'm not even ethnically Danish. I'm half-Iranian and just happen to look more white than I look brown, which makes it rather hurtful since I didn't really feel ethnically Danish or ethnically Iranian when I went to school, and I made my way through law school by studying <i>really hard </i>and managing grades that were near-perfect by basically not sleeping.<br /> <br /> I dedicated my <i>life </i>to this job essentially.<br /> <br /> It's not me arguing against you, it's me trying to vent in this thread basically.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1002344#post1002344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is unfortunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1002344#post1002344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And your support is appreciated!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least <i>something </i>is appreciated. :V","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T06:08:34-08:00","id":1002512,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, I have not had a good week. Monday I found out that a friend of mine was pressured by a taxi driver into pimping herself out to him and another taxi driver and fare they had with them. She got out safely, but now legal action is being taken. Wednesday I was consoling complete strangers at the University Starbucks who had no clue of American relatives were safe. Thursday I helped an imam clean up the shattered remnants of his mosque's windows. Friday I had to remind my teenage sister that hitting me because she's annoyed by something I said isn't appropriate because my parents wouldn't. Yesterday, my parents spent a good hour making fun of the things I like, humiliating me for asking them to stop, and saying that I have a &quot;holier than thou&quot; attitude for doing so.<br /> <br /> I'm doing better with my depression and anxiety, but this week is really messing with my zen. I have a really small circle of friends, and one of them recently went off to Saskatchewan for RCMP training, so my support network is a little strained right now since I feel awful leaning heavily on one of my other friends right now because we all have our own baggage to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T12:55:16-08:00","id":1002612,"title":"","content":"Sorry to hear that. Problems never came one by one, do they? I appreciate you helping people despite your own problems, that speaks highly of yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T06:24:26-08:00","id":1002859,"title":"","content":"No, they certainly do not Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a>, I needed that.<br /> <br /> This has been one hell of a bad week for... most of North America, I think, and having a space like this to vent is helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:27:21-08:00","id":1003744,"title":"","content":"Seriously.<br /> <br /> At least something's looking up. My kid was kicked out of school a while ago and we finally managed to get him into a new, good one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T03:19:49-08:00","id":1003839,"title":"","content":"My morning sicknesss has yet to subside. I'm 25 weeks pregnant it should be over already. I ran out of the medication (Zofran how i love you &lt;3 )that was actually working and making it so i could eat, and function, and my insurance is a bunch of dickweasels and are refusing to fill it as they JUST filled for 30 weeks ago, and they only allow 30 a month. (This is likely because its expensive, for the 30 pills its like 650 bucks.)<br /> <br /> So i've spent the last two days in bed damn near 24/7 sleeping a ton because i just cant be awake. I cant function, I cant eat, i'm dizzy blah blah fucking blah. I was also out of weed so i was double fucked. Its making me depressed as shit, because i'm having to ask for extra help with my daughter, because I cant even walk first thing in the morning, so the stairs are a no go.) I just want to curl into a ball in bed and sleep until its time to give birth. My body is exsausted...<br /> <br /> I finally borrowed some money to go to the dispensary and get more weed, I had planned to take this week off of smoking, but it helps my morning sickness, so since i cant get the zofran i have no choice. However the time when i need its effects most I CANT use it. (Ie. while my husband is at work and i'm home alone with the baby). Even IF my husband was okay with me smoking while watching the baby alone(it doesnt effect my ability to be a parent thank you very much. I function just fine while high <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I'm under investigation by CPS, and they are doing random unnanoucned house visits. I promised them i wasnt smoking while home alone with the baby, if they showed up while i was high, id be fucked.<br /> <br /> I hate this. I want my body back, between this and the intermitinet horrifying insomnia i'm jsut done with this pregnancy its draining me in so many ways, to the point i'm considering getting my tubes tied once loki is born, because I cant do this again...i just cant. If i got pregnant within 2 years of his birth i think it would destroy my mental health, because i'm declining pretty hard this pregnancy, i cant imagine the third will be better as my first i was plauged with issues too, 2nd was worse...I dont trust birth control (be it pills, shot, or iud) because HAHAHA jokes on me loki is a depo shot baby. 99% effective my ass. Pills make me ragey and depressed, so not an option, patch sears my skin, I HATE CONDOMS. The IUD scares the shit out of me, noooo i dont want something rammed into my uterus and LEFT THERE.That sounds like the opposite of a good idea to me. Plus the scary ass risks thanks no thankks.<br /> <br /> I dont even know what the fuck i'm talking about anymore. I'm very high and feel amazing for the first time in 3 days. I'm not looking forward to going to sleep, cause I KNOW i'll wake up feeling like shit again...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T15:55:31-08:00","id":1005141,"title":"","content":"Since I'm basically looking for advice everywhere I might as well do it here.<br /> <br /> A group of friends I cared a LOT about stopped talking to me from one day to the other. One said she needed a pause from everything, the others just followed her example. The problem is, they only removed me from their life, while they keep chatting, playing and having fun as usual. Tentatives to talk to them ended badly, with them accusing me of not respecting their desires. Which is true, not gonna deny it, but the whole thing triggered me so hard.<br /> <br /> I'm also borderline and have severe anxiety and abandonment issues. The result of adding all that together gave birth to one of the worst months of my life. Things are not good right now, and the more I see them discarding me, the worse it gets. They said they'll contact me eventually, but I doubt it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T16:09:28-08:00","id":1005144,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a>, I have empathy for that situation. It's been a long time ago now, but I remember the sting like it was yesterday, that I too found myself suddenly without any of the friendships I'd been believing in for years - I was suddenly a complete outsider when I'd previously thought of myself as basically everyone's friend, and it took time for me to find comfort in that state.<br /> <br /> And I know it's easier said than done, but I recommend moving on. Find a way to be <i>you</i> and be satisfied with that, rather than letting others have this kind of power to make you feel lesser. I found that once I no longer needed any friends, it was easy to not only find more friendships, but deeper and more meaningful ones as well.<br /> <br /> At any rate, whatever you decide to do, I want you to know you've got at least me rooting for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T16:50:45-08:00","id":1005155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1005144#post1005144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a>, I have empathy for that situation. It's been a long time ago now, but I remember the sting like it was yesterday, that I too found myself suddenly without any of the friendships I'd been believing in for years - I was suddenly a complete outsider when I'd previously thought of myself as basically everyone's friend, and it took time for me to find comfort in that state.<br /> <br /> And I know it's easier said than done, but I recommend moving on. Find a way to be <i>you</i> and be satisfied with that, rather than letting others have this kind of power to make you feel lesser. I found that once I no longer needed any friends, it was easy to not only find more friendships, but deeper and more meaningful ones as well.<br /> <br /> At any rate, whatever you decide to do, I want you to know you've got at least me rooting for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, really. It does mean a lot.<br /> <br /> It's just they were a fundamental part of my life and now I just feel gutted. I don't deny my mistakes, but being left hanging is just horrible. Sigh, we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T16:08:45-08:00","id":1015397,"title":"","content":"Deprssion. <br /> <br /> I'm still in the hospital. I was given false hope this morning that I would get to go home today. I've officially been here a full week.<br /> <br /> I caught the flu, it hit my lungs bad. Now I dont feel sick anymore but my lungs still need help to do their job and I require oxygen round the clock. Nasal cannula during the day, CPAP at night.<br /> I'm being told that it's possible this lung issue isn't just from a virus. Okay doc well figures it the fuck out instead of getting my hopes up.<br /> <br /> I have seen my one year old twice. That's it. For a grand total of maybe 30 minuets. I miss my baby, I miss being home.<br /> So all the energy I had when I was told the supposed good news ranked when they ended up saying no you can't go home.<br /> <br /> I've just laid in my bed crying and sleeping I feel defeated and done. I want to go home to my husband and child. I want to not be in constant pain in my back from laying in this hospital bed all day.<br /> <br /> I'm drained. It's that simple.<br /> <br /> They have me on Dilaudid and Flexeril for my pain, Ambien for sleep. And a truck load of other crap for other shit.<br /> <br /> I'm tired of pills, tired of hearing my oxygen monitor beep when my stats drop to low. Tired of this fucking nasal cannula drying out my nose.<br /> <br /> I miss my baby the most being away from her is the hardest thing I've ever done, she's okay, but I'm not. I'm really not. The depression today is just hurting me. They gave me Ativan because I had an anxiety attack or something I just am at the end of my rope with being in this hospital. And the finish line seems to be moved away Everytime I get close","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 12-10-2016, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T13:56:10-08:00","id":1016228,"title":"","content":"That sounds extremely frustrating. I do hope you get to go home soon, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar897_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"897\" data-vbnamecard=\"897\">Scelesta</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T21:52:22-08:00","id":1016401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1016228#post1016228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds extremely frustrating. I do hope you get to go home soon, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar897_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"897\" data-vbnamecard=\"897\">Scelesta</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was super frustrating!<br /> <br /> I got discharged yesterday thank goodness. Not empty handed, i still require oxygen(THANKS LUNGS for not working right), so i got an oxygen machine and some tanks from the hospital, still need my nebulizer treatments, so i was given a nebulizer machine, and have sleep apnea so in a couple weeks have to do a stupid sleep study so my insurance will cover the cpap machine. The doctors REALLY wanted me to go home with a cpap machine thats how bad my sleep apnea is appearntly, however they couldnt get the higher ups to approve, and my insurance of course said nto without a sleep doctor testing her first. <br /> <br /> Oh well, I'm home thats what matters. Still depressed as shit. Self medicating on diluaded and weed *shrugs* guess the depression wasnt from the hospital etc. My one year old was beyond excited to see me and fell asleep in my arms while we sat on the couch. I missed that so much","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T02:47:49-08:00","id":1016472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1016401#post1016401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It was super frustrating!<br /> <br /> I got discharged yesterday thank goodness. Not empty handed, i still require oxygen(THANKS LUNGS for not working right), so i got an oxygen machine and some tanks from the hospital, still need my nebulizer treatments, so i was given a nebulizer machine, and have sleep apnea so in a couple weeks have to do a stupid sleep study so my insurance will cover the cpap machine. The doctors REALLY wanted me to go home with a cpap machine thats how bad my sleep apnea is appearntly, however they couldnt get the higher ups to approve, and my insurance of course said nto without a sleep doctor testing her first.<br /> <br /> Oh well, I'm home thats what matters. Still depressed as shit. Self medicating on diluaded and weed *shrugs* guess the depression wasnt from the hospital etc. My one year old was beyond excited to see me and fell asleep in my arms while we sat on the couch. I missed that so much</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you can get through the whole sleep study thing quickly. I did one earlier this year and it took six months from referral to getting my results. Fortunately, I <i>don't</i> have sleep apnea, but it was still a frustrating process.<br /> <br /> Glad to hear you're home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T23:45:32-08:00","id":1031029,"title":"","content":"Seeing my therapist tomorrow. I haven't checked in with the witch doctor since last month, and that was the only time I've seen her. I'm a little nervous, and kinda confused about how to drop my innate shield of deflecting conversation away from my issues. Anyone have advice on how I might be able to just drop my guard, push through or &quot;trick myself&quot; into maybe being more forthcoming about my feelings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T01:47:01-08:00","id":1031048,"title":"","content":"You could try writing down what you want to discuss on a note and hand it over at the start of the session. If you do you could preface it with &quot;I tend to deflect when it comes to my issues so I write some of them down here.&quot; or something similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T08:13:30-08:00","id":1031162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1031029#post1031029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have advice on how I might be able to just drop my guard, push through or &quot;trick myself&quot; into maybe being more forthcoming about my feelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>It took me months building up trust with my old therapist to get to the point where I could start opening up. Literal months. Unfortunately she ended up moving and I got (yet another) new therapist, and I really didn't want to go through another half a year of getting to the point where I could open up. What I did, and it may or may not work for you, is I told my new therapist in the third meeting &quot;I need to talk. Please don't speak, let me get this all out. I need to pretend I'm not talking to you and I'm just talking to myself&quot;. And that's what I did. I shut my eyes, told myself I was alone in the room (for about ten to fifteen minutes) and started talking like I would if I were talking to myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:10:01-08:00","id":1032778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1031029#post1031029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing my therapist tomorrow. I haven't checked in with the witch doctor since last month, and that was the only time I've seen her. I'm a little nervous, and kinda confused about how to drop my innate shield of deflecting conversation away from my issues. Anyone have advice on how I might be able to just drop my guard, push through or &quot;trick myself&quot; into maybe being more forthcoming about my feelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have a drink beforehand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:28:14-08:00","id":1032788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1032778#post1032778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have a drink beforehand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know the comment was kind of tongue-in-cheek, but...<br /> <br /> Yeah, actually that could help. So long as you don't have a substance abuse issue, stopping for a quick drink might not be a bad idea. In the early days of meeting my old therapist (AKA the good one), I'd often stop off at a bar for a quick beer on the way. It helped &quot;loosen my lips&quot; before the meeting and often made the inevitable unpacking of my issues a little easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:42:32-08:00","id":1032961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1032788#post1032788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the comment was kind of tongue-in-cheek, but...<br /> <br /> Yeah, actually that could help. So long as you don't have a substance abuse issue, stopping for a quick drink might not be a bad idea. In the early days of meeting my old therapist (AKA the good one), I'd often stop off at a bar for a quick beer on the way. It helped &quot;loosen my lips&quot; before the meeting and often made the inevitable unpacking of my issues a little easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I had to quit drinking. I don't disagree with the advice, but I do deal with some substance issues. Thanks, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:00:39-08:00","id":1033004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1032961#post1032961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I had to quit drinking. I don't disagree with the advice, but I do deal with some substance issues. Thanks, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the response I was actually hoping for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Good work, little brother.<br /> <br /> So, serious answer, deep breaths and repeating to yourself that whatever happens in there goes no further than that room. Remind yourself that it is a safe space and that everything you say not only is kept confidential, but can also help the therapist help you. Seemingly insignificant details can be VERY telling to the therapist.<br /> <br /> And above all, no matter what happens, we love ya anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T18:32:52-08:00","id":1033080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1032961#post1032961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I had to quit drinking. I don't disagree with the advice, but I do deal with some substance issues. Thanks, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, there are so many things I want to say, but the only one that really matters is; You made the right, healthy choice to quit. Always, always, always remember that. You're stronger than a lot of people who have a problem but never admit it, let alone take steps to remedy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T20:33:49-07:00","id":1092208,"title":"","content":"I think I feel another episode building again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T23:33:13-07:00","id":1094787,"title":"","content":"I'm going to do something stupid tonight. I can't help it. I need the relief. The pain. The ritual comfort. I'm covered in scars anyway. Just a few more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T16:30:06-07:00","id":1094964,"title":"","content":"I actually wish you didn't have to. Then again I am binge eating and then puking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T19:14:23-08:00","id":1285456,"title":"","content":"what does it say about someone when they say they want to help you but just set off a major episode of depression?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T19:03:06-07:00","id":1403320,"title":"","content":"Because I figure a lot of us are probably in a bad place these days and maybe could do with this thread coming back so they have somewhere to vent... lemme start:<br /> <br /> Anyone else's virtually-uncontrolled depressive episodes and severe anxiety steadily destroying them every second they reside in an increasingly-hostile country? Because ha ha hi","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T22:16:23-07:00","id":1403340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1403320#post1403320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I figure a lot of us are probably in a bad place these days and maybe could do with this thread coming back so they have somewhere to vent...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyone else's virtually-uncontrolled depressive episodes and severe anxiety steadily destroying them every second they reside in an increasingly-hostile country? </div> </div> </div>(raises hand)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32483-the-mental-health-thread?p=1403320#post1403320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ha ha hi</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah-ha, ahh, aha, haha, hah, hoo...<br /> <br /> \u200bYou ever feel something in your brain presenting you with an immediate choice, &quot;Laugh or cry, <i>right now</i>. If you don't laugh right now, you're gonna cry,&quot; so you immediately force out a little uncomfortable giggle?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T11:40:47-07:00","id":1411659,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve had to take a step I never thought I\u2019d reach, though why I never thought that is kind of it\u2019s own big box to unpack. I\u2019m asking my job for a leave of absence due to stress and ongoing mental health issues. <br /> <br /> Even though I\u2019ve already been given the go-ahead and the blessing of basically the most senior person in my office as well as my direct supervisor I still feel... ashamed about it? I worry that my other coworkers will resent me for leaving during a crunch time. Every step of dealing with the paperwork feels like it\u2019s questioning whether I\u2019m really feeling what I\u2019m feeling and amplifying the voice in my head that says I\u2019m not actually depressed I\u2019m just lazy and cowardly. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure I\u2019ll feel better about it once I\u2019ve actually finalized everything, but right now \u2018not\u2019 working somehow feels like the hardest thing I\u2019ve ever done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}